window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4701,"title":"Chapter 4701: Chapter 4700: Eon! II","paragraphs":["Chapter 4700: Eon! II","His Imposition was a truly domineering one as the Phoneme of Tyranny appeared above him and spun with an incandescent purple glow. Everything seemed to slow down as his entire visage radiated splendor. His small figure immediately gave off an extremely imposing and terrifying air, and when his leg began to move down, THE Scorched was alarmed as it felt its existence seemingly about to be cut into countless pieces and collapsed.","THE Scorched Leviathan of Cinders roared with a majestic voice that shook the Wastes, its Dogma erupting from the very core of its burning existence.","“My flames cannot be severed by anything in Existence! That which burns eternally knows no blade, no edge, no cutting force! I am fire unending, and fire cannot be divided!”","...!","One sought to cut by placing their foot down, and one denied this as they said they could not be cut.","In the next moment, Noah’s brilliant figure forcefully brought down his foot in its entirety.","BOOM!","The collision of Imposition and Dogma lasted less than a heartbeat.","Blue-gold light erupted from Noah’s descending foot like an existential blade carving through reality itself. The Phoneme of Tyranny burned with such intensity that it overwrote the very concept of what could and could not be severed. His Imposition did not argue with the Dogma. It did not debate. It simply declared with such absolute authority that the Dogma’s philosophical framework crumbled before it could fully establish itself.","THE Scorched Leviathan of Cinders’ eyes showed utter incredulity as the severing light passed through its existence. Its flames, which had burned since before THE Fallout, which had consumed multiple entities to fuel their eternal conflagration, were cut apart like paper before a blade that recognized no limitation.","It wanted to ask, “Bro, what the fuck was this? I didn’t even get to salivate or chase after you?!”","But its existence was already dimming into oblivion, its Way collapsing, its Cognizance fading, its very concept of self being severed into fragments that could no longer maintain coherence.","|Imposition victorious over Dogma.|","|Analysis: THE Scorched Leviathan’s Dogma operated on the conviction that its flames were eternal and indivisible.|","|However, your Imposition was backed by the full immensity of your Depth, the Phoneme of Tyranny, and the Philology of Undifferentiated Mana.|","|The Phoneme of Tyranny grants absolute authority to your declarations when sufficient immensity supports them.|","|Your Imposition did not attempt to argue that flames could be severed. It simply declared that your foot was the sharpest blade, making the question of what can or cannot be cut irrelevant.|","|Against a Dogma that relies on defining limitations, an Imposition that ignores limitations entirely will always prevail if backed by sufficient weight.|","...!","As Noah looked at the collapse of yet another Civilization under his hands, his gaze was cold and imperious as he observed everything that represented the Way and existence of this creature begin to be bundled up into a brilliant song of golden light by his Phonemes.","Similar to THE Emerged, but because the Depth of THE Scorched was a bit greater, two golden strings formed from the remnants of the Civilization.","They began to flow toward him.","|Loot generated from THE Scorched Leviathan of Cinders.|","|2 Fragments of THE Moirai Threads obtained.|","|Current Fragment Count: 2/9|","|Note: Higher Depth entities yield greater Fragment quantities.|","...!","Noah kept them inside of his existence calmly as he took another step and disappeared even further inward, prepared to smoothly bypass the regions that he had in his memory before he had an encounter with one of the more terrifying types of existences.","THE Secretive Eon!","—","Across The Wastes of THE Fallout.","The end of Existence came with a lot of things as different entities faced different challenges and entirely different results.","The veil between the Living and the Dead was completely torn as the lands of the Living and the Dead effectively did not exist anymore.","All that existed was the landscape after THE Fallout.","It was ashen domains of destruction and brilliance in equal measure, as it seemed like an apocalypse and also the emergence of something unfathomably new.","A few minutes after the Second Phase of THE Fallout had ended. In an unknown region of Observable Existence.","“Ah...”","A consciousness woke up as if it had been in a long and endless slumber.","The consciousness was none other than the Great Usurper, Eckert!","But as he woke up at this time, he found himself confined in what felt like a relatively small space.","His Idle Existence had covered an extremely expansive region of the Lands of the Dead as he knew how it felt when he covered such an expansive space.","But at this moment, he felt contained.","What was...","|Emergency Consciousness Preservation Protocol – Complete.|","|The emergence of THE Fallout and its subsequent actions over Observable Existence distorted and expanded your existence in a grotesque fashion.|","|For the sake of survival of a cognizant consciousness, a risk was taken to utilize the force of THE Fallout to infuse your consciousness into the Fragment of The Axiom of Primordial Paradox.|","|The gamble was successful due to the chaotic Weavings of Existence.|","|Your consciousness was contained within the Fragment of The Axiom of Primordial Paradox, but the effects of THE Fallout were pervasive.|","|Your existence has been branded with the Curse of THE Existential Ceiling.|","|Your existence has been branded as a Scorched.|","|The Scorched are entities whose very existence has been permanently set ablaze by The Fallout. They burn continuously with the multicolored flames of existential annihilation, and rather than being consumed, they have learned to fuel themselves with the destruction.|","|Your consciousness is wreathed in perpetual flames of The Fallout.|","|You can project and weaponize Fallout energy.|","|You are immune to further Fallout damage.|","|You feed on destruction and decay.|","|You would have gradually lost your original personality and memories, but the Fragment of The Axiom of Primordial Paradox prevents this deterioration.|","|You are now a Cinder, a newly Scorched Lifeform.|","|Your consciousness is contained in the Fragment of The Axiom of Primordial Paradox and has integrated with it by 1% so far.|","|Idle Expansion with the emergence of Idle Loot of THE Fallout is now possible.|","|Proceed?|","...!","Eckert’s consciousness shone brightly as he viewed all these prompts for another instant before he nodded with enthusiasm, his mind bright as he wondered...","Did Osmont come out the other side okay?","Because at this moment, it did not seem like he could reach him!","But he would go slowly and see just what had changed with him and with existence at large. And...where the hell were his Disciples of THE Creature?!"]},{"number":4702,"title":"Chapter 4702: Chapter 4701: Eon! III","paragraphs":["Chapter 4701: Eon! III","Others had easy lives. Others struggled.","But if ever you found yourself living an easy life, you should be worried. Deeply, profoundly worried. Because Existence was a sadistic teacher who believed in learning through suffering.","If the lessons stopped, it didn’t mean you had graduated. It meant the teacher was preparing something special. Something that would make all previous lessons look like warm-up exercises. Noah had learned this truth the hard way, which was, coincidentally, the only way Existence ever taught anything.","If the path before you was smooth and unobstructed, something was horrendously wrong. Either you were being fattened for slaughter, or you had already died and simply hadn’t noticed yet.","At this moment.","Noah had trekked through The Wastes as he followed the events of the Partial Simulation closely, and at this moment, he was staring at the grand and seemingly endless boundary of THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.","His eyes radiated an imperious light of power and conviction, burning with the certainty of one who had weighed the risks and found them acceptable. His gaze was steady, his stance unwavering, and when he spoke, his voice carried the weight of absolute commitment.","“In for a penny, in for a pound.”","BOOM!","And right after, he entered a chaotic region of Existence that was trying to pull his Weavings in every single direction simultaneously.","But his body was already pulsing and radiating Phonemes of The First Tongue, his immensity causing him to look like an unstoppable force with an indomitable momentum as he remained steady throughout until he was deposited...","BOOM!","Into a glorious place.","His vision adjusted as he looked around to see The Stoa of Dogmata. Exactly as he saw in the Partial Simulation.","The endless colonnade of pillars stretched before him in impossible grandeur, each one carved from crystallized authority that predated differentiation itself. Inscriptions of ancient Dogmata glowed upon their surfaces, some burning with cold fire, others weeping tears of solidified time. The zones of doctrine shimmered between the pillars like veils separating different philosophical realities, and further in, multicolored clouds obscured the depths of this place in impenetrable mystery.","But what the Partial Simulation had not fully conveyed was the ground beneath his feet.","The earth he stood on was obsidian, black and gleaming like volcanic glass that had been polished by eons of existence. Obsidian tendrils of crackling light spread across its surface like veins of destabilizing power, pulsing with energies that would have torn apart a weak THE Surface Depth entity in moments.","|Welcome to the Second Circle of THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.|","|Current Location: The Stoa of Dogmata.|","|Caution: The ground itself carries destabilizing energies.|","...!","Noah sensed and observed all of this, but the vast entirety of his attention turned to his right at this moment.","There, just like in the Partial Simulation, was the image of a serene and glorious woman.","Eon!","THUMP!","Okay, so his heart beat a little faster. Not in a juvenile way and not because he was smitten, but in that anticipatory way when you met an extremely unpredictable variable that could collapse you at any moment.","And this entity had a light smile as she looked toward him with a light of intrigue.","This time around, he caught her gaze before she looked away in a bored fashion since he knew she would be here, and their gazes met.","She was small in stature, almost delicate in appearance, with features that held an ageless quality that made it impossible to determine if she was young or ancient beyond measure.","Her face was composed and regal, with high cheekbones and dark eyes that seemed to hold depths far greater than any physical form should contain. There was a stillness about her, a sense of absolute control and purpose that radiated from her very being!","Her hair was dark as the void between stars, but strands of gold flowed through it like rivers of light through an endless night, catching the ambient glow of the Stoa in ways that seemed almost deliberate. A white-blue robe covered her form, simple yet somehow more elegant than the most elaborate garments, as if the fabric itself knew it was privileged to drape across her shoulders.","And her eyes!","Oh!","Her pupils seemed to be the simplest and most common pupils, dark and unremarkable at first glance. And yet...","|Warning.|","|You have stared into eyes that may harm your existence if you gaze for too long.|","|Recommendation: Limit direct visual contact.|","...!","Staring into her eyes alone for too long could harm him.","Noah’s gaze flashed with defiance at this as he blinked, and he cautiously floated toward this terrifying entity as he spoke out calmly.","“Hello. You are one of the few cognizant beings I have met since the end of THE Fallout. I am-”","As he was speaking, the terrifying entity seated ahead looked away into the depths of this domain. Her voice came measured and unhurried, each word placed with the precision of someone who had spent eternities choosing exactly what to say and when to say it.","“I know who you are, Scale Breaker. I watched you take your first stumbling steps in the Primordial Genesis Shore.”","BOOM!","Her gaze finally settled on him with the weight of ages.","“Whether you have grown bolder or merely more foolish since then, I have not yet decided.”","BOOM!","Her words were heavy as Noah instantly became stern.","She was there?","In Ginnungagap?!","He did not recall seeing anything about her or even closely resembling her in all the Ginnu Lifeforms there. She looked at his silence and surprise as she continued looking ahead calmly, her posture unchanged, her attention seemingly fixed on something in the distant depths that only she could perceive.","Noah’s reply came cautiously, his voice measured. “You were there when THE Primordial Chaos, THE Creature, and THE Living Temporal fought? And none of them sensed you either? You weren’t involved in that entire conflict?”","...!","At such words, THE Secretive Eon’s expression remained unchanged. When she spoke, there was no defensiveness, no need to justify. Only quiet, glorious, interminable certainty.","“THE Creature knew I was there from the moment he arrived. The others...” A slight pause came that was almost dismissive. “They saw what they expected to see, which was nothing at all. But that is the way of things.”","Her head tilted, a fraction of movement that somehow conveyed vast consideration.","“You call what happened there a conflict. Perhaps it was, from where you stood. But it was not anything much.”","The faintest ghost of something unreadable crossed her features before vanishing.","“That you know who I am is unexpected. I will grant you that much. But it makes your presence here all the more puzzling.”","She turned to regard him fully, and her calm was more terrifying than any display of power could have been.","“Do you believe yourself grand now, Scale Breaker? Because you have laid claim to The First Tongue?”","The question hung in the air, requiring no answer.","“You know what I am. You know what entities such as myself do to ones such as yourself. And yet here you stand.”","Her dark eyes studied him with an attention that felt like being weighed on scales older than Existence itself.","“I find myself curious despite my better judgment. Why?”","Why.","The question was a simple one as Noah felt a sense of danger and stopped moving forward, looking at this terrifying being as he said...","“Just my intuition.”","...!","BOOM!","Intuition.","The word left her lips like she was tasting something she had not encountered in a very long time.","“Intuition...”","Her eyes grew distant for a moment, seeing something far beyond the Stoa, far beyond this moment entirely.","Then she smiled.","“What a curious and ridiculous thing to say.”","Her gaze refocused on him with renewed interest!"]},{"number":4703,"title":"Chapter 4703: Chapter 4702: Eon! IV","paragraphs":["Chapter 4702: Eon! IV","Intuition.","Noah said these words because truly, his intuition was one of the few things he followed, paired by the fact that no matter how dangerous this could potentially be, he had an Anchor Point he could go back to.","And yet THE Secretive Eon reacted as if she had heard these exact words before.","Noah thought about things carefully before he kept his distance and proceeded to sit down just like her while staring out into the same direction she was staring out to.","He felt like he had to choose his next few words carefully as this entity was a bit unique, but there could be something to gain. When it came to entities like her, it was always information.","Much of Existence was filled with mysteries, but entities like her held vast knowledge already due to their power.","So he began simply after he gathered his thoughts.","“Before THE Fallout, I had a conversation with THE Living Paradox similar to this. Right before he initiated everything. Meeting someone else like him after THE Fallout felt unique, and thus my intuition brought me here.” He kept his gaze fixed on the distant expanse ahead. “When the other side is not trying to collapse me, I find the conversations can be revealing.”","...!","His words were calm, and when THE Secretive Eon heard them, she scoffed quietly while keeping her gaze ahead. Her hair flickered with radiance, strands of gold catching light that seemed to come from nowhere.","“You would place me and THE Living Paradox on the same pedestal? I find myself wondering whether that speaks more to how highly you think of him or how highly you think of yourself.”","Something flickered in her dark eyes that might have been amusement.","“You are the weakest of those four, and yet you move as if you stand among equals, as if the gap between you and them is merely a matter of time rather than an insurmountable chasm. You have not met or known of others apart from them, but still you move the way you do, still you hold yourself as you hold yourself.”","Her head tilted slightly.","“I can see it in your eyes, Scale Breaker. That same look I have seen in others across the ages. That arrogance, that feeling of infinite self-worth, as if Existence itself is meant to be yours, as if you were destined for something grand and all of this is merely the prelude to your inevitable ascension.”","Her gaze remained fixed on the distant expanse, seeing something far beyond the Stoa.","“It is never so easy. A few laid claims before you and learned that truth in ways they did not survive. THE Primordial Paradox laid claim to Paradox itself and believed himself infallible, untouchable, beyond the reach of consequence. Where is he now? Eaten. Devoured. Not a shred of his Weavings remain, and he was a million times more powerful than you are at this moment.”","BOOM!","Shocking words came from her as Noah sternly kept his gaze straight, his mind buzzing.","“THE Primordial Paradox is collapsed? Then THE Living Paradox...”","THE Secretive Eon waved her hand with a small gesture of absolute finality.","“THE Living Paradox consumed THE Primordial Paradox and became him, a creature with no claim devouring one who held absolute claim, and in doing so expressing that ideology more purely than its original bearer ever did.” The faintest curve touched her lips. “Paradox, it seems, has a sense of irony.”","She fell silent for a long moment before speaking again.","“I waste my breath saying this, and I know that I do, for more often than not those like you listen to no one, but I will say it regardless because perhaps this time will be different, though I suspect it will not be.”","Her gaze remained fixed on the endless expanse ahead.","“Take a step back, Scale Breaker, and reevaluate yourself. Do not believe yourself something special. Do not think that you have measures or protections that others lacked, or convince yourself that it is somehow impossible for you to die because of who you are. THE Primordial Paradox had many plans and many contingencies, just as you do, and he was collapsed all the same. THE Creature had many plans and many contingencies, and yet here we are, speaking of what became of them rather than speaking with them.”","Her head turned slightly, just enough that he could see the edge of her composed features.","“Existence is grand and unfathomable. THE Creature is something. THE Living Paradox is trying to be something. Others are already something. You, as of this moment, are not anything.”","There was no malice in her voice, no contempt, only truth delivered with the patience of one who had seen this conversation play out countless times across countless ages!","“If I were to offer you counsel, and I am not certain you are capable of hearing it, I would tell you to unmake everything you are and become something small, a worm or a fly, something that moves through Existence without drawing its gaze. Grow in silence, gather strength in shadow, and only when you have reached THE Absolute Depth should you allow yourself to unfold into what you truly wish to be.”","Her dark eyes finally met his directly, and the weight of ages pressed against his existence.","“Otherwise, you are courting death with every step you take, every single step, and sooner or later death will answer your courtship.” Her lips curved into something that was almost sad. “It always does.”","...!","THE Secretive Eon told him how he should live.","But Noah’s eyes burned with defiance.","Him? Crawl like a worm until he was powerful enough to stand?","What would his Tyranny say to such cowardice? Tyranny did not grovel. Tyranny did not hide. Tyranny stood in the open and dared Existence to challenge it.","What would his Quintessence stand for if he abandoned everything that made him who he was? The very core of his being rejected the notion of diminishing himself for the sake of survival.","How brilliant would his Mana shine if he smothered it beneath caution and fear? Mana was meant to blaze. It was meant to illuminate. It was not meant to be hidden away like something shameful.","No.","He sat there grandly without replying, but one could see the air of defiance around him that seemed to reject every single word of THE Secretive Eon.","He would not become a worm.","He would not become a fly.","He would remain exactly what he was, and he would grow stronger as exactly what he was, and if Existence sought to collapse him for it, then Existence would find that he did not collapse easily.","And THE Secretive Eon saw this without even turning her head.","She smiled with the expression of someone who had witnessed this same defiance countless times before and knew precisely how it ended.","Then she continued looking on ahead, saying nothing more.","...!","Extra chap should be out!"]},{"number":4704,"title":"Chapter 4704: Chapter 4703: I Am!","paragraphs":["Chapter 4703: I Am!","What does it mean to be oneself?","Many across the ages have grappled with this question, and none have arrived at an answer that satisfies all. Some say the self is merely the sum of one’s experiences, a collection of memories and traumas and joys that accumulate like sediment at the bottom of a river.","Others argue that the self is something innate, a core that exists before experience, before memory, before even the first breath of consciousness.","There are those who believe the self is an illusion, a story we tell ourselves to make sense of the chaos that surrounds us. And there are those who believe the self is the only thing that truly exists, with everything else being merely a reflection of our inner truth projected outward onto the canvas of reality.","But perhaps the most profound truth about the self is this: everyone will tell you who your self is, and who to be.","Parents will shape you in their image. Teachers will mold you according to their ideals. Friends will influence you with their expectations. Enemies will define you by opposition. Society will demand conformity.","Power will demand submission. And through it all, countless voices will whisper and shout and scream about who you should become, how you should act, what you should believe, and why you should change.","But in the end, one can only be themselves.","Because nobody knows how you can be your true self apart from you. No sage, no ancient entity watching from the shadows of existence can tell you who you are at your core. They can offer counsel. They can share wisdom. They can warn of dangers and promise rewards. But the fundamental question of selfhood can only be answered by the one asking it.","And sometimes, the answer comes not through contemplation, but through assertion, through defiant declaration. Not through becoming what others say you should be, but through embodying what you know yourself to already be.","—","Noah’s defiance was clear as at this time, he felt his Existence and Phonemes buzzing while he looked directly at the calm figure of THE Secretive Eon.","“I am realizing more and more that power comes in different forms.” His voice was steady, contemplative, yet underlaid with something that pulsed with growing conviction. “If I look at my power now, I could strictly designate myself as a THE Surface Depth or THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity, and that would be accurate. But it is also inaccurate, because I can do things no Intermediate Depth entity could do. I was able to go to the Earliest Folds. To the Infinite Unfurling. To Ginnungagap itself. I was able to evade the imprisonment in THE Belly of Existence and THE Loom when others could not. I was able to do things that no THE Intermediate entity could do, without ever stepping into THE...”","BOOM!","His eyes shone with an unfathomable light of immensity. A profound and unique air filled with ancientness and immensity began to radiate from him, and the very Stoa of Dogmata seemed to tremble in recognition of something taking shape.","“So when you say I am not at the level of THE Creature or you, perhaps in some aspects that is true. But there are things I can do that THE Creature cannot do. There are places I have been that THE Creature has not reached. I have done with The First Tongue what THE Creature never did. There are truths I have touched that THE Creature has not grasped.” His gaze burned brighter. “And if that is the case, then in those aspects, I am more powerful than THE Creature. In those aspects, I exceed him.”","BOOM!","Blue-gold light surged around him with profundity, his eyes shining like blazing suns as if he was extrapolating and expanding a glorious epiphany that had been building within him since the moment he first touched The First Tongue.","“You say I do not have any comparable power to them. That I am weaker than them. That I should hide until I am stronger, should crawl like a worm until I earn the right to stand.” His voice did not rise, did not fall, but each word landed with the weight of absolute conviction.","“And yet I believe I can move freely just like them. Because what Surface or Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity can sit here and talk to you without worry? THE Creature could talk to you as I am talking to you now. THE Living Paradox could do so. And now, I am doing so.”","He let that truth settle into the air between them.","“Because in some ways, my standing, my glory, my distinction, the very weight of my name, in some ways I am already like you and all others. That is my Way. That is my Immensity.” His eyes blazed with finality.","“I am not strong. I am not weak. I simply am.”","BOOM!","...!","His blood buzzed. His Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons buzzed. His Organ of Civilization buzzed!","His mind buzzed as he felt like he had grasped and asserted an inner truth about himself that nobody could deny, a truth that Existence itself was forced to acknowledge, to the point that he embodied it!","|Your Way has been observed and asserted and embodied with unfathomable clarity.|","|You have done something only those exceeding THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty can do.|","|Background Information from The First Tongue: Way Expression at Fundamental Depth – Declaration|","|At THE Fundamental Depth, an entity’s Way can be expressed through Declaration, the act of speaking truth into Existence and having Existence reshape itself to accommodate that truth.|","|Existential Declaration:|","|- Statements made with full authority become temporarily true|","|- “There is no fire here” could temporarily negate all flame-based Principles in an area|","|- “My enemy cannot move” could generate a Principle of Binding that locks a target in place|","|- “I am invincible” could create temporary immunity to all forms of harm|","|- The more absolute the declaration, the greater the cost to maintain|","|Way Manifestation:|","|- The entity can manifest their Way as a tangible force in reality|","|- A Way of Judgment could manifest as scales that weigh the sins of all present|","|- A Way of Death could manifest as an aura that withers all it touches|","|- These manifestations are extensions of the entity’s very being|","|Background Information from The First Tongue: Way Expression at Absolute Depth – Embodiment|","|At THE Absolute Depth, an entity’s Way transcends expression and becomes Embodiment. The entity does not merely use their Way or declare their Way. They become their Way. Their existence and their truth become indistinguishable.|","|Conceptual Embodiment:|","|- The entity’s Way becomes so intertwined with Observable Existence that they essentially become a living law|","|- THE Living Paradox embodies contradiction itself|","|- THE Creature embodies the primordial nature of existence itself|","|- THE Primordial Chaos embodies entropy and disorder itself|","|- Attacking them means attacking the very concept they represent|","|Existential Veto:|","|- Can simply declare that something does not apply to them, permanently|","|- Unlike temporary immunity, this veto becomes a fact of their existence|","|- “Death does not touch me” could become a permanent truth rather than a maintained declaration|","|- This explains how beings like THE Living Paradox can embody contradictions that would destroy lesser entities|","|Way Legislation:|","|- The entity can legislate truths related to their Way into permanent existence|","|- THE Living Paradox could legislate “Contradictions can coexist” as a permanent law of reality|","|- THE Creature could legislate “All things that exist are my children” as an absolute truth|","|- These legislations reshape Observable Existence itself|","|Sovereign Absolutism:|","|- Within the scope of their Way, the entity’s authority is absolute|","|- No being of lesser Depth can contest their sovereignty within their domain of embodiment|","|- Only other Absolute Depth entities can challenge their legislations|","|Current Assessment:|","|What you have just done was a partial form of Embodiment only possible from THE Absolute Depth of Absolute Sovereignty stage.|","|You have embodied your Way spectacularly to declare that your power cannot be designated into any specific stage.|","|Your existence has deemed your Depth to be THE Formless Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.|","|Your power and capabilities are too unique to fit into any demarcated Depth.|","|You are not Surface. You are not Intermediate. You are not Fundamental. You are not Absolute.|","|You are Formless.|","|You simply are.|","...!","HUUM!","His existence buzzed with glory!","THE Formless Depth!","Oh!","Extra chap due to cliffhanger","No cliffs!"]},{"number":4705,"title":"Chapter 4705: Chapter 4704: All Must Die I","paragraphs":["Formless Depth.","Noah’s entire existence buzzed with unfathomable brightness as he felt his mind so clear.","What was this? His body felt freer, like a cool sensation was spreading across his existence as everything coursed with immensity and vibrancy. The very fabric of reality seemed sharper and more defined!","It even felt more colorful all around, enough to make one ask: was this why people took drugs? Because it felt fucking fantastic.","But his drug right now was an immense sense of Clarity and Conviction.","Because it was unfathomably clear to him who and what he was. He felt like he could breathe much easier after knowing and accepting his Existence. There was no more uncertainty, no more grasping at definitions that did not fit, no more trying to squeeze himself into categories that were never designed to contain something like him.","He was Formless.","He simply was.","And in this clarity, he learned many things.","First was just how ridiculous those who attained THE Absolute Depth of Absolute Sovereignty were.","Embodiment was the defining factor, the thing that separated the truly transcendent from everything else.","With Embodiment, one could never truly collapse entities like THE Living Paradox, THE Primordial Chaos, and THE Creature . These beings had undergone a metamorphosis so complete that they no longer existed as separate things from the concepts they wielded. They had become those concepts. Their flesh was philosophy. Their blood was ideology.","Their very breath was the manifestation of truths so fundamental that Existence itself could not function without them.","THE Living Paradox embodied contradiction itself. Every impossibility, every logical inconsistency, every thing that should not be able to exist yet did, all of it flowed through him like rivers through a landscape. To collapse him would require the elimination of paradox from all of Existence, and paradox was woven into the very fabric of reality.","How could something exist and not exist simultaneously? It shouldn’t be possible, and yet it happened constantly. That impossibility was THE Living Paradox .","THE Creature embodied the primordial nature of existence itself. Supposedly, every entity that had ever existed, every Civilization that had ever risen and fallen, every thought that had ever been conceived, all of it traced its lineage back to him in some fashion.","THE Primordial Chaos embodied entropy and disorder itself. The gradual decay of all ordered things, the inevitable march toward dissolution, the fundamental truth that nothing could remain static forever, all of this was his domain.","And if you wanted to collapse them, to truly and permanently end their existence, it meant attacking the very concepts they represented.","If one wanted to collapse THE Creature, did that not mean they had to collapse Existence itself? How could you destroy the embodiment of existence without destroying existence in the process? It was a logical impossibility, a paradox in its own right.","As he thought of this, Noah’s mind buzzed as he released beams of blue-gold light from his eyes. The revelation was too grand to contain, too profound to keep within the boundaries of his physical form!","His expression was one of wonder. \" Is this why THE Living Paradox attacked THE Creature with THE Fallout? It was an attack on Existence itself, altering Existence overall, which would in turn be an attack on THE Creature’s Absolute Embodiment?\"","...!","He felt like he was grasping at things he didn’t even know existed. The architecture of power at the highest levels was so far beyond what he had previously understood that it made his earlier conceptions seem childish in comparison.","THE Fallout wasn’t just destruction for destruction’s sake. It was a surgical strike against the very concept of Existence, designed to wound THE Creature in a way that conventional attacks never could.","Brilliant.","Terrifying, catastrophic, and utterly monstrous in its implications, but brilliant nonetheless!","At this time, in the middle of this grand epiphany as his existence continued to buzz and a transformation was underway, THE Secretive Eon spoke.","\"I may have judged you too harshly.\"","There was no urgency in her tone and no surprise, only the calm acknowledgment of something she had observed.","\"I dismissed you entirely when we first spoke, and I must say I was even disappointed. Another fledgling stumbling into waters far too deep, I thought. Another one who would drown before learning to swim.\" She paused, her dark eyes settling on him with renewed consideration. \" But it appears you have potential.\"","\" Potential. That is what The First Tongue stood for the most, in the end. The capacity to become something more than what you currently are. I considered you a fledgling before, one who did not understand the depths he was wading into. You should now be considered something slightly more. A blind man with a walking stick, perhaps. Still unable to see, but at least capable of feeling your way forward without stumbling into every obstacle.\"","Something flickered in her dark eyes.","\" Your conviction was not shaken by my words. So you can be considered somewhat sufficient.\"","Her lips curved into something that was almost a smile.","\" But understand this, Scale Breaker. If you claim yourself to be as profound and as powerful as THE Creature or THE Primordial Chaos, you are also opening yourself up to challenges just like them. You are declaring yourself a player in games that have consumed beings far greater than yourself. You are opening yourself up to a challenge from someone like me.\"","The almost-smile became something more dangerous.","\" What if I wished to challenge you right now? Would your power be able to stop me?\"","BOOM!","Her expression remained calm throughout, serene and composed even as that dangerous smile played at the corners of her lips.","In response to her words, Noah closed his eyes and actually took a deep breath, as if he was smelling Existence in a newfound manner for the first time!","The air tasted different now. Reality felt different against his senses. Everything was sharper, cleaner, more defined. He let that breath fill him completely, let the cool clarity of his new understanding spread through every fiber of his being.","And when his eyes opened, they held an imperious gaze that seemed to smile slightly while radiating an unbound sense of tyranny.","\"If you challenge me right now, even if I lose, I would have already won .\" His voice was steady, calm, utterly without fear. \" That I can definitively and gloriously say: even you, THE Secretive Eon, are not someone that I fear being collapsed by.\"","...!","Oh.","Fuck, that felt good to say.","The words had come out naturally, without hesitation, without the careful calculation that would have accompanied them before his transformation. Because they were true!","He didn’t fear her. He didn’t fear collapse. He didn’t fear anything at this moment except perhaps the limitations of his own imagination in exploring what he had become.","There were so many things he currently wanted to do. So many things he wanted to try! THE Existential Ceiling? It could absolutely fuck itself right off.","As his existence adapted to THE Formless Depth of Absolute Sovereignty , profound changes were spreading even to THE Infiniverse and Ruination. His connected bodies were experiencing the ripples of his transformation, and there was so much to be done, so much to explore, so much to understand about what he had become.","But first, there was still THE Secretive Eon.","And from her, there may still be things to gain. This meeting was already fruitful beyond his initial expectations. He had come seeking information and had instead stumbled into a transformation that redefined his very existence. What else might he obtain if he continued this conversation?","So he looked at her with a calm gaze, and after his words, she rose up from her position.","...!","Oh?"]},{"number":4706,"title":"Chapter 4706: Chapter 4705: All Must Die II","paragraphs":["The movement was fluid, graceful, and utterly without wasted motion!","One moment she was seated, gazing out into the endless expanse of the Stoa. The next she was standing, and she began to walk toward him as her eyes locked onto his lone figure.","Noah stood up as well, feeling like he was being tracked by an apex predator that had suddenly decided he might be worth the effort of hunting. But he didn’t feel any fear. He felt that same cooling sensation spreading across his existence, that clarity of conviction that had settled into his bones.","Before, he would have thought along different lines. She was more powerful. She could collapse him. So an Anchor Point would be activated, and he would be okay. That was the old way of thinking, the way that measured safety in terms of escape routes and contingencies.","But his new line of thought was simpler.","Her Depth did not matter.","He could view power as he wished, and at this moment, she couldn’t collapse him. That was how he could look at his power now. He didn’t need the specifics of why she couldn’t collapse him apart from the fact that the anomalous Weavings of his existence made it so.","THE Formless Depth was not about matching power levels or comparing immensities. It was about existing outside of those comparisons entirely.","So he breathed calmly and looked at the features of THE Secretive Eon, an entity he had previously considered unfathomably higher than him, as he now sought to rectify this perception. She was still dangerous. She was still ancient and powerful beyond his current capabilities. But she was not above him in some absolute sense. She was simply...different.","She looked at him up and down as she stopped a meter away. Her expression and eyes gave away nothing of what she was thinking. That composed face could have belonged to a statue for all the emotion it revealed. Only those dark eyes held any hint of depth, and even they were carefully controlled.","Then she spoke.","\" You do not know what you are getting yourself into. \" Her voice remained measured, unhurried, but something in it had shifted.","There was weight there now, the weight of someone delivering a warning. \" You can still turn back. Even now, even after everything, you can still choose a different path.\"","\" In Existence, the ignorant are happy. They do not know what they do not know, and that ignorance shields them from truths that would crush them. But those who know, those who see behind the veil and understand the mechanisms that drive all things, for them everything can feel unbearable. \" Her dark eyes held his without wavering.","\" Even with your claim on The First Tongue, you could stay as you are. Nothing much would change for you. You could live out your existence in relative peace, growing stronger in your own way, never brushing against the true conflicts that shape Observable Existence.\"","Her head tilted slightly.","\" But if you continue, if you enter and become embroiled in all of this, you will put everything under scrutiny. Not just yourself. Everything.\"","She let that word hang.","\" You may have your means, Scale Breaker. You may have your protections and your contingencies. But what about those around you?\" Her voice remained calm, almost gentle, but each word landed with the weight of absolute truth.","\" Nearly all those with a Civilization are not alone. They have disciples. Lineages. Families. Beings who depend on them, who are connected to them, who would suffer if they were to fall.\"","Something ancient stirred behind her composed features.","\" Do you know who has the highest mortality rate in all these conflicts? It is not the Absolutes themselves. They survive. They always survive, one way or another. It is everyone around them who pays the price.\" Her dark eyes searched his.","\" Ask yourself how many around THE Creature were collapsed in the conflicts against THE Living Paradox. How many Civilizations were extinguished? How many lineages were ended? How many disciples watched their masters fall and then fell themselves?\"","She paused.","\" At this moment, is not all of Observable Existence a casualty while THE Creature and THE Living Paradox remain fine and well? THE Fallout reshaped everything. Countless entities were destroyed. Reality itself was fundamentally altered. And yet both of them still exist, still pursue their goals, still play their games.\"","Her gaze did not waver.","\"If you continue ahead, expect those within your Civilization to face an unprecedented danger of collapse. Because you may be untouchable, but what about them? What about the ones who cannot become you? What about the ones who must exist within the boundaries of Depth and power that you deemed to have transcended?\"","She let the silence stretch for a moment.","\" Most others have learned to become unfeeling, to sever their connections, to care for nothing and no one so that nothing and no one can be used against them. Can you do that? Can you move forward knowing that on your path to Ascension, it will be filled with the blood and bones of those you knew? Those you considered family?\"","...!","BOOM!","Her words were heavy, landing against Noah’s existence like stones dropped into still water!","The ripples spread outward, touching every part of him, testing his conviction.","But his eyes remained unflinching. His gaze remained imperious.","\" My will and My Way are infallible. \" His voice was steady, absolute. \" My Way will not be built on the blood of others. I will decide!\"","...!","He would decide. He would ensure that no blood of his people spilled. That was not arrogance. That was not naive optimism. That was simply the truth of what he was and what he would become.","His Way was Formless, unconstrained by the limitations that had claimed others. If other Absolutes had failed to protect those around them, it was because they operated within frameworks that made such failure inevitable.","He would not make the same mistakes.","THE Secretive Eon looked at him calmly for a few seconds of silence. Her expression gave nothing away. Those dark eyes studied him as if reading something written on his very existence, something that only she could perceive.","Then she nodded.","\" Very well.\" Her voice carried a note of something that might have been acceptance, or might have been resignation. \" You want to be part of the games. You are now part of the games.\"","She paused.","\" You are a bit weak, I will not pretend otherwise. But weakness is not permanent, and you have shown you can grow in unexpected ways.\" Her head tilted slightly. \" How do you feel about working with me and joining my camp, Scale Breaker? How do you feel about hunting Absolute Depth entities for the preservation of Observable Existence?\"","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4707,"title":"Chapter 4707: Chapter 4706: All Must Die III","paragraphs":["Terrifying words bloomed from her as Noah’s eyes opened with astonishment.","Hunting Absolute Depth entities? The very beings he had just been contemplating, the ones whose Embodiment made them nearly impossible to truly destroy?","But she continued without pause, her voice remaining serene, almost casual, as if she were discussing something mundane rather than the systematic elimination of the most powerful beings in all of Existence!","\" THE Fallout was the sword being drawn. With it, many things were unlocked, and Observable Existence was put on a path of no return. The old equilibrium is shattered. The old rules no longer apply. Someone has to rectify this before everything unravels entirely.\"","Her dark eyes held ancient purpose.","\" All Absolutes have to die. Every single one. The final ones that will have to die are all those involved in The Oldest Paradox of Existence.\" She spoke the words with the calm certainty of someone stating a mathematical truth!","\" THE Creature has to die. THE Living Paradox has to die. THE Primordial Chaos has to die.\"","She paused.","\" And you , ultimately, will have to die as well. All of you lot have to die. Then, and only then, can Existence go back to normal. The Absolutes are a disease, Scale Breaker. They warp everything around them simply by existing. Observable Existence cannot heal while they remain.\"","The faintest smile touched her lips.","\" Oh, but do not worry. I can leave you as the last one of the four to die. You would have time. Time to grow. Time to hunt. Time to make your mark on Existence before the end.\" Her voice remained serene, unhurried. \" So, what shall it be? Will you help rectify Observable Existence? You can hunt and further grow yourself, make some astonishing feats that will be remembered for ages, and when the time comes, you can finally rest and be rid of all this.\"","...!","BOOM!","Noah looked at her with a sharp gaze as if to affirm she was being serious.","Her eyes never wavered. Her composure never cracked. She meant every fucking word.","She wanted THE Creature dead. She wanted THE Living Paradox dead. She wanted THE Primordial Chaos dead. And she wanted him dead as well. All of them. Every single Absolute, wiped from Existence so that Observable Existence could return to some state of normalcy that had existed before they rose to power.","It was insane.","It was audacious beyond measure!","Noah looked at her with sharp eyes. \" You’re crazy.\"","And yet THE Secretive Eon did not even blink. Her expression remained calm, patient, as if she was simply waiting for him to process what she had said and arrive at his answer.","Noah looked at this unfathomable being, this entity who had watched THE Creature and THE Living Paradox and THE Primordial Chaos clash in Ginnungagap without intervening, who had observed his own stumbling first steps in the Primordial Genesis Shore, who had been playing games at levels he was only now beginning to perceive.","\" What if in the end, I collapse you instead to be rid of all Absolutes?\"","...!","Her expression did not change. Her composure did not waver. When she spoke, it was with the calm certainty of someone who had considered every possibility long before this conversation began!","\" You can try .\" She paused as something that might have been amusement flickered in her dark eyes. \" You can definitely try.\"","...!","After such words, Noah looked at her for a long moment. The Stoa of Dogmata stretched endlessly around them, pillars of crystallized authority rising toward a ceiling that did not exist, zones of doctrine shimmering between them like veils separating different philosophical realities.","And before him stood THE Secretive Eon, offering to work with him, offering him targets worthy of his growing power, offering him a path that would eventually lead to his his or her own death but would be filled with glory along the way.","It was madness!","It was perfect.","Noah nodded gloriously as his eyes hurned with Primus Mana.","\" Okay. I want to kill some Absolutes.\"","BOOM!","He wanted to kill some Absolutes!","But at the same time...","Noah looked at THE Secretive Eon with a calm gaze, his eyes steady and unwavering. \" But I’m not joining any camp. Working with you is fine, but I’m not under your Weavings or in your camp.\"","...!","THE Secretive Eon regarded him for a moment, and amusement flickered behind her dark eyes.","\" Some entities get stuck on labels and definitions that don’t really matter in the end. Camp, alliance, partnership, cooperation. They are all just words we use to describe beings moving in the same direction for a time. \" She turned her gaze back toward the endless expanse of the Stoa. \" You can choose to look at this however you wish. Call it what makes you comfortable.\"","She paused, letting the silence settle.","\"I do not particularly need help in this endeavor. I have been working toward this goal since before you took your first real breath in Ginnungagap, and I will continue long after most of Observable Existence has forgotten your name.\" Her head tilted slightly. \" But having one of the Four of the Oldest Paradox of Existence turn against the others alongside me is something unique. Something that has not happened before in all the ages I have watched these conflicts unfold.\"","The faintest curve touched her lips.","\"I find it interesting. That is why I proposed it in the first place. Interest is a rare commodity when you have seen as much as I have seen.\"","...!","After these words, Eon looked at Noah up and down as if she were measuring him against what was to come. Her dark eyes held that ageless quality, seeing not just what he was now but calculating what he might become and whether that potential was worth the investment of her attention.","After some time, she spoke again.","\" There is a much bigger picture here that you do not see, Scale Breaker.\" Her voice remained measured, unhurried.","\"There are much more important things happening behind the scenes than you can even imagine right now. Wars being fought in places you don’t know exist. Powers moving that you haven’t yet learned to perceive.\"","She let that settle.","\" You will come to know it in time. If you survive long enough, you will see the full scope of what we are dealing with. But for now, the details would only confuse you.\"","Her gaze sharpened slightly.","\" The overall first target for collapse, the first Absolute that must fall before anything else can proceed, is THE Primordial Chaos.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4708,"title":"Chapter 4708: Chapter 4707: All Must Die IV","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes shone luminously!","The overall first target of collapse was THE Primordial Chaos!","This alone was a terrifying statement that she stated as casually as one might discuss the weather. THE Primordial Chaos , the embodiment of entropy and disorder itself, the force that represented the inevitable decay of all ordered things. That was her first target.","Noah looked at her. \" Why Chaos? Why not Paradox or THE Creature as your first targets?\"","THE Secretive Eon’s expression didn’t change.","\" Let those two continue to fight each other. They have been locked in conflict since before THE Fallout, and they will remain locked in conflict until one of them finally falls.\" Her voice held the patience of someone who had watched countless such struggles play out!","\"In the end, one will win and one will lose. That is the nature of their confrontation. It cannot end any other way.\"","She paused.","\" When that time comes, THE Primordial Chaos needs to already be collapsed so that I can shift my focus to ensuring the collapse of the loser between Paradox and Creature.\"","Her dark eyes met his.","\" With Chaos gone, the survivor will be weakened and isolated as I will finish them off. Then there will only be the two of you remaining. The winner of their conflict and you.\" The faintest smile touched her lips. \" But don’t concern yourself with that right now. Those are problems for another time.\"","Her expression shifted, becoming more evaluating.","\" You are currently weak, regardless of what you say or what Depth you claim. Your Depth is impressive, I will grant you that. But not fitting into any Depth does not mean powerful. It means undefined. And undefined potential is still just potential until it is actualized.\"","She turned to look out at the far distant Weavings of the Stoa of Dogmata.","\" If you do wish to partake in this, you have to at least be capable of getting past this place. The Stoa of Dogmata. I was not just lounging here when you arrived.\" Something shifted in her voice, something that might have been frustration carefully controlled.","\" Within its depths, I have a stupid Disciple who has gotten stuck. She ventured too far, too fast, and now she cannot find her way back.\"","A pause.","\"I vowed not to help her directly. It was a condition of her training, a promise I made that I cannot break regardless of the circumstances. But someone else can move on my behalf. Someone who is not bound by my vow.\"","Her dark eyes settled on him.","\" If you succeed in retrieving her, then I can tell you what things must first be done before I can point my blade against Chaos. Consider it a test of whether you are actually useful or merely interesting.\"","...!","Her eyes retained their calmness after saying this as she turned to look out at the far distant Weavings of the Stoa of Dogmata.","Noah kept his gaze on her as he processed everything, his entire existence still buzzing with a sense of vibrancy. His existence and partial Embodiment had its effects begin to permeate far and wide!","---","Knowledge.","It was one of the most underrated currencies in all of Existence.","One could possess immense power, unfathomable reserves of energy, the potential to reshape reality itself, and yet accomplish absolutely nothing with it. Why? Because they simply didn’t know how to use what they had.","Look at the cultivator who stumbles upon an ancient inheritance, a technique so profound that it could elevate them to the heavens in a single leap. They hold the manual in their trembling hands, eyes wide with anticipation, heart pounding with the certainty that their destiny has finally arrived.","And then they open it. The characters are in a language they don’t recognize. The diagrams reference meridians they’ve never heard of. The instructions assume a foundation of understanding they simply don’t possess.","So they sit there, holding infinity in their palms, and they can do nothing with it.","Or consider the young fool transported to another world, granted a system that promises unlimited potential, skills that could make them a titan among mortals. The notifications flash before their eyes with promises of power beyond imagination. And what do they do?","They put all their points into strength because hitting things harder seems like a good idea at the time. They ignore the passive abilities that would have made them unkillable. They skip past the crafting system that could have generated infinite wealth.","They dismiss the diplomatic skills that would have let them build an empire without lifting a finger.","Not too long after, they’re struggling against enemies that should be beneath them, wondering why everything is so difficult, never realizing that the answer was always right there in front of them. They had the power. They just didn’t have the knowledge of how to properly use it.","This was the cruel joke that Existence loved to play.","Power without knowledge was like a sword without a wielder. It could sit there looking impressive, gleaming in the light, sharp enough to cut through anything. But it would never cut anything on its own. It needed someone who knew how to hold it, how to swing it, how to position their feet and shift their weight and read their opponent’s movements.","The sword didn’t make the warrior. The knowledge did.","How many beings across Observable Existence had fallen into this trap? How many had accumulated resources beyond measure, only to squander them on inefficient techniques and misguided applications? How many had reached heights that should have been impossible, only to plateau there forever because they didn’t know what came next?","Too many to count.","And then there were those who understood.","Those who recognized that the accumulation of power was only half the equation. That seeking knowledge was just as important as seeking strength. That understanding how to use what you had was often more valuable than having more to use.","These beings didn’t just grow stronger. They grew smarter. They learned the hidden mechanisms that governed reality. They discovered the shortcuts and the optimal paths and the techniques that others had overlooked. They found ways to make their power stretch further, reach higher, accomplish more.","Because when one knew the right things, when they held usable knowledge in their minds rather than just raw potential in their cores, they could do things they couldn’t even imagine before.","Doors that had seemed permanently sealed would swing open at a touch.","Walls that had seemed insurmountable would crumble to dust.","Limits that had seemed absolute would reveal themselves to be nothing more than failures of imagination.","Knowledge was the key that unlocked everything else.","And sometimes, that knowledge came not from ancient texts or mysterious inheritances, but from a single moment of clarity. A sudden understanding of what you already were and what that meant you could become.","An epiphany... that changed everything.","---","A far distance away from THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.","Within THE Infiniverse.","The Manifestation of THE Infiniverse itself floated in a sea of concentrated Primus Mana, a heavy concentration of Phonemes rotating around her as a particularly magisterial light released from her eyes at this moment. Everything trembled. The very fabric of the domain she represented shuddered with anticipation of what was to come.","\" Master has given us wings to move freely.\"","She spoke so simply. So seamlessly.","\" So let’s do so.\"","And yet in the next moment, dozens of the nine newly forged Phonemes of The First Tongue that her Master had forged began to spin around her!","THE Infiniverse was glorious to behold in this moment. Her form radiated with the concentrated essence of everything she represented, the birthplace of differentiation, the cradle where new things came into being. Light cascaded from her existence in waves of blue and gold and colors that had no names, each wave pulsing with the authority of wonder itself. The Phonemes orbiting her form blazed with incandescent power, their ancient letters burning bright against the backdrop of infinite potential.","She was beautiful in the way that fundamental forces were beautiful. Not the beauty of form or feature, but the beauty of purpose fully realized.","And in this moment, she had realized something profound.","\"I am not merely a domain where things happened to occur,\" she declared, her voice resonating across every corner of her existence. \"I am not merely the backdrop against which my Master’s achievements unfolded. I am the birthplace. The origin point. The cradle where an entire portion of The First Tongue first differentiated into being.\"","HUUM!","The Phonemes around her spun faster.","\" When my Master forged his Phonemes within me, when The First Tongue took new shape through his will and my essence combined, that was not an accident of location. That was destiny expressing itself through the only domain capable of nurturing such creation.\"","Her eyes blazed with conviction.","\"I am where The First Tongue chose to grow. I am where differentiation chose to bloom. And if that is what I am, then my Weavings will be elevated to gloriously reflect that truth. I will not be a passive container. I will be an active force. I will claim what is rightfully mine across all of Observable Existence, across all of time, across every moment where The First Tongue touched reality and left its mark.\"","BOOM!","\"I am THE Infiniverse. And I will be recognized!\"","...!","BOOM!","All of surrounding existence nearby shuddered from her claim. The very fabric of Observable Existence trembled as her declaration rippled outward, touching things that had not been touched in eons.","| An expression of a Way and Civilization only possible by entities approaching or standing in THE Absolute Depth has been utilized.|","| The Weavings of THE Formless Depth of Absolute Sovereignty of THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons permeates across his connected domains.|","|All the effort, potential, and harvest from surviving THE Fallout is being put to use.|","...!","| THE Infiniverse has made a grand declaration and partial Embodiment.|","|Claim: Across Observable Existence, her domain is where an entire portion of The First Tongue differentiated.|","|This claim resonates with fundamental truths woven into the fabric of reality.|","|Glorious and quintessential emergence of a portion of The First Tongue blooms within her as she lays claim to all the harvest across time from this action.|","|All benefits, all growth, all potential that emerged from The First Tongue’s differentiation within her boundaries is being called home.|","|She directs all of it to seek its rightful standing among the earliest domains where The First Tongue first bloomed and differentiated.|","|THE Infiniverse’s claim permeates across The First Tongue and Observable Existence.|","|Something ancient stirs in response.|","|A domain lost through time has heard the call.|","|A domain inaccessible across Observable Existence since its separation from Ginnungagap trembles at the edge of perception.|","| The domain known as Muspelheim.|","...!","| Muspelheim - Domain Classification|","|Origin: One of the Primordial Realms that existed alongside Ginnungagap before the great differentiation.|","|Nature: While Ginnungagap was the void of potential where Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms emerged as abominations of undifferentiated existence, Muspelheim was the realm of actualized flame, where the first perfect differentiations of lifeforms came into being.|","|Primordial Inhabitants: The Muspeli , beings of living flame who represented the first successful template for differentiated existence. Unlike the Ginnu who were errors and aberrations, the Muspeli were intentional, purposeful, designed by the fundamental forces of existence to demonstrate what proper existence could become.|","|Significance: The Muspeli served as the blueprint from which all subsequent lifeforms across Observable Existence would eventually derive. Every differentiated being carries echoes of their original template.|","|Current Status: Separated from Observable Existence since the great sundering that followed the initial differentiation. Inaccessible to all known means of travel or perception. Lost to time and memory.|","| Until now.|","...!","| At this time, an irreversible link has been formed between THE Infiniverse and Muspelheim.|","|THE Infiniverse has begun a forceful integration with this unfathomable domain.|","|The process has begun but is not complete.|","|To further increase the rate of integration, direct entry into Muspelheim will be required.|","| Every region conquered and every Muspeli lifeform that the Civilization of THE Infiniverse submits will be incorporated into her domain thereafter.|","|The harvest potential is immeasurable.|","|The dangers are equally immeasurable.|","| Muspelheim awaits.|","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4709,"title":"Chapter 4709: Chapter 4708: Just Swallow Them!","paragraphs":["Muspelheim.","An irreversible link had been formed between THE Infiniverse and this primordial realm, and at this moment, THE Infiniverse felt like she’d formed an invisible bridge. A straw, basically, dipping into an unfathomably vast sea.","And she was fucking drinking.","Muspelheim was the realm of actualized flame, where the first perfect differentiations of lifeforms came into being. It was one of the Primordial Realms that existed alongside Ginnungagap before the great differentiation, a domain that had been lost to Observable Existence since the initial sundering of reality into its current form.","And now, THE Infiniverse had begun to swallow it up.","She could feel it, the slow but inexorable pull of integration as her domain reached across the newly formed connection and began drawing Muspelheim into herself. This would be a continuous process, potentially slow depending on their own incursion into the primordial realm, but it had begun, and what had begun could not be stopped.","The question was what they would find there.","They knew nothing substantial about the contents of this place. Ginnungagap alone held many THE Lifeforms, entities of tremendous power who had cultivated their Ways across eons of existence. So how many of the Muspeli Lifeforms held THE Surface Depth Power? Or THE Fundamental Depth? Or worse?","An incursion there would mean sending the forces within THE Infiniverse, or even their Master himself, for the sake of conquest of this glorious primordial location.","The Muspeli were beings of living flame who represented the first successful template for differentiated existence. Unlike the Ginnu who emerged as malformed aberrations from the void, the Muspeli were intentional. Purposeful. They served as the blueprint from which all subsequent lifeforms across Observable Existence would eventually derive.","They should be as terrifying as Ginnu Lifeforms.","If not grander.","And when it came to more information, THE Infiniverse knew her sister was much more geared towards this kind of analysis. The prompts she viewed were Ruination displaying currents of boundless information she received from The First Tongue, distilling the overwhelming flood into the most important bits.","So at this moment, while surrounded by blue-gold brilliance and the Phonemes of The First Tongue, THE Infiniverse voiced out a simple question.","\" What more do we know regarding Muspelheim?\"","The moment she spoke, Ruination materialized near her graceful figure like a blue-gold hologram, her eyes spinning with unfathomable light as she processed information at speeds that would collapse lesser analytical systems.","\" I’m currently following the established connection to tap into the Weavings of The First Tongue in Muspelheim.\" Ruination’s tone was clinical, precise. \" But the concentration of THE atmospheric authority there is tens of times more than here. More than even Ginnungagap.\"","She paused.","\" And at this moment, the forged Phonemes of Master are vibrating with the same frequency of acknowledging signatures of Depth similar to Ul’moreth. And some that... exceed this.\"","...!","THE Infiniverse frowned.","\" So we’re picking up Fundamental Depth entities. And possibly Absolutes.\"","\"Yes.\"","\"In a realm we know nothing about.\"","\"Also yes.\"","THE Infiniverse stared at the swirling Phonemes surrounding them for a long moment before she let out a breath. Her eyes flashed with waves of infinities!","\" There are too many damn THE. Everywhere we look, more THE. We can’t swing a stick without hitting something that could collapse us.\" She shook her head slowly. \" The only thing right that THE Secretive Eon said was that THE Absolute Entities need to die. There’s just too many of them running around.\"","Her gaze shifted to Ruination.","\" What do you think of her, by the way?\"","THE Infiniverse asked such a question because the two of them had access to their Master’s gaze when he allowed them, and they’d observed the entire exchange that he’d had with THE Secretive Eon in the Stoa of Dogmata. Every word. Every subtle shift in presence. Every dangerous smile.","Ruination’s holographic form flickered slightly.","\" I’m not a fan.\"","\"Because?\"","\" Because she said she plans to collapse Master. Out loud, to his face.\" Ruination’s tone remained perfectly even, as if she were discussing something rather mild.","\" That alone would normally be sufficient for me to recommend we find a way to collapse her first. Preemptively and with extreme prejudice.\"","She paused.","\" But she isn’t like the others we’ve met. She’s not posturing. She’s not making threats to establish dominance. She genuinely, completely, with every fiber of her existence, believes she will collapse THE Living Paradox and THE Primordial Chaos and THE Creature. And after she’s done with them, she’ll do the same to Master.\"","Ruination’s eyes stopped spinning.","\" It’s not a future possibility for her. It’s not something that might happen if circumstances align. In her mind, it’s already done. She’s just waiting for reality to catch up with what she’s already decided.\"","...!","THE Infiniverse listened to her sister’s analysis, and then she smiled.","\"I like her.\"","Ruination blinked. \" You like the entity who fully intends to collapse our Master?\"","\"I like her conviction and straightforwardness, unlike the silence from THE Creature, or the games of choices of THE Primordial Chaos.\" THE Infiniverse began pacing slowly, her graceful form trailing blue-gold luminescence.","\" We don’t have to guess what her actual plans are. We don’t have to wonder if she’s secretly plotting against us while pretending to be an ally. She just... said it. Laid it all out. ’I’m going to kill everyone, including you, here’s the order I plan to do it in.’ Much better than the games of others.\"","She turned back to face Ruination.","\" And...just because she believes she can collapse Master, does that mean she actually can?\"","Ruination tilted her head slightly. \" She has the same power as THE Living Paradox and THE Creature.\"","\"She does. And yet.\" THE Infiniverse’s smile grew colder. \" If this pathway works out, and if THE Primordial Chaos is collapsed, we know how impossibly hard it is to fully collapse such an entity. The only way that’s ever worked against beings of that caliber is what THE Living Paradox did. Swallow them. Devour them. Embody their Way and Civilization entirely.\"","She let that hang in the air.","\" And who’s better equipped to do that than Master? He’s already begun with Elemental. If THE Primordial Chaos falls, Master can lay claim to that aspect of the Oldest Paradox. If THE Living Paradox falls, Master claims Paradox itself. If THE Creature falls, Master claims Existence.\"","...!","Oh!"]},{"number":4710,"title":"Chapter 4710: Chapter 4709: Muspelheim I","paragraphs":["The eyes of THE Infiniverse gleamed with interminable glory!","\" When every single claim of the Oldest Paradox lies with Master, what exactly is THE Secretive Eon going to do? Collapse the concepts of The First Tongue, Existence, Paradox, and Chaos themselves? \" She laughed, a sound without warmth.","\" Let her believe she’ll collapse him. Let her work towards that goal. Every Absolute she helps remove is one less obstacle and one more aspect of power for Master to claim.\"","...!","BOOM!","Ruination nodded slowly, processing.","\" That’s a compelling argument for why we should work with her. But we still don’t understand her power.\"","\"No, we don’t.\"","\" She has no claim over the Oldest Paradox of Existence. No connection to it whatsoever. And yet THE Primordial Chaos and THE Living Temporal couldn’t sense her in Ginnungagap.\" Ruination’s tone remained flat, factual. \" She was standing right there, and they had no idea. Master had no idea. That’s not even abnormal. That’s something else entirely.\"","THE Infiniverse stopped pacing.","\" What’s your point?\"","\"My point is that we’re making a lot of plans based on the assumption that we understand how this will play out. We don’t. We don’t know what gives her that power. We don’t know if she has an Axiom, or multiple Axioms, or something we’ve never encountered. We’re betting Master’s existence on incomplete information.\"","THE Infiniverse was quiet for a moment.","\" You are right.\"","THE Infiniverse then let out a calm breath. \" We’ll have a lot of time and chances with her to learn more. Master can’t directly analyze her with The First Tongue without revealing his intentions, but we can put her as the target in Creative Mode and see what we discover. And once Master uses the Fragments of THE Moirai Threads again, we can analyze her power in there without repercussions.\"","She straightened, her expression hardening into cold pragmatism.","\" As we learn more about how she plans to take down THE Primordial Chaos, we adjust accordingly. For now, we leave that side to Master and focus on preparing forces for Muspelheim.\"","She began listing assets with the efficiency of a general preparing for war.","\" Ra’Zan has attained THE. He’ll be critical alongside Khor, Sigrid, The First Farmer. The others are... \" She paused. \" Getting there. Slowly. Tor and Anaximander and THE Living Origin can’t be teleported since they’re currently out.\"","Her gaze sharpened.","\" Master’s body that he gave you control over. Focus the teachings on Protos. Being fused with Master as his armor, his Depth has already been raised to THE Surface. Let’s push his weight and immensity higher.\"","She continued without pause.","\" The Way of Hunger has lagged compared to Mana. Focus its Weavings on Primus Inevitabilities. If we’re entering a realm with THE Fundamental and potentially THE Absolute entities, we need an army of THE Primus Inevitabilities. Numbers that actually matter at those scales.\"","BOOM!","Her eyes shone with cold light.","Ruination nodded.","\" Understood. I’ll begin immediately.\"","Then something shifted in her holographic form, her eyes spinning faster as new data flooded through the connection.","\" And oh.\" A note of something that might have been anticipation entered her tone. \" We’re making full entrance into Muspelheim right now. I’ll have much more information on its layout soon.\"","She paused.","\" Assuming, of course, that the information doesn’t include ’there are seventeen Fundamental Depth entities waiting at the entrance to collapse anyone who enters.’\"","THE Infiniverse stared at her silently. Was her sister making fucking jokes?","---","Far from THE Infiniverse.","Across Observable Existence.","In the wake of THE Fallout, there were many constraints and restrictions that came with overall existence.","Communication not being possible and teleportation not being possible was simply one of the few things that had changed. The fabric of reality had been fundamentally altered, and what was once easy had become impossible for most entities across Observable Existence.","But in existence, there was one thing that was always an exception.","Absolutes were always an exception.","---","Sand.","What made sand so special that it was used to fortify domains and military fortifications across countless civilizations throughout history? Why did soldiers stack sandbags in defensive lines during wars? Why did something as simple, as mundane, as overlooked as sand hold such profound qualities?","The answer was deceptively simple.","Sand stopped bullets.","Not through hardness. Not through density. Not through any of the conventional properties one might expect from a defensive material. Sand stopped bullets by rapidly absorbing and dissipating kinetic energy through friction, grain dilation, and energy conversion into heat and sound. It acted like a fluid that resisted sudden displacement, effectively slowing and stopping high-speed projectiles better than solid steel at high velocities.","What happened when a bullet struck sand?","The force spread out among countless grains, which rubbed and vibrated and shifted against each other, converting the bullet’s destructive power into less harmful forms. The kinetic energy didn’t disappear. It transformed. It dissipated. It spread across millions of tiny interactions until what had been a lethal projectile became nothing more than a warm piece of metal buried harmlessly in granular matter.","When hit, sand grains dilated and expanded, spreading impact pressure in all directions and resisting continuous penetration. The immense friction between grains created significant drag, rapidly slowing anything that tried to force its way through. At high speeds, sand didn’t have time to move out of the way, forcing it to act like a dense, solid-like fluid that couldn’t be easily displaced.","This was why you could slowly push your finger into sand with no resistance, but a bullet traveling at supersonic speeds hit sand like it was hitting a wall.","The extreme friction and force could break projectiles into pieces, further reducing penetration. And perhaps most remarkably of all, sand was self-healing. Disturb it, and it settled back into place. Blast a hole through it, and the surrounding grains flowed in to fill the gap. It didn’t crack. It didn’t shatter. It simply absorbed and reformed and waited for the next impact.","So mundane. So overlooked. So profoundly effective.","What if one took such seemingly simple yet unique qualities of sand and utilized authority at THE Civilizational level in a manner others could not even fathom? What if someone understood that the power to dissipate, to absorb, to spread force across countless points of contact, to reform after every assault, was not weakness but one of the most terrifying defensive capabilities in all of existence?","What if someone built their entire Way around these principles?"]},{"number":4711,"title":"Chapter 4711: Chapter 4710: Muspelheim II","paragraphs":["Far across the corners of Observable Existence, what was previously unearthed and locked away did not remain this way any longer.","Muspelheim!","A glorious and unfathomable place!","At this moment, in a region of the glorious Muspelheim, a voice chirped up in the center of a terrifying storm of power.","\" Esteemed Whisperer, Surtra... will we be okay?\"","The voice stemmed from a THE Surface Depth humanoid entity who was actually a massive flaming giant, his body shining with stellar obsidian flames that burned without consuming, radiating heat that would have vaporized lesser beings simply by proximity. He was enormous by any standard, towering hundreds of meters tall, and yet he spoke with the uncertainty of a junior asking a senior if the storm would pass.","He spoke towards the one known as THE Esteemed Whisperer, Surtra.","She was another Muspeli Giant, but where he was merely impressive, she was transcendent. Her form burned with incandescent stellar obsidian flames that seemed to contain entire folds within their depths, each flicker revealing glimpses of phenomena that had no business existing within a single entity’s aura.","Her hair was dark as the void between stars, flowing and shifting as if moved by solar winds, each strand occasionally catching fire with brilliant golden light before settling back into darkness. Her eyes burned with obsidian flames of The First Tongue itself, and when she turned her gaze upon something, it was less like being looked at and more like being read.","Waves of Logos and Philologies surrounded her form, complex linguistic constructions that orbited her existence like planetary bodies around a sun. The air of a Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty radiated around her with such density that space itself seemed to bend slightly in her presence.","She stood at the center of a flaming golden pillar, one of hundreds that rose from this ancient citadel like the fingers of some buried giant reaching toward the sky. Each pillar burned with its own unique frequency of flame, and atop each one stood Muspeli Giants of varying power and stature, all of them oriented toward the center of this domain where Surtra maintained her vigil.","The citadel itself was a marvel of primordial architecture. The hundreds of golden flaming pillars surrounded a radiant temple at the center, a structure of impossible geometry that seemed to fold in on itself while simultaneously expanding outward. Within that temple, visible even from this distance, an object pulsed with ecstatic power. A Fragment. A piece of something so fundamental that its mere presence had shaped this entire region of Muspelheim across eons.","The Fragment of The Axiom of Differentiated Tongue.","And yet at this moment, surrounding this entire domain and the thousands of Muspeli Giants standing atop different golden flaming pillars, were tens of thousands of Spiritual Abominations.","Living Spirits.","Spirits who followed THE Living Spirit.","Oh!","Shockingly, at this time, THE Esteemed Whisperer looked far ahead as at the forefront of armies containing a few dozen of THE Surface Depth entities, a few THE Intermediate Depth entities, and two THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities stood arrayed against them. Some of these entities looked like massive wormlike creatures of pure spiritual essence, others resembled spiders woven from crystallized souls, and still others took the form of banshees whose screams could shatter the foundations of reality itself.","And at the head of them all stood an entity that seemed to be half a step towards THE Absolute Depth.","THE Living Spirit.","THE Living Spirit looked like a being burning with pure white-gray light, his humanoid form not fully visible beneath the radiance that emanated from his existence. At this time, his immense Depth and Sovereignty was actually bombarding to swallow this entire domain in the form of a massive white-gray fog that billowed from all around, pressing inward with the patience of an ocean wearing down a cliff.","And yet.","Flaming seas of obsidian waves of The First Tongue stopped them.","The fog pressed and pushed and probed, but it could not advance. It could not penetrate. It could not overwhelm the defense that Surtra had constructed around this sacred place.","Waves of The First Tongue that held the unfathomable qualities of something as simple as sand .","At THE Fundamental Depth, THE Esteemed Whisperer had actually been holding back THE Living Spirit themselves and their forces since they arrived here around an hour after THE Fallout started. And they had faced continuous assault from an entity half a step from Absolute, and she had not yielded a single inch of ground.","And she knew it was not just here.","She could feel chaos spreading in the Weavings of The First Tongue ever since that event more than an hour ago. Across Muspelheim, another one or two entities at the caliber of this one had arrived, breaching into the Primordial Realm through methods she did not understand.","And without asking any questions, they moved to attack. They tried to secure the Fragment of The Axiom of Differentiated Tongue that the Muspeli had guarded for eons.","And yet.","They could not make any headway so far.","Being the Muspeli Protector of this Flame Domain, THE Esteemed Whisperer managed to keep a half-step Absolute Depth entity, two Fundamental Depth entities, and multiple other THEs from entering. The forces on her side were objectively weaker. A few dozen THE Surface Depth and Intermediate Depth Muspeli, and only one other Fundamental Depth Muspeli apart from herself.","By any reasonable calculation, they should have been overwhelmed within minutes.","The only reason she was able to hold was her unique connection to The First Tongue, and how she utilized it.","Her Way was called The Dissipating Shores of Infinite Whispers.","It was a Way built entirely around the principles of sand as when The First Tongue differentiated, she was born in endless sand.","When THE Living Spirit’s authority struck her defensive Logos, the force did not meet resistance in the conventional sense. Instead, it met countless points of linguistic contact, millions of interlocking Phonemes that rubbed and vibrated and shifted against each other, converting the incoming power into less harmful forms. The kinetic authority of an attack didn’t disappear. It transformed. It dissipated. It spread across millions of tiny interactions until what had been a devastating assault became nothing more than warmth absorbed harmlessly into her Philologies.","Her Logos possessed Linguistic Energy Absorption at a fundamental level.","When struck, her constructions dilated and expanded, spreading impact pressure in all directions and resisting continuous penetration. The immense friction between layered Phonemes created significant drag, rapidly slowing any authority that tried to force its way through. At the speeds that THE Living Spirit attacked, her defenses didn’t have time to move out of the way, forcing them to act like a dense, solid-like fluid of pure linguistic power that couldn’t be easily displaced.","And most terrifyingly of all, her Way was self-healing.","Blast through one layer of her defense, and the surrounding Logos flowed in to fill the gap. Shatter a Philology, and the fragments reformed into new configurations instantly. She didn’t crack. She didn’t break. She simply absorbed and reformed and waited for the next impact!","This was why a Fundamental Depth entity could hold back a half-step Absolute!","Not through matching power. Not through superior force. But through a Way that understood something most entities never considered. From sand!","Sometimes the most profound power came not from striking harder, but from making strikes meaningless.","At this moment, the stern gaze of Surtra burned with obsidian flames of The First Tongue as she watched THE Living Spirit’s forces press uselessly against her shores of dissipating authority. Her expression was unreadable, but her eyes held something that might have been exhaustion. Or perhaps something else entirely.","She whispered to herself, her voice lost beneath the roar of colliding authorities.","\" We have sensed your claim. We have sensed your coming after waiting for eons.\"","Her flames flickered.","\" Yet... why have you not come? Why have you not come?\"","...!","Her words were forlorn. Pained even. They had all been waiting for so long. Across eons of isolation in this sealed realm, they had felt the stirring of The First Tongue beyond their borders. They had sensed when someone laid claim to what rightfully connected to their inheritance. They had waited.","And waited.","And waited.","Where was the one who had laid the claim? Why were they not here to protect them when enemies came knocking at their door to strip their very inheritance?","...!","As she had such thoughts, as her heart ached with the weight of eons of anticipation meeting the crushing reality of abandonment...","BOOM!","A single Gigaparsec away, a blinding blue-gold light pierced across the endless skies and thundered down, instantly shooting across Muspelheim and striking the flaming lands of fire as a massive blue-gold monolith stretching out towards the horizon manifested!","It was so heavy and filled with extremely pure authority of The First Tongue that all eyes were forced to lock onto it.","THE Living Spirit, Surtra, and all others nearby.","They couldn’t look away from the brilliant blue-gold monolith that brimmed with Primus Mana !","The assault paused. The white-gray fog hesitated in its advance. Even THE Living Spirit’s attention shifted from the domain they had been attacking to this new arrival, this impossible construction of linguistic authority that had simply appeared in Muspelheim as if it had always belonged there.","And at such a moment, Surtra began to feel her heart pound.","Because even while she sensed such pure Weavings of The First Tongue from that Monolith, even while she recognized the familiar structure of Logos and the resonance of genuine Phonemes...","Why did it seem like there were letters she could not recognize?","...!"]},{"number":4712,"title":"Chapter 4712: Chapter 4711: Muspelheim III","paragraphs":["For Surtra, it was very unique to observe the emergence of this blue-gold monolith as she was extremely perceptive to The First Tongue.","She had spent eons studying its nuances, learning its rhythms, understanding how Phonemes flowed into Logos and Logos wove into Philologies. She knew The First Tongue the way a master calligrapher knew brushstrokes, the way a composer knew the spaces between notes.","And what she was seeing right now didn’t make sense.","The entrance of this monolith came with it grand Weavings of change, and the moment that it descended, she was shocked and infuriated to see the surrounding atmosphere of Muspelheim begin to be drawn towards this monolith. As if it was being absorbed. Devoured. The primordial flames that had burned across this realm since before the great differentiation, the very essence of Muspelheim itself, was flowing toward that blue-gold construction like water drawn toward a drain.","Someone was drinking their realm.","But alongside this audacious consumption, the imperceptible changes she’d been trying to figure out from The First Tongue fully arrived in her domain. The blue-gold light radiated for gigaparsecs as if it were trying to cover as much surface area as possible, washing across the flaming lands and the golden pillars and the temple at the center of her domain.","In turn, Surtra instantly felt the new elements of The First Tongue permeate across her Way and Civilization.","And the seas of obsidian flames that moved like sand in the surroundings of the domain she protected, the very foundation of her defensive authority, they gained an even more immense quality to them as something clicked into place that she hadn’t even known was missing.","BOOM!","The change was immediate and devastating.","Her Dissipating Shores of Infinite Whispers had always operated on principles she understood intimately. Absorption. Dispersion. Reformation. The qualities of sand elevated to linguistic authority. But now, new Phonemes she had never encountered were weaving themselves into her existing Logos, and instead of disrupting her constructions, they amplified them.","It was as if she had been speaking The First Tongue with an accent her entire existence, and someone had just shown her the proper pronunciation.","The seas of obsidian flames that surrounded her domain surged outward with renewed force. Where before they had held the line against THE Living Spirit’s assault, now they pushed back. The white-gray fog that had been pressing inward suddenly found itself facing resistance it hadn’t anticipated.","The fog recoiled.","THE Living Spirit’s forces, tens of thousands of Spiritual Abominations that had been maintaining constant pressure against her defenses, were actually pushed back at this time. Not by much. Perhaps a few kilometers. But after minutes of stalemate, any movement at all was significant.","And Surtra hadn’t done anything differently.","The blue-gold light had simply made her existing Way more effective. More complete. As if her understanding of The First Tongue had been operating at ninety percent efficiency her entire existence, and now it was finally reaching its full potential.","Surtra was stern and shocked as she kept her gaze on that radiant blue-gold monolith. Her obsidian flame eyes burned with intensity as she voiced out silently, the words barely a whisper even to herself.","\"Is it you? Have you arrived?\"","It was only a thought in her head. A hope she and many others had carried for eons, nursed through countless cycles of waiting and wondering if the claim they’d sensed would ever be fulfilled.","She blinked in the next moment as if she was seeing things.","But she could swear that in front of the endlessly rising blue-gold monolith, she saw the appearance of a blue-gold humanoid hologram with piercing eyes that began to gaze at the vastness of Muspelheim radiantly.","The hologram was there for only an instant. A flicker of presence. A suggestion of awareness.","And then it was scanning the realm, taking in everything, processing information at speeds that made Surtra’s own considerable perception seem sluggish by comparison.","Someone was watching!","---","In THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.","Noah’s eyes were bright as he received boundless waves of information from Ruination and THE Infiniverse regarding all the changes and the connection that had just occurred with Muspelheim.","Prompts descended before his vision with comprehensive detail.","|Muspelheim Integration - Initial Survey Complete|","|The surrounding atmosphere and geographical details of Muspelheim have been mapped across a radius of 847 Gigaparsecs from the entry Monolith.|","|Atmospheric Composition: Primordial flame essence, concentrated THE Civilizational Authority, and dense Weavings of The First Tongue permeate the entire realm.|","|Authority Concentration: Approximately 47 times higher than Ginnungagap.|","|Hostile Presence Detected|","|Living Existential Authority of Spirits sensed permeating around a central entity.|","|Entity Classification: The strongest is Halfway to THE Absolute Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.|","|Designation: THE Living Spirit.|","|Current Activity: Assault on a Muspeli-defended domain approximately 1 Gigaparsec from entry Monolith.|","|Forces Under Command: Tens of thousands of Spiritual Abominations, dozens of THE Surface Depth entities, multiple THE Intermediate Depth entities, 2 THE Fundamental Depth entities.|","|Indigenous Population Assessment|","|The Muspeli are surrounded by Mana and The First Tongue.|","|Similar to Ginnu Lifeforms, they appear to be native practitioners of linguistic authority.|","|Classification: Potential friendlies.|","|Note: Their defensive constructions are currently being amplified by the forged Phonemes of THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons. The effort from all this will be harvested.|","|High-Value Target Identified|","|A domain is currently under assault by the forces of THE Living Spirit.|","|At its very center, concentrated authority suggests the presence of an Axiom or a Fragment of an Axiom.|","|Designation: Unknown. Requires closer investigation.|","|Recommendation: The Muspeli are defending something of tremendous significance. Their success or failure may impact the integration of Muspelheim into THE Infiniverse.|","Noah read over all of these prompts, processing the information with the speed that his enhanced existence allowed. Muspelheim was already proving to be exactly as dangerous as they’d anticipated. THE Living Spirit alone was a problem, and that wasn’t even accounting for whatever other entities might have entered the primordial realm during THE Fallout.","But there were also opportunities here.","An Axiom. Or a Fragment of one.","He turned over to THE Secretive Eon.","\" What do you think about THE Living Spirit? Or Muspelheim?\"","...!","THE Secretive Eon looked at him as if wondering why he hadn’t already left to go deeper into the Stoa of Dogmata to bring back her Disciple. Her dark eyes held that same unreadable quality they always did, giving nothing away about her thoughts or intentions.","But she answered calmly.","\" The first isn’t really much. Just one among those that have to die.\" She said it the way someone might discuss removing a weed from a garden. A task to be completed, nothing more.","\" And Muspelheim... how exactly did you find out about that? Have you actually began doing something decent with your claim apart from just shouting it?\"","She tilted her head slightly.","\" That is among one of the Primordial Realms that should have been released as a result of THE Fallout. Ginnungagap and Muspelheim fall under The First Tongue. Helheim should be under Paradox. \" Her eyes sharpened slightly. \" And one of our targets in planning the collapse of THE Primordial Chaos is the Primordial Realm of Early Existence connected to Chaos...\"","She paused.","\" Jotunheim. It should be hidden across the gaps of Chaos and Existence out there right now, and I will need to cripple it before going against THE Primordial Chaos directly.\"","BOOM!","Her words were terrifying in their implications. She wasn’t just planning to collapse THE Primordial Chaos. She was planning to systematically dismantle everything connected to him first. Cut off his support. Destroy his foundations!","This was not the strategy of someone who fought fair.","This was the strategy of someone who had thought about this for a very, very long time.","Noah processed where things were at this moment and how to move on from here before he spoke.","\" I’ve just gained entry into Muspelheim, but it seems that THE Living Spirit is already there. Presumably with other entities either following THE Living Paradox or moving out of their own volition.\"","He paused.","\" THE Living Spirit seems to be halfway towards THE Absolute Depth. I don’t fear them the same way that I don’t fear you...\"","A slight smile touched his features.","\" But even though I don’t make the distinction of who is stronger and who is weaker based on Depth alone, I currently don’t seem to have a sharp blade that’s able to cut a Depth almost at the level of Absolute.\"","His gaze met hers directly.","\" Would you happen to have a sharp blade for me to use? After all, this is one of the Absolutes that need to die. Preferably before they fully become Absolute Depth.\"","...!","His words contained an abundance of information. He had entry into Muspelheim. He had identified THE Living Spirit as a target. He was asking her for weapons.","And he was doing all of this while simultaneously supposed to be rescuing her Disciple from the Stoa of Dogmata.","THE Secretive Eon turned to look at him as if she were reevaluating him entirely.","Her gaze remained calm and didn’t give anything away, but something shifted behind those dark eyes. Perhaps she was reconsidering her initial assessment. Perhaps she was simply amused by his audacity.","She raised her hand soon after.","On her palm, a brilliant light of something unfathomably grand began to shine. It was small, barely larger than a marble, but the authority radiating from it was so dense, so profound, so fundamentally significant that Noah felt his entire existence orient toward it instinctively.","A prompt bloomed before his vision.","| The light of a Fragment of an Axiom shines before you.|","...!"]},{"number":4713,"title":"Chapter 4713: Chapter 4712: A Sharp Blade!","paragraphs":["A Fragment of an Axiom.","Noah looked at THE Secretive Eon up and down as he processed what had just happened. Just how ridiculous was this being that she was able to freely pull out a Fragment of an Axiom when he asked for a sharp blade?","He’d asked for a weapon.","She’d handed him a piece of fundamental reality!","The Fragment in her palm was a deep crimson marble that seemed to contain storms within its small form. It pulsed with chaotic light, red and black and something that wasn’t quite either, swirling in patterns that refused to repeat themselves. Looking at it for too long made his eyes ache, not from brightness but from the sheer wrongness of what it represented.","This was a piece of something that predated the rules of Observable Existence, a shard of an Axiom that had helped define what Chaos meant at the most fundamental level.","\" This is a Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem, \" Eon said. \" Chaos-based. One of the more useful pieces I’ve collected over the eons.\"","She rotated her palm slightly, letting the crimson marble catch light that shouldn’t have existed in this space.","\"It can select up to nine targets simultaneously and lower their Depth to a level below their current classification. A Fundamental Depth entity becomes Intermediate. An Intermediate becomes Surface. A Surface becomes Pre-THE .\" She paused. \" Temporarily, of course. The effect doesn’t last forever. But it lasts long enough.\"","Her dark eyes met his.","\" You asked for a sharp blade. This is sharper than anything you could swing with your hands. It doesn’t cut bodies. It cuts Depth itself.\"","...!","And then she threw it to him.","Noah’s hand shot out and grasped The Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem , and the moment his fingers closed around it, prompts bloomed before his vision.","| Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem - Obtained|","|Classification: Axiom Fragment (Chaos-Aligned)|","|Origin: THE Axiom of Mayhem , one of the foundational Axioms governing disorder and upheaval across Observable Existence.|","|Primary Function: Depth Suppression|","|Effect: Can designate up to 9 targets simultaneously.|","|Upon activation, all designated targets have their Depth of Absolute Sovereignty temporarily reduced by one full classification level. It will cost you.|","|Duration: Variable based on target’s resistance and user’s authority.|","|Cooldown: Significant. Cannot be used in rapid succession.|","|Secondary Function: Passive Chaos Resonance|","|While held, the Fragment creates subtle disruptions in ordered systems within proximity.|","|Chaotic elements in the environment become marginally more responsive to user’s will.|","|LIMITATION: Only THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities can utilize this Fragment. One’s Depth has to be sufficient enough to activate the complex musings of Chaos within.|","|Attempts to activate by entities below this classification will result in backlash proportional to the gap between user’s Depth and required Depth.|","...!","Noah looked at that limitation.","Only THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities can utilize it.","He wasn’t at Fundamental Depth. He wasn’t even at Surface Depth in the conventional sense. His classification was THE Formless Depth, something that existed outside the normal hierarchy entirely. But limitations like this were written for entities who operated within conventional frameworks. They were written for beings whose power could be measured and categorized and contained within neat definitions.","His power couldn’t be.","He pocketed the Fragment and looked back at Eon.","\" Your body here has to go into the Stoa of Dogmata, \" she said, gesturing toward the perilous regions ahead. \" Teleportation isn’t viable across Observable Existence since THE Fallout, so what will you do?\"","Noah clenched his hand around the Fragment.","\" Rules are rules. But many rules don’t apply to Absolutes, right?\" He met her gaze evenly. \" I’ll find my own way to work around it.\"","He then looked over toward the Stoa of Dogmata, toward the zones of crystallized doctrine and ancient philosophical authority that stretched endlessly into the distance.","\" Who is your Disciple? And what do I need to watch out for in there that could hold back even someone like you?\"","THE Secretive Eon raised her hand, and an illusory image materialized in the air between them.","It showed a small fairy-like figure with crimson wings that seemed to be made of condensed authority rather than physical matter. Her hair was golden, flowing around her tiny form like liquid sunlight, and her eyes held a sharpness that seemed entirely too old for her delicate features. She couldn’t have been more than a foot tall, but something about her presence in even this illusory representation suggested she was far more dangerous than her size implied.","\" This is Nyx. My Fundamental Depth Disciple.\"","She paused.","\" Well. Fundamental Depth Weight. But still at Intermediate classification. She’s an experiment of mine since Ginnungagap.\" Her dark eyes settled on Noah. \" She broke the scales before you did.\"","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes flashed as he processed what she’d just said.","Fundamental Depth Weight while still at Intermediate classification!","That meant this fairy-like entity had the existential presence, the sheer immensity of being, that matched Fundamental Depth entities!","An entity whose power didn’t match their classification. Who existed outside the normal rules. Who had somehow accumulated Weight far beyond what their Depth should allow.","Eon had called her an experiment.","How long had THE Secretive Eon been working on ways to break the conventional power structure? How many beings had she created or cultivated who existed outside normal parameters? And if Nyx had Fundamental Depth Weight, what was holding her back in the Stoa of Dogmata?","\" Further in, the Stoa of Dogmata can make many impossible things possible,\" Eon said. \" THE Fallout corrupted many things in obscene manners. Corrupted Domains have strange Weavings of Existence that don’t follow conventional logic.\"","She tilted her head slightly.","\" I’ve ascertained that the region ahead likely nullifies power through some ancient methodology. Perhaps it strips away accumulated Weight. Perhaps it enforces a baseline state on all who enter. Perhaps it does something else entirely.\" Her gaze settled on him. \" If you just wrap this up successfully, then we can really get started on the actual work.\"","A pause.","\" Oh, and keep me updated on what happens with Muspelheim.\"","After such words, she waved her hands as if shooing him away, and she sat down in the same spot where he’d first found her. Her posture settled into something that looked like it could wait for another few eons without complaint.","Noah looked at her calmly.","Then he looked ahead at the perilous regions filled with Dogma in the surrounding environments. Zones of crystallized belief and ancient philosophical authority stretched before him, each one representing a different doctrine that had been elevated to fundamental truth within this Corrupted Vault. To pass through them, one would likely have to utilize multiple different Impositions with nearly every step, constantly asserting one’s own truth against the weight of accumulated conviction.","It would be exhausting for most entities.","It would be dangerous for any entity whose Way wasn’t firmly established.","But not for him!","\" Light work. Light fucking work.\"","Noah went ahead!","---","Meanwhile, in THE Infiniverse.","Another body of Noah stood in the sea of concentrated Primus Mana, surrounded by the spinning Phonemes that Ruination had been cultivating. His eyes were closed in concentration, his awareness split between his primary form entering the Stoa of Dogmata and this secondary existence that remained connected to his domain.","The Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem.","He could feel it in his other body’s hand, that crimson marble of chaos-aligned authority. He could sense its power, its potential, and its limitation.","Only THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities can utilize this Fragment.","Rules were rules.","But not for Absolutes.","And while he wasn’t Absolute in the conventional sense, his Formless Depth was a glorious one.","His hand plunged into his chest.","Not physically, but existentially. His fingers reached past flesh and bone and conventional matter, diving into the core of his existence where THE Heart of Infinite Lexicons pumped Glorious Genesis Blood of Potential through every aspect of his being.","He reached through the connection that bound all his bodies together, that made them one existence despite their physical separation.","And from his other body’s grasp, across the impossible distance between THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap and THE Infiniverse, the crimson marble that represented an Axiom Fragment was pulled through.","It emerged from his chest in a flash of red-black light, materializing in his waiting palm as if it had always been there.","Rules were rules.","But not for Absolutes.","And his Formless Depth said that he could move things between his bodies regardless of what conventional limitations suggested.","His Formless Depth said that the Fragment was where he needed it to be, and reality simply had to accommodate that truth!","Noah opened his eyes and looked at the Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem resting in his palm.","Now he had a sharp blade in Muspelheim.","And in the Stoa of Dogmata, his other body continued forward into the corrupted depths, ready to retrieve a fairy with Fundamental Depth Weight who had somehow gotten herself stuck in a domain that could make the impossible possible.","Light work!"]},{"number":4714,"title":"Chapter 4714: Chapter 4713: Archai I","paragraphs":["Imperialism.","It was a word that carried weight across every corner of Observable Existence, even if most entities never consciously recognized it for what it was.","At its core, imperialism was simple. It was the extension of power beyond one’s original boundaries. The reaching out of influence to encompass that which did not originally belong to you. The transformation of the foreign into the familiar, the independent into the dependent, the free into the claimed.","Many viewed imperialism through a narrow lens of morality, as if it were simply good or evil, justified or unjustified. But existence itself didn’t operate on such clean distinctions. The truth was far more uncomfortable.","Nearly every force of power utilized imperialism.","If you had power, you were a colonizer.","The first apocalypse Noah had gone through was due in some form to imperialism. The Beast World, or really, the Demon World had stretched out their hands to encompass a tiny blue planet that had never asked for their attention. They had looked upon this planet and seen something to be claimed, to be conquered, to be absorbed into their greater sphere of influence. The lives lost, the civilizations disrupted, the entire trajectory of humanity altered, all of it stemmed from that fundamental impulse to expand.","And it wasn’t unique to those particular invaders.","Every Civilization that had ever risen to prominence had done so through expansion. Every Way that had ever achieved THE classification had grown by encompassing more and more of reality within its framework. Every entity that had ever attained Absolute Depth had done so by making their truth so pervasive, so all-encompassing, that existence itself bent to accommodate them.","THE Creature embodied existence itself. Was that not the ultimate act of imperialism? To claim the very concept of being as your own domain?","THE Living Paradox had consumed THE Primordial Paradox . Was that not conquest at the most fundamental level?","THE Primordial Chaos spread entropy and disorder wherever he touched. Was that not the expansion of influence by another name?","Imperialism covered the vastness of existence like a blanket that most entities never noticed because they were already wrapped within it. If there was a Way to expand , if there was a method to grow one’s influence and claim more of reality as one’s own, then perhaps Imperialism itself would be the grandest Way of all.","Because in the end, existence rewarded those who reached.","And it consumed those who didn’t.","---","Across his existence, Noah could also be considered to have utilized imperialism over the last months and years.","He had conquered many lands and expanded his influence across existence. He had claimed territories, absorbed authorities, and extended the reach of his Civilization into domains that had never heard his name before. Each victory, each acquisition, each new connection forged was another thread in the grand expansion he was weaving.","And the latest act of imperialism was THE Infiniverse executing a partial Embodiment and beginning to claim Muspelheim.","Now, Noah had to go through with it.","He had to get things ready, because even though he had just obtained a Fragment of an Axiom and held THE Formless Depth, he couldn’t just rush in without a plan. The main question remained, and it was a heavy one.","How could he take care of Fundamental Depth entities and even half-a-step Absolute Depth entities?","He had his means, yes. The Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem could lower their Depth temporarily. His Formless Depth meant he existed outside conventional power comparisons. His mastery of The First Tongue gave him tools that most entities couldn’t even comprehend.","But their quantifiable immensity and weight was still greater than his.","The answer, of course, was in his Formless Depth.","\" Are things ready?\"","He asked Ruination lightly, and her reply came soon after.","|Integration Status - Final Phase|","|The 9 newly forged Phonemes are finishing their integration with core Philologies.|","|Perpetual Harvest: Integration at 97%. Philological structure adapting to incorporate new linguistic elements.|","|Undifferentiated Mana: Integration at 94%. Core framework being restructured at fundamental level.|","|Cheating Architect: Integration at 91%. Novel pathways forming between existing and new Phonemes.|","|Result: All integrated Principles are beginning to transform into something else. Classification pending.|","|First Tongue Proficiency Update|","|Continued advancement as a Perfect Speaker with newly forged Phonemes has unlocked additional capabilities.|","|New Capability: Information extraction from complex, corrupted, or ancient domains.|","|The First Tongue has been utilized to study the Stoa of Dogmata and THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.|","|Purpose: To uncover the Weavings of power used by entities in higher stages before differentiation.|","|Discovery: Ancient expressions of power predate modern methodology.|","|Ancient Expression Identified: Aletheia |","|Classification: THE Surface Depth equivalent (Pre-Differentiation Era)|","|Modern Equivalent: Assertion|","|Meaning: \"Unconcealment\" or \"Truth revealed\"|","|Core Principle: Aletheia is the act of revealing a truth that was always present but hidden from perception. Unlike modern Assertion which requests Existence’s acknowledgment, Aletheia operates on the understanding that truth is not created but uncovered.|","| Key Distinction: The speaker does not declare something to be true. They unveil what has always been true but was concealed.|","|Philosophical Foundation: Truth exists independently of observation. The skilled practitioner simply removes the veil that hides it from others.|","...!","Noah’s eyes sharpened.","Right.","Most THE Entities at this time used Assertion, Imposition, Declaration, and Embodiment for THE Surface Depth, Intermediate, Fundamental, and Absolute respectively. These were the modern expressions of power, the methods that entities in the current era utilized to exert their authority over reality.","But the enemies he might face from times of or before differentiation were different.","They utilized Dogma, a more powerful form of Imposition that he had already encountered. And now, Ruination had uncovered the equivalent of what methods the truly powerful utilized for THE Fundamental and Absolute stages.","THE Surface Depth ancient expression was deemed to be Aletheia.","But the ancient expressions of power above Intermediate were something else entirely.","| Ancient Expression Identified: Thesis|","|Classification: THE Fundamental Depth equivalent (Pre-Differentiation Era)|","|Modern Equivalent: Declaration|","|Meaning: \"A placing\" or \"A proposition set forth\"|","|Core Principle: Thesis is the act of placing a new truth into Existence that did not exist before and having it function as if it always had. It operates through philosophical proposition rather than raw authority.|","|Characteristics:|","|- Creates temporary new Principles by proposing them into existence.|","|- The proposition must be logically coherent within its own framework.|","|- Other entities can challenge a Thesis through dialectic debate.|","|- A successfully challenged Thesis collapses entirely.|","|- An unchallenged Thesis becomes increasingly real over time, eventually solidifying into permanent truth.|","|Philosophical Foundation: Thesis draws from the tradition of dialectic, where truth is arrived at through proposition and challenge. A Thesis is not a declaration of power but an invitation to debate. If the proposition survives scrutiny, it earns its place in reality.|","|Example Application: \"I propose that within this space, strength is determined by wisdom\" creates a temporary Principle where physical power scales with intellectual understanding. If no entity can successfully argue against this proposition, it solidifies into local truth.|","...!","Oh!","| Ancient Expression Identified: Apophasis|","|Classification: THE Absolute Depth equivalent (Pre-Differentiation Era)|","|Modern Equivalent: Embodiment |","|Meaning: \"Denial\" or \"Negative declaration\"|","|Core Principle: Apophasis is the most profound and paradoxical of the ancient expressions. It operates through negation, defining what something is by declaring what it is not. At its highest level, an entity using Apophasis becomes so thoroughly defined by what they are not that they transcend normal limitation.|","|Characteristics:|","|- Operates through systematic negation rather than positive declaration.|","|- \"I am not mortal\" is stronger than \"I am immortal\" because it eliminates the concept rather than opposing it.|","|- At its peak, an entity can negate the very concepts that could harm them.|","|- Can only be countered by an Apophasis that negates the negation, creating paradox.|","|Philosophical Foundation: Apophasis comes from the tradition of negative theology, where many understood not by what it is but by what it is not. This approach recognizes that positive definitions always limit, while negation liberates. To say \"I am strong\" binds you to a concept of strength. To say \"I am not weak\" removes weakness without binding you to any particular definition of its opposite.|","|Example Application: \"I am not bound by causality. I am not subject to time. I am not limited by space.\" Each negation removes a fundamental constraint until the entity exists outside normal parameters entirely. They have not declared themselves free; they have simply removed the chains.|","|Combat Application: Apophasis at its highest level is nearly unbeatable because there is nothing to attack. An entity who has negated enough of their definable qualities becomes something that cannot be targeted by conventional means. The only counter is to negate their negations, but this creates paradoxes that can destabilize local reality.|","...!","Noah looked at the prompts with bright eyes.","They were....ridiculously heavy!"]},{"number":4715,"title":"Chapter 4715: Chapter 4714: Archai II","paragraphs":["The implications alone made his mind race with possibilities. Thesis meant that Fundamental Depth entities from before differentiation didn’t simply declare their truth into existence through overwhelming authority. They proposed it. They invited challenge. And if their logic held, if their framework was coherent, their truth became more real than anything a modern Declaration could achieve.","Because it had been tested. Because it had survived scrutiny. Because existence itself had examined it and found no flaw.","And Apophasis was even more terrifying.","Modern Embodiment meant becoming what you were, fully and completely merging with the concept you represented. But Apophasis was the opposite approach achieving the same result through a different path. It meant unbecoming what you were not. Systematically removing every limitation, every constraint, every definition that could be used against you until you existed outside the boundaries that trapped other entities.","An entity using Apophasis didn’t need to be stronger than their opponent.","They simply needed to not be something their opponent could affect.","|Current Capability Assessment|","|Based on your Formless Depth and current integration status:|","| Thesis: Potentially possible with great exertion of your Way and the elevation of your Principles. Success rate variable based on the coherence of your propositions and the philosophical framework of your opponents.|","|Partial Embodiment/Partial Apophasis: Currently impossible under normal circumstances unless your weight and immensity experiences significant increase.|","|Exception: Rare moments of existential epiphany or unique environmental factors may allow successful execution of Partial Embodiment or Partial Apophasis.|","|Note: Even this limited capability is a terrifying achievement brought to fruition solely by the nature of your Formless Depth. No other entity at your current stage could even approach these ancient expressions.|","...!","Noah twirled the Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem as he read these prompts, feeling the pulsing power within his existence as he envisioned all the possibilities before him.","The main differences were becoming clear to him now.","Declaration versus Thesis. Both created truth, but through fundamentally different mechanisms. Declaration created through authority, through the raw weight of one’s Civilization imposing its reality upon existence. Thesis created through proposition, through logical coherence and philosophical framework. Declaration was harder to challenge directly but easier to overpower if you simply had more authority. Thesis was vulnerable to logical attack but became incredibly stable if left unchallenged.","An entity from Ginnungagap or Muspelheim using Thesis could potentially be defeated through debate rather than combat.","But an entity using Thesis that went unchallenged would have truth more solid than anything a modern Declarer could achieve.","And Embodiment versus Apophasis represented the same dichotomy at the highest level.","A clash between them would create fundamental paradoxes.","One entity saying \"I am this\" while another said \"I am not that\" in direct opposition could reshape local reality entirely.","At such a time, beside Noah in the sea of blue-gold Mana, the figure of the holographic Ruination appeared with an excited expression on her features.","|Master, I’ve managed to break down what your Principles could be distinguished as. I finished integrating the last few Phonemes into them.|","Her face was brilliant and filled with enthusiasm as she spoke, and illusory diagrams began to form around her as she explained.","|Your action of altering them and adding Phonemes into them elevated them to an ancient form of Principles that even Ginnu Lifeforms or Muspeli Lifeforms won’t necessarily have access to. So much has changed since before differentiation. The knowledge was lost. The methodology was forgotten. But from pushing The First Tongue to permeate freely in the Corrupted Vault, more of this information has been obtained.|","The diagrams shifted and reformed, displaying complex linguistic structures that pulsed with power.","|The designation given is: The Undifferentiated Principles. Archai.|","|Archai Classification - Overview|","|Before Principles became the stable truths that govern modern Observable Existence, they existed in a fluid, undifferentiated state called Archai (singular: Arche). These are the raw building blocks of reality, Principles that have not yet decided what they are.|","|Core Characteristics of Archai:|","|- Exist in superposition, capable of becoming any related Principle until observed or claimed.|","|- Respond to the philosophical framework of whoever interacts with them.|","|- Can be \"convinced\" to differentiate into specific Principles through argumentation and demonstration.|","|- Extremely dangerous because their undefined nature means they could become anything, including something lethal.|","|- Highly valuable because claiming an Arche allows one to shape what Principle it becomes.|","|Types of Archai Discovered:|","|Arche of Becoming: Undifferentiated principle of change, transformation, and potential. Could become Principles of Growth, Decay, Evolution, or Destruction. Responds to philosophical arguments about the nature of change.|","|Arche of Logos: Undifferentiated principle of reason, word, and order. Could become Principles of Truth, Language, Logic, or Structure. Responds to demonstrations of rational coherence.|","|Arche of Nous: Undifferentiated principle of mind, consciousness, and perception. Could become Principles of Thought, Awareness, Will, or Memory. Responds to displays of mental clarity and purpose.|","|Arche of Physis: Undifferentiated principle of nature and inherent quality. Could become Principles of Element, Essence, Character, or Being. Responds to authentic expression of one’s true nature.|","|Arche of Telos: Undifferentiated principle of purpose, and completion. Could become Principles of Apocalypse, Destiny, Goal, Death, or Fulfillment. Responds to clarity of purpose and direction.|","...!","The waves of information were glorious ones, and Ruination ended the presentation with even grander revelations.","|Principle Evolution Status|","| Your own Principles are elevating to become Undifferentiated Principles.|","|This transformation befits your Undifferentiated self.|","|This transformation befits the quality of your Mana and your Way.|","|Your Principles are becoming Archai.|","|Confirmed Transformations In Progress:|","|- The Archai of Undifferentiated Mana|","|- The Archai of Perpetual Harvest|","|- The Archai of Cheating Architect|","|Additional Archai will bloom as integration continues.|","|Practical Application: These Archai can be examined for effectiveness alongside the ancient expressions of Dogma or Thesis in the Stoa of Dogmata and Muspelheim.|","|Note: You will be among the few entities since before differentiation to wield Principles in their Undifferentiated state. Even most Ginnu Lifeforms and Muspeli Lifeform and othet types of Lifeforms belonging to Primordial Realms may have lost access to them.|","...!","Noah looked at all of these prompts with eyes that burned with blue-gold light.","Archai.","Undifferentiated Principles that had not yet decided what they were.","His Perpetual Harvest was becoming something that could be Growth or Decay or Evolution or Destruction depending on how he chose to express it. His Cheating Architect was becoming something that could bend rules in ways that hadn’t been defined yet. His Undifferentiated Mana was becoming the Arche of Mana itself, the raw building block from which all Mana-based Principles could potentially emerge.","Against modern opponents who used rigid, differentiated Principles, he would be able to shift and adapt in ways they couldn’t anticipate. Against ancient opponents who might recognize what Archai were, he would be speaking a language they understood but hadn’t heard in eons.","Either way, he had advantages that no one else, or very few, currently possessed!"]},{"number":4716,"title":"Chapter 4716: Chapter 4715: Archai III","paragraphs":["Archai!","For Noah, who had been looking to streamline his power so that he didn’t have so many different aspects of things that he didn’t utilize, the Archai were actually a profound and unique solution. Undifferentiated Principles that could become anything their grander concept represented.","This might even be a way to think about how he could bring down his 159 THE Stanchions of Infinity.","What use was such a high number when he only continued to utilize fully a select few of them?","The Stanchions were powerful, yes. Each one represented a facet of his authority, a pillar supporting the vast structure of his Civilization. But having 159 pillars meant that most of them stood unused, gathering metaphysical dust while only a handful bore the actual weight of his advancement. It was inefficient. It was cluttered. And in a realm where clarity of purpose strengthened one’s Way, clutter was a liability.","If he could condense multiple Stanchions into single Archai that encompassed all their related concepts, he would lose nothing while gaining coherence. A single Arche of Apocalypse could replace a dozen Stanchions related to damage, annihilation, entropy, and collapse. A single Arche of Genesis could replace another dozen related to beginning, formation, growth, and manifestation.","Fewer pillars. Greater stability. More profound expression!","Well, it was something to consider for later.","As he thought about all of this, he focused on the main matter at hand which, at the end of the day, remained his immensity and weight paired up with knowledge of himself and his Formless Depth.","And the two directions now were Muspelheim and THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.","He was already in the Vault, so he simply had to make his entrance into Muspelheim.","\"Is transfer to Muspelheim already possible?\"","|Yes, Master.|","Ruination’s response came with accompanying diagrams that illustrated the pathway she had prepared.","|Muspelheim itself is similar to the early Veiled Shore of THE Creature or THE Infiniverse in that the corrupting effects of THE Fallout did not manage to permeate throughout fully. The primordial flames that define that realm acted as a natural barrier against the entropic decay that consumed so much else. That is how I was able to begin spreading the influence of our First Tongue for a few gigaparsecs already to begin gathering information in Muspelheim.|","The diagrams shifted, showing a crystalline structure forming in the space between realms.","|The entry into that primordial realm uniquely is going to be through a pathway that forms into a blue-gold Monolith. A... Dungeon that you and your forces can use to enter as a doorway.|","...!","Noah shook his head at this as he smiled.","A Dungeon.","He remembered how in the blue planet, countless Monoliths had appeared as Dungeons to facilitate gateways for the invasion of the forces of the Demons and Beasts.","Those towering structures had torn through the fabric of the Blue Planet’s reality, allowing armies to pour through from other realms when Dungeon Breaks occured. They had been instruments of conquest, tools of imperialism wielded by forces that viewed humanity as nothing more than resources to be harvested.","And now, here they were.","He was the one creating the Monolith. He was the one opening the gateway. He was the one preparing to send forces through to claim territory that didn’t belong to him.","Existence turned, and those who had once been conquered became conquerors in their own right.","He breathed out at this moment as he raised his hand and felt the waves of blue-gold brilliance cascading through them. The Primus Mana responded to his will, swirling around his fingers like loyal servants eager to fulfill any command.","But eagerness wasn’t enough.","He needed more immensity and weight of his existence so that he could continue to support his Formless Depth to be capable of doing the things that others could not even imagine. He needed more Fragments of the Moirai Threads to get to nine so that he could have a full simulation until potential death. He needed to do many things.","And he knew he wasn’t the only one moving rapidly across existence at this moment.","THE Creature was not sitting still.","Nor was THE Living Paradox.","Nor was THE Primordial Chaos.","He was not the only one that could get stronger. All the others had been preparing for eons for this eruption of power. They had laid foundations while he was still learning what Mana even was. They had built Civilizations long befode he was struggling to survive his first apocalypse. They had accumulated weight and immensity across timescales that made his entire existence look like a single breath in an eternal conversation.","Who knew whether THE Creature or THE Living Paradox were already close to attaining the Second Scale of Existence?","There was no sitting still in such a terrifying environment.","Also, at this moment, even though it was hard, he would send another body to roam the Wastes of THE Fallout for the sole purpose of mapping and seeing if he could more easily locate Lumivara, Ul’moreth, The Fisherman, and others who had backed his Way.","They had likely been scattered when the chaos erupted. Finding them again was crucial, not just for the power they represented but because they had trusted him.","And he didn’t abandon those who trusted him.","Alongside that...","\" Let’s go. To Muspelheim.\"","His voice carried the weight of decision, the finality of a course chosen and committed to.","\" THE Living Spirit will be good practice for THE Living Elemental and the future Absolutes, and whether they can be toppled. Get Protos, Khor, Sigrid, Ra’Zan, and all the others who have attained THE to also join me soon. Their Depths will need to be forged in hardship and blood.\"","He paused, another thought crystallizing.","\" Oh, and proceed to set another anchor point here.\"","|Understood.|","He gave the order as his body began to be wrapped in a brilliant blue-gold light. His eyes remained brilliant and piercing as he thought of countless possibilities, of battles to come and enemies to face and truths to uncover. The light wrapped around him and solidified into a radiant crystalline Monolith structure, a gateway of his own making that would serve as the doorway to conquest.","And his entire figure disappeared!"]},{"number":4717,"title":"Chapter 4717: Chapter 4716: Where Is He?","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4716: Where Is He?","Across the Wastes of THE Fallout.","In a region filled with ash and flames and chaos, a graceful figure moved through the devastation with purpose that refused to waver.","Lumivara.","Her radiant humanoid form blazed against the surrounding darkness, an ethereal tail of pure light trailing behind her like banners of defiance. Fox-like features adorned a face of terrible beauty, with eyes that burned with golden blue luminescence and ears that swept back through hair that seemed woven from captured starlight.","Her brilliance illuminated the surrounding ash, pushing back the oppressive gloom that pervaded this cursed region.","Distinct signatures of Mana permeated across her Way of Light.","That blue-gold thread woven into her essence, the gift her Master had bestowed upon her, pulsed with steady rhythm as she used it to guide her search. It was a beacon and a compass both, connecting her to something greater than herself even in this realm of isolation.","At this moment, she had a stern gaze as she moved across the Wastes while trying to follow signatures of Mana. Trying to locate her Master in a region that did not allow for communication or teleportation.","The Wastes scrambled everything. They twisted space and severed connections. They made the simple act of finding someone into an ordeal that could take years or decades or longer.","But she was determined.","And she knew the others that she had recruited in THE Belly of Existence would be trying to do the same.","All the entities she had touched with the gift of Mana, all those who had sworn themselves to her Master’s Way.","They were out there. Searching. Refusing to give up.","And so, she continued on.","A few minutes later, as she crossed a region of volcanic flames where the very ground bled fire and the air itself seemed to burn, her expression shifted.","It became serious.","Her golden blue eyes narrowed as she looked behind her, her tail spreading wide in instinctive readiness. She sensed it before she saw it. The vibrant aura of multiple entities appearing, each of them carrying different depths of power that pressed against her senses like physical weight.","And then she saw them.","The figure that emerged first from the flames was magnificent in a way that demanded acknowledgment. She did not know him but...","This was...Gilgamesh!","He strode through the volcanic chaos as if it were a pleasant garden, his form radiating authority that predated civilizations. His features were carved from something older than mere flesh, a face of terrible beauty shining with glory!","Golden hair swept back from a brow that had worn crowns when crowns still meant something. His eyes blazed with the light of Genesis Principles.","He wore armor that seemed grown rather than forged, plates of paradoxical gold and obsidian that shifted between states of being as if unable to decide what they truly were. And in his bearing, in every step he took, there was the unmistakable weight of Fundamental Depth.","A Leader among Leaders!","Behind him, eighteen Early Creatures lined up like majestic titans.","They burned with THE Surface and Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty, their forms massive and terrible in their grandeur. Paradoxical obsidian-gold armor adorned their bodies, matching their leader’s aesthetic in a display of unified purpose.","But that wasn’t what made Lumivara’s blood run cold.","Two of these Intermediate Depth Early Creatures held obsidian spears.","And mounted on those spears were severed heads.","The heads of collapsed entities.","Entities that seemed to be pulsing still with residual waves of their Way, Ways that had glimmers of... Mana.","That blue-gold thread. That gift. That connection to her Master.","And the figure of Gilgamesh himself was grasping in his hand a chain that bundled a man whose Way burned with Light and Mana. The chained entity’s body was on the edge of collapse, his form flickering between states of existence as if it couldn’t decide whether it was still alive or already dead. His eyes, when they met Lumivara’s, held nothing but apology.","She recognized him.","She recognized them all.","The heads on the spears. The chained being. All her followers that she had exposed to Mana in THE Belly of Existence. All those she had told to find the Master should they get separated.","Her responsibility.","Her failure.","“OOOH!”","Lumivara roared out with fury that made the volcanic flames recoil. Light exploded from her form, now nine tails blazing with radiance that turned the surrounding ash to glass. The signature of Mana within her burned brighter than it ever had, responding to her rage with equal intensity.","Gilgamesh looked at her calmly.","His expression didn’t change. His posture didn’t shift. He regarded her outburst the way one might regard a particularly loud insect, with mild interest and no concern whatsoever.","“We have been searching for the signatures of Mana and coming across lesser things constantly.”","His voice was deep and resonant, carrying the weight of ages in every syllable. It was the voice of a king who had ruled when kingship was absolute, when his word was law and his judgment was final.","“You seem a bit stronger than the rest. You must be his stronger follower.”","He tilted his head slightly, studying her with eyes that had witnessed the birth of many things.","“Do you know the whereabouts of your Master? Do you know where this man is?”","An illusory image appeared between them.","The Scale Breaker!","The blue-gold brilliance that surrounded him. The eyes that held depths that even Gilgamesh couldn’t fully fathom.","The First Leader looked at the image, then at the chained Intermediate Depth entity, then at the collapsed heads on spears held by his subordinates.","“The others kept their mouths sealed tightly.”","There was no satisfaction in his voice. No cruelty. Just statement of fact.","“I hope you won’t be the same. I take no pleasure in cruelty or torture, but Osmont must be found.”","He stepped forward, and the volcanic flames parted around him like servants clearing a path for royalty.","“So, little fox. The one whose signature you currently carry, that glimmer of blue in your Way, do you know where he is? Can you sense him?”","HUUUUUM!","As he spoke, multiple Genesis Principles seethed around his body, manifesting as countless weapons that materialized from nothing. Swords and spears and axes and halberds, each one a Phantasm that had shaped history, each one capable of annihilating lesser entities through concept alone.","His Fundamental Depth Weight crashed out like a billowing sea, pressing down upon the region with authority that demanded submission. The volcanic flames bent toward him as if in worship. The ash swirled in patterns that echoed ancient script!","Oh!","Oh!","Gilgamesh! Gilgamesh! Gilgamesh!","And Lumivara roared out in defiance.","Light and Mana erupted from her in a glorious pillar of brilliance that shot toward the burning sky. Her nine tails spread wide, each one becoming a blade of pure radiance. Her Way expanded outward, pushing back against his Weight with everything she had.","She would not kneel, and she would not speak.","And if she died here, she would die without betraying the one who had given her purpose!","Her eyes flickered with defiance as truly, she had hoped to at least see him again after all these eons. To relieve how he protected her in The Infinite Unfurling.","Oh."]},{"number":4718,"title":"Chapter 4718: Chapter 4717: Depth! I","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4717: Depth! I","Wu Wei.","The concept had existed long before cultivators gave it a name, long before philosophers debated its meaning in quiet gardens and mountain temples.","It was woven into the very fabric of existence itself, a truth so fundamental that most entities never recognized it even as they lived within its embrace.","Effortless action.","Consider water.","It does not struggle against the rock in its path. It does not rage and scream and demand that the obstacle remove itself. It simply flows around, finding the path of least resistance while never abandoning its destination. Given enough time, that gentle pressure carves canyons. Given enough persistence, that soft yielding reshapes mountains.","Wu Wei was the understanding that true effectiveness came not from forcing outcomes but from responding spontaneously and appropriately to situations as they arose. It was the recognition that Existence had its own momentum, its own currents and flows, and that fighting against those currents exhausted one’s strength while achieving nothing.","But moving with them, adding one’s own intention to the existing flow, that was how empires were built and destinies were shaped.","This did not mean complete passivity or resignation.","The water still moved. The water still sought the sea. The water still carried within it the power to erode stone and flood valleys and reshape the very face of the world. Wu Wei was not about doing nothing. It was about doing the right thing at the right time in the right way, without wasted effort, without unnecessary struggle, without the friction that came from opposing the natural order.","It was responsive, non-coercive action.","A persistent, gentle pressure that never relented but never forced.","Across Observable Existence, those entities that had achieved the greatest heights understood this truth even if they called it by different names. They did not fight against the currents of fate. They read those currents, understood them, and then positioned themselves to be carried where they wished to go. They made themselves into vessels that the flow of existence itself wanted to fill.","The struggles that consumed lesser entities, the raging against circumstances, the desperate grasping for control, these were the hallmarks of those who had not yet learned. They exhausted themselves pushing against doors that opened inward. They broke themselves against walls that had doorways just to the side.","But those who understood Wu Wei?","They arrived at their destinations fresh and ready, having spent no more energy than the journey required.","Existence did not reward force. It rewarded alignment. It rewarded those who understood that the greatest power was not the power to impose one’s will upon reality, but the power to recognize which way reality was already flowing and to add one’s weight to that flow.","—","Now, Noah always went with the flow.","Whatever happened, he reacted and moved accordingly.","There were Primordial Realms connected to the Oldest Paradox of Existence?","Okay.","THE Infiniverse had made a Partial Embodiment and connected herself to Muspelheim as she now actively devoured it, and it needed to be conquered to make this process even faster?","Okay.","He didn’t rage against circumstances. He didn’t demand that reality reshape itself to match his expectations. He simply observed what was, understood its currents and flows, and then positioned himself to move with maximum effectiveness.","He flowed like water.","Like a gentle, pounding pressure that would always find a way.","And so...","HUUUUM!","He materialized outside of a massively rising blue-gold Monolith within Muspelheim.","His form coalesced from streams of azure and golden light, the signature of his Undifferentiated Mana painting itself across the primordial skies like a declaration written in fire. He wore robes that seemed woven from crystallized starlight, fabric that shifted between states of matter as if unable to decide what it truly was.","His features were sharp and angular, holding a type of beauty that was more conceptual than physical, the face of someone who had transcended the need for conventional appearance but chose to maintain one anyway.","His eyes burned with blue-gold brilliance, depths within them that seemed to contain entire folds.","And around him, Muspelheim spread in all its ancient glory.","The landscape was Mana and Flames given form and purpose. Obsidian plains stretched toward horizons that blazed with eternal flames, their surfaces reflecting light that had burned since before differentiation.","Mountains of crystallized magma rose like monuments to forgotten titans, their peaks wreathed in smoke that carried whispers of The First Tongue. Rivers of molten gold carved channels through the darkness.","The sky above was not a sky at all but an endless ocean, currents of seafire dancing in choreography that had been perfected over eons.","And Noah could see gigaparsecs away.","The auras of many powerful entities across the Depths of Absolute Sovereignty blazed like signal fires in the distance. Muspeli Lifeforms moved. And opposing them, different but equally powerful, the forces of THE Living Spirit marshaled!","As Noah looked at all of them, prompts bloomed before him.","|Welcome to Muspelheim|","|Primordial Realm of The First Spark |","|Status: Pre-Differentiation Domain, partially corrupted by THE Fallout at peripheral regions|","|Indigenous Population: Muspeli Lifeforms, native speakers of The First Tongue|","|Detected Entities within Sensory Range:|","|- THE Surface Depth signatures: 166|","|- THE Intermediate Depth signatures: 34|","|- THE Fundamental Depth signatures: 5|","|- Half-Step Absolute Depth signatures: 1 (THE Living Spirit)|","|First Tongue Saturation: 94.7% (Highest recorded outside of Ginnungagap)|","|Warning: Indigenous population possesses inherent sensitivity to First Tongue authority hierarchies.|","...!","—","From her position among the obsidian spires, Surtra watched the newcomer’s entrance with eyes that had witnessed the birth of many things.","She did not know who he was.","His Depth was unreadable, masked behind something that her senses couldn’t penetrate.","But then her existence began to buzz.","The makeup of her Phonemes, those fundamental building blocks of The First Tongue that were woven into every Muspeli Lifeform, began to pulse. They vibrated at frequencies she had never felt before, resonating with something in that distant figure’s presence like tuning forks responding to a perfect pitch.","And she understood.","This was a quality unique to Muspeli Lifeforms, this sensitivity to The First Tongue’s hierarchy. It showed who among them held the most authority with the primordial language, who had mastered more Phonemes, who had gone deeper into the linguistic foundations of reality itself. When a greater speaker appeared, the lesser speakers felt it in their very being.","At this moment, Surtra could feel that the grand entity who had just appeared held the highest authority over The First Tongue.","Not just high.","The highest.","Higher than any Muspeli Lifeform she had ever encountered. Higher than the ancient masters she knew of in other locations in Muspelheim who had preserved The First Tongue through eons of isolation. Higher than anyone had any right to be.","He...should be the glorious entity that laid THE Claim.","She couldn’t be entirely sure because she could not sense his Depth. But The First Tongue never lied. The resonance in her Phonemes could not be faked or manufactured. Either this entity held supreme authority over their sacred language, or reality itself had begun to deceive them.","And reality did not deceive Muspeli Lifeforms about The First Tongue.","So at this moment...","Surtra raised her arms toward the burning sky, her form blazing with obsidian flames that had been kindled before differentiation separated the realms.","“Let the Bells of Muspelheim ring loudly!”","Her voice carried in The First Tongue, each Phoneme resonating through the primordial realm like bells struck by the hand of destiny.","“Signal to all the others that The One Who Laid The Claim that no others have been able to do has appeared! After eons of waiting, the one we were promised has come!”","...!","BOOOOM!","The moment her words ended, the other Muspeli Lifeforms reacted.","Brilliant obsidian flames shot above from positions scattered across gigaparsecs of primordial landscape. Each flame was a voice, a confirmation, a recognition of what Surtra had proclaimed. They rose from the obsidian plains and the crystallized mountains and the banks of molten rivers, each one carrying the signature of a Muspeli Lifeform who had felt the same resonance in their Phonemes.","And then the epic scene truly unfolded.","Obsidian flames began to dance in the endless skies of Muspelheim.","They wove patterns that spelled out words in The First Tongue, proclamations visible across the entire realm. They rang with frequencies that were not quite sound and not quite light but something more fundamental than either.","As if they catalyzed a reaction, even more flames manifested.","The sky itself seemed to catch fire in a new way, the eternal burning intensifying into something that was less combustion and more celebration. The flames danced and rang in a unique symphony that began to spread out across Muspelheim, each new voice joining the chorus until the entire primordial realm vibrated with the message.","The One Who Laid The Claim had appeared.","After eons of waiting, he had come.","As the sound and flames reached past the Monolith Noah had just appeared in, his eyes shone with recognition. Prompts appeared in front of him, translating what he was witnessing into terms he could fully comprehend.","|Cultural Context: The Bells of Muspelheim|","|Throughout the history of Muspeli Lifeforms, every fundamental aspect of existence has been claimed by one entity or another. Existence claimed. Paradox claimed. Chaos claimed. Sovereignty claimed. Every great truth, every foundational concept, every pillar upon which Observable Existence rests has been laid claim to by some THE Entity.|","|But The First Tongue has never been claimed.|","|The language that predates all languages. The Phonemes from which all expression ultimately derives. The foundation of communication itself. No entity had ever possessed the authority to lay claim to it because no entity has ever mastered it fully enough to do so.|","|The Muspeli Lifeforms, as native speakers of The First Tongue, have waited for this moment since their Cognizance. They believed that one day, an entity would arise who could lay the claim that none others could make.|","|Your Way is THE Way of The First Tongue.|","|Current Status: The Bells of Muspelheim are ringing. The Flames of Muspelheim are dancing as they believe THE One Who Laid The Claim has been proclaimed.|","|Note: This title carries immense weight among Muspeli Lifeforms. They may view you as a prophesied figure rather than merely a powerful invader about to consume Muspelheim.|","...!","Noah’s eyes shone brightly as he looked at these prompts.","Possibilities flashed in his mind.","Existence flowed.","The gentle pressure of water against stone, given enough time, accomplished what brute force never could.","And Noah smiled as he began to descend toward the obsidian plains where the Muspeli Lifeforms waited with flames of welcome rather than flames of war.","THE Living Spirit gazed towards him with a calm gaze as things were likely about to get very chaotic!","But he wanted to see. There was so many things he wanted to try out as he wanted to see!","6/6 Keep the Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming!"]},{"number":4719,"title":"Chapter 4719: Chapter 4718: Depth! II","paragraphs":["The unique sensation of THE Formless Depth across his body continued to be an extremely odd one as Noah descended alone toward the citadel of vibrant pillars surrounded by the forces of THE Living Spirit.","The best way he could explain THE Formless Depth was an extremely cooling vibrant sensation of power. It flowed through him like liquid starlight, touching every aspect of his existence with its impossible quality. The Phonemes of The First Tongue and Logos and Philologies inside of him reinforced his foundation even faster than before, each one humming with increased efficiency as if THE Formless Depth gave them permission to operate beyond their normal limits. His Organ of Civilization and Heart pumped even denser and grander, the blue-gold Mana coursing through channels that seemed to widen and deepen with every passing moment.","And his mental state...","THE Formless Depth seemed to amplify a sense of calmness and arrogance that seemed unmatched.","It wasn’t the arrogance of delusion or the calmness of ignorance. It was something deeper, something that emerged from the fundamental truth of what he had become. As if his Depth was telling his existence that regardless of what would be thrown at him in the future, he had to domineeringly and calmly get through it.","After all, he had THE Formless Depth!","It was why he freely floated ahead at this moment even though a Half-Step Absolute Depth THE Living Spirit was looking at him from the citadel below. Multiple Fundamental Depth entities surrounded that being like generals attending their emperor. Tens of Intermediate Depth spirits formed ranks behind them, their combined weight enough to crush lesser civilizations into dust.","And his Weight and immensity, in their eyes, may only be categorized as Intermediate, if they could feel it at all.","Yet he still felt calmness and freedom from worry in all this.","THE Formless Depth was ecstatic and dangerous, and he had to be careful with it. Likely, even if he came across THE Creature right now, he felt like he would only gaze upon him calmly and even think he could take him on.","Eventually, yes.","But right now, the results would truly be very different.","THE Creature had accumulated weight and immensity across timescales that made Noah’s existence look like a candle flame compared to a star. THE Living Paradox had consumed THE Primordial Paradox and claimed authority over the concept of contradiction itself. THE Primordial Chaos had been spreading entropy since before differentiation separated the realms.","Noah was powerful, but he wasn’t delusional.","Not yet, anyway.","But this was the potential his Depth held! The grandness and immensity to even look upon THE Creature, THE Primordial Chaos, and THE Living Paradox and say... so what?!","That potential would be realized in time.","For now, he had lesser enemies to educate.","As he approached the citadel, he felt one of THE Fundamental Depth spirits near THE Living Spirit speak a few words to their leader. The massive presence that was THE Living Spirit seemed to consider for a moment, then nodded with glacial deliberation. And this terrifying thing, this Fundamental Depth entity, began to float up toward him.","The spirit that rose to meet Noah was a nightmare given form and purpose.","Its body was a twisted amalgamation of concepts that should never have been combined. The core of its being resembled an Udug demon of ancient terror, a massive humanoid form that stood three times Noah’s height with skin that seemed carved from solidified shadows. Its face was a mask of cruel angles and sharp ridges, with seven eyes arranged in a pattern that suggested malevolent intelligence and twelve horns that curved backward from its skull like a crown of darkness.","But this was no mere demon.","This was a spirit that had achieved THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","Its form flickered between states of being, solid one moment and ethereal the next, as if it couldn’t decide whether it wanted to be matter or energy or something else entirely. Chains of gray light wrapped around its arms and torso, not as restraints but as weapons, each link containing the compressed essence of subjugated Ways. Its hands ended in claws that seemed to cut through space itself, leaving trails of darkness in their wake.","And the weight that radiated from it...","That weight pressed down upon Noah like the judgment of ancient fiends!","The spirit stopped a hundred meters from him, its seven eyes all focusing on his form with expressions that ranged from contempt to curiosity to hunger.","\" Are you supposed to be the reinforcement of these flaming giants?\"","Its voice was like grinding stone mixed with screaming wind, carrying waves that made the air itself recoil.","\" Do you even know who you stand against? If you did, you would at least not hide your Depth.\"","The spirit tilted its head, those seven eyes narrowing.","\" You aren’t cowering and shitting yourself before my weight, so you should be Fundamental? Let me show you the difference in our Depths so that an ant like you knows just who you face.\"","...!","At such words, waves of obsidian gray light buzzed from the spirit’s form as its Way bombarded Noah with crushing authority. The weight of THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty descended upon him like a mountain range collapsing, like the pressure at the bottom of an infinite ocean, like the grinding of tectonic plates that cared nothing for what was caught between them!","But Noah remained floating.","Even as such a terrifying weight descended on him, his position didn’t waver. His expression didn’t change. His eyes continued to regard the spirit with that calm, almost lazy attention that seemed entirely inappropriate for someone facing a Fundamental Depth entity.","| Arche of Perpetual Harvest - Active Response|","|The budding Arche of Perpetual Harvest is exerting tremendous effort to process incoming authority.|","|Current Function: Oppressive force redirection and conversion.|","|Result: Only 10% of pressure directed against you is actually received. The remaining 90% is being converted into harvestable essence and fed back into your reserves.|","|The spirit seems very committed to feeding you. I’m not sure he understands what’s happening, but his dedication to making you stronger is almost touching.|","|Sustainability: Current harvest rate exceeds drain rate. You are technically profiting from this assault.|","...!","Noah blinked as he looked at the prompts.","Was Ruination also becoming influenced by the arrogance and calmness of his Formless Depth? Her prompts seemed a bit freer!","His eyes shone brightly as he looked at THE Fundamental Depth entity before him even more closely.","Lens of Civilization activated, and information crystallized before him.","|Entity Analysis: Gal’Thûrak the Subjugator|","|Classification: Udug Spirit Variant (Elder Form)|","| Depth: THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Distinction: THE Terror of Chains|","|Way: The Way of Subjugation|","|Principles:|","|- Principle of Binding |","|- Principle of Domination |","|- Principle of Fear Manifestation|","|- Principle of Authority Theft|","|Civilization: The Chained Collective (14,847 subjugated entities)|","|Notable Capabilities: Can temporarily steal aspects of defeated opponents’ Ways. Chain constructs possess semi-autonomous hunting behavior. Fear aura intensifies against those who recognize his reputation.|","|Weakness Assessment: Heavily reliant on psychological warfare. Actual combat capability, while formidable, does not match the terror his reputation suggests.|","...!","After he looked at this, Noah still felt his body buzzing somewhat. THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty was still not a walk in the park for him at this moment, regardless of how much the Arche of Perpetual Harvest mitigated. The pressure that did get through was still immense, still taxing, still demanding!","He stayed freely in the skies right now, but the moment this entity made a true Declaration, they might be able to knock him down or he would be forced to use The Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem.","But he truly wanted to test the limits of his own power and budding Archai!"]},{"number":4720,"title":"Chapter 4720: Chapter 4719: Depth! III","paragraphs":["At this moment, his mind buzzed with glory as he cycled everything he had to utter out something that only Fundamental Depth entities could produce.","He formed a Thesis in his mind.","The process was heavy.","It demanded everything he had and more.","His Philologies began to restructure themselves, arranging into patterns that he had only just learned existed. The Phonemes of The First Tongue vibrated at frequencies that pushed against the boundaries of what his current immensity could support. His Logos blazed with blue-gold fire as they prepared to serve as the framework for something that should have been beyond his reach.","The drain on his reserves was immediate and staggering.","But THE Formless Depth held firm.","It told him that this was possible. That the normal rules didn’t apply to him. That if he wanted to speak with the voice of Fundamental Depth, then he would speak with the voice of Fundamental Depth and reality could adjust its expectations accordingly.","He opened his eyes.","Above his head, THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons manifested and opened its pages, each one blazing with Phonemes that had never been observed before. The book rotated slowly, its presence announcing that what came next was not mere words but linguistic law being written into existence.","He would write his Thesis in his book!","And Noah spoke.","\"I propose that within Muspelheim, only those to whom I grant permission may draw power from The First Tongue.\"","HUUM!","The words emerged not as sound but as truth seeking validation.","\" All others who attempt to access its authority shall find their connection severed, their Phonemes silenced, their foundations denied. This is my Thesis. Let reality examine it and find no flaw.\"","...!","It was a terrifying Thesis.","And the moment he uttered it, the response was immediate.","Around Noah, lines of Logos and Philologies vibrated with frequencies that made space itself hum in sympathy. From him, a blast of blue-gold light erupted and cascaded across Muspelheim, spreading outward at speeds that defied conventional measurement. The light touched everything, Muspeli Lifeforms and Spirit armies alike, testing and categorizing and implementing.","The demon spirit Gal’Thûrak watched this display with an expression that shifted rapidly.","\" Who do you think you are to declare such a thing?!\"","His voice thundered with outrage, his chains rattling as they prepared to strike.","And yet before he fully finished his words, he felt a change.","His expression became astonished.","Then shocked.","Then somber.","Then incredulous as he looked toward Noah.","Something fundamental had shifted in his connection to power. Something that had always been there, so constant that he had never noticed it, was suddenly different. Diminished. Restricted.","At the same time, prompts bloomed before Noah with comprehensive detail.","|Thesis Actualization Report|","| Thesis: \"Within Muspelheim, only those to whom I grant permission may draw power from The First Tongue.\"|","|Status: Partially Applied|","|Coverage: Current region of Muspelheim (approximately 0.3% of total realm)|","|Resource Expenditure: Approximately 67% of available immensity was utilized in initial actualization.|","|Achievement: You have taken a true step toward utilizing the power of someone who has laid a claim on an aspect of the Oldest Paradox of Existence. The First Tongue recognizes your authority to regulate its access within your sphere of influence. Congratulations on telling reality that you get to decide who speaks its oldest language.|","|Thesis Effects on Non-Permitted Targets|","|Core Principle: Mana is the authority behind everything. All Principles are composed of Phonemes of The First Tongue. All Ways and Civilizations, regardless of their specialized forms, ultimately draw their power from this primordial source.|","|By severing access to The First Tongue, you have cut non-permitted entities off from the foundation upon which all their power rests.|","|Specific Effects:|","|Mana Flow: Reduced by 100% within coverage area. Non-permitted entities cannot draw upon ambient Mana or channel it through their systems. Their reserves drain without replenishment.|","|Principle Function: All Principles rely on Phonemes for their operation. Without access to The First Tongue, Principles operate at approximately 45% efficiency as they struggle to function on stored reserves alone.|","|Way Expression: Ways are specialized forms of The First Tongue. Non-permitted entities find their Way partially muted, operating at roughly 50% of normal output.|","|Authority Regeneration: Without access to The First Tongue’s ambient power, authority regeneration drops by approximately 65%. Non-permitted entities are burning fuel they cannot replace.|","|Civilization Functions: Civilizations draw power from Mana to fuel their operations. Any Civilization features within coverage area cease drawing new power and begin depleting reserves.|","|Cumulative Effect: Non-permitted entities operating at approximately 45-55% of their normal capability, with this percentage decreasing over time as reserves drain without replenishment.|","|Note: Gal’Thûrak appears to have just realized his chains no longer rattle with the same enthusiasm.|","|Thesis Challenge Window|","| As per the ancient expression of Thesis, other entities may challenge this proposition through dialectic debate. If successfully challenged, the Thesis collapses entirely.|","|Current Challenge Status: No challenges registered. The spirit seems too busy being shocked to form a coherent philosophical argument.|","|If Thesis Remains Unchallenged: Gradual solidification into local truth. After sufficient time without successful challenge, the Thesis will become permanent law within its coverage area, no longer requiring your immensity to maintain.|","|Strategic Assessment|","|The Spirit before you has just lost roughly half his effective power and is slowly losing more.|","|He knows it.|","|He knows you did it.|","|He does not know how, whether you can do it again, or how long it will last.|","...!","As Noah read the prompts explaining his Thesis, he felt the drain on his immensity. It was substantial, yes. The cost of proposing such an audacious truth into existence was not small.","But he also felt that drain rapidly being refilled.","The Arche of Perpetual Harvest continued its work, converting the ambient First Tongue energy in the region into harvestable essence. The very language he had just claimed authority over was now feeding his recovery. The more his enemies relied on The First Tongue, the more they powered his restoration.","He looked toward THE Fundamental Depth Spirit before him.","Gal’Thûrak’s seven eyes were wide with an emotion that looked remarkably like fear. His chains hung limply at his sides, no longer rattling with eager violence. The weight that had pressed down upon Noah moments ago had diminished to something almost ignorable.","Noah smiled calmly.","\" You asked who I am?\"","His voice carried across the burning skies of Muspelheim, reaching not just Gal’Thûrak but THE Living Spirit far behind and his armies and the giants of the Muspeli Lifeforms who watched from their positions.","\" Allow me to introduce myself.\"","He floated forward slightly, his robes of crystallized starlight shifting around him like the mantle of a king.","\"I am someone who can question whether your existence should even be before me.\"","The words were casual. Almost lazy. As if he were discussing the weather rather than the fundamental nature of reality.","\" Now, since you have brought yourself to me, I will leave your existence intact if you present your Civilization to me and kneel in apology.\"","He paused, letting the offer hang in the air.","\" Otherwise...\"","His eyes met Gal’Thûrak’s seven with perfect calm.","\" Your Depth, regardless of where it is at, will face collapse today.\"","...!","He said these words calmly and casually, as if making such a threat to a Fundamental Depth entity was the most natural thing in existence. As if he did this every day. As if the being before him was not THE Terror of Chains but merely an inconvenience that had placed itself in his path!","Gal’Thûrak stared at him in astonishment.","THE Living Spirit, far behind in the citadel, shifted its massive presence in a way that suggested sudden and intense interest, and then a frown as the effect of the Thesis exerted itself here!","The One Who Laid The Claim had not merely arrived.","He had announced his authority in a way that none of them could deny!"]},{"number":4721,"title":"Chapter 4721: Chapter 4720: Depth! IV","paragraphs":["THE Terror of Chains, Gal’Thûrak.","His gaze was heavy as he stared at the entity who had shockingly uttered out what looked to be a Declaration, but seemed to be so much more.","More than that, they proclaimed not giving permission to others utilizing The First Tongue.","For the declaration to actually stay, for it to take hold and begin affecting reality itself, what did that mean regarding this being whose Depth could not be discerned?","He couldn’t be Half-Step Absolute Depth or Absolute, right?","Such beings were rare beyond measure. THE Living Spirit was Half-Step Absolute, and his presence alone had been enough to subjugate the Muspeli Lifeforms here and claim dominion over vast swathes of this primordial territory. If another being of similar caliber had arrived, Gal’Thûrak would have sensed it. The weight of such existence couldn’t be hidden.","And yet...","This entity’s Depth was unreadable. His power was masked behind something that Gal’Thûrak’s senses couldn’t penetrate. And the declaration he had just made was functioning, actually functioning!","Even if he was Fundamental, how was his declaration affecting Gal’Thûrak so severely? How could he command The First Tongue like so?! He didn’t even seem like a Muspeli Lifeform!","Gal’Thûrak’s seven eyes flickered toward THE Living Spirit, who remained floating near the citadel far below. At the same time, he sent a private message through channels that only those bound to THE Living Spirit’s Civilization could access.","\" Sir, what shall I do here? My Way seems to be in peril as we cannot properly gauge this being. Could he be at your level?\"","The message carried his genuine concern, his confusion, his request for guidance. He had served THE Living Spirit faithfully for eons. He had subjugated countless entities in his master’s name. He had earned the right to ask for counsel in moments of uncertainty.","...!","But THE Living Spirit did not reply.","The silence stretched for one heartbeat. Two. Three.","Gal’Thûrak’s expression became even heavier as understanding dawned.","The Sir wanted to use him to test things out. THE Living Spirit was observing, waiting, allowing his subordinate to probe the enemy’s capabilities so that he could gauge the threat without exposing himself to unknown danger. It was a logical strategy. It was a cold strategy. It was exactly what Gal’Thûrak himself would have done in his master’s position.","But that didn’t make it any less bitter to be the one used as the probe.","Still, Gal’Thûrak had lived for long!","Eons upon eons of existence had taught him many things. Pride was useful when it served survival. Pride was a liability when it didn’t. Lesser beings, those young fools who had accumulated power without wisdom, would bellow out in rage at an enemy who had somehow made a declaration that caused them to lose access to The First Tongue. They would attack blindly, seeking to prove their superiority through force.","And they would die.","Gal’Thûrak had not survived this long by being a fool.","His chains fell silent at his sides. His seven eyes closed, one by one, until only the central eye remained open. And then, in a movement that seemed to defy everything his title represented...","\" It seems I have, in haste, stood against someone I did not understand.\"","His voice emerged calm and measured, carrying none of the earlier contempt.","\" For this transgression, I shall kneel in apology.\"","...!","And then THE Terror of Chains, THE Fundamental Depth entity whose very name had made civilizations tremble, whose chains had bound countless Ways and dragged them into servitude, whose existence had been synonymous with conquest and domination for longer than most entities had existed...","Knelt.","His massive form descended from its hovering position, obsidian-gray limbs folding beneath him as he lowered himself before Noah. His twelve horns, which had always pointed proudly toward the heavens, now angled toward the burning earth of Muspelheim. His chains pooled around him like the shed skin of a serpent, no longer weapons but mere accessories.","\" However ,\" Gal’Thûrak continued, his voice still measured, \" presenting my Way is a bit harder. It is intertwined with my Civilization and with those I have bound over the eons. To present it would be to unravel everything I have built. I hope this apology will suffice for the moment while we discuss terms.\"","...!","Silence descended upon this region of Muspelheim.","The Muspeli Lifeforms stared in disbelief, their obsidian flames flickering with confusion.","The armies of THE Living Spirit wavered in their formations. Intermediate Depth entities exchanged uncertain glances. The other Fundamental Depth spirits near the citadel shifted uncomfortably, their certainties shaken by the sight of one of their own abandoning pride so completely.","And THE Living Spirit himself...","His expression showed coldness and a trace of anger.","The massive presence that dominated this region of Muspelheim rippled with displeasure that made the air itself grow heavy. He had wanted Gal’Thûrak to engage, to probe, to reveal the stranger’s capabilities through combat. Instead, his subordinate had surrendered without a single exchange of power.","He had learned nothing new.","Noah looked at this powerful demon before him as he wholly did not expect this.","Where was the pride and arrogance that he had always come to know? Every enemy he had faced, from the lowest Beast World invader to the mightiest THE Entities, had met him with certainty in their own superiority. They had attacked first and questioned never. They had died with confusion in their eyes, never understanding how someone of lesser apparent power had overcome them!","But this one...","This one had actually thought.","This one had assessed the situation, recognized the danger, and chosen survival over pride!","Were those of higher Depth so perceptive and so protective of their Ways that they actually moved with logic?","It was almost disappointing.","Almost.","|Submission Recognition Protocol|","|Through the brilliance of your Way and actions, you have caused a Fundamental Depth entity to kneel before your grandeur.|","|Entity Affected: Gal’Thûrak the Subjugator|","|Action: Voluntary submission and apology|","|Consequence: The Way and Civilization of Gal’Thûrak will never be capable of proudly standing up before you. This is not a limitation you imposed. This is a limitation he imposed upon himself by choosing to kneel. His own existence now recognizes you as superior, and that recognition cannot be undone through force alone, regardless of Depth.|","|Combined Effect Assessment:|","|Previous Limitation: Your Thesis restricts his access to The First Tongue, reducing his capability to approximately 50%.|","|New Limitation: His voluntary submission reduces his capability to stand against you specifically by an additional factor.|","|Result: Gal’Thûrak can only express approximately 10% of his Depth and immensity against you.|","|THE Terror of Chains has successfully terrorized himself into impotence against you.|","| Harvest Drawn: Infinite Potential has been granted for this action. Your weight continues to increase.|","...!"]},{"number":4722,"title":"Chapter 4722: Chapter 4721: Depth! V","paragraphs":["The action was a glorious and heavy one!","Noah had come here prepared for battle. He had expected to test his Thesis against Fundamental Depth resistance, to see how his Archai performed under pressure, to learn the limits of his Formless Depth through conflict! Instead, his enemy had simply... surrendered.","It felt anticlimactic.","It felt-","WUU!","At such a pivotal moment, a terrifying aura bloomed.","Noah’s eyes flashed coldly as even though he moved, it was still too fast.","It was Half-Step Absolute Depth making a move, and it was undeniable.","BOOM!","Before anything could even be perceived or seen, an immense pressure smacked Noah from the skies and forcefully pushed him down. The weight was beyond anything Gal’Thûrak had produced!","It was gravity multiplied by authority multiplied by the sheer immensity of a being that stood half a step from the absolute peak of existence.","A Declaration bloomed in the skies above, words of power that rewrote local reality with the casual ease of breathing.","\" Only those with my permission can remain floating.\"","BOOM!","It was a heavy and profound Declaration!","Noah’s body plummeted.","The Arche of Perpetual Harvest worked frantically to convert the incoming force, but even at any percentage conversion, the remaining percentage was staggering. His Formless Depth screamed that he should be able to resist this, that normal rules didn’t apply to him, but the gap between Intermediate and Half-Step Absolute was not a gap that could be bridged through quality alone.","Not yet.","His feet hit the obsidian flaming earth of Muspelheim with force that sent shockwaves rippling outward. A crater formed beneath him, spreading cracks through the primordial stone that had existed since before differentiation. Flames erupted around him, responding to the violence of his landing with sympathetic fury.","And there he stood.","His figure shone with defiance in the heart of that crater. Blue-gold light crackled across his body, his Mana responding to the assault with instinctive resistance. His robes of crystallized starlight had torn in places, revealing skin that gleamed with the same azure-golden luminescence. His hair whipped around his face from residual force, and his eyes blazed with light that refused to dim.","He did not stumble.","He did not fall.","He stood in that crater as if he had chosen to be there, as if the earth of Muspelheim should be honored to support his weight, as if being forced from the sky was merely an inconvenience rather than a humiliation!","And he calmly raised his head to look above.","THE Living Spirit had appeared near Gal’Thûrak.","The entity was massive in a way that transcended physical dimension. Its form was composed of countless spirits compressed into a singular presence, faces and limbs and eyes all merged into something that was both one and many simultaneously. It burned with power that made the eternal flames of Muspelheim seem like candles, and its attention pressed down upon reality with weight that warped space itself.","This was Half-Step Absolute Depth.","This was what stood between the Fundamental and the true peak.","This was his true enemy.","|Declaration Impact Analysis|","|Declaration: \"Only those with my permission can remain floating.\"|","|Source: THE Living Spirit (Half-Step Absolute Depth)|","|Effect: Forced grounding of all entities within Declaration radius who lack explicit permission.|","|Your Status: Grounded. The Declaration overrode your spatial positioning through raw authority differential.|","|Damage Assessment: Against anything with a glimmer of Absolute Depth, you still require unique means to stand against them. The immensity of their Depths is incalculable by normal standards.|","| Even with your Thesis in place, even with your Formless Depth and glorious Foundation, 40% of your existence’s integrity was affected and destabilized by the power of THE Living Spirit.|","|Current Recovery: Existence stabilizing. Damage converting to experience. The Arche of Perpetual Harvest is doing its best, but there’s only so much it can harvest from being slapped out of the sky like a particularly ambitious insect.|","| THE Living Spirit is testing you. He wanted to see how you’d respond to overwhelming force after his subordinate’s submission denied him information. You are currently providing that information.|","...!","As THE Living Spirit stared down at Noah from above, he reached out with one of his countless limbs and smacked his kneeling follower with casual contempt.","The blow sent Gal’Thûrak sliding across the burning sky, his chains rattling as he absorbed the impact.","\" Grow a spine,\" THE Living Spirit said, his voice emerging from a thousand mouths simultaneously, \" and never kneel again. The enemy is merely at Fundamental Depth.\"","BOOM!","Gal’Thûrak rose from where he had been struck, his seven eyes opening one by one as he straightened his massive form. The chains around him began to rattle once more, though with noticeably less enthusiasm than before.","\" Sir didn’t answer when I called out before,\" Gal’Thûrak said, his voice calm despite the blow he had just received. \" It almost seemed like you wanted me to sacrifice my Way to gather information about this enemy.\"","...!","THE Living Spirit glared at Gal’Thûrak with cold fury.","The accusation hung in the air between them, unspoken but understood. Yes, that was exactly what THE Living Spirit had wanted. Yes, he had been willing to let his subordinate be destroyed if it meant learning the enemy’s capabilities. And yes, Gal’Thûrak had seen through the strategy and chosen self-preservation over loyal sacrifice.","Neither of them acknowledged it directly.","Neither of them needed to.","Their gazes turned toward Noah.","And Noah stared back at them.","The region around him vibrated and trembled as his existence worked to repair itself. He could feel the damage the Declaration had caused, the destabilization that rippled through his foundation like cracks in glass. It wasn’t critical. It wasn’t permanent. But it was a reminder that Half-Step Absolute Depth was not something he could face casually.","Not with his current immensity.","Not with his current weight.","He stretched, rolling his shoulders as blue-gold light flickered across his form. The cracks in his existence sealed themselves, his Formless Depth refusing to accept the damage as anything more than temporary inconvenience. His Arche of Perpetual Harvest worked continuously, converting the ambient power of Muspelheim into resources that fueled his recovery.","And then he waved his hand.","From his body, from the deepest reserves where he kept his most precious assets, he pulled out a radiant marble.","BOOM!","The moment The Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem emerged into open air, a shuddering aura erupted outward.","Reality itself seemed to recoil from the object. The flames of Muspelheim flickered in confusion, unsure whether they should burn brighter or extinguish entirely. The obsidian earth beneath Noah’s feet cracked further, not from force but from fundamental instability. Even the weight of THE Living Spirit’s Declaration seemed to waver, as if the local laws of reality were suddenly negotiable.","THE Living Spirit’s gaze changed.","The countless eyes that composed his form all focused on that marble with intensity that hadn’t been present before. He recognized what Noah held!","But Noah remained gloriously calm and defiant in the face of this terrifyingly powerful enemy.","He held The Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem loosely, almost carelessly, as if it were a toy rather than a piece of one of the fundamental truths that governed existence. His eyes met THE Living Spirit’s countless gazes without flinching.","And he smiled.","\" Let’s have a bit of Mayhem, shall we?\"","BOOM!","|Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem - Activation Sequence|","|An unfathomable weight of your Way is being committed to activate the Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem.|","|This is not a small expenditure.|","|Activation Status: Initiating.|","|Effect Upon Full Activation: Targetted entities within range will experience temporary Depth reduction. THE Living Spirit’s Half-Step Absolute Depth will be pulled down. Gal’Thûrak’s already diminished capability will crater further. The playing field will be forcibly leveled through the introduction of fundamental chaos into the local hierarchy of power.|","|Mayhem is easy to start. It’s considerably harder to survive.|","...!","WAA!"]},{"number":4723,"title":"Chapter 4723: Chapter 4722: It Is Not Enough I","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4722: It Is Not Enough I","Mayhem.","It was a word that held weight far beyond its simple syllables. It stood for disorder and destruction, of systems breaking down and certainties crumbling into dust. It was the promise that nothing built could last forever, that every structure would eventually fall, that every order would eventually dissolve into the formless chaos from which it emerged.","Many entities feared mayhem.","They built walls against it. They constructed hierarchies and laws and Principles designed to hold it at bay. They convinced themselves that through sufficient power, sufficient order, sufficient control, they could keep the chaos outside their domains forever.","They were wrong.","In the end, everything flowed toward chaos and entropy.","This was not nihilism. This was simply the fundamental truth of existence itself. Order required energy to maintain. Structure demanded constant effort to preserve. But chaos? Chaos was the default state. Chaos was what remained when effort ceased. Chaos was patient in a way that order could never be, because chaos did not need to do anything except wait.","And chaos always won eventually.","It was why, as much as many underestimated THE Primordial Chaos and did not speak of him in the same sentences as THE Creature and THE Living Paradox, his power was obscene and unfathomably real.","THE Creature represented existence itself, the foundational truth that things were.","THE Living Paradox represented contradiction, the impossible truth that things could be and not be simultaneously.","But THE Primordial Chaos represented the end state of all things. The destination toward which every river of existence inevitably flowed. The final answer to every question ever asked.","Entropy.","Dissolution.","The return to...formlessness.","His power did not need to be flashy. It did not need to be dramatic. It simply needed to be patient, because time itself was his ally. Every moment that passed brought all of existence one increment closer to the chaos he embodied. Every structure that formed was already in the process of falling apart. Every order that arose was already beginning to decay.","THE Primordial Chaos did not need to win battles.","He simply needed to wait for everyone else to lose.","At this time, the clearest depiction of mayhem and what chaos could do could be seen in the Wastes of THE Fallout.","Away from the heavy conflict in Muspelheim.","Away from the unmentioned and unknown and ongoing battles between THE Creature and THE Living Paradox.","In the Wastes of THE Fallout, multiple Declarations of THE Fundamental Depth entities permeated as the battle between THE First Leader, Gilgamesh, and Lumivara unfolded.","The landscape itself had been torn apart by the conflict!","What had once been regions of ash and volcanic flame now bore the scars of conceptual warfare. Craters the size of small realms marked where Declarations had clashed against Declarations. Rifts in space itself showed where the weight of Fundamental Depth had proven too heavy for reality to bear. The air shimmered with residual authority, fragments of power that had nowhere to go now that the Declarations that spawned them had been shattered.","Lumivara stood at the center of a devastated plain, her nine tails spread behind her like broken banners of war.","No.","Not nine tails.","Seven.","Two had been severed earlier in the battle, their stumps still leaking crimson gold blood that hissed where it touched the corrupted ground. Her radiant humanoid form, which had always blazed with the brilliance of captured starlight, now flickered with the uncertainty of a flame. Her fox-like features, usually so sharp and beautiful, were twisted with pain and defiance.","And across her chest, a huge gash wept crimson gold blood in steady rivers.","The Way of Unity had been carved into her flesh alongside the physical damage, and that conceptual wound rejected the union of her very cells. Her body wanted to heal. Her Principles demanded regeneration. But the Declaration that had inflicted the injury insisted that what had been separated could not be rejoined.","Around her, Declarations of her own blazed in defensive formation.","“My Light shall blind all who seek to harm me.”","“My radiance burns with the fury of Mana.”","“Within my presence, darkness cannot approach.”","Each Declaration was a masterwork of Fundamental Depth authority. Each one would have been enough to annihilate armies of lesser entities. Each one represented the culmination of eons of cultivation, of refinement, of pushing the Way of Light to heights that few had ever achieved.","Her power should have been more than enough to wipe the floor with any common THE Fundamental Depth entity.","But she did not face a common one now!","She faced Gilgamesh!","THE First Leader stood forty meters away, his form radiating authority that predated civilizations. Golden hair shone upon a face that had worn crowns when crowns still meant something. His armor of paradoxical gold and obsidian shifted between states of being, solid and ethereal simultaneously, as if unable to decide what it truly was.","Around him, crimson gold weapons floated in perfect formation.","Swords and spears and axes and halberds, each one carrying heavy and immense Declarations of its own. They orbited his form like planets around a sun, waiting to be called upon, eager to taste blood once more.","One spear in particular leaked crimson gold luminescence.","Lumivara’s blood.","The blood from the wound across her chest.","And the Declarations that surrounded Gilgamesh made her own seem like children’s prayers by comparison.","“All treasures belong to the King.”","“That which is divided shall be unified under my authority.”","“Paradox bends to my will, for I am THE First Leader.”","“Unity is inevitable within my presence.”","The Way of Unity, backed by Paradox itself, pressed against Lumivara’s defenses with weight that made the air itself groan. Where her Light pushed outward in radiant defiance, his Unity pulled inward with gravitational certainty. Where her Declarations insisted on separation and independence, his Declarations demanded convergence and submission.","His forces stood at a distance, eighteen Early Creatures with their obsidian spears and paradoxical armor.","They did not make a move.","They did not need to!","Their Leader faced Lumivara himself, and that was more than sufficient.","Gilgamesh looked at the wounded fox with eyes that held something almost like respect. Almost like pity. His expression was calm, measured, the face of a king who had seen countless enemies fall before him and would see countless more.","“It seems you are much more familiar with Mana than the others were.”","His voice carried across the devastated plain, each word weighted with ancient authority.","“The ones we captured, the ones whose heads now adorn my subordinates’ spears, they had only the faintest glimmers of that blue-gold thread. But you...” He tilted his head, studying her. “You are saturated with it. It flows through your Way like blood through veins.”","He stepped forward, and the weapons around him shifted in response.","“Are you close with Osmont? Do you remember him fondly?”","The questions were casual, conversational, as if they were not standing in the aftermath of a battle that had reshaped the landscape.","“How would he react should you perish here? Should you be collapsed entirely, your Way scattered across the Wastes like ash in the wind?”","He paused, and something that might have been genuine consideration crossed his features.","“It would be a shame to collapse you. Let us not do that. I have no issue with you personally, little fox. You are merely a means to an end.”","His hand reached out, and the blood-stained spear floated to his grasp.","“So just... call upon Osmont. Tell him you need him to come save you. As a Leader, he will come.”","His eyes met hers, and for a moment, something ancient and heavy passed between them.","“All of us Leaders... we bear this heaviness and weight. We cannot abandon those who follow us, even when wisdom demands we stay away. It is our blessing and our curse. Call him, and this can end without your collapse.”","...!","Lumivara looked at this ancient king, this being of incomprehensible power who had cornered her so thoroughly.","She looked at the blood leaking from her chest, at the stumps where two of her tails had been, at the devastation that surrounded them both.","She patted her chest.","The movement sent fresh waves of agony through her existence, but she did it anyway. Her hand came away coated in crimson gold blood, thick and luminescent and carrying the essence of her Way within it.","And she wiped that blood across her face.","Like war paint!","Like a declaration of her own!","Her eyes met Gilgamesh’s, and despite the pain, despite the exhaustion, despite the overwhelming certainty of her defeat, they blazed with defiance that refused to dim.","“Just fight, you motherfucker.”","...!"]},{"number":4724,"title":"Chapter 4724: Chapter 4723: It Is Not Enough II","paragraphs":["For a long moment, Gilgamesh simply stared at her.","Then he sighed.","It was a heavy sound, filled with something that might have been disappointment or might have been respect or might have been both intertwined so thoroughly that even he couldn’t separate them.","\" Very well.\"","He raised his hand, and the weapons around him began to spin faster.","Lumivara responded with everything she had left.","\"MY TAILS ARE THE SHARPEST IN EXISTENCE, AND THEY SHALL PIERCE EVERYTHING BEFORE ME!\"","BOOM!","The Declaration erupted from her with force that cracked the ground beneath her feet. Her seven remaining tails blazed with light so intense that the Wastes themselves recoiled, and then they transformed. No longer flowing extensions of her form, they became blades of concentrated radiance, each one carrying the full weight of her Way behind it.","They surged toward Gilgamesh like the wrath of dying Folds.","The very Wastes were torn by their passage. Space itself split where they traveled, unable to contain the sharpness she had declared into existence. Ash and flame and corrupted matter all fell away before her assault, annihilated by light that refused to acknowledge any obstacle.","Gilgamesh watched them come.","His eyes shone with immensity, with the weight of eons, with the accumulated authority of a being who had stood at the pinnacle of existence since before most entities learned to crawl.","And with pity.","\" ALL THAT IS DIVIDED SHALL BE UNIFIED. ALL THAT IS MANY SHALL BECOME ONE. ALL THAT OPPOSES ME SHALL JOIN ME OR CEASE.\"","BOOM!","His Declaration unfolded with force that made Lumivara’s seem like a whisper against a hurricane.","The Way of Unity, backed by the full weight of THE First Leader’s existence, crashed against her bladed tails with absolute authority. It did not deflect them. It did not block them . It unified them!","What had been seven became one.","What had been sharp became dull.","What had been an attack became... nothing.","SNAP!","Her tails, all seven of them, were bisected simultaneously as Gilgamesh’s Declaration cut through her own like a blade through silk. The sharpness she had declared was unified into a single point that collapsed under its own conceptual weight. The light she had summoned was unified into a darkness that could not illuminate anything.","And Gilgamesh himself moved forward.","His hand grasped the blood-stained spear with casual ease, and he crossed the distance between them in a single step that seemed to last forever.","The spear thrust toward Lumivara’s heart- towards her Heart of Light.","She roared with defiance even as the blood from her bisected tails ran down her form in crimson gold rivers. Even as her remaining tails, now stumps that wept luminescence, thrashed uselessly behind her. Even as every part of her existence screamed that this was the end!","Crimson gold tears leaked from her eyes, mixing with the blood she had painted across her face.","And in that moment, she did not think of escape. She did not think of survival. She did not think of the battle or the enemy or the pain that consumed her existence.","She thought of her master.","Of the entity who had given her Mana when she had only Light. Who had elevated her from a minor thing in The Infinite Unfurling to someone who could eventually stand against Fundamental Depth entities. Who had held her like the little fox she had been, stroking her fur.","She just wanted to see him again.","To be held by him one more time.","To hear his voice telling her that she had done well.","The spear came closer, its point gleaming with inevitability.","And Gilgamesh’s voice rang out from all around, heavy with the weight of a king who had witnessed too many endings.","\" Sometimes... we try and try our best. And sometimes, it is not enough.\"","His words carried no mockery or satisfaction. Only ancient understanding.","\"It is not to say you were lacking. Your Way is brilliant. Your determination is admirable. Your loyalty to your master is something I can respect.\"","The spear reached within inches of her chest.","\" Sometimes, Existence is just really unfair.\"","His eyes met hers one final time.","\" Rest, little fox. I will find your master another way.\"","...!","At such a time!","At such a pivotal moment where it looked like Lumivara’s fate was sealed!","A voice boomed across the Wastes of THE Fallout.","\" Yes, sometimes, Existence is unfair...\"","Gilgamesh’s eyes widened.","His spear, inches from Lumivara’s heart, stopped.","And it was not because he chose to stop it, but because something stopped it for him!","BOOM!","Boundless waves of obsidian gold hair descended from above like a curtain of judgment. Each strand carried weight that made Gilgamesh’s weapons tremble. Each fiber blazed with Mana so dense and pure that the corrupted Wastes themselves seemed to recoil from its presence.","The hair crashed against Gilgamesh’s crimson gold weapons, and those treasures that had conquered civilizations shattered like glass against stone!","An impenetrable wall formed between Gilgamesh and his prey.","Hair woven so densely that light itself could not pass through. Hair that thrummed with Declarations of its own, Declarations that made both Lumivara’s and Gilgamesh’s seem modest by comparison.","And beside that vibrant obsidian gold wall, a figure appeared next to Lumivara.","He was covered entirely in hair.","Obsidian gold strands flowed from every inch of his form, cascading around him like a living cloak that responded to his will. The hair moved with purpose, with intention, with the casual authority of someone who had long since stopped needing to prove anything to anyone. Where it touched the corrupted ground of the Wastes, the corruption fled.","Waves of obsidian Undifferentiated Mana surrounded him like an endless sea, so dense and pure that it seemed less like energy and more like liquid existence given form. The air itself bent around his presence, not in fear but in acknowledgment. Reality recognized this being and treated him with the deference reserved for those who had transcended normal hierarchies.","His face could not be seen beneath the curtain of hair.","But somehow, somehow, one could almost envision him smiling at this moment.","Lumivara looked toward this hairy figure with a tear-stricken face.","Shock and then recognition bloomed in her eyes. Disbelief. Hope. And then something that might have been called joy if joy could be mixed with relief so profound that it bordered on collapse!","She lunged toward him.","Her wounded form, bleeding from a dozen injuries, missing two tails entirely, carved with the Way of Unity that rejected her healing, threw itself at this figure with abandon that spoke of absolute trust.","She embraced him!","Her arms wrapped around his hairy form, and her face pressed against his chest as sobs wracked her body!","The hairy entity stood there for a moment, accepting her embrace as he sighed!","After all, the two of them had been in THE Belly of Existence for a long, long time.","His hairy hand rose and stroked the head of the little fox with gentleness that seemed impossible for someone radiating such immense power.","\" There, there.\"","His voice was warm and comforting, holding the weight of someone who had arrived exactly when he was needed and knew it.","\" It’s okay.\"","He continued to stroke her hair as she cried against him, her tears mixing with the blood that covered her form as he let her have this moment.","Then he turned toward Gilgamesh.","The hairy figure regarded THE First Leader with what might have been curiosity or might have been contempt or might have been simple assessment, his face remaining hidden beneath that curtain of obsidian gold while the weight of his attention pressed down upon the ancient king with unmistakable authority.","\" Why would a Leader be bullying a child?\"","The words carried across the devastated plain with casual authority that made the air itself tremble.","And then...","BOOM!","An unbelievably immense force shining obsidian gold smashed into Gilgamesh with violence that defied comprehension!","It was not an attack in any conventional sense but simply pressure, the weight of existence itself deciding that Gilgamesh should not be standing where he was standing.","Gilgamesh’s massive and unbeatable figure was flung backward like a leaf caught in a hurricane!","He who had conquered civilizations, he who had stood against armies, he who had made Lumivara seem like a child before his authority despite her being a Fundamental Depth entity saturated with Mana, was sent careening through the corrupted air of the Wastes with no ability to resist or slow his trajectory!","When he finally stopped, cratering into the corrupted Wastes with force that sent shockwaves rippling outward for miles, one could see his forehead.","It was cracked.","A single fissure ran from his hairline to his brow, splitting the perfect features that had worn crowns as crimson gold Unity flowed from the wound like blood from a mortal injury, the essence of his Way leaking from him in steady streams that spoke of damage far deeper than the physical.","And it did not heal.","The crack remained stubborn and impossible, refusing to close despite the immense regenerative capabilities that someone of his Depth should possess, a testament to the power that had inflicted it!","His gaze turned heavy and somber as he rose from the crater of Wastes, his ancient eyes focusing on the hairy figure standing beside Lumivara with an intensity of reassessment and recalculation.","He looked at that impossible entity, and understanding dawned in his ancient eyes.","From the light that had smashed into him, from the pressure that had flung him backward, from the wound that refused to close despite everything his Way of Unity demanded...","He could sense a glimmer of Absolute.","It was not fully Absolute, not the complete and total authority of someone who had reached the true peak of existence, but it was a glimmer, a taste, a promise of what lay within that hairy form that could not be ignored or dismissed!","And this...","This was heavy.","Truly, truly heavy!","For the first time since the battle began, for the first time since he had cornered Lumivara and demanded she call upon her master, for the first time since he had declared his intention to find Noah Osmont through any means necessary...","Gilgamesh looked upon an enemy and felt uncertainty.","At this moment, Ul’moreth, THE Primeval Titan, had arrived."]},{"number":4725,"title":"Chapter 4725: Chapter 4724: Against A Legend! I","paragraphs":["Axioms had to be truly terrifying things.","Just a Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem allowed for one to lower the Depth of another, and this alone was a capability that could reshape the outcome of any battle, but what did the other Fragments that completed the entire Axiom do? What capabilities lay dormant in the pieces he had not yet obtained? And what could one do with an entire Axiom of Mayhem fully assembled and bent to one’s will?","Noah had such thoughts racing through his mind as he put all his weight on activating a mere Fragment, and even then the process felt impossible, like trying to lift a mountain with hands that were already trembling from exertion.","But something occurred soon after which allowed him to feel a load taken off his shoulders, a weight that had been pressing down upon his reserves suddenly vanishing as if it had never existed.","| Thesis Actualization Complete|","|Your Thesis \"Within Muspelheim, only those to whom I grant permission may draw power from The First Tongue\" has gone unchallenged.|","| Challenge Window: Expired. No entity attempted dialectic debate against your proposition.|","|Status: Actualized. Your Thesis has solidified into local truth within its coverage area.|","|Previous Maintenance Cost: 67% of available immensity required for active maintenance.|","|Current Maintenance Cost: 0%. The Thesis now maintains itself as an accepted truth of this region.|","|Congratulations, Master. You proposed that you should control who gets to speak reality’s oldest language, and Existence examined your proposition, found no one willing to argue against it, and shrugged in acceptance.|","|Your immensity and weight are now fully available for other applications.|","...!","The moment such a thing occurred, Noah felt his existence pulse with weight and immensity once more as reserves that had been committed to maintaining his Thesis flooded back into his core, filling him with power that had been unavailable just moments before.","He looked at the marble spinning in his grasp, and his eyes shone with blue-gold brilliance as he spoke words that carried the weight of someone who had laid claim to The First Tongue itself.","\"The First Tongue commands you, little marble. Don’t believe yourself grander than it.\"","HUUUUM!","The moment such words boomed out across the burning landscape of Muspelheim, his immensity of THE Formless Depth surged outward and exerted itself onto the Fragment with authority that sought no resistance, and the marble that had been demanding tribute as if it were the superior force began to spin with a crimson obsidian glow that spoke of activation rather than negotiation!","Above, THE Living Spirit looked down with coldness!","And then the light of the Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem flashed out far faster than Planck speed and permeated across this entire region of Muspelheim with inevitability that could not be dodged or blocked or denied!","Noah’s existence began to buzz with sensations that straddled the line between agony and ecstasy, his body trying to lift from the crater he had been thrown into as if gravity itself had decided to reconsider its earlier judgment!","His eyes met THE Living Spirit’s countless gazes, and he smiled with the calm confidence of someone who had always wanted to test himself against such a being and was finally getting his chance.","\"I have heard many legends about you. Stories of The Earliest Folds...\"","His voice carried across the burning skies, reaching not just THE Living Spirit but his armies and his subordinates and the Muspeli Lifeforms who watched from their positions.","\"I always wondered about your fate, and the fate of THE Living Dimensional, THE Living Quantum, THE Living Concept, and even THE Living Temporal. \" He tilted his head, studying the massive entity before him with genuine curiosity. \" Did they stand with THE Creature, or THE Living Paradox? Seeing you moving out here like this all safe and sound... does that mean that you bent the knee to Paradox?\"","He broke free from the constraints and floated higher, his robes of crystallized starlight billowing around him as the Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem continued to pulse with crimson obsidian light in his grasp!","\"Is the grand Living Spirit moving under his command? Were you told to come here to Muspelheim under the orders of THE Living Paradox? Are there others like you here? Quantum? Concept? That bum fucker Elemental? \"","His smile widened, and there was something almost predatory in it now, the expression of someone who had found prey worthy of the hunt.","\" You see, I have so many questions, and I don’t think that you are one to give answers freely. So I will take it upon myself today to see if a legend can be cracked, to see if the entities that I used to only hear legends about can be brought low.\"","He raised his hand, and the Fragment pulsed in response as if eager to demonstrate its capabilities.","\" Tell me, O Living Spirit... do you bleed?\"","...!","THE Living Spirit looked down at this entity who dared to speak to him in such a manner, this being whose Depth should have made him nothing more than an insect to be crushed, and his countless faces twisted with burning lividity that made the eternal flames of Muspelheim seem cold by comparison.","His form, composed of countless spirits compressed into singular presence, roiled with calm fury that he had not felt in eons!","And yet he could feel it.","The change!","The shift in his existence that the Fragment had wrought.","His weight, his immensity, his Depth that had stood at Half-Step Absolute... something was wrong with it now, something fundamental had been altered by that crimson obsidian light!","At the same time, prompts bloomed before Noah with comprehensive detail.","|Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem - Activation Report|","|An immense concentration of your THE Civilizational Units of Everything has flooded into the Fragment to power its activation on selected targets.|","|THE Organ of Civilization pulses brilliantly as the engine of your Civilization and bears all the cost. Current strain: Significant but sustainable. Your foundation holds firm.|","|Selected Targets and Results:|","| Target 1: THE Living Spirit|","|Original Depth: Half-Step Absolute Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Fragment Effect: Resisted. When two Absolute capabilities meet, complexities bloom. A Fragment of an Axiom is a part of an Absolute, and THE Living Spirit was partly an Absolute himself. The clash of these authorities resulted in partial effect rather than full implementation.|","| Current Depth: Peak of THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Assessment: Still terrifyingly powerful, but no longer operating with the weight of someone touching the Absolute. He has been pulled back from the threshold he stood upon. Whether this makes him manageable or merely less impossible remains to be seen.|","| Target 2: Gal’Thûrak THE Subjugator|","|Original Depth: THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Fragment Effect: Full implementation. No Absolute qualities to resist.|","|Current Depth: THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Assessment: That fucker has fallen from Fundamental to Intermediate. Combined with his earlier submission and your Thesis restrictions, he is now operating at a fraction of his former capability. He seems like a good candidate to either kill for multiple Fragments of Moirai Threads or to imprison in THE Infinite Desmoterion.|","|What would having a Fundamental Depth prisoner do for your Way?|","|Additional Targets: The other Fundamental Depth follower of THE Living Spirit surrounding the citadel of flames below has also been affected. They now stand at Intermediate Depth as well.|","|You have just created a target-rich environment of former Fundamental Depth entities who are now within a range you can more feasibly engage. Whether you harvest them for Moirai Threads or collect them for THE Infinite Desmoterion, the options before you are considerably more palatable than they were thirty seconds ago.|","...!","Noah looked at these vibrant prompts and absorbed their implications in an instant, understanding blooming alongside opportunity as he recognized just how dramatically the Fragment had shifted the dynamics of this confrontation.","THE Living Spirit, reduced from Half-Step Absolute to peak Fundamental.","Gal’Thûrak, fallen from Fundamental to Intermediate.","The other Fundamental Depth entities around the citadel, all now standing at Intermediate as well.","An army of legends brought low by a single activation.","He made his move without hesitation, his figure shooting upward with rapidity that left afterimages of blue-gold light trailing behind him as he rocketed toward THE Living Spirit with intent that could not be mistaken for anything other than violence.","He did not underestimate a legend like THE Living Spirit, not even for a moment, because he knew that peak Fundamental Depth was still a height that exceeded his own weight and immensity by significant margins, knew that the countless spirits composing that entity’s form represented eons of accumulated power and knowledge and combat experience.","But at some point, legends fell.","At some point, the stories that had made children tremble and empires kneel became merely that, stories of beings who had once been untouchable but were now bleeding in the dirt like everyone else.","He was more than okay acting as the blade to weed out this legend!"]},{"number":4726,"title":"Chapter 4726: Chapter 4725: Against A Legend! II","paragraphs":["A great man once said that those who cling to death, live, and those who cling to life, die.","To live, one had to be ruthless and ready for death at any moment.","To live and thrive in the post-apocalyptic age of THE Fallout, one had to be utterly obscene and prepared for death to come knocking at any time without warning or mercy.","For Noah, it was a simple thing as he was already ruthless and ready for death if it came, had been ready since the first apocalypse came to his tiny blue planet and taught him that existence cared nothing for fairness or justice or the desperate hopes of those who wished to survive!","Every being across existence lived and died, and he had not met any that were impervious to this fact yet, not THE Entities at the highest levels nor the primordial beings that had existed since before differentiation nor even the legends whose names were spoken in whispers across countless realms.","Even THE Primordial Paradox was collapsed, right?!","And THE Living Spirit...","He wanted to see if he could institute this reality for it.","So defiant against the Declaration this being had laid down, defiant against the authority that had smashed him from the skies and forced him into a crater, he rose up against it through sheer will and weight as he breathed out slowly.","\"Hoo...\"","Everything slowed down.","When Noah looked up, he saw the cold eyes of THE Living Spirit as the entity gazed down at him with the calm fury of something that had been shown disrespect by a creature it considered beneath notice.","He saw Gal’Thûrak behind and to the side, the demon spirit’s seven eyes wide with an ashen expression as he felt his own Depth diminished, as he recognized what the Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem had done to him, and this being who had called himself THE Terror of Chains actually scrambled backward through the burning air as if distance could save him from what was coming.","Noah saw all of this with clarity that seemed to stretch each moment into eternity, and he raised his left hand with an expression becoming immensely calm, the kind of calm that preceded storms and catastrophes and the ending of things that had seemed eternal.","On his raised hand, a bow began to form.","Blue-gold light crystallized from the ambient Mana of Muspelheim, weaving itself into a weapon that seemed less crafted and more grown, a bow of such elegant lethality! The limbs curved with mathematical perfection, inscribed with Phonemes of The First Tongue that blazed with authority, and the string that connected them thrummed with tension that spoke of violence yearning to be released.","Noah used his right hand to pull on the bow string, his fingers finding their position with the ease of someone who had done this countless times before, and as he drew the string back toward his cheek, a radiant blue-gold arrow began to form between his grip and the bow itself.","The arrow’s edge was sharp beyond sharpness, pointed directly toward THE Living Spirit with intent that could not be mistaken for anything other than murder.","How could he be as ruthless as possible here?","The answer was already burning in his mind as he considered his assets, his Thesis that had been actualized, his enemies who could barely access The First Tongue due to that very Thesis, and the opportunity that lay before him like a banquet waiting to be devoured.","His voice echoed out calmly as he declared a new Thesis while tugging at every last drop of immensity he had left within him, building upon the foundation he had already established with brilliance that bordered on cruelty.","\" My arrow chains and severs upon all those that can barely access The First Tongue.\"","...!","His eyes burned with ingenuity as he worked on an already built Thesis to declare such a devastatingly simple proposition, using the restrictions he had already imposed as the framework for something even more horrific!","His enemies could barely access The First Tongue because of his earlier Thesis.","And now his arrow would chain between them, would sever their Ways and their Civilizations with the inevitability of a sentence that had already been written.","His eyes remained locked on THE Living Spirit as he let loose the bow string with a motion that seemed almost gentle, almost casual, as if he were not about to commit an act of mass devastation that would echo across this primordial realm.","And the arrow flew.","Existence distorted around its passage, space itself bending to accommodate something that moved too fast and carried too much weight to be contained by normal physics. A light of established Thesis wrapped around the arrow like a shroud, like a promise, like a death sentence written in blue-gold fire!","Halfway to the cold-faced Living Spirit, the arrow disappeared.","WAP!","This glorious moment stretched in slowed time as Noah and THE Living Spirit continued locked onto each other, their gazes meeting across the burning air of Muspelheim with intensity that made the eternal flames seem cold, the attack Noah had thrown out nowhere to be seen as if it had simply ceased to exist.","And then, horrifically...","OOOOOH!","A furious and horrified roar echoed out from the surroundings of the citadel where the forces of THE Living Spirit had been positioned, a sound of absolute terror from something that had just realized death had arrived without warning or mercy!","Noah’s arrow had not been aimed at THE Living Spirit at all.","It had appeared an inch away from another spirit, one that used to stand at THE Fundamental Depth before The Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem had dragged it down, a monstrous entity whose form resembled a Cetus of ancient legend. Its body was massive and serpentine, scales of gray-white spirit essence covering a form that stretched for miles, with jaws that could have swallowed small realms and eyes that blazed with the fury of oceanic depths that had never known sunlight.","It roared as its Way of Spirit Water tried to make a stand against the arrow that had materialized before its existence, ancient Principles activating in desperate defense as Declarations attempted to form around its body like shields.","But an earlier Thesis had already cut off its access to The First Tongue.","And this arrow carried a Thesis that built upon that previous Thesis while holding a weight no Intermediate Depth entity could truly withstand!","The Cetus had been Fundamental, had stood at heights that would have made it nearly untouchable under normal circumstances, but currently it was dragged down to Intermediate by the Fragment’s power, and what occurred next was just utter devastation of a Way!","It seemed like a long time, but all of this was happening in a fraction of a femtosecond.","The arrow burning with Thesis pierced across the Cetus with the ease of a blade through mist, its blue-gold radiance carving through spirit essence and Way alike as if they were made of paper rather than the accumulated authority of eons. The great serpentine form shuddered once, twice, and then its Way shattered like glass struck by a hammer, fragments of Spirit Water scattering across Muspelheim in a display that would have been beautiful if it were not so terrible.","Its Civilization collapsed in the same instant, the connections it had built over countless years severing all at once as its existence ceased to be anything more than resources waiting to be harvested.","And then the arrow flew ever faster.","It did not stop with a single kill.","My arrow chains and severs upon all those that can barely access The First Tongue!","This terrifying Thesis allowed for an utterly horrendous and ruthless action to occur as the arrow warped through space to find its next target, an Intermediate Depth Spirit whose form resembled a writhing mass of ethereal tentacles, and it pierced through that existence with the same casual ease before chaining to the next target and the next and the next!","Eight THE Intermediate Depth Spirits.","Thirty-six THE Surface Depth Spirits.","The arrow moved through them like it was popping bubbles, multiple sounds echoing out across existence as a single projectile pierced dozens of Civilizations in sequence, leaving behind dim eyes and collapsing Ways as it carved a path of devastation through the forces of THE Living Spirit!","Pop.","Pop.","Pop!","POP!!!"]},{"number":4727,"title":"Chapter 4727: Chapter 4726: Against A Legend! III","paragraphs":["Each sound was a Civilization ending, a Way shattering, an existence that had accumulated power over eons being reduced to nothing more than harvest waiting to be claimed.","And then the arrow warped one final time to appear before the eyes of a scrambling Gal’Thûrak in the skies!","The demon spirit’s seven eyes went wide with horror and fear that he had not felt in eons, his chains rattling uselessly at his sides as he recognized that death had come for him in the form of a blue-gold arrow that had just murdered his colleagues without slowing down.","\" PLEASE!\"","His roar was desperate and pathetic, the sound of someone who had spent his existence subjugating others suddenly finding himself on the other end of absolute power, and the terror in his voice was so raw and so genuine that it might have moved a lesser being to mercy.","Noah was not a lesser being.","But in the next moment, as the arrow surged toward Gal’Thûrak with the inevitability of a death sentence already signed, a massive white-gray claw appeared in its path!","THE Living Spirit moved with speed that defied even the slowed perception of this moment, one of his countless limbs extending across the distance between himself and his subordinate as he refused to lose another...well, actually, the last follower to this impossible enemy!","The claw was massive and terrible, composed of compressed spirits that screamed silently as they were forced into service, and it caught the arrow with a grip that released gray bursts of Immensity in all directions.","\" SPIRITS CANNOT BE SEVERED BY MORTAL WEAPONS!\"","BOOM!","The Declaration crashed against Noah’s Thesis with the weight of someone who had been ancient when THE Fallout was merely a possibility rather than a reality, and the arrow holding the terrifying Thesis buzzed in THE Living Spirit’s deformed and radiant claw as two authorities contested for dominance.","The arrow stopped.","THE Living Spirit looked toward Noah with eyes that blazed with fury beyond anything he had shown before, with rage that spoke of losses that could not be calculated and insults that could not be forgiven.","And then he looked past Noah, toward the surroundings of the citadel where his forces had been stationed.","All of them had slumped down like dolls whose strings had been cut.","The Cetus. The tentacled horror. The eight Intermediate Depth spirits. The thirty-six Surface Depth entities. All of them lay still and silent, their Ways shattered and their Civilizations collapsed, nothing remaining but corpses that had once been legends in their own right.","An instant later, those corpses began to move.","They flew out toward Noah as if drawn by invisible strings, rising from where they had fallen and streaming through the burning air of Muspelheim toward the entity who had killed them, and one by one, they sank into his back with sounds like stones dropping into still water.","As each one was drawn into him, Noah’s immensity and weight erupted higher and higher!","The first corpse, a Surface Depth spirit, added its essence to his foundation.","The second and third and fourth followed, each one making him burn brighter.","THE Intermediate Depth spirits came next, their accumulated authority flooding into his existence with force that made the air around him shimmer and distort.","And finally, the Cetus, the former Fundamental Depth entity whose Way of Spirit Water had been shattered by a single arrow, sank into his back and elevated his foundation in ways that made everything before seem like appetizers before a feast!","Blue-gold flames surrounded Noah in a corona of power that seemed to grow with every corpse he absorbed, making him look glorious and tyrannical in ways that defied easy description. He had just collapsed dozens of Civilizations in a single blow. He had collapsed a Fundamental Depth entity in a single blow! Even if he was utilizing a Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem to reduce their Depths, even if he had built his attack on an already established Thesis, the achievement was staggering!","What a terrifying wonder he had become!","He carried out such a ruthless action with the casual ease of someone who had long since stopped feeling guilt for doing what needed to be done, and in the heavy silence that followed, prompts bloomed before him with comprehensive detail!","|Mass Harvest Report|","|Civilizations Collapsed: 45|","|Breakdown:|","|THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty (Spirit Water - Cetus Variant): 1|","|As directed, everything about this entity has been transformed into Harvest that is amplified and devoured to elevate your Foundation and Way. Its accumulated authority over eons, its Principles of oceanic depth and spirit essence, its connections and its knowledge and its very existence have all been converted into fuel for your advancement.|","|THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty: 8|","|8 entities have been transformed into the optimum loot of 12 Fragments of Moirai Threads.|","|Current Moirai Thread Fragment Count: Previous + 12. Full Simulation till death possible.|","|THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty: 36|","|All 36 entities have had everything about them transformed into Harvest that is amplified and devoured to elevate your Foundation and Way. They didn’t have much individually, but quantity has a quality all its own.|","|Foundation Status: Burning. Your comparative Weight, even while not being entirely accurate in its capabilities due to your Formless Depth, is rising comparably to be 70/100th the Immensity of THE Creature and THE Primordial Chaos at Intermediate Depth.|","|Current Comparative Weight: Approximately 70/100th.|","...!","BOOM!","Noah floated in the burning skies of Muspelheim as an imposing humanoid figure whose weight and immensity bellowed around him like a declaration of war against everything that dared to oppose him, and he stared up toward THE Living Spirit with eyes that blazed through the flames surrounding his form.","Those flames.","Those billowing blue-gold flames of Primus Mana that surrounded him made him seem like a flaming entity whose face could barely be observed through the conflagration, a being of fire and fury and absolute authority whose features were glimpsed only in fragments between the dancing tongues of power that wreathed his entire existence.","The weight burning from him was so immense that reality itself seemed to bend around his presence, the air distorting and the flames of Muspelheim leaning toward him as if paying homage to something that burned hotter and brighter than their eternal fires could ever hope to match.","And when he breathed, one could see furious blue-gold flames rushing from his nose and mouth with every exhale, fire that spoke of power so concentrated that it could not be contained within a mere physical form!","He looked like a wild celestial humanoid beast, something that had crawled out of the primordial fires that existed before existence learned to cool, and the flames billowing from his nose and mouth emanated so much heat that it truly felt like these flames alone could utterly scorch to cinders any THE Surface Depth Civilizations just by being near!","The very act of his breathing had become a threat!","The very fact of his existence had become a Declaration!","...!","Oh!"]},{"number":4728,"title":"Chapter 4728: Chapter 4727: All Things Live And Die I","paragraphs":["All beings rose to power.","THE Creature rose to power as he was THE Intermediate Depth once, climbing through the stages of Absolute Sovereignty like everyone else before reaching heights that made him synonymous with existence itself. So was THE Living Paradox and THE Primordial Chaos, both of them having passed through the lower Depths before ascending to the peaks they currently occupied!","So when it was stated that Noah had 70/100th the power of THE Living Paradox or THE Creature at Intermediate Depth, this was only a point of comparison for them at that specific stage of their journey!","Would the immensity of any common Intermediate Depth entity even come close to matching the immensity of THE Creature at Intermediate Depth?","The answer was a clear and resounding no.","THE Creature at Intermediate Depth had already been a monster beyond monsters, a being whose foundation was so profound and whose accumulation was so vast that comparing him to ordinary Intermediate Depth entities was like comparing an ocean to a puddle. The same was true for THE Living Paradox and THE Primordial Chaos, beings who had been exceptional even at lower Depths, whose foundations had been built on concepts so fundamental that their immensity dwarfed their supposed peers.","It was estimated that at most, a powerful Intermediate Depth entity, the renowned beings who had grand Civilizations and who had built up their foundations to the absolute peak as they waited for a spark to enter Fundamental Depth, such entities could maybe come close to matching a tenth of what the immensity of THE Creature had been at that stage.","...!","And even that estimate could be off!","This was the power that Noah currently held as he continued rising through the burning skies of Muspelheim, his form wreathed in blue-gold flames that made him look less like a man and more like a celestial phenomenon given consciousness and purpose.","He came to float on the same level as THE Living Spirit, the two of them facing each other across a distance that seemed both vast and insignificant at the same time, predator meeting predator in the eternal dance of those who refused to acknowledge anything as superior to themselves.","The two looked at each other dangerously.","THE Living Spirit’s form had shifted from the amorphous mass of countless spirits into something more defined, more intentional, a humanoid shape that suggested he was taking this confrontation seriously enough to consolidate his presence into a singular expression of power. His face, if it could be called that, held contained calmness and immensity that spoke of eons of existence and countless battles survived.","His voice came out slow and heavy, each word carrying the weight of mountains settling into place.","\" Are you him?\"","HUUUM!","A simple question that resonated through the burning air of Muspelheim with implications that stretched far beyond its three words.","One that Noah remained nonchalant to as blue-gold flames spilled out of his mouth with every syllable and scorched the surroundings, his Weight and Immensity still acclimating to the massive influx of harvested essence as he replied with casual dismissiveness.","\" Such a question could have so many answers, big guy .\" The flames around him danced with amusement that matched his tone. \" But what is this? Are you feeling talkative? I thought we would fight first, establish a baseline, and have a talk after. Preferably as your Way is collapsing.\"","...!","They began to converse, but it occurred so rapidly that not even a nanosecond had passed or would pass for them anytime soon, their exchange happening in the spaces between moments where lesser beings could not perceive or participate.","And Noah affirmed the effects of the Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem that had dimmed in his existence, running calculations through his mind as he assessed that the Depth reduction would last at least a few minutes conservatively and up to an hour or more moderately!","So he looked upon this Legend with eyes that burned with blue-gold fire, and as he watched, their body became more clear, more defined, more intentional in its presentation.","The amalgamation of spirits that had composed THE Living Spirit’s previous form consolidated into a humanoid muscular entity that stood imposing against the backdrop of Muspelheim’s eternal flames. His skin was gray and white, shifting between the two colors in patterns that seemed to follow rules that had nothing to do with normal biology, and multiple shining gray eyes were scattered across different parts of his body, on his shoulders and his chest and his forearms, each one tracking Noah with independent awareness.","He looked alien and off-putting in ways that transcended simple aesthetics, a being that had emerged from concepts that predated the forms most entities wore, but despite this strangeness, he possessed his own sense of regality that could not be denied.","He looked at Noah closely, those countless gray eyes examining him up and down with scrutiny that missed nothing.","\" Your usage of ancient power. Your Declaration with The First Tongue .\" His voice was measured and analytical now, the tone of someone piecing together a puzzle that had just become far more interesting than expected. \" Are you the one who has claimed THE First Tongue? And still currently emerging? Still weak?\"","His eyes narrowed with understanding that was equal parts respect and predatory interest.","\" It is why you did what you did with my forces, but you had to rely on a Fragment of an Axiom to give yourself an edge?\"","...!","The words were heavy with implications as Noah’s eyes shone sharply.","He tilted his head and spoke with flames licking around his words.","\" Do those within THE Loom not communicate? Do you not know about me?\" His smile was sharp enough to cut. \" Or did THE Living Paradox keep information about me to his closest dogs, and you did not make the cut as one of the dogs who licks him the most? Because even THE Living Elemental seems closer to Paradox...\"","Noah’s words burned with brilliance that made the air itself recoil, each syllable a calculated strike at pride that had existed for eons beyond counting.","THE Living Spirit continued to look at him calmly, absorbing the insult without visible reaction, before his voice emerged imposing and ominous in ways that made the eternal flames of Muspelheim seem to dim.","\" Maybe information was withheld about you because of what you represent. \" His countless eyes gleamed with hunger that could not be disguised. \" THE Living Paradox would gain much for eating the one who claimed THE First Tongue. So would Elemental and many others. I wouldn’t blame them for not sharing such information.\"","He paused, and something that might have been a smile crossed his alien features.","\" Just like they wouldn’t blame me for the fact that I won’t be telling anyone about your appearance here. I would want you... all to myself.\"","His form seemed to grow more solid, more present, more real as he spoke his ambitions aloud.","\" After all, the benefits to usurping One Who Laid A Claim are many. Just look at THE Living Paradox and the heights he has reached.\" His eyes blazed with dreams that had suddenly become possibilities. \" Can you imagine it, Youngest Claimer? THE Living Spirit eating you and joining the ranks of THE Creature and THE Living Paradox? \"","BOOM!","His eyes shone with an ominous and terrifying light that spoke of hunger and ambition and the willingness to do whatever was necessary to achieve heights that had seemed impossible just moments before, and Noah’s visage frowned even as a devilish smile curved across his features.","The flames billowing around him became more controlled, more focused, more intentional as he responded to the threat with calm that bordered on arrogance.","\" Are you sure about that ?\" His voice carried the weight of someone who had heard such threats before and remained standing while those who made them had long since ceased to exist. \" It is ambitious. This can also play to my favor. You tell nobody about me here, and I get to potentially collapse THE great Living Spirit with nobody being the wiser.\"","He floated forward slightly, his flames reaching toward THE Living Spirit like eager servants.","\" Can you imagine that, O Weakest of THE Emerged Leaders?\"","...!","His words were heavy with mockery that cut deeper than any blade, but THE Living Spirit’s eyes smiled dangerously in response, countless gray orbs crinkling with amusement that spoke of someone who enjoyed the game even as the stakes rose to lethal heights.","\" Existence is all about risks .\" THE Living Spirit nodded with the gravity of someone who had gambled with his existence countless times and won. \"I assure you that I take you very seriously the moment I affirmed your identity. Anybody that has laid a claim is not a normal entity. I expect you to be slippery. I expect you to be hard.\"","His form pulsed with power that made the air around them both grow heavy.","\" But hey, such is existence.\"","His smile widened, revealing teeth that seemed to be made of compressed spirits screaming in silent agony.","\" And you didn’t think you were the only one who could play around with Fragments of Axioms, right? Even with my Depth slightly reduced, with enough power...\"","His voice dropped to something almost gentle, almost caring, almost horrifying in its false concern.","\" I worry for you, O Youngest Claimer. I truly, truly worry for your safety. Come, let me invite you to an endless slumber inside an Infinite Spiritual Depth. There, you can dream of The First Tongue while I will actualize it for you.\"","...!","Noah’s expression remained valiant and calm even as in the next moment, above THE Living Spirit, a terrifying singularity bloomed into existence with force that made reality itself groan in protest!","A gray scythe began to manifest from that singularity, its blade curved with the promise of endings that could not be avoided and its handle wrapped in chains of spiritual essence that writhed with tortured awareness. The weapon was massive and terrible, designed not for combat but for harvesting, for reaping, for claiming the existence of those unfortunate enough to stand before its edge.","And it manifested with the light of a Fragment of an Axiom!","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply as he recognized what he was seeing!","He had expected one of THE Living Existences to have tools up their sleeves as a Fragment of an Axiom was one such tool, but still, it seemed like things would not be made easy for him!","Because that Fragment blooming above THE Living Spirit shone with the splendor of a Paradoxical Axiom, the essence of contradiction itself woven into a weapon that could probably do things that defied normal understanding of what was possible!","But he remained calm.","Because at this moment, from below, two auras of Fundamental Depth neared his position with speed.","The Muspeli Giants.","The ones who had been holding back the weight of the previous Half-Step Absolute Depth THE Living Spirit before Noah’s Fragment had reduced him to peak Fundamental!"]},{"number":4729,"title":"Chapter 4729: Chapter 4728: All Things Live And Die II","paragraphs":["Muspeli Lifeforms were ancient beyond measure, their origins stretching back to the time of differentiation itself when The First Tongue was still settling into the patterns that would define it for eons to come.","They were akin to an idealized blueprint of The First Tongue during that primordial era, their very existence shaped by the linguistic foundations of reality in ways that made them uniquely sensitive to its nuances and fluctuations. They held just as much if not more connection and sensitivity to The First Tongue compared to Ginnu Lifeforms from Ginnungagap, their Phonemes resonating with frequencies that other entities could barely perceive let alone replicate.","Where Ginnu Lifeforms had developed in the depths of Ginnungagap, Muspeli Lifeforms had emerged in the eternal flames that burned before fire learned to consume, their forms shaped by heat that was less combustion and more pure expression of primordial energy.","And Muspelheim itself was unfathomably vast.","The realm stretched across distances that defied conventional measurement, gigaparsecs upon gigaparsecs of burning landscape that had existed since before differentiation separated the realms and would likely continue burning long after the current conflicts had faded into forgotten history. Obsidian plains gave way to crystallized mountains of magma, which gave way to rivers of molten gold, which gave way to forests of flame that grew and spread and consumed and regrew in cycles that had been repeating since time learned to flow forward.","The Muspeli Giants lived in scattered clusters all over this incomprehensible expanse, each cluster forming its own domain with its own traditions and its own interpretations of The First Tongue’s sacred teachings. They were not unified under a single ruler or governing body, but rather existed as a confederation of powers bound together by their shared heritage and their mutual commitment to preserving the linguistic foundations that had given them existence.","They had elected Protectors to stand over each domain cluster of Muspeli Lifeforms, beings of immense power who had proven themselves worthy of guardianship through trials that would have broken lesser entities. Surtra THE Esteemed Whisperer was one such Protector, her authority over her domain cluster absolute and her dedication to The First Tongue unwavering.","Some Protectors were similar to her in power, standing at THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty with Ways that had been refined over eons of careful cultivation. Others were even grander, having pushed beyond Fundamental into the rarefied heights of Half-Step Absolute where the gap between themselves and true Absolutes became measurable in ways that mattered.","But each one was astonishing in their own right!","They preserved and protected what they knew of The First Tongue, maintaining libraries of Phonemes and repositories of linguistic knowledge that had survived THE Fallout and all the chaos that came before it. They took care of this sacred place burning with the glorious allure of The First Tongue, ensuring that its flames never dimmed and its language never fell silent.","For eons, they had waited.","For eons, they had protected.","And now, the Bells of Muspelheim were ringing because The One Who Laid The Claim had finally appeared.","---","At this time, an unknown gigaparsecs away from the region where Noah was facing down THE Living Spirit, a very different scene was unfolding.","There was a region where the obsidian flames that characterized most of Muspelheim transformed into something else entirely, where the fire shifted from black-gold to brilliant neon that painted the landscape in colors that seemed to exist outside the normal spectrum. Neon flaming mountains rose toward skies that burned with the same impossible hues, their peaks wreathed in fire that was less heat and more pure concentrated essence of The First Tongue itself.","A massive floating continent burned with glory in the skies above this neon realm, its underside dripping with molten light that fell like luminescent rain toward the mountains below. This was a sanctuary!","And currently, an immense war was erupting across this peaceful place.","THE Civilizational Authority scattered all around as varying Depths of Absolute Sovereignty clashed with violence that reshaped the neon landscape with every exchange. Declarations bloomed and shattered. Principles collided and annihilated each other. Ways pressed against Ways in contests of will and weight that left permanent scars on reality itself.","The corpses of neon flaming Muspeli Lifeforms lay scattered across the burning mountains and floating platforms, their bodies still burning brightly with the flames that had defined their existence even though the very concept of existence had been destabilized within them to force their collapse. They had died defending their home, died protecting the knowledge they had preserved for eons, died fighting against invaders who sought to claim what did not belong to them!","But alongside their corpses lay the corpses of the invaders themselves.","The forces of THE Living Concept had paid dearly for every inch of ground they had claimed.","Hundreds of Pre-THE entities lay dead, their forms dissolving into conceptual fragments that scattered on winds that should not have existed. Dozens of THE Surface Depth Early Creatures and Living Concepts had fallen as well, their sophisticated Ways and carefully cultivated Principles proving insufficient against the ferocity of Muspeli Lifeforms defending their sacred ground.","The dead of both sides numbered in the thousands.","But above, the war continued to be waged with intensity that made everything below seem like mere skirmishes.","Intermediate Depth entities clashed in formations that wheeled and struck and retreated and struck again, their Declarations creating zones of altered reality filled with Impositions that overlapped and contradicted each other in ways that made navigation impossible for lesser beings.","Fundamental Depth entities engaged in duels that reshaped the geography of the floating continent itself, their exchanges measured not in seconds but in femtoseconds, their power sufficient to annihilate everything around them if not carefully contained, multiple Declarations burning!","And at the very top of this hierarchy of violence, two titans faced each other with power that dwarfed everything else on the battlefield.","THE Living Concept hung in the burning neon sky like a nightmare given form and purpose, his body composed of countless concepts compressed into a singular presence that defied easy comprehension. He was tall beyond tallness, his form shifting between states of meaning as different concepts rose to prominence and faded away. One moment he seemed to embody destruction, his limbs wreathed in the idea of ending. The next he embodied inevitability, his presence suggesting that all resistance was futile. The next he embodied hunger, and everything around him seemed to lean toward his form as if drawn by conceptual gravity.","He burned with the glorious allure of Half-Step Absolute Depth, his authority pressing down upon the battlefield with weight that made reality itself groan in protest.","THE Living Concept, another living Legend...was also in Muspelheim!"]},{"number":4730,"title":"Chapter 4730: Chapter 4729: All Things Live And Die III","paragraphs":["And facing THE Living Concept was a Half-Step Absolute Depth Muspeli Lifeform whose entire body blazed with neon flames that seemed to burn hotter than the sun folds and brighter than any star folds.","This Protector stood as tall as THE Living Concept, his form humanoid but clearly inhuman, muscles wrapped in fire. His eyes were wells of neon light that contained depths suggesting intelligence and power accumulated over eons beyond counting. His voice, when he spoke, carried Phonemes that made the air itself restructure around his words.","Four Fundamental Depth Muspeli Lifeforms fought alongside him, their forms varied and magnificent, each one a testament to the diversity that existed within their kind.","They pressed against three Fundamental Depth Early Creatures who served THE Living Concept, and despite being outnumbered, The Early Creatures were clearly on the losing side as the Muspeli Lifeforms fought with coordination born of shared heritage and rejuvenated purpose.","Because they could hear the Bells of Muspelheim ringing from afar.","The sound had reached even here, even this distant corner of the primordial realm. They knew what those bells meant!","And they would not let invaders distract them from this moment of destiny!","Among the Fundamental Depth Muspeli Lifeforms fighting in the chaos below the clash of titans, one was particularly unique in appearance.","He was small, standing perhaps a fourth of normal human height, his diminutive stature a stark contrast to the giants that characterized most of his kind. But what he lacked in size he made up for in presence, his form burning with neon flames that seemed disproportionately intense for his tiny body.","He was furry and humanoid, a mammalian biped whose features resembled something close to hamster, with large expressive ears that twitched with every shift in the battlefield’s dynamics and whiskers that seemed to sense the flow of Mana itself.","His fur was golden beneath the neon flames that wreathed him, and his eyes sparkled with intelligence and curiosity that seemed almost childlike despite the ancient power that lurked behind them.","His name was Galileo , and despite his appearance, he was one of the most respected Fundamental Depth entities in this entire domain cluster!","Near him, fighting with coordinated ferocity that spoke of long partnership, was what looked to be a dog.","But this was no ordinary canine.","The Dog stood twice Galileo’s height, which still made him small compared to most combatants on this battlefield, but his presence more than compensated for his physical stature. He resembled a golden retriever of the most idealized variety, his fur gleaming with health and vitality even as neon flames danced across his coat. His build was muscular beneath that gorgeous fur.","His eyes burned with neon light that held depths of intelligence and loyalty, and when he moved, he moved with grace that made other Fundamental Depth entities seem clumsy by comparison.","The Dog pulsed with THE Intermediate Depth power, his Way somehow perfectly complementing his master’s despite the apparent disparity in their Depths.","Together, they had just finished dispatching an Early Creature that had made the mistake of thinking Galileo’s size meant weakness, its conceptual form dissolving into fragments that scattered across the neon-lit battlefield.","At this time, a voice echoed out directly into Galileo’s consciousness, bypassing the chaos of battle to deliver its message with perfect clarity.","| Galileo, follow the Bells of Muspelheim and ensure the safety of The One Who Laid The Claim.|","The voice belonged to the Half-Step Absolute Depth Muspeli Lifeform fighting above, the Protector of this sanctuary whose power had kept THE Living Concept at bay despite the invader’s own Half-Step authority.","| They are not strong like THE Creature or Chaos. THE Creature had The Alfs of Alfheimr backing him when he rose to power. Chaos had Jotunheim. We have to do our job.|","| Expend as much power as you can to ensure we can perform our role. I will take care of things here.|","...!","Galileo heard the voice and felt his small face buzz with ferocity that made his whiskers stand on end and his ears flatten against his skull.","He nodded once, a sharp motion that carried finality.","Then he reached out with one tiny hand and patted the flank of the Dog that stood twice his size, his fingers finding the familiar warmth of the Dog’s fur beneath the neon flames that danced across it.","\" Let’s go, Duke.\"","His voice was surprisingly deep for his small frame, carrying waves that spoke of Phonemes mastered over eons of careful study.","Duke barked in response, a sound that was less animal vocalization and more declaration of intent, and waves of extremely pure Mana erupted from his golden form with intensity that made nearby combatants stumble and stare.","The bark carried joy and eagerness and absolute loyalty!","And at speeds that made even THE Living Concept glance over from his battle with the Protector, his countless conceptual eyes tracking something that had just moved faster than anything at Intermediate Depth should have been capable of moving...","WAP!","Duke and Galileo disappeared.","Not even a glimmer of their light could be seen as they vanished from the battlefield, their trajectory carrying them toward the distant region where the Bells of Muspelheim originated!","THE Living Concept’s eyes narrowed, but before he could respond, the Protector pressed his attack with renewed ferocity, demanding his full attention and preventing any pursuit!","---","Strength!","Strength came in different forms.","This was a truth that many entities failed to understand, too focused on personal power to recognize the broader weavings of force that wove through existence. They measured strength in Depth and immensity, in the weight of one’s Way and the authority of one’s Declarations, and they dismissed anything that did not fit neatly into these categories as irrelevant.","But strength was more complex than simple personal cultivation.","Sometimes, inheritance of forces aligned with one’s Way was also a form of strength, a form of power that could not be measured by examining an individual in isolation.","THE Creature had not risen to prominence alone. Others had backed him during his ascent.","THE Primordial Chaos had benefited similarly from another place- Jotunheim, the realm of Chaos Giants providing him with backing that transformed personal potential into actualized power.","Even THE Living Paradox, for all his individual might, had drawn upon forces beyond himself.","No entity reached the peak alone.","No entity could.","Existence was too vast, too dangerous, too filled with those who would destroy rising powers before they could threaten established hierarchies. Personal strength was necessary but insufficient. What separated those who achieved the heights from those who fell along the way was often not individual capability but the web of support and alliance and inherited force that surrounded them!"]},{"number":4731,"title":"Chapter 4731: Chapter 4730: All Things Live And Die IV","paragraphs":["In the region burning with obsidian flames, the tension had reached a breaking point where the next moments would determine everything.","Noah did not look back to THE Fundamental Depth Muspeli Lifeforms behind him as they sent him unique waves of Mana to communicate, their messages carried on frequencies that only those attuned to The First Tongue could perceive and understand.","The strongest one here was Surtra, THE Esteemed Whisperer.","| The Muspeli Lifeforms are here to stand beside The One Who Laid The Claim.|","Her voice resonated through the Mana itself, warm and fierce and absolutely certain.","|You have the backing of our Ways as we follow The First Tongue. We realize this is a bit abrupt and would have ideally enjoyed things playing out differently, with proper introductions and ceremonies befitting such a momentous occasion, but existence is never so simple. The enemy is here and so are we. We are here for you to command.|","...!","The foremost Muspeli Lifeform who had been keeping THE Living Spirit at bay while Noah harvested the forces below spoke such words with the calm certainty of someone who had waited eons for exactly this moment!","Noah smiled, his gaze still locked on the enemy above whose countless gray eyes watched this development with cold calculation.","|Two Fundamental Depth Muspeli Lifeforms have officially backed The First Tongue and aligned their Ways with yours.|","|Boundless Infinite Potential is being harvested from this alliance. Their accumulated authority, their eons of dedication to The First Tongue, their willingness to stand beside you in battle against a Half-Step Absolute entity, all of it flows into your foundation as recognition of what it means to have laid claim to The First Tongue.|","...!","Noah glanced at this prompt sharply and nodded with appreciation that he didn’t have time to properly express, acknowledging the weight of what these Muspeli Lifeforms were offering him even as his mind remained focused on the threat that loomed above with a Fragment of a Paradoxical Axiom manifesting in his grasp.","He didn’t have time to get to know these powerful Muspeli Lifeforms behind him, didn’t have time to learn their histories or understand their Ways.","But there could be time for introductions later.","They just needed to survive an encounter with a ridiculously powerful enemy first!","And to do so...","\" We shall have others join us as well.\"","HUUUUM!","He said these words calmly as from afar, the radiant blue-gold Monolith that served as the gateway between Muspelheim and his domain shone with brilliance!","From it, the figure of THE Infiniverse herself appeared in humanoid form, her manifestation carrying the weight of an entire realm compressed into a singular presence that demanded acknowledgment from reality itsel!","She was adorned in bejeweled multicolored battle wrappings that seemed woven from the fabric of countless absorbed territories, gems of every hue imaginable studding armor that shifted between states of matter as if unable to decide what it wanted to be. Her features were sharp and imperious, and her gaze as she stared toward THE Living Spirit was cold enough to make the obsidian flames around her seem warm by comparison.","Behind her, multiple THE entities emerged from the Monolith.","Khor came first, her small form burning with the hunger.","Sigrid followed, alongside Ra’Zan who emerged with his bony skull staff clutched in skeletal fingers. Phonemes danced around his decrepit form, weaving patterns that spoke of endings that could not be avoided and decay that could not be stopped!","Riya, Titano, The First Farmer, Henry, Malphas, and Moiraine followed in succession, each of them burning with a light of a Depth that had been elevated and enhanced by their connection to Noah’s Way!","The First Tongue surrounded them all.","Noah glanced at them from afar as they spread out across the burning skies of Muspelheim.","\" Stay on the periphery and impose your Way from a distance.\"","His voice carried across the battlefield with authority that brooked no argument, the command of someone who understood both the capabilities and limitations of his forces.","\" The enemy this time is a powerful fucker, and direct engagement will get you killed. Fight! Fight! FIGHT!\"","BOOM!","He said such words as his people, surrounded by the light of his Mana, listened to him and spread out across the obsidian-flamed landscape like pieces on a board being positioned for a decisive gambit.","All but one.","THE Infiniverse did not retreat to the periphery.","Her Depth was unique, holding the weight and immensity of the entirety of the changing and transforming Infiniverse which was even now swallowing Muspelheim and converting it into part of her ever-expanding domain.","She was not a normal entity whose Depth could be measured against conventional standards. She was a realm given consciousness, a civilization become singular, and her power scaled with everything she had consumed and continued to consume.","Similar to Noah, her Depth could not be categorized by normal means.","And shockingly, she raised her legs as if they were hammers meant for breaking Primordial Realms and began shooting toward THE Living Spirit as if she were a nuclear bomb aimed at a target that had dared to threaten her Master!","...!","Noah saw this as he smiled wryly at her initiative.","Behind him, Surtra erupted with sandy flames that carried the weight of Fundamental Depth authority.","The other Fundamental Depth Muspeli Lifeform beside her closed their eyes in concentration as Logos and Philologies of The First Tongue wrapped around their existence with density that made the air shimmer, and these linguistic constructs formed into drops of flaming rain that shot out with glorious fervor toward THE Living Spirit in an assault that combined the physical and the conceptual into something that was more than either alone!","Meanwhile, from the periphery where Noah had commanded them to remain, his forces added their authority to the assault.","Khor unleashed decillions of jaws of hunger surrounded by Phonemes of The First Tongue, each maw carrying the weight of her Way as they surged toward THE Living Spirit in a tide of devouring intent.","Ra’Zan grasped his bony skull staff and instantly caused a storm of rotating bones and poison filled with THE Civilizational Authority of Mana to swirl above THE Living Spirit, creating a dome of death that pressed down from above while the other attacks came from all sides.","Beside the embattled legend, Gal’Thûrak was scared shitless.","The demon spirit who had called himself THE Terror of Chains now cowered in the shadow of his master as attacks from every direction converged on their position. His seven eyes darted frantically, his chains rattling with fear rather than eager violence, his entire existence screaming that he should flee even as loyalty or perhaps simple terror kept him rooted in place.","Noah looked at this gloriously unfolding scene as he rose to face THE Living Spirit directly, his blue-gold flames billowing around him with intensity.","THE Living Spirit stood calm amidst the approaching storm. In his hand, he grasped the half-manifested Scythe that burned with the light of a Fragment of a Paradoxical Axiom.","Noah met those countless eyes with his own blazing gaze, and his voice emerged calm and measured despite the chaos of battle erupting around them.","\"I want to give you the respect of an entity of your standing, the proper acknowledgment of someone who has stood at the heights of existence since before THE Fallout reshaped everything we knew.\"","His flames burned brighter as he moved.","\" But I don’t want a long drawn-out battle just because you are THE Living Spirit. I have things to do and places to be and an existence to reshape according to my will.\"","BOOM!","He smiled with the calm confidence of someone who had already decided how this would end.","\" Let’s settle this in the next few seconds, okay?\"","...!","His words were heavy, the declaration of someone telling a legend that their legend would end quickly rather than with the epic struggle such beings usually demanded!","THE Living Spirit erupted with ominous power in the next moment, his form solidifying further as he prepared to meet the combined assault.","The Scythe in his hand blazed with Paradoxical light that made reality itself uncertain about what was possible and what was not.","\" Oh, it will be settled.\"","His voice emerged from countless mouths simultaneously, a chorus of spirits all speaking the same words with the same deadly certainty.","\"It will be settled.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4732,"title":"Chapter 4732: Chapter 4731: All Things Live and Die V","paragraphs":["Okay.","So, fighting against an entity like THE Living Spirit was not an easy task.","His power was already constrained in ways that should have made this battle decisively one-sided. From Noah’s established Thesis, he had no access to The First Tongue as his Genesis Principles were closed off from the linguistic foundations that powered them.","His regeneration of authority was locked out, unable to draw upon the ambient Mana that should have been replenishing his reserves with every passing moment. His connection to the very language of reality had been severed, leaving him fighting with reserves that depleted without refilling.","His power was also no longer Absolute as he stood only at THE Fundamental Depth now, dragged down from the Half-Step heights he had occupied before the Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem had done its work. He faced two Fundamental Depth Muspeli Lifeforms whose Ways burned with the authority of beings who had protected The First Tongue since before THE Fallout.","He faced Noah, whose Formless Depth defied conventional measurement and whose flames billowed with intensity that matched the eternal fires of Muspelheim itself. He faced THE Infiniverse, whose weight carried the accumulated mass of an ever-expanding realm that was even now devouring the very territory they fought upon!","And he faced multiple other THE entities from THE Infiniverse, each one adding their authority to the assault from the periphery in an unrelenting storm of Assertions and Impositions.","And yet...","More than ten seconds passed as this being actually did not fall!","10 Seconds!","Noah looked at him with an imperious gaze that seemed to ask one simple question: how fucking dare he?!","Ten seconds might have seemed like nothing to lesser beings, but in a battle between entities of this caliber, ten seconds was an eternity. They moved in femtoseconds, thought in attoseconds, and exchanged blows at speeds that would have appeared as frozen stillness to anyone observing from outside.","Ten seconds meant ten quadrillion femtoseconds of continuous combat , ten quadrillion moments where attacks landed and Declarations clashed and Ways pressed against Ways in contests of absolute authority.","And THE Living Spirit endured it all.","The reason for his unbeatable stance and stature right now was of course his Depth, even reduced as it was, and his Way of Spirit that had been refined over eons beyond counting. But more than either of those, it was the Fragment of an Axiom he wielded that kept him standing when he should have fallen long ago.","The Scythe.","It hung in his grasp like an extension of his will, its blade curved with promises of endings that transcended normal death and its handle wrapped in chains of spiritual essence that writhed with tortured awareness. The power of THE Living Spirit wrapped around it heavily, merging weapon and wielder into something that was more than either alone.","Even Lens of Civilization didn’t reveal his status sheet nor the identity of the Fragment he carried, the Axiom from which it had been taken remaining a mystery.","But the effects were clear enough.","THE Living Spirit would wave this Scythe, and any Assertions made by Khor or Ra’Zan or the others from the periphery would simply be nullified as if they had never been spoken. The jaws of hunger that should have devoured his defenses dissolved into nothing. The storms of bone and poison that should have corroded his Way scattered like mist before morning sun.","The weight of their combined authority, which should have pressed him down into submission, slid off his existence like water off stone.","THE Infiniverse, who swung her legs like imperial primordial hammers with force that could have shattered lesser realms, was pushed back with every exchange. Her weight drained with every strike she landed, the Scythe somehow siphoning the very immensity she brought to bear and turning her own power against her.","And as Noah formed a new Thesis, speaking it into existence with authority that only someone who had claimed The First Tongue could muster, it smashed onto THE Living Spirit with impact that would have smashed any normal Fundamental Depth entity. The Thesis hung around him like chains of linguistic law, his heavy Depth pressing like an unrelenting hammer that sought to crush him into submission!","But THE Living Spirit stood strong.","He made grand Declarations of his own, his countless mouths speaking words of power.","Some of those Declarations targeted the forces on the periphery, seeking to one-shot kill Sigrid or Ra’Zan or any of the others whose Depths were insufficient to withstand direct attention from someone of his caliber.","But Surtra and the other Fundamental Depth Muspeli Lifeform brought down their own terrifying immensity in response, their Ways interposing between THE Living Spirit’s Declarations and their intended targets with the practiced coordination of beings who had fought together for eons.","Surtra had held back THE Living Spirit even when he was at Half-Step Absolute Depth with her unique Way, her sandy flames somehow capable of diffusing and redirecting authority that should have overwhelmed her. She was not stronger than him, had never been stronger than him, but her Way was perfectly suited to defense and delay in ways that made raw power comparisons irrelevant.","Nothing passed past them.","And all that was left was a glorious scene with Noah and THE Infiniverse surrounding THE Living Spirit with their Depth and immensity, gradually wearing him down as one singular factor revealed itself at this moment that would become a defining feature many would come to realize in the very near future.","As THE Living Spirit took on all these attacks, all these Depths, Noah’s random Thesis constructs and THE Infiniverse throwing her weight around like a fat primordial realm seeking to crush an insect beneath her mass, he was actually waiting for something.","He was waiting for a gap in their attacks.","He was waiting for...exhaustion to hit them.","Because they were not only throwing their Depths at him with reckless abandon, but his Fragment of an Axiom was actively nullifying and even draining them of their Weight with every exchange. The Scythe was designed for exactly this purpose, to turn extended battles into wars of attrition where his opponents expended themselves against his defenses while he conserved and even grew stronger from their efforts.","It was a strategy that had worked countless times before.","It was a strategy that should have been working now.","Yet...","It didn’t seem to be doing anything?","They didn’t look any more exhausted now than they had ten seconds ago. Their attacks came with the same ferocity, the same weight, the same relentless pressure that had characterized the opening moments of this battle. In these ten seconds, they had all attacked and moved in femtoseconds, exchanging quadrillions of blows and Declarations and Assertions without any visible sign of depletion.","They had been attacking for a relatively long fucking time.","They had been asserting, imposing, and declaring their Ways again and again against his Spirit, hammering at his defenses with authority that should have been diminishing with every exchange but somehow remained constant.","As if they held an infinite backing behind them.","\" Ah...\"","At this point, the eyes of THE Living Spirit lit up with understanding that had been slow to come but arrived with the force of revelation.","His countless gray eyes blinked as he seemed to see something others couldn’t, his perception shifting to frequencies that revealed truths hidden from normal observation.","He thought he saw faint blue-gold lines extending from THE Youngest Claimer and onto all his people here, threads of connection that pulsed with Mana flowing in only one direction. They reached all the others, and through those lines, their Depths were being replenished endlessly.","Infinitely.","\"Ah...\"","THE Living Spirit felt like he finally understood what he was facing.","Every one of those behind The Oldest Paradox of Existence had something that made them unique, some quality or capability that set them apart from other entities at similar Depths. THE Creature had his connection to existence itself. THE Living Paradox had his mastery of contradiction. THE Primordial Chaos had his inevitability of entropy.","Was this the perk behind THE Youngest Claimer?","Infinity?","The ability to provide endless resources to those connected to his Way, to replenish their Depths faster than any enemy could drain them, to turn every battle of attrition into a guaranteed loss for whoever stood against him?","It would explain how he had been able to make the claim over The First Tongue, how someone of his apparent youth and relatively modest personal power had accomplished something that no entity in all of existence had ever achieved!","THE Living Spirit came to this realization with the calm acceptance of someone who had lived long enough to recognize when circumstances had shifted against him irreversibly.","When he felt his own Way that continued to deplete, when he noticed his weight and immensity not refilling because he remained locked out from The First Tongue by the established Thesis, he understood with perfect clarity that this battle was... lost.","There was no path to victory here.","No strategy that would allow him to outlast opponents who could not be outlasted.","No technique that would let him overcome enemies who simply did not run out of resources.","But he was still calm.","After all, this was just his other Half-Step Absolute Depth Spirit Body.","In Spirit Shelter of THE Loom, another remained! His true existence, or at least a more complete version of it, waited in safety beyond the reach of THE Youngest Claimer and his infinite backing. Even if this body collapsed here, even if this portion of his existence was destroyed and harvested, he would continue.","It would be a worthy collapse, he supposed, falling under one of Those Four. One of those who had laid their claims on aspects of The Oldest Paradox of Existence. There was no shame in being defeated by such an entity, no diminishment of his legend in losing to someone who represented a fundamental truth of reality itself.","It was oka-","BOOM!","In the midst of his thoughts, in the moment where acceptance had begun to settle into resignation, the Scythe in his hands was knocked to the side from the hammer legs of THE Infiniverse!","Her strike came with the force of a realm compressed into a single blow, and even his grip, which had held that weapon through countless battles across eons of existence, could not maintain its hold against such overwhelming impact.","The Scythe spun away from his grasp.","And in front of him...","BOOM!","The vibrating body of THE Youngest Claimer squeezed into the gap that THE Infiniverse’s strike had created!","One of Noah’s hands came to clamp down on his hand that had been holding the Scythe, fingers burning with blue-gold flames that seared into spiritual essence with heat that transcended normal fire.","And his other hand grasped onto his massive gray neck with grip that spoke of finality!","Noah held onto THE Living Spirit as he smiled with a devilish light. His eyes burned with immense Depth that defied categorization, with the weight of someone who had laid claim to something that belonged to the very foundations of existence.","\" In existence, all things live and die, O Spirit.\"","His voice emerged calm and measured, almost gentle, the tone of someone explaining an obvious truth to a child who had somehow failed to understand it.","\"It is time for you to die.\"","...!","A Legend gazed at an anomaly calmly even amidst such an unprecedented moment, those countless gray eyes meeting blazing blue-gold without fear or desperation. He had lived for eons beyond counting. He had survived THE Fallout and the chaos that came before it. He had stood at heights that most entities could not even comprehend.","And now he faced his ending at the hands of THE Youngest Claimer.","The anomaly gazed back, his mouth and nose releasing lava-like blue-gold flames with every breath, fire that was less combustion and more pure expression of authority made manifest. These flames began to dance over the grayish skin of THE Living Spirit, spreading across his form like eager servants consuming a feast that had been long denied to them.","Where the flames touched, spiritual essence began to dissolve.","Where the flames spread, the accumulated authority of eons began to break down.","Where the flames burned, a Legend began to end.","And Noah held on with grip that would not release, his smile never wavering as he brought an end to a glorious battle that had lasted ten seconds and ten quadrillion femtoseconds and would be remembered for far longer than either!"]},{"number":4733,"title":"Chapter 4733: Chapter 4732: Harvests! I","paragraphs":["A magnum opus was said to be the greatest work of an artist or craftsman, the singular achievement that defined their existence and stood as testament to everything they had learned and become.","But this was a limited view.","A magnum opus did not have to be singular. It did not have to be final. The greatest work was not necessarily the last work, nor was it the work that others deemed most impressive by their own limited standards of measurement.","Sometimes, a magnum opus was simply the work that felt right in the moment of its creation, the achievement that resonated with the deepest parts of one’s being and announced to existence itself that yes, this was what they were capable of, and no, they were not yet finished becoming more.","Noah had many moments of glorious defining achievements scattered across his journey from a tiny blue planet to the primordial depths of existence itself, but at this time, holding the neck of THE Living Spirit, an entity who he had only ever heard of in the Stories of The Earliest Folds...","This was a moment!","Blue-gold flames billowed over his body and washed over the grayish form of THE Living Spirit with hunger that could not be denied, and as he looked at the many cold eyes of this being who gazed at him calmly even as his existence began to break down, Noah sneered in distaste.","\" What a shame. This turns out not to be your main body?\"","His grip tightened, flames intensifying.","\" What a fucking shame...\"","BOOM!","Yes.","The moment he had gotten his hands on THE Living Spirit, he had sought to give him a speedy entry into THE Infinite Desmoterion, to add a Half-Step Absolute Depth legend to his growing collection of imprisoned powers.","But the prompt that rose shattered that ambition.","|Imprisonment Failure|","|The selected target for THE Infinite Desmoterion is only partially defeated. This manifestation represents a Spirit Body rather than a complete existence.|","|The complete Depth of their Existence still remains untouched in another location. Full subjugation of their core existence is required for imprisonment.|","| Until that core is captured and defeated, entry into THE Infinite Desmoterion is not possible.|","...!","He couldn’t draw this fucker into his prison as the main component that made up their existence was not here, was sitting safely in some Spirit Shelter within THE Loom while this expendable body fought and died in his place.","It would have been a glorious thing to have a Half-Step Absolute Depth entity in his prison, a legend whose authority he could draw upon and whose knowledge he could extract over eons of careful interrogation!","If he was ambitious enough, he could make it his goal to find Spirit, Elemental, Concept, and others to lock them all in his prison, building a collection of THE Living Existences that would make even THE Creature pause!","But if this wasn’t viable...","\" The Civilization I am standing over collapses all it has to me.\"","BOOM!","The Thesis blazed into existence with authority that only someone who had claimed The First Tongue could muster, and the body of THE Living Spirit buzzed as cracks began to spread across its surface like fractures appearing in ancient stone.","And yet this being showed absolutely no emotion.","His many gray eyes focused on Noah with the calm acceptance of someone who had already made peace with this particular ending, countless gazes studying the entity who had accomplished what should have been impossible.","\"I now know what gives you an edge.\"","His voice emerged from multiple mouths simultaneously, unhurried despite the cracks spreading through his form.","\"I have many ways to go about things now. We will meet again sooner or later, so be sure to stay alive until then.\"","The cracks deepened, but still he spoke.","\" THE Creature and THE Living Paradox run rampant as they believe everything shall fall to them. Little guys like us also want a piece of the pie, you know? We also have ambitions.\"","His eyes gleamed with something that might have been camaraderie or might have been manipulation.","\" None of us truly back THE Creature or THE Living Paradox or even THE Primordial Chaos. All of us are ultimately seeking our own glory. Even those who follow you or back you... they are likely looking for their own glory. Don’t believe anyone is truly backing your Wa-\"","\" Get the fuck outta here, man.\"","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes flashed with tyranny as he interrupted THE Living Spirit’s attempt to sow discord with his dying breaths, refusing to let this legend have the final word even as his existence crumbled.","In the next moment, the Thesis Noah had declared blazed blue-gold with intensity.","The body of THE Living Spirit shuddered violently, cracks spreading through it like porcelain struck by hammers, and inside those fractures, unfathomable seas of white-gray light roared with the accumulated authority of eons being forcibly released!","Noah opened his mouth like a fiendish beast and devoured it all like a black hole consuming a dying star!","If he couldn’t imprison it, he would eat it.","Eating a Half-Step Absolute Depth THE Living Existence was also bound to be nutritious!","HUUUUM!","|Harvest of Legend!|","|Unfathomable effort has been put in by you and many others in facing a Half-Step Absolute Depth entity of glorious status. The coordination of Fundamental Depth Muspeli Lifeforms, THE Infiniverse, and your assembled forces created conditions where the impossible became merely improbable.|","|Infinite Potential is harvested and amplified under the Arche of Perpetual Harvest. All participants gain immensely from this victory.|","|The Weight of a Half-Step Absolute Depth THE Living Spirit is being harvested and devoured. An unfathomable harvest! An impossible harvest given your level!|","|And yet it occurred.|","|Your Claim over The First Tongue is further solidified through this victory. Your Way has become even clearer, the path forward illuminated by the authority you have consumed.|","|Alongside the elevation of your Weight and Immensity, there is more than enough harvest to accomplish your goals of streamlining your existence. The foundation you have been building can now support the transformations you have been planning.|","HUUUUM!"]},{"number":4734,"title":"Chapter 4734: Chapter 4733: Harvests! II","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4733: Harvests! II","These prompts rolled down as Noah’s figure burned with the glory of someone who had just consumed power that should have been beyond his reach!","His outline showed a muscular humanoid entity that looked like a celestial fiend given form and purpose, blue-gold flames billowing over his entire body as steam rose off of him with splendor.","His skin glinted like reinforced blue-gold crystal forged from the fires of The First Tongue itself, and his Foundation and Weight could be felt rising up gloriously as the harvest settled into his existence and became part of him!","Near him, THE Infiniverse burned with her own flames, her body wreathed in blue-gold fire made up of Phonemes of The First Tongue that danced across her bejeweled armor and made her seem less like a realm given consciousness and more like a fiend of expansion and consumption.","Khor floated nearby, her small form surrounded by radiant blue-gold flames of Mana and Hunger that elevated her Depth even as her abyssal eyes gleamed.","Sigrid, Ra’Zan, Riya, The First Farmer, and all others who had come to support him and fought against THE Living Spirit had radiant blue-gold flames surrounding them as their Depths elevated from the shared harvest of this impossible victory!","At such a time...","The massive blue-gold Monolith in the distance began to vibrate with intensity that drew attention from everyone present.","In the next moment, the environment of Muspelheim began to be pulled toward it even more rapidly, the obsidian flames and crystallized mountains and rivers of molten gold all flowing toward that gateway as if reality itself was being funneled through a drain!","Surtra, THE Esteemed Whisperer, looked toward this phenomenon with a frown that creased her ancient features, her sandy flames flickering with concern.","“Sir... what would the meaning of that Monolith be?”","She saw what it was doing, saw how it was consuming her home realm with accelerating hunger, and she had to ask even though part of her knew the answer.","Before Noah could even reply...","HUUUUM!","Neon-colored flames blazed from the distance with brilliance that cut through the obsidian fire of Muspelheim like a beacon of different power entirely!","Glorious auras bloomed soon after, and the figure of a radiant golden dog appeared with a unique small entity atop it, both of them moving with speed that defied their apparent Depths as they arrived before the assembled forces could even properly register their approach.","Galileo and Duke!","Duke’s golden fur gleamed with health and power even as neon flames danced across his coat, his muscular form radiating THE Intermediate Depth authority that seemed perfectly complementary to his rider.","Atop him sat Galileo, the small furry Muspeli Lifeform whose diminutive stature belied his Fundamental Depth power, his large ears twitching as he took in the aftermath of the battle and the impossible sight of THE Living Spirit’s essence still being absorbed into the blazing figure before him.","Their gazes settled on Noah.","In his glorious sensation of power and immensity, Noah had to blink at the new entrants just to make sure he was seeing right.","Was that a golden retriever Muspeli Lifeform and a fluffy humanoid hamster neon flaming Muspeli Lifeform?","The entities of existence seemed to truly have all sorts of forms as giants was not applicable to every single one of them, and these two proved that diversity extended even to the ancient guardians of The First Tongue.","They seemed to have arrived here as reinforcements, but they came rather late as the battle had already concluded in spectacular fashion. While the two sides gazed at each other across the burning skies of Muspelheim, the fluffy lifeform atop the dog spoke up first.","“I was sent here to ensure the safety of The One Who Laid The Claim, but my help does not seem to be required.”","His voice was surprisingly deep for his small frame, carrying waves that spoke of Phonemes mastered over eons.","“Surtra.”","He nodded toward the sandy-flamed Muspeli Lifeform who looked forward and nodded back with respect that spoke of long familiarity between them, as if these two had known each other for eons and trusted each other implicitly.","Galileo and Duke floated ever closer, the golden dog’s tail wagging with barely contained excitement as they came to hover a distance before Noah’s blazing form.","Galileo looked at Noah up and down with large eyes that sparkled with ancient intelligence, his whiskers twitching as he assessed the entity who had just devoured a legend.","“You’re a bit different than what I envisioned...a bit smaller, but I sense The First Tongue listening to you more than me in this region.”","His ears flicked forward with curiosity.","“I am Galileo, and I have been raising the Noble Mount of The One Who Laid The Claim. This here is Duke, a glorious product of The First Tongue! He is faster than any Fundamental Depth entity, his speed almost approaching Absolutes...”","He patted Duke’s golden fur with obvious pride.","“What does The One Who Laid The Claim call himself? And what might that ominous Monolith devouring everything about Muspelheim be?”","Galileo asked such questions calmly as Noah smiled at these new entrants while looking at the dog named Duke who had his tongue out, gazing at him with eyes of pure excitement as if he had been waiting his entire existence to meet this moment.","A Muspeli Lifeform whose speed approached Absolutes?","This in itself was a work of wonder!","But before addressing any of this, Noah completely devoured every glimmer of traces remaining of THE Living Spirit.","Then he floated toward a corner of the skies where an entity was trying to make themselves as small as possible.","Gal’Thûrak.","Uniquely, this was actually the last surviving member of the legion of THE Living Spirit, having survived when no others did through a combination of his master’s protection and his own desperate cowardice.","Noah went toward this being, his blazing form casting blue-gold light across the terrified demon spirit whose seven eyes darted frantically for any escape route that didn’t exist.","This Fundamental Depth entity with his lowered Depth, who had already kneeled to Noah and could express not even ten percent of his power, trembled as the flames approached.","Noah waved his hand toward the fearful Gal’Thûrak with casual authority.","A light flashed.","The entity disappeared.","There wasn’t even resistance or anything to worry about as THE Terror of Chains began to be processed in the prison inside of THE Organ of Civilization, his existence now fuel for Noah’s growing power rather than a threat to be concerned about.","As Noah did this, he replied to Galileo.","“I am THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons. Genesis Monarch is fine.”","WAA!"]},{"number":4735,"title":"Chapter 4735: Chapter 4734: Harvests! III","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4734: Harvests! III","His voice carried the weight of someone announcing a title that existence itself had acknowledged!","“And that Monolith is the gateway through which Muspelheim is moving as I take it into a domain where beings like the one I just killed will not be capable of entering.”","...!","As he said all of this, he was already moving and waving his hands as he beckoned toward the Fragment of an Axiom that THE Living Spirit had been using to fight them, the Scythe that had nullified so many of their attacks now lying abandoned in the burning skies.","He also looked toward the Fragment that radiated the light of another Axiom in the center of the ancient citadel that Surtra had been protecting, the original treasure that had drawn THE Living Spirit here in the first place.","There were many potential spoils in the wake of this battle, and a lot more things to get done.","After his words, Surtra and Galileo looked at each other silently as if communicating through means that required no words, and Noah calmly continued.","“Who is The One Who Laid The Claim on The First Tongue to Muspeli Lifeforms?”","He asked such a simple question, seeking to understand exactly what his new title meant to these ancient guardians.","Surtra and Galileo looked at each other before they answered at the same time.","“The leader of Muspelheim.”","Noah nodded at these words as finally, it seemed time to collect the benefits of laying claim to The First Tongue.","He turned to them with eyes blazing with purpose.","“Then trust in me and my words. There is much to be done and there is little time for everything. Are there any other invaders in other regions of Muspelheim?”","At such a question, Galileo nodded with gravity that made his small form seem larger.","“Someone calling themselves THE Living Concept. The battle against him is still ongoing.”","...!","Noah’s eyes shone brightly at this revelation.","Concept was also here? How...powerful was he compared to Spirit?","There were many questions buzzing through his mind, but for now, it was time to quantify the boons from everything that had occurred!","Noah nodded to the words of Galileo.","“Then I’ll be quick with what I am currently doing. Give me a second.”","He turned to the sandy-flamed guardian.","“Surtra, can you secure that Fragment of an Axiom down there?”","He spoke casually as if he was a landlord that had inherited Muspelheim and was now claiming everything for himself, but Surtra nodded simply at his words before she descended to collect the Fragment.","What was the reason they had been protecting it this whole time?","They were waiting for him!","As she did this, Noah smiled and closed his eyes, his whole body continuing to billow with flames as he listened to the many prompts buzzing before him!","|THE Infinite Desmoterion – Status Report|","|A new prisoner has been processed and integrated into your Prison of Way of Existence.|","|Prisoner: Gal’Thûrak, formerly known as THE Terror of Chains|","|Original Depth: THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Current Depth: THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty (reduction of Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem effect now wiped out by you)|","|Status: Imprisoned. His Way is now fuel for your Civilization.|","|THE Infinite Desmoterion Integration Benefits:|","|By imprisoning a THE Fundamental Depth entity, even one currently reduced to Intermediate Depth, your prison’s authority has expanded significantly.|","|Passive Authority Generation: Your prison can pull upon the authority equivalent to 25% of Gal’Thûrak’s peak output continuously. This authority flows directly into your Foundation and weight. His entrance has opened the pathway for 25% of the Weight of all others imprisoned, with the exception of THE Warden, Ozymandias, to be freely flowing into your Foundation And Depth.|","|Knowledge Extraction: Memories and techniques accumulated over eons of existence are being catalogued. Gal’Thûrak will be asked to share everything they know regarding THE Loom and other matters. Well, not asked as much as commanded.|","|Your first Fundamental Depth prisoner. THE Warden, Ozymandias, will meet with him soon.|","...!","|Foundation Status Report|","|Your Weight and Immensity have attained a Perfect Foundation.|","|Through the harvest of THE Living Spirit’s Half-Step Absolute Depth existence, the imprisonment of a Fundamental Depth entity, and the accumulated gains from collapsing dozens of Civilizations, your foundation has reached a critical threshold.|","|Comparative Depth Assessment:|","|Your Immensity now equals the full 100% Immensity of entities like THE Creature or THE Living Paradox when they were at THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.|","|Previous Comparative Weight: 70/100th|","|Current Comparative Weight: 100/100th|","|Significance: You have matched the foundation that the greatest entities in existence possessed at your comparative stage. THE Creature at Intermediate Depth. THE Living Paradox at Intermediate Depth. THE Primordial Chaos at Intermediate Depth. You now stand where they once stood.|","|Your Formless Depth continues to defy conventional categorization, but in terms of raw weight and immensity, you have achieved what few entities in all of existence have ever achieved at this stage of development.|","|While yes, Your Way does not care for comparisons, it is also ideal to see where you are objectively. The gap between you and the peaks is still vast, but you’re now climbing the same mountain they climbed. Just... faster. Much, much faster.|","...!","|Fragment Acquisition Report|","|The Fragment wielded by THE Living Spirit has been secured.|","|Fragment Identified: Fragment of THE Axiom of Attrition|","|Axiom Classification: One of the Paradoxical Axioms, representing the concept that all things diminish through conflict while the patient observer grows stronger.|","|Fragment Capability: Nullification and Drainage|","|This Fragment allows the wielder to nullify 75% of incoming attacks, regardless of Depth, by draining their weight and adding a percentage of it to their own reserves. Extended combat becomes increasingly favorable as opponents expend themselves while the wielder accumulates their spent authority.|","|Usage Requirements: Significant immensity required for activation. Most effective when wielder can sustain prolonged engagement.|","|THE Living Spirit wss nullifying and draining, but as he was draining the authority of THE First Tongue, which he could not use or access...he got fucking nothing out of it.|","...!","HUUUUM!","The prompts were many and they were grand, but Noah looked at all of them as he took in the weight of his achievements!","A Perfect Foundation matching the legends...but he wasn’t even content with it! Why match anyone when he could exceed them?!"]},{"number":4736,"title":"Chapter 4736: Chapter 4735: Harvests! IV","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4735: Harvests! IV","He could match the foundation of others, but he was not content in merely doing just that.","THE Creature and THE Primordial Chaos had their own foundations in their own time as they reached heights that only they could reach because of the foundations they had built. They had climbed to peaks that seemed unreachable, had achieved things that seemed impossible, had become synonymous with power itself because of what they had accumulated during their ascent!","But if Noah proceeded to build something that even they had not built before, his own accomplishments and his own glorious weavings of existence would even come to exceed them.","Matching legends was merely the first step.","Surpassing them was the goal!","The Logos and Philologies of The First Tongue all around him vibrated with immensity as they seemed to agree in fervor, the very language of reality resonating with ambitions that it found worthy of acknowledgment!","As he was having such thoughts, the figure of THE Esteemed Whisperer floated over with the other Fundamental Depth Muspeli Lifeform, their forms burning with sandy and linguistic flames respectively as they brought the glorious object that had been at the center of the citadel of flames they had protected for eons beyond counting.","Behind them, the other Muspeli Lifeforms that had been protected and watching the battle from a distance came forward in what could only be described as a procession of ancient entities.","Multiple Intermediate Depth Muspeli Giants whose forms burned with variations of obsidian and gold flame.","Multiple Surface Depth Muspeli Lifeforms whose bodies ranged from towering humanoids to serpentine creatures of pure fire to beings whose shapes defied easy categorization.","They all came forward as if participating in a ceremony that had been rehearsed across eons of waiting.","They looked toward Noah with doubt and analysis, as if they were measuring up the entity that many of them had not thought of before today.","Because what the entity who laid claim to The First Tongue represented was something of major importance to most of these giant lifeforms. Vut only the most powerful ones, the Protectors and their closest advisors, truly understood what such a thing meant for existence itself.","The rest had only basal rudimentary knowledge, simply knowing the legends of figures like THE Creature or THE Primordial Chaos eventually finding their way and claiming aspects of existence before returning to Muspelheim to receive acknowledgment.","So it looked like a procession of ancient beings that were both examining and elevating the brilliance of THE Genesis Monarch, their gazes carrying curiosity and skepticism and hope in equal measure.","Noah smiled calmly and took this all in stride as he looked at the object that THE Esteemed Whisperer was bringing.","And without him even realizing it...","The figure of Galileo and Duke appeared inches away from him with casual ease that spoke of speed beyond normal perception!","The small lifeform that was Galileo continued to look at him up and down as if he was still assessing Noah, those large eyes sparkling with intelligence that belied his fluffy appearance.","Meanwhile, the figure of Duke sniffed Noah with a wet nose that radiated warmth, and then his tongue lapped out in what could only be described as enthusiastic greeting!","The golden dog came forward to nudge him, moving around his body like a neon light of pure excitement, circling and weaving with speed that made tracking his position nearly impossible.","Noah’s hand reached out to pat this dog, but he couldn’t lock onto its position!","Every time his fingers approached where Duke had been, the Muspeli Lifeform had already moved to a different location, his speed truly approaching what Galileo had claimed.","It was only when Duke chose to stop in front of him with shining flaming neon eyes did the golden retriever bring his head forward with tongue lolling and tail wagging.","Noah’s hand finally made contact, his fingers sinking into fur that was simultaneously soft and warm and thrumming with ridiculously pure Mana, and he scratched behind those golden ears as Duke’s tail wagged with even greater intensity.","Galileo watched this interaction with satisfaction.","“He is simple-minded in nature and doesn’t have any complex thoughts apart from being told that in the future, his grand Master would arrive and unlock his true potential.”","His deep voice carried fondness for his longtime companion.","“He is supposed to be the mount of The One Who Laid The Claim, as he was born in the fires of Muspelheim in concentrated Philologies of The First Tongue. His speed is merely the surface of what he could become.”","...!","Oh?","A uniquely mutated simple-minded creature that The One Who Laid Claim to The First Tongue could unlock the full potential of?","Noah noted this down for later as he smiled at the thought of riding on a dog instead of something that one would routinely think of as a mount. It was unconventional, perhaps even absurd, but he had long since stopped caring about convention!","But at this moment, he kept his gaze on the object that THE Esteemed Whisperer brought as around him, the figures of THE Infiniverse, Sigrid, Riya, The First Farmer, and others also gathered nearby with shining eyes.","Surtra came to a stop before Noah, her sandy flames dimming slightly in deference as she raised her hands to present what she had been protecting.","“Genesis Monarch.”","Her voice carried the weight of someone fulfilling a duty that had defined her existence for longer than most civilizations had existed.","“For eons beyond counting, we have protected this Fragment. We have fought and bled and watched our kin fall to keep it from those who would misuse it. THE Living Spirit came for it, as others have come before him, and we held them all at bay.”","Her eyes burned with intensity that made her sandy flames seem cold by comparison.","“We did this because we knew that one day, The One Who Laid The Claim would come.”","She extended her hands, and the object rose from her palms.","“I present to you the Fragment of THE Axiom of Differentiated Tongue. May it serve you as it was always meant to.”","The Fragment floated toward Noah with the inevitability of something returning home after a long journey.","It was a crystalline prism of impossible geometry, its surfaces shifting between states that seemed to exist in multiple dimensions simultaneously. Light bent around it in ways that created halos of linguistic meaning, each angle revealing Phonemes that danced at the edge of comprehension. Its core burned with a flame that was less fire and more pure expression of The First Tongue itself, a concentrated essence of the very language that had defined reality since before differentiation.","When it came to hover before Noah, his entire existence pulsed in resonance!","Every fiber of his being vibrated at frequencies that matched the Fragment’s emanations, as if recognizing something that had always belonged to him and was only now being returned. His blue-gold flames intensified!","The Fragment unveiled itself before him.","|Fragment of THE Axiom of Differentiated Tongue|","|Classification: One of the Absolute Axioms representing the foundational nature of The First Tongue itself|","|Origin: This Fragment embodies the principle that all things in existence can be understood through their linguistic components. Before there was matter or energy or concept, there was language. And language can be broken down into its constituent parts.|","|Core Capability: Phonemic Deconstruction|","|This Fragment allows the wielder to break down anything it comes in contact with into its components of Phonemes, or what their Phonemes would be if they possessed linguistic foundations.|","|Against Declarations and Thesis: Enemy Declarations can be deconstructed into their constituent Phonemes, rendering them ineffective as the linguistic structure that gives them power is systematically dismantled.|","|Against Partial Embodiments: Physical or conceptual manifestations can be analyzed and reduced to their foundational linguistic components, revealing weaknesses and allowing for targeted disruption.|","|Against Ways and Civilizations: The underlying Phonemic structure of any Way can be perceived and potentially restructured, allowing for deep understanding of how others have built their foundations.|","|Secondary Capability: Structural Analysis|","|Beyond combat applications, this Fragment provides unprecedented insight into the architecture of existence itself. The wielder can perceive how Phonemes combine to create meaning, how meaning combines to create authority, and how authority combines to create reality.|","|This analytical capability allows for optimization of one’s own linguistic foundations, identifying inefficiencies and redundancies.|","|Resonance Status: Perfect. This Fragment recognizes you as The One Who Laid The Claim. Its capabilities are fully available to you without restriction. No cost. No limitation. A scary reality as what does this say if THE Creature holds a full Axiom of Existence? Or THE Primordial Chaos holding a full Axiom of Chaos?|","|Note: You now hold Fragments of THE Axiom of Mayhem, THE Axiom of Attrition, and THE Axiom of Differentiated Tongue. Three Fragments from three different Axioms.|","...!","Noah looked at the vibrant details of the Fragment of an Axiom that represented his side of the oldest question in existence, the side of differentiation and language and the building blocks from which all meaning emerged.","His already radiant figure wreathed in blue-gold flames began to pulse with an intense light as he gazed upon this Fragment with understanding blooming in his mind!","When he looked at this Fragment, he felt like he had found an answer to a question he had been carrying for the past two hours.","The streamlining of his existence.","The reduction of redundancy!","The optimization of everything he had built into something more elegant and more powerful!","This Fragment could help him achieve all of it!","4/4 Keep the Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming!"]},{"number":4737,"title":"Chapter 4737: Chapter 4736: Compression! I","paragraphs":["Capítulo 4736: Compression! I","Celebrations were curious things in the grand weavings of existence.","For most beings, celebrations marked achievements both small and grand, moments where they could pause and acknowledge that they had accomplished something worthy of recognition. A battle won. A threshold crossed. An enemy defeated!","These were all occasions that warranted raising a glass or singing songs or simply taking a moment to breathe and appreciate what had been done.","But for others, for entities like THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons, celebrations were luxuries that could not yet be afforded.","How could one celebrate when the peaks still loomed so far above? How could one pause to acknowledge achievement when THE Creature and THE Living Paradox and THE Primordial Chaos still stood at heights that made current accomplishments seem like the first steps of a long journey? How could one rest when every moment spent resting was a moment that enemies spent growing stronger?","For such entities, true celebration could only come when they stood at the apex of existence and gazed down below at the masses.","Only then, when there was no one left above them, when every peak had been conquered and every rival surpassed, could they truly pause and acknowledge what they had built.","Until then, there was no celebration.","There was only much more to be done!","—","A great man once said that the self is an illusion, that one should relax and stop striving and simply realize that they were one with everything already.","To relax.","Fuck that guy.","Noah’s eyes shone brightly as he did not dwell on the fact that he had just decimated one of the bodies of THE Living Spirit. He continued to forge ahead and strived forward as at this moment, he closed his eyes while grasping the Fragment of THE Axiom of Differentiated Tongue.","The sensation that he had while holding onto this object was a unique one, as if it was a baseball bat or an object that he used to play with when he was young on that tiny blue planet. Of course, he knew that this was just the familiarity of sensation brought about due to The First Tongue and this being an object intimately related to it.","But its capabilities were ridiculous compared to the fact that they came with absolutely no cost at all!","Since entities like THE Creature and THE Living Paradox likely had either completed Axioms or multiple Fragments, the things they could do were absolutely ridiculous. Noah had to play a lot of catch-up to match what they had accumulated over eons.","But at this moment, he was advancing.","“Structural Analysis.”","HUUUUM!","A brilliant blue-gold light shone from the Fragment in his hands as it pulsed and covered his entire figure in radiance that seemed to penetrate every layer of his existence!","The light broke down everything that Noah was into its constituent components and laid them bare before his perception with clarity.","One of the features of the Fragment was activated, and what it showed him was nothing less than the complete architecture of his own existence!","|Structural Analysis Complete|","|Subject: THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons|","|The following is a comprehensive breakdown of your existence as perceived through the lens of Phonemic Deconstruction.|","|THE FIRST TONGUE: CORE PHONEMES|","|Original 18 Phonemes of The First Tongue:Fire, Water, Earth, Air, Void, Light, Darkness, Life, Death, Time, Space, Order, Chaos, Unity, Division, Beginning, Ending, Paradox|","|These are the foundational linguistic units that existed since before differentiation. You have claimed authority over all of them.|","|The 9 Forged Phonemes:Quintessence, Infinity, Tyranny, Fortune(Loot), Advantage(Cheats), Narrative (Protagonist),Harvest, Hunger, Potential|","|These are Phonemes of your own creation, linguistic units that did not exist until you spoke them into being. They represent your unique contribution to The First Tongue itself.|","|Total Phonemic Authority: 27 Core Phonemes|","|Classification: Complete linguistic foundation for a Claimer of The First Tongue|","|ARCHAI: THE FOUNDATIONAL AUTHORITIES |","|Your Archai represent the fundamental principles that govern your existence:|","|The Arche of Cheating Architect: The engine that drives impossibility into reality|","|The Arche of Undifferentiated Mana: The fuel that knows no exhaustion|","|The Arche of Perpetual Harvest: The principle that all effort yields reward...etc|","|These Archai form foundation upon which everything else rests.|","|THE 159 STANCHIONS OF INFINITY|","|Current Status: 159 THE Stanchions of Infinity serve as the pillars supporting your infinite nature.|","|Assessment: Redundant. Inefficient. Multiple Stanchions perform overlapping functions.|","|Streamlining Potential: High.|","|THE GRIMOIRE OF INFINITE LEXICONS|","|Status: Active. Represents your foundation as a linguistic architect.|","|Function: Houses the accumulated knowledge and authority of your Way.|","|Integration: Deeply woven into your existence at the most fundamental level.|","|THE ORGAN OF CIVILIZATION|","|Status: Active and expanding.|","|Contains: THE Infinite Desmoterion|","|Function: Generates continuous authority and weight from imprisoned entities while housing the infrastructure of your Civilization.|","|DEPTH AND WEIGHT|","|Depth Classification: THE Formless Depth (defies conventional categorization)|","|Comparative Weight: 100/100th the Immensity of THE Creature or THE Living Paradox at THE Intermediate Depth|","|Foundation Status: Perfect. Ready for further elevation.|","|THE NINE LEXICAL PILLARS|","|First Pillar – Conceptual Lexicon: Allows formation of Logos embodying pure concepts. Grants ability to speak reality through conceptual authority.|","|Second Pillar – Outerversal Lexicon: Enables Logos construction transcending...|","|Third Pillar – Ingenious Lexicon: Focuses on creative and innovative Logos...|","|Fourth Pillar – Kuklos Lexicon: Specializes in Logos involving cycles, repetition, and infinite existential return...|","|Fifth Pillar – Megalos Lexicon: Grants ability to speak words affecting existence across vast distances...|","|Sixth Pillar – Singed Lexicon: Allows formation of Logos combining The First Tongue with primordial flame. Grants ability to inscribe with fire that cannot be extinguished...|","|Seventh Pillar – Paradoxical Lexicon:...Allows speaking truths that should be impossible.|","|Eighth Pillar – Eldritch Lexicon:...Grants ability to speak words and Thesis defying conventional understanding.|","|Ninth Pillar – Veridical Lexicon: Focuses on Logos of absolute truth and certainty. Allows speaking words that cannot be denied or contradicted.|","|FRAGMENTS OF AXIOMS|","|Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem: Reduces the Depth of targets.|","|Fragment of THE Axiom of Attrition: Nullifies and drains incoming attacks.|","|Fragment of THE Axiom of Differentiated Tongue: Breaks down anything into Phonemic components.|","|THE EDICTS OF PROGRESSION|","|Your Way of THE Mana Architect used to follow a nine-stage path:|","|Edict 0 – The Uninitiated: Manaless existence with latent potential.|","|Edict 1 – The Spark: Awakening of the Mana Locus.|","|Edict 2 – The Reservoir: Expansion of Mana capacity.|","|Edict 3 – The Weave: External expression of Mana.|","|Edict 4 – The Glyph: Internalization of perfected Weaves.|","|Edict 5 – The Heart: Transformation of Locus into active engine. Birth of Haki.|","|Edict 6 – The Aegis: Forging of Living Existential Armor.|","|Edict 7 – The Codex: Evolution to Living Mana Codex. Access to Arcana Glyphs.|","|Edict 8 – The Principle: Transcendence of existence’s rules. Creation of personal Principles.|","|Edict 9 – THE Mana Architect: THE classification.|","|Assessment: The Edicts provide clear progression for followers of your Way, but their integration with your other systems shows room for optimization.|","...!","Noah felt all of this information wash over him with clarity!","1/5"]},{"number":4738,"title":"Chapter 4738: Chapter 4737: Compression! II","paragraphs":["He felt every atom within him, every weaving, every connection between systems that he had built over the course of his journey. It was as if someone had handed him a complete blueprint of a machine he had been operating by instinct, and now he could finally see exactly how each component connected to every other component.","And more importantly, he could see the inefficiencies.","The redundancies.","The places where streamlining could transform good into perfect.","A moment later, the Fragment in his hand shone as it began to radiate waves of additional information!","|Streamlining Proposals|","|The following are potential optimizations identified through Structural Analysis. They are listed in order of alignment with your existence’s own inclinations.|","| PROPOSAL ONE: PHONEMIC CONVERGENCE|","|Priority: Highest. Your own existence was already pondering this path.|","|Current State: 159 THE Stanchions of Infinity support your infinite nature through overlapping and sometimes redundant functions.|","|Proposed State: Converge all 159 THE Stanchions of Infinity to fit the 27 Core Phonemes of The First Tongue. The 18 original Phonemes and the 9 you designed would each become a pillar of your foundation.|","|Result: Each of the 27 Phonemes would house multiple Stanchions worth of function, compressed and refined into linguistic perfection. Your entire existence would have its foundation encompassing THE First Tongue itself.|","|Significance: This would truly make you The Claimer of THE First Tongue in the most literal sense. Your foundation would BE The First Tongue, and The First Tongue would BE your foundation. They would be inseparable.|","...!","BOOM !","Noah’s eyes remained closed as he absorbed this first proposal, and he felt his existence hum with recognition!","Yes.","This was what he had been sensing since he laid claim to The First Tongue. The Stanchions were scaffolding that had served their purpose, but now they could become something more elegant, more powerful, more fundamentally aligned with what he represented.","Twenty-seven pillars instead of one hundred fifty-nine.","Each one a Phoneme.","Each one irreducible and essential.","His mind turned to the other areas of his power that could benefit from similar treatment, and understanding bloomed with calm ingenuity.","\"The Edicts...\" he murmured to himself. \"They’re decent enough, but... they don’t fully integrate with the Lexical Pillars.\"","He could see it now with the clarity that the Structural Analysis provided.","The Nine Edicts of Progression guided followers through stages of growth, from Uninitiated to Architect. But the Nine Lexical Pillars and their connection to The First Tongue existed separately.","But...nearly all the THE entities produced in his Civilization was due in some form from him teaching them THE First Tongue.","What if each Edict...corresponded to a Lexical Pillar?","The Spark could potebtially align with the Conceptual Lexicon, the awakening of Mana being fundamentally a conceptual shift in one’s existence. The Reservoir could align with the Megalos Lexicon, expansion of capacity being an expression of tremendous scale. The Weave could align with the Ingenious Lexicon, external expression requiring creative and innovative construction.","He could map each Edict to a Pillar, creating a progression where advancing through the stages of his Way automatically deepened one’s connection to The First Tongue.","\"And the Archai...\" Noah continued, his mind racing with possibilities.","The Principles of Existence, but now grander as they incorporated his 9 new Phonemes!","The Arche of Cheating Architect. The Arche of Undifferentiated Mana. The Arche of Perpetual Harvest.","These and other foundational authorities could be woven into the very fabric of the Edicts themselves, so that progressing through each stage automatically deepened one’s connection to these principles. Not as separate systems to be learned, but as inherent features of walking the path at all.","Someone at Edict 3 would naturally begin experiencing minor expressions of Perpetual Harvest as their Weaves generated returns.","Someone at Edict 5 would naturally begin channeling aspects of Undifferentiated Mana through their awakened Heart, their reserves regenerating faster than before.","Someone at Edict 7 would naturally begin touching the edges of Cheating Architect as their Codex allowed them to design abilities that bent conventional rules.","The Archai would be baked into the progression itself!","|Additional Proposal Detected|","|Your processing has identified a streamlining path not initially calculated.|","|PROPOSAL TWO: EDICT-PILLAR INTEGRATION|","|Fuse each of the Nine Edicts with its corresponding Lexical Pillar. Practitioners advancing through your Way would automatically develop specialized connection with The First Tongue early and slowly while aligned with their stage of progression.|","| PROPOSAL THREE: ARCHAI INFUSION|","|Weave the Archai into the Edict progression as inherent features rather than separate systems. Each stage of advancement would deepen connection to Cheating Architect, Undifferentiated Mana, Perpetual Harvest proportionally...|","|Combined Effect: Your Way would become a seamless whole rather than a collection of integrated systems. Followers would not learn multiple frameworks but would walk a single path that naturally encompasses everything.|","|Assessment: This level of integration would create the most elegant and powerful system of cultivation ever designed.|","...!","Noah opened his eyes, and they blazed with blue-gold fire that reflected the magnitude of design!","The Fragment of THE Axiom of Differentiated Tongue had shown him what he could become.","Twenty-seven Phonemes as the pillars of his foundation.","Nine Edicts fused with Nine Lexical Pillars.","The Archai woven into every stage of progression.","Everything streamlined. Everything elegant. Everything uniquely, irreducibly his!","After everything was clear, there wasn’t really much to be done except proceed ahead.","Noah’s eyes blazed with certainty as he spoke words that would reshape his very existence.","\" Proceed with all 3 proposals.\"","BOOM!","His existence buzzed with an unfathomable sense of glory!","Three proposals. Three immense changes. The first one was the major transformation that affected him directly, while the other two clarified the progression of his Way and how his followers could proceed from nothing all the way to THE!","The Fragment in his hand illuminated with an intense light as Noah floated in the skies of Muspelheim, its crystalline surfaces burning with Phonemes that danced at the edge of comprehension.","And then...","THUMP!","The sound of his heart boomed out like a drum and permeated all around Muspelheim, the concentrated waves of The First Tongue buzzing as if even they could sense what was coming!"]},{"number":4739,"title":"Chapter 4739: Chapter 4738: Seals! I","paragraphs":["Every Muspeli Lifeform present felt that heartbeat in their own existence, felt it resonating with frequencies of transformation on a scale they had never witnessed.","THUMP!","The beat of his heart was clear, and the changes unfolded within his existence!","Twenty-seven Points of Singularities bloomed within him as they represented the skeleton of his foundation! Each one corresponded to a Phoneme of The First Tongue, burning with concentrated authority that drew the scattered Stanchions toward them like gravity wells attracting celestial bodies!","THE Infinity Stanchion of Infinity, THE Manadynamics Stanchion of Infinity, THE Boundless Stanchion of Infinity, and multiple others drifted toward the singularity representing The Phoneme of Infinity!","They collapsed into it with force that made reality shudder, their separate authorities merging into something far more concentrated and far more powerful than they had been individually!","THE Protagonist Stanchion of Infinity, THE Plot Stanchion of Infinity, and multiple others drifted toward the singularity representing The Phoneme of Narrative!","They fused together with the inevitability of rivers flowing toward the sea, their narrative authorities becoming one unified expression!","THE Fortune Stanchion of Infinity, THE Loot Stanchion of Infinity, THE Treasure Stanchion of Infinity, and multiple others drifted toward the singularity representing The Phoneme of Fortune!","THE Tyranny Stanchion of Infinity, THE Dominion Stanchion of Infinity, THE Sovereignty Stanchion of Infinity merged into The Phoneme of Tyranny!","THE Cheats Stanchion of Infinity, THE... collapsed into The Phoneme of Advantage!","THE Hunger Stanchion of Infinity, THE Devouring Stanchion of Infinity, THE Consumption Stanchion of Infinity merged into The Phoneme of Hunger!","THE Potential Stanchion of Infinity...","THE Quintessence Stanchion of Infinity...","THE Harvest...","And the Original 18 Phonemes called to their corresponding Stanchions with equal fervor!","THE Fire Stanchion of Infinity, THE Singed Stanchion of Infinity, THE Combustion Stanchion of Infinity merged into The Phoneme of Fire!","THE Water Stanchion of Infinity, THE Megalos Stanchion of Infinity... collapsed into The Phoneme of Water!","THE Earth Stanchion of Infinity, THE Foundation Stanchion of Infinity... fused into The Phoneme of Earth!","THE Air Stanchion of Infinity...","THE Void Stanchion of Infinity... collapsed into The Phoneme of Void!","THE Light Stanchion of Infinity, THE Helios Stanchion of Infinity... fused into The Phoneme of Light!","THE Darkness Stanchion of Infinity..","THE Life Stanchion of Infinity...","THE Death Stanchion of Infinity...","THE Time Stanchion of Infinity, THE Temporal Stanchion of Infinity, THE Relativity Stanchion of Infinity merged into The Phoneme of Time!","THE Space Stanchion of Infinity, THE Quantum Stanchion of Infinity, THE Dimension Stanchion of Infinity collapsed into The Phoneme of Space!","THE Order...THE Chaos...and on and on and on!","They could fill up entire pages if every single one was listed!","But in totality...","One hundred fifty-nine Stanchions.","Twenty-seven Singularities.","Each Phoneme now contained multiple Stanchions worth of function, compressed and refined into linguistic perfection that had never existed before in all of existence!","All concepts that made him, all the Stanchions that had stood as the pillars for THE Faraday Cage, every single one was taken toward the fitting Phoneme as Noah’s existence was streamlined into something elegant and terrible and absolutely unprecedented!","|Phonemic Convergence In Progress|","|159 THE Stanchions of Infinity are being redistributed across 27 Core Phonemes.|","|Original 18 Phonemes:|","|The Phoneme of Fire absorbs: 6 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Water absorbs: 5 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Earth absorbs: 6 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Air absorbs: 5 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Void absorbs: 6 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Light absorbs: 6 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Darkness absorbs: 5 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Life absorbs: 7 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Death absorbs: 6 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Time absorbs: 7 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Space absorbs: 6 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Order absorbs: 5 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Chaos absorbs: 6 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Unity absorbs: 5 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Division absorbs: 5 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Beginning absorbs: 6 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Ending absorbs: 5 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Paradox absorbs: 7 Stanchions|","|The 9 Forged Phonemes:|","|The Phoneme of Quintessence absorbs: 6 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Infinity absorbs: 8 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Tyranny absorbs: 7 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Fortune absorbs: 6 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Advantage absorbs: 5 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Narrative absorbs: 6 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Harvest absorbs: 6 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Hunger absorbs: 5 Stanchions|","|The Phoneme of Potential absorbs: 7 Stanchions|","|Total Redistribution: 159 Stanchions across 27 Phonemes|","| Status: Complete.|","...!","THUMP!","THUMP!","THUMP!","Noah’s heart thundered with each Phoneme that finalized its absorption, each beat sending shockwaves across Muspelheim that made the obsidian flames dance in patterns they had never formed before!","The assembled Muspeli Lifeforms watched with eyes wide and flames flickering, witnessing something that their ancestors had only spoken of in whispered legends!","THE Infiniverse trembled as she felt her connection to Noah shift and deepen!","Khor’s abyssal eyes widened with genuine surprise, her ancient perception recognizing that what she was witnessing had never occurred in all the eons she had existed!","Sigrid’s ordered flames burned brighter in response to the restructuring occurring within the one she loved!","|Convergence Complete|","| Your existence has been fundamentally restructured.|","|Previous Foundation: 159 THE Stanchions of Infinity serving as scattered pillars|","|Current Foundation: 27 Phonemic Singularities containing all previous authority in concentrated form|","|Assessment: Your foundation IS The First Tongue. They are now inseparable and indistinguishable.|","| You are THE First Tongue made manifest.|","|THE First Tongue is you given voice.|","...!","The moment the convergence completed, Noah’s existence ignited!","His body burned with blue-gold plasma that was less fire and more pure concentrated authority given visible form! His eyes shot beams of light upward into the burning skies of Muspelheim as if his very perception had become too powerful to be contained!","His mouth opened and he ROARED!","The sound that emerged was not merely loud. It was linguistic! It carried Phonemes that had never been spoken together before, twenty-seven notes of a chord that existence itself had to bend to accommodate!","Above him, a radiant Grimoire materialized and opened with pages that burned with inscriptions shifting between all twenty-seven Phonemes in endless permutation!"]},{"number":4740,"title":"Chapter 4740: Chapter 4739: Seals! II","paragraphs":["THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons had transformed alongside him!","And this single Grimoire put a heavy strain on the surrounding atmosphere due to how immense it was!","Heavy!","IMMENSE !","The air around Noah compressed and distorted as if unable to bear the weight. The obsidian flames of Muspelheim bent toward him! The very fabric of this primordial realm groaned under the pressure of what he had become!","|Critical Threshold Exceeded|","| The weight of your Way and Civilization has spilled past what THE Creature or THE Primordial Chaos were able to accomplish at Intermediate Depth.|","|Previous Comparative Weight: 100/100th of THE Creature at Intermediate Depth|","| Current Comparative Weight: 150/100th|","|Your Weight continues to rise far past any established parameters of this stage, seeking a foothold at THE Fundamental Depth in a manner nobody else has taken before.|","| You are becoming heavier through linguistic perfection, through foundational elegance, through becoming something that existence has never had to bear before.|","BOOM!","The weight continued to build as something new began to emerge within Noah’s restructured existence!","|Physique Emergence Detected|","|Your Phonemic Convergence has triggered an unforeseen development.|","|When foundation becomes perfect, when every component serves its ideal purpose without redundancy, the result is not merely a stronger existence but a fundamentally different category of existence.|","|You are developing a Foundational Physique.|","| Physique Designation: THE Indestructible Lexicon of Absolute Weight|","|This is not a physique of flesh and blood. This is a physique of linguistic authority made manifest. Your body has become a vessel for the 27 Phonemic Singularities, and each Singularity carries the concentrated weight of everything it absorbed.|","...!","| THE Indestructible Lexicon of Absolute Weight - Complete Analysis|","|Core Nature:|","|Your physique is composed of 27 Phonemic Singularities. These Singularities are now designated as THE 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue.|","|The 18 Primordial Seals:|","|The Seal of Fire|","|The Seal of Water|","|The Seal of Earth|","|The Seal of Air|","|The Seal of Void|","|The Seal of Light|","|The Seal of Darkness|","|The Seal of Life|","|The Seal of Death|","|The Seal of Time|","|The Seal of Space|","|The Seal of Order|","|The Seal of Chaos|","|The Seal of Unity|","|The Seal of Division|","|The Seal of Beginning|","|The Seal of Ending|","|The Seal of Paradox|","|The 9 Forged Seals:|","|The Seal of Quintessence|","|The Seal of Infinity|","|The Seal of Tyranny|","|The Seal of Fortune|","|The Seal of Advantage|","|The Seal of Narrative|","|The Seal of Harvest|","|The Seal of Hunger|","|The Seal of Potential|","|Each Seal contains:|","|- Multiple former Stanchions compressed into singular expression|","|- Direct connection to its corresponding Phoneme of The First Tongue|","|- Weight that scales with the totality of what it represents|","|Physique Capabilities:|","| FIRST CAPABILITY: Singular Expression|","|You may express any single Seal with all its accumulated weight. When you invoke The Seal of Infinity, you invoke every concept of boundlessness absorbed into it. When you invoke The Seal of Fortune, you invoke all Stanchions within it simultaneously.|","|A single Seal carries the weight that once required multiple Stanchions to express.|","| SECOND CAPABILITY: Weighted Declarations|","|Your Declarations and Thesis constructs can now be geared toward specific Seals naturally. A Declaration invoking The Seal of Tyranny carries the combined weight of dominion and sovereignty compressed into linguistic perfection.|","| These Weighted Declarations are inherently heavier than normal Declarations. They press down upon reality with force that conventional authority cannot match.|","|THIRD CAPABILITY: The Crushing Depth|","| Your Formless Depth now expresses itself through weight rather than conventional measurements. When you exert your Depth, you crush enemies beneath the accumulated heaviness of 27 Seals bearing down simultaneously.|","|Everything on your path will be flattened when you choose to exert the full heaviness of THE Indestructible Lexicon of Absolute Weight.|","| FOURTH CAPABILITY: Seal Resonance|","| Multiple Seals may be invoked in combination, their weights multiplying rather than merely adding. Invoking The Seal of Fire alongside The Seal of Hunger creates pressure that exceeds what either could produce alone.|","| FIFTH CAPABILITY: Gravitational Presence|","|Your mere existence now carries passive weight. Lesser beings in your presence will feel the pressure of your physique bearing down upon them. Those with insufficient foundation will find it difficult to stand, to breathe, to maintain coherent thought.|","|This is not an attack. This is simply what you are now. Heavy. Immense. Inescapable. Fat!|","|Physique Classification: Unprecedented|","|No entity in recorded existence has developed a physique through Phonemic Convergence. You have developed yours through becoming The First Tongue incarnate.|","...!","Noah floated in the burning skies of Muspelheim as his transformation completed, his body wrapped in blue-gold plasma that distorted space itself.","The 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue pulsed within his existence like stars arranged in a constellation that spelled out his name in the oldest language.","Heavy.","He had become so impossibly heavy.","When he breathed, the air compressed around him. When he moved, reality bent to accommodate his passage. When he merely existed, everything nearby felt the weight of what he had become.","The Grimoire above him burned with light displaying the 27 Seals in arrangements that shifted with each heartbeat.","| Edict-Pillar Integration: Complete|","|Archai Infusion: Complete|","|All three proposals have been successfully implemented.|","|Your Way of THE Mana Architect is now a seamless whole.|","...!","Noah opened his eyes fully, and they blazed with weight that made even the Fundamental Depth Muspeli Lifeforms present take involuntary steps backward.","He smiled.","And even that simple expression carried heaviness that made the obsidian flames around him flatten as if pressed down by invisible hands.","There was still no celebration.","But there was satisfaction that bordered on joy.","And there was still much more to be done because...sheesh!","THE 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue!","Noah felt them pulsing within his existence like twenty-seven hearts beating in perfect synchronization, each one carrying weight that pressed against the fabric of reality itself. They were not separate from him. They were him. Twenty-seven concentrated expressions of everything he had become, everything he represented, everything he would continue to build.","The Seal of Fire burned with primordial heat that predated combustion itself.","The Seal of Infinity stretched toward horizons that had no end.","The Seal of Tyranny pressed down with authority that demanded submission from existence.","The Seal of Narrative whispered of stories yet to be written and protagonists yet to rise.","Each one was heavy. Each one was profound. Each one was a pillar of his foundation that could now be expressed with concentrated force that his previous scattered Stanchions could never have achieved.","Noah waved his hand soon after as he focused on one Seal in particular.","THE Absolute Seal of Infinity.","BOOM!"]},{"number":4741,"title":"Chapter 4741: Chapter 4740: Seals! III","paragraphs":["The Seal bloomed into existence above his palm, and the moment it manifested, Galileo and Surtra were pushed back in astonishment as waves of pressure erupted from its mere presence!","Duke whimpered slightly before sitting in the air with eyes of veneration, the golden retriever’s tail tucked as he recognized something far beyond his current comprehension.","The Seal itself was circular in form, perhaps three meters in diameter, and it burned with countless intricate blue-gold lines that wove patterns of impossible complexity across its surface. The lines and strokes within seemingly gave meaning to the Phoneme of Infinity while also containing within them the pillars of his foundation that had been absorbed into this singular expression.","Where one line ended, another began without interruption.","Where one pattern seemed to reach completion, it folded back into itself and continued forever.","The very act of looking at this Seal conveyed the concept it represented, boundlessness made visible, endlessness given form, infinity compressed into something that could actually be perceived by minds that were not built to comprehend such things.","And within those infinite patterns, Noah could sense the Stanchions that now resided here. All of them compressed and refined and made more powerful through their merger into this singular Seal.","The radiant Seal of Infinity spun above him with slow majesty, and he understood that he could do many things with it. He could use it to attack, unleashing the full weight of infinity upon enemies who would be crushed beneath concepts they could not comprehend. He could use it to defend, wrapping himself in boundlessness that could not be breached. He could make Declarations or Thesis constructs through it, speaking words of infinity that would carry weight no normal Declaration could match.","But what struck him most was how heavy the Seal felt as it exerted pressure all around that was stifling!","Space itself creaked beneath the Seal’s presence, reality groaning as if it were saying with exhausted desperation: bro, you’re fucking heavy!","The obsidian flames of Muspelheim bent away from the Seal as if afraid to touch it. The air compressed into visible distortions. Even the other Fundamental Depth entities present had to brace themselves against the weight that radiated from this single expression of Noah’s foundation.","As Noah analyzed this Seal with eyes that burned with understanding...","|Harvest Threshold Achieved|","|With the establishment of your foundation integrated ever so closer with THE First Tongue, a new source of Infinite Potential has become accessible.|","|30% of The Infinite Potential generated by the usage of The First Tongue across existence, both in the present and the past, has begun to be harvested by the Arche of Perpetual Harvest.|","| Not a single drop of potential will be unaccounted for.|","|Every being that speaks a Phoneme. Every Declaration that invokes The First Tongue. Every Thesis that draws upon linguistic authority. 30% of the potential generated by these actions now flows to you as The One Who Laid The Claim.|","|As control over The First Tongue continues to be cemented and your Depth rises evermore, all 100% of The Infinite Potential of the Usage of The First Tongue will be yours.|","|Contextual Assessment:|","|Because THE Creature, THE Living Paradox, and THE Primordial Chaos likely actively enjoy the harvest of their own claims, consider what they receive:|","|THE Creature harvests from all those existing and moving across existence. Everything that lives, everything that moves, everything that simply IS contributes to his power.|","|THE Living Paradox harvests from all paradoxical actions or existences. Every contradiction, every impossibility made real, every truth that should not be true feeds his authority.|","|THE Primordial Chaos harvests from everything chaotic and filled with disorder. Which is fucking everything, because entropy touches all things eventually.|","|It is maddening to realize how powerful they are and how many boons they have been enjoying for eons as you get closer to them.|","|You’re gonna need to do a lot to get close to them, big guy.|","...!","Ruination continued to have fun with her prompts as Noah felt an influx of Infinite Potential gush down into his existence!","It filled his Formless Depth even more, pouring into the 27 Seals and making them burn brighter, making them grow heavier, making his weight continue to become even more imposing with each passing moment.","The Depth of his Civilization skipped past THE Surface Depth and settled far into Intermediate Depth as his personal Weight spilled toward Fundamental Depth!","It was a fucking glorious thing!","As he felt all of this, as he basked in the sensation of power flooding into him from sources that would never run dry...","\" This...\"","Galileo’s voice emerged with shining eyes of interest and wonder as he looked at the Seal spinning above Noah’s palm. His large ears were fully erect, his whiskers twitching with excitement that his Fundamental Depth perception could not fully contain.","\" This feels without a doubt to be a Phoneme of The First Tongue, and yet it does not match any of the Phonemes of The First Tongue that I know!\"","His fluffy form practically vibrated with scholarly curiosity as he floated closer, Duke padding through the air beside him with ears perked forward.","\" Fire, Water, Earth, Air, Void, Light, Darkness, Life, Death, Time, Space, Order, Chaos, Unity, Division, Beginning, Ending, Paradox. These are the 18 Phonemes. This is not any of them!\"","...!","His words were grand as toward this observation, Noah looked at the ancient Muspeli Lifeform with calm tyranny burning in his gaze.","\" This is just one of the 9 new Phonemes I have recently designed.\"","His voice carried weight that matched the Seal spinning above him.","\" The First Tongue is no longer just made up of 18 Phonemes.\"","...!","The words caused an immense silence to descend across the burning skies of Muspelheim.","Galileo looked at him with widening eyes that seemed to grow larger with each passing moment, his fluffy features frozen in an expression of absolute disbelief.","Surtra trembled in the distance, her sandy flames flickering erratically!","The other Fundamental Depth Muspeli Lifeform beside her went still as stone.","The Intermediate Depth giants who had been watching from a respectful distance felt their flames gutter and surge as understanding began to dawn.","The Surface Depth Muspeli Lifeforms looked at each other with expressions that ranged from confusion to dawning horror to something that might have been fervor.","In the next moment, all the Muspeli Lifeforms played his words in their minds again and again, parsing them for any possible misinterpretation, searching for any way that they could have misunderstood what THE Genesis Monarch had just claimed.","But there was no misunderstanding.","He forged new letters of The First Tongue.","The First Tongue, which had existed since before differentiation. The First Tongue, which had been complete and perfect and unchanging for eons beyond counting. The First Tongue, which the Muspeli Lifeforms had dedicated their entire existence to protecting and preserving.","He had added to it.","What the fuck!?","THUNK!","Galileo’s knees hit a metaphorical floor in the skies of Muspelheim as he knelt toward Noah, Duke immediately following suit by lowering his golden body into a bow!","THUNK!","Surtra descended to her knees with sandy flames billowing around her in patterns of absolute submission!","THUNK! THUNK! THUNK!","The other Muspeli Lifeforms followed, Fundamental and Intermediate and Surface Depth alike, all of them kneeling in the burning air as the full weight of what they had just learned settled upon their ancient consciousnesses!","He forged new letters of The First Tongue!","The moment this was affirmed, all that they knew was undeniable!","He was not merely The One Who Laid The Claim. He was not merely the leader of Muspelheim by right of linguistic authority. He was someone who had done what no entity in all of existence had ever done before!","He had expanded the very language that reality was written in!","So at this moment, the Muspeli Lifeforms knelt toward THE Genesis Monarch with reverence!","Noah looked at this scene calmly, taking in the sight of ancient beings kneeling themselves before him, and he was about to tell them to stop this, when...","|URGENT NOTIFICATION|","|With the establishment of your foundation integrated ever so closer with THE First Tongue, capabilities that were impossible before are becoming possible now.|","| Through your integrated connection, The First Tongue senses across the murkiness of the Wastes of THE Fallout.|","|The Wastes are filled with chaotic energies that prevent communication absolutely. No signal should pass through. No awareness should penetrate. And yet...|","| The First Tongue senses the potential collapse of pillars of your Civilization.|","|Little information has been obtained due to your current Depth and Weight pitted against the Absolute rejection of communications and weavings across existence. The murkiness resists. The chaos interferes. But fragments have emerged.|","|Information Obtained:|","|Ul’moreth and Lumivara face the weavings of an entity identified as Gilgamesh.|","|At this time, signs of an Absolute identified as THE Weavers have made their descent.|","|These pillars of your Civilization are in peril and face a high chance of cessation and collapse.|","|It is unknown where they are.|","|It is unknown if this is slightly in the past, ongoing present, or future.|","|The murkiness obscures temporal positioning as thoroughly as it obscures spatial location.|","|What is known: They need help. And you cannot currently reach them.|","...!","Noah’s expression became heavy as his eyes pulsed with immensity that erupted from him in waves he could not fully control!","Multiple THE Surface Depth Muspeli Lifeforms fainted from this accidental eruption of his tyrannical pressure, their ancient forms slumping in the air as their consciousnesses simply could not withstand the weight of his sudden surge!","Ul’moreth.","Lumivara!","His hands clenched into fists as blue-gold flames erupted around him with intensity that made even the Fundamental Depth entities present flinch, and the Seal of Infinity spinning above him pulsed with his weight as twenty-seven Seals resonated!"]},{"number":4742,"title":"Chapter 4742: Chapter 4741: Give and Take! I","paragraphs":["Muspelheim continued to steadily be devoured into the blue-gold monolith.","Ancient flames that had burned since before differentiation were being unmade piece by piece, compressed into that impossible structure Noah had willed into existence. Rivers of molten authority flowed upward against every natural law, drawn toward something that defied conventional understanding as it all flowed to THE Infiniverse!","And yet there was a heavy, suffocating silence that nobody could explain.","All the Muspeli Lifeforms present looked toward Noah!","Noah who at this moment turned in the direction where Galileo and Duke had come from, his expression shifting into something cold and calculating.","THE Living Concept was out there. Assaulting. Killing. Treating Muspeli Lifeforms like obstacles to be swept aside with casual indifference.","But that wasn’t what made his blood blaze the most.","Lumivara and Ul’moreth were somewhere in the Wastes of THE Fallout. He didn’t know where. Couldn’t sense them through the corrupted mess that separated different regions of post-Fallout Existence.","And an Absolute bore down upon them.","THE Weaver.","Not a Half-Step embarrassment like THE Living Spirit. A genuine, categorical Absolute operating at THE Absolute Depth of Existence itself.","Noah’s mind raced.","He had one body here in Muspelheim. Another in The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature. A third moving through THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap to retrieve Eon’s Disciple as part of their tenuous arrangement.","Existence post-Fallout was heavily resistant to clones. The corrupted fabric of reality itself seemed to reject the multiplication of singular existences, as if the laws governing identity had been rewritten specifically to be a pain in the ass.","But Noah continued to defy restrictions.","He should be able to deploy another body to the Wastes of THE Fallout. Should be able to seek the location of Lumivara and Ul’moreth despite barriers that would’ve stopped anyone else cold.","His eyes blazed with Tyranny!","The newly forged Seals threatened to spill out with his immense weight, each one pulsing beneath his skin like caged beasts demanding release. Twenty-seven concentrated expressions of everything he had become, everything he represented, everything he would continue to build.","And what was unique here, what set him apart from any reasonable existence facing such circumstances, was that he knew an Absolute was bearing down on his people...and he was still planning to go there anyway.","Not fearful or hesitant!","Fear was for those who had something to lose and no way to protect it. Noah had everything to lose and the absolute conviction that he’d find a way regardless.","But...","He had to have a plan.","It was great and all not to be fearful. Tyranny demanded nothing less than absolute confidence in the face of impossible odds. But if he simply threw a body into an Absolute’s hands without preparation, without strategy, without understanding what he was actually facing...","How catastrophic would the results be?","And yet Ul’moreth and Lumivara couldn’t be collapsed!","Ul’moreth had given him knowledge of The First Tongue that fundamentally transformed his understanding of Existence itself.","Lumivara, that little fox, also could not die!","They were pillars of his Civilization.","He would not allow them to fall.","So he had to come up with a solution against an Absolute.","Blue-gold plasma began bleeding from his form, swirling around him like the corona of an angry star. His hair lifted. His robes rippled in winds that existed only for him. The 27 Seals pulsed with barely contained tyranny within him as space itself compressed around his figure.","He looked like an angered celestial fiend whose wrath could unmake countless folds.","He felt like one too.","\"Utilize the Full Moirai Thread.\"","HUUM!","The words resonated through Existence with weight that made nearby Muspeli Lifeforms take involuntary steps backward!","Above Noah’s existence, reality itself seemed to part like curtains being drawn aside by invisible hands.","A massive golden thread bloomed into manifestation!","This wasn’t the single Fragment he’d used before. This wasn’t the partial glimpse into potential futures that had shown him THE Secretive Eon and the dangers of THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.","This was the combined Thread from nine Fragments, woven together into something that pulsed with the authority of fate itself!","The Thread was thick as a river of liquid gold. Each pattern represented a different branch of the infinite tree of potential futures, a different answer to questions that hadn’t yet been asked.","It descended toward Noah with the inevitability of destiny accepting a challenge.","| Full Moirai Thread Activation Initiated.|","|Nine Fragments have been combined into a Complete Thread.|","|This represents the maximum possible extraction from THE Existential Paradox Loop without direct interface.|","|Capability: Complete Simulation of potential futures until point of collapse or death.|","|Unlike Partial Simulation, Full Simulation provides:|","|- Comprehensive detail rather than fragmentary glimpses|","|- Extended temporal range of observable futures|","|- Ability to explore branching decision points with your own inputs|","|- Full sensory and cognitive immersion in simulated events|","|Warning: Full Simulation is not reality.|","|Events observed may not occur exactly as shown.|","|Decisions made in simulation do not bind future actions.|","|However, information gathered represents highest probability outcomes based on current trajectory.|","|Initiating Full Simulation of THE Existential Paradox Loop...|","...!","The golden Thread shot forward and pierced Noah’s chest!","His entire existence shuddered as the Thread wrapped around his heart with pressure that made his previous partial experience feel like a gentle caress. His consciousness expanded outward in directions that had no names, perceiving possibilities that hadn’t yet crystallized into actualities.","His eyes glazed completely gold.","|Full Simulation Active.|","|Current Objective Detected: Finding solution to stand against THE Weaver, an Absolute of THE Living Paradox.|","|Simulation will explore decision branches related to this objective.|","|Beginning primary sequence...|","|Timeline Analysis: Primary Branch|","|Seeking additional resources and information before direct confrontation.|","|Your consciousness extends across your multiple deployed bodies simultaneously.|","|One body remains in Muspelheim overseeing consumption.|","|One body remains in The Early Veiled Shore maintaining Civilization operations.|","|One body moves through THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.|","|Potential Decision Point: Leverage existing alliance with THE Secretive Eon for assistance against Absolute-class threat.|","|Executing decision branch...|","...!"]},{"number":4743,"title":"Chapter 4743: Chapter 4742: Give and Take! II","paragraphs":["The simulation crystallized around Noah’s perception with perfect clarity.","He found himself in the Stoa of Dogmata, the endless colonnade of ancient pillars stretching in all directions. Their surfaces still burned with inscriptions of Dogmata from eras that predated differentiation itself.","And there, exactly where she’d been during their previous encounters, sat THE Secretive Eon.","Her small, delicate form remained composed upon the obsidian ground. Dark hair with rivers of gold caught light that seemed to come from nowhere. Her white-blue robe draped across her shoulders with elegant simplicity. Those dark eyes held depths that could swallow entire civilizations without noticing.","She didn’t turn as his simulated body approached.","\" You have returned quickly, Scale Breaker.\" Her voice emerged measured and unhurried. \"I find myself wondering how you have so much time on your hands to play around.\"","Noah moved to take position near her, maintaining the distance their previous interactions had established.","\"I collapsed the Half-Step Absolute Depth body of THE Living Spirit.\"","THE Secretive Eon received this news with the same composure she showed toward everything. Her head inclined slightly in acknowledgment, a fraction of movement that somehow conveyed complete understanding of what such an achievement represented.","\" You are one of the Four from The Oldest Paradox of Existence, \" she said, her voice carrying neither surprise nor particular interest. \" The First Tongue, Existence, Paradox, and Chaos. The pillars upon which that ancient conflict was built.\"","Her gaze remained fixed on the distant expanse ahead.","\" If you weren’t even able to find a way to handle Spirit while holding a Fragment of an Axiom, you would truly be far too weak. You would not measure up to the others who share your classification among the Four.\" The faintest hint of contempt touched her words.","Noah absorbed these words while formulating his next approach.","\"In Muspelheim, THE Living Concept is also present. They seemed to have been sent by Paradox specifically to that location.\"","THE Secretive Eon nodded with nonchalant dismissal.","\" Picking off Primordial Realms of others and whatever Fragments of Axioms they may contain is natural. \" Her tone suggested she was discussing weather patterns rather than systematic destruction.","\" Muspelheim held treasures from before THE Fallout reshaped Existence, from before The Infinite Unfurling. Of course Paradox would send agents to claim what could be claimed.\"","Noah observed that this information produced absolutely no interest in Eon.","Her attention remained fixed on whatever she perceived in the distant depths of the Stoa. Her composure was unbroken!","So he shifted approaches entirely.","\" In the Wastes of THE Fallout, an Absolute is making a move against members of my Civilization.\"","Nothing.","\" THE Weaver,\" Noah continued. \" One of Paradox’s instruments operating at THE Absolute Depth. They bear down upon pillars of my foundation.\"","He let those words settle before delivering his request.","\" Since they’re an Absolute, they’re one of your targets. One of those who need to die according to the objectives you pursue.\" His gaze met hers directly despite the warnings his existence screamed about prolonged eye contact. \" I’m asking if you can make a move to end THE Weaver.\"","THE Secretive Eon pondered his words briefly.","Then she turned to look at him fully.","HUUM!","The weight of her attention settled upon Noah like the pressure of deep oceans!","Her dark eyes studied him with intensity that felt like being weighed on scales older than Existence itself. She looked him over slowly, deliberately, up and down as if assessing him anew despite their previous interactions.","Small in stature, almost delicate in appearance, with features that held an ageless quality that made it impossible to determine if she was young or ancient beyond measure!","When she finally spoke, her words came with patient finality.","\" Scale Breaker, we are not friends.\"","The statement was delivered without malice, without particular emphasis. Just fact being established.","\"I care very little if anyone from your Civilization dies. Failure to protect your people is failure of your Way. I can do one nice thing like giving you a Fragment when you mentioned Muspelheim, but I am not obligated to do anything else for this little... alliance.\"","Her dark eyes held his without wavering.","\" By the way, return my Fragment if you’re done with it.\"","She paused, and when she continued, her voice carried notes of casual dismissal.","\" When it comes to THE Weavers... they rank fairly weak amongst Absolutes. But they innately have Three Bodies, so its akin to facing 3 little tiny weak Absolutes... \" Her head tilted with consideration. \" But they are still Absolutes. You would likely be crushed.\"","Her gaze grew more distant.","\"I could move against them, yes. But Paradox is not my target right now. Chaos is. Killing one of Paradox’s Absolutes will cause deviations in my plans, and I don’t particularly feel the need to accommodate that at this moment.\"","She turned back to face the distant expanse of the Stoa.","\" So you, Scale Breaker, are on your own. As you should be. As all Absolutes are. Find your own solution against that Absolute.\"","Her voice carried edges that hadn’t been present before.","\" You need to have one thing abundantly clear between us. Our relationship is that of give and take. I have been more than giving so far. You cannot simply take. If you have something to give, give.\"","...!","Noah found his eyes pulsing with dangerous light within the simulation!","Her words were calm and cold, delivered with the patient certainty of someone who had no need to justify their position to anyone.","THE Secretive Eon observed his reaction and smiled.","While remaining seated with her legs crossed, she placed her chin upon her hand with casual elegance. Her dark eyes sparkled with something that might’ve been amusement or anticipation.","\" Oh?\" Her voice carried dangerous undertones wrapped in silk. \" I sense you’ve gotten a bit more weight on you since our last meeting. Your power isn’t subtle, Scale Breaker.\"","Her smile widened.","\" Are you feeling like rebelling? Itchy? you want to try and go against me as your first real Absolute?\"","BOOM!","The question wasn’t a threat.","It was an invitation!"]},{"number":4744,"title":"Chapter 4744: Chapter 4743: Give and Take! III","paragraphs":["Chapter 4743: Give and Take! III","Noah’s response came after a moment of deliberate control.","Rather than answering with words or foolish aggression, he waved his hand with calculated precision.","Two objects materialized before him.","The first was a Fragment that pulsed with chaotic energy barely contained within its crystalline structure. Patterns of mayhem and destruction swirled within its depths...THE Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem that Eon had lent him.","The second Fragment burned with different authority entirely. Where the first spoke of active destruction, this one whispered of gradual wearing, of persistent erosion, of patient victory through endurance...THE Fragment of THE Axiom of Attrition.","“A Fragment I obtained from THE Living Spirit,” Noah said calmly. “It’s yours if you make a move against THE Weaver.”","...!","THE Secretive Eon observed the offered Fragments with expression unchanged.","Then she yawned.","The gesture was small, delicate, and absolutely devastating in its dismissal.","Her hand reached out and casually reclaimed the Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem, the treasure she’d lent him returning to her possession with the inevitability of property recognizing its true owner.","She glanced at the remaining Fragment, the Axiom of Attrition that Noah had won through his defeat of THE Living Spirit.","Then she shook her head.","“Not enough.”","The words were delivered without negotiation, without room for counter-offer.","“Three more Fragments of similar quality, or something of genuinely equivalent value, might convince me to shift my plans and move against THE Weaver.” Her dark eyes met his with absolute finality. “Until then, focus your other body on retrieving my Disciple as previously agreed upon. That arrangement remains in effect regardless of whatever additional requests you wish to make.”","...!","|Simulation continues...|","|Unable to leverage THE Secretive Eon for direct intervention.|","|Decision Point: Alternative approaches required.|","|Executing next branch...|","|You take the Fragment of THE Axiom of Attrition with you.|","|THE Secretive Eon has reclaimed THE Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem.|","|You depart THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.|","|Destination: The Wastes of THE Fallout.|","|Objective: Locate Lumivara and Ul’moreth.|","|Secondary Objective: Develop solution for confronting Absolute-class threat without external assistance.|","...!","|You manifest in the gray desolation of the Wastes.|","|The corrupted landscape stretches endlessly in all directions.|","|Ashen clouds swirl overhead, vibrant with energies that would destroy lesser beings.|","|The ground beneath your feet shifts with uncertainty, reality itself confused about its own configuration.|","|You begin conjuring your Absolute Existential Seals.|","|The 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue manifest around your form!|","|Each one pulses with concentrated weight, enhancing your perception, extending your reach, amplifying your authority.|","|You attune yourself as deeply as possible to The First Tongue.|","|The 18 Core Phonemes resonate within your existence.|","|Your 9 unique Phonemes pulse with readiness.|","|Through linguistic authority, you attempt to pierce the interference that blankets these Wastes.|","|Seeking any trace of Lumivara’s distinctive signature.|","|Seeking any echo of Ul’moreth’s ancient presence.|","|Progress: Minimal.|","|The Wastes actively resist such detection.|","|Corruption interferes with even The First Tongue’s authority.|","|You persist regardless.|","...!","|Simultaneously, you process the tactical reality of your situation.|","|THE Weaver operates at THE Absolute Depth.|","|This is not Half-Step classification like THE Living Spirit.|","|This is genuine Absolute authority. Categorical superiority over your current state.|","|Analysis of potential countermeasures:|","|The Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem could theoretically reduce an opponent’s effective Depth.|","|However, THE Secretive Eon has reclaimed that Fragment.|","|The Fragment of THE Axiom of Attrition remains in your possession.|","|Its authority involves gradual erosion, persistent wearing, patient victory through endurance.|","|Assessment: Insufficient against genuine Absolute in direct confrontation.|","|Further Analysis:|","|THE Living Spirit was a Half-Step Absolute. A pale shadow of true Absolutes. A trash bum cosplaying as something greater than he actually was.|","|THE Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem was effective against him because his foundation was incomplete. His Depth was not genuine. His claim to Absolute classification was hollow.|","|THE Weaver, THE Weavers, are different.|","|Genuine Absolute. Complete foundation. Real claim to THE Absolute Depth.|","|Even if you still possessed THE Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem, its effect would be minimal.|","|Reducing a genuine Absolute’s effective Depth by a fraction would still leave them categorically superior to your current state.|","|You require alternative solutions.|","|Solutions that do not rely on matching power with power.|","|Solutions that leverage your unique capabilities rather than attempting to bridge unbridgeable gaps.|","|Contemplation continues as you search the Wastes...|","...!","The golden light of the Full Moirai Thread pulsed around Noah’s form as the simulation continued processing potential futures.","In Muspelheim, his physical body remained motionless. Blue-gold plasma still swirled around him like the corona of an angry star. The Muspeli Lifeforms watched with mixture of awe and concern, none daring to interrupt whatever profound process had claimed their unlikely ally’s attention.","Within the simulation, Noah’s consciousness grappled with the fundamental problem that had defined his entire existence since awakening to Infinite Mana.","How did one who hadn’t yet reached the apex stand against those who already resided there?","How did a Scale Breaker break scales that existed beyond his current reach?","It was a heavy question to ponder on at this moment!","But as Noah grappled with this, he also paid close attention to the workings of the Full Simulation itself.","Because it actually had many benefits!","He learned what would happen from small, simple things in these interactions. Like what happened if he shared news of his victory with Eon.","The answer was clear now.","He needed to not tell her about collapsing THE Living Spirit. The moment he did, she’d ask for her Fragment back.","He could keep that for as long as possible.","And the simulation... remained a simulation. Nothing that happened within it was real. He inherently did not offer his newly found Fragment of THE Axiom of Differentiated Tongue in actual Existence, but was there any harm in doing so in a simulation just to see if it could move Eon?","The answer was no!","His eyes shone brightly as he discovered a key point in these simulations!"]},{"number":4745,"title":"Chapter 4745: Chapter 4744: Skoll!","paragraphs":["Chapter 4744: Skoll!","He could make choices he would normally never make just for the sake of information gathering and exploring other possibilities!","He could go back to Eon and see if a different future could unfold if he offered things he wouldn’t offer otherwise in Existence. Test what leverage actually worked. Discover her true price without paying it, and even gain without losing anything since it was a simulation!","But before that...","He made another decision.","There was still the matter of finding Lumivara and Ul’moreth in these vast Wastes. Still the matter of developing solutions against an Absolute that didn’t rely on Eon’s intervention. Because while reliance on others was a form of power, the power of others was not always reliant.","The simulation could explore multiple branches simultaneously.","|Simulation Resuming.|","|Decision Point: Continue exploration of the Wastes while seeking alternative solutions.|","|Your Seals of Absolute Tongue continue to expand across the corrupted landscape.|","|The 27 Seals pulse outward, triggering resonance with The First Tongue wherever traces of it exist.|","|While searching, a secondary consideration emerges.|","|You recall information obtained earlier regarding the Muspeli Lifeform designated as Duke.|","...!","|Galileo’s words echo in your memory.|","|Duke: A unique anomaly born in the fires of The First Tongue.|","|Speed exceeding any Fundamental Depth entity.|","|Velocity approaching Absolute classification despite lacking the Depth to match.|","|Galileo mentioned that Duke’s full potential could be unleashed by you specifically.|","|The connection to The First Tongue that birthed this creature resonates with your claim over that same linguistic foundation.|","|Decision Point: Investigate Duke’s latent potential while continuing search operations.|","|Executing branch...|","...!","|In Muspelheim, your body turns attention toward Duke.|","|The golden retriever sits nearby with tongue lolling out, seemingly oblivious to the significance of events unfolding around him.|","|You place your hand upon his head.|","|You attempt to utilize The First Tongue to initiate whatever transformation might be possible.|","|Initial findings: No obvious oddities detected.|","|You study the makeup of this unique lifeform more carefully.|","|Biology of Duke – Analysis:|","|Physical form appears to be standard canine configuration adapted to Muspelheim’s primordial environment.|","|Fur composed of crystallized flame particles that shift through neon spectrums.|","|Musculature optimized for explosive acceleration rather than sustained output, and Logos and Philologies of The First Tongue|","|Nervous system operates at frequencies that exceed normal temporal limitations.|","|Core finding: Duke’s speed is not a product of raw power. It is a product of fundamental resonance with something deeper.|","|The First Tongue left unique anomalous traces in this creature’s very existence when it was born.|","|Those traces remain dormant. Waiting. Unactivated.|","|You proceed carefully.|","|You wish to continue your search while experimenting with the method to unlock whatever latent potential Duke possesses.|","|Solution: Bring Duke to the Wastes. Combine objectives.|","|Executing...|","...!","The simulation shifted as Noah made his decision.","And the scene that unfolded was... something.","A man jumping onto the back of a golden retriever and using him as a mount.","Not exactly the image of cosmic dignity that THE Genesis Monarch typically projected. But fuck it. Practicality trumped aesthetics!","Noah settled atop Duke’s broad back, his legs finding natural positions along the creature’s flanks. The golden fur beneath him radiated warmth that pulsed with neon light, and Duke’s muscles tensed with eager anticipation.","The Wastes of THE Fallout stretched endlessly in all directions around them.","Gray desolation as far as perception could reach. Ashen clouds swirling overhead. Corrupted reality shifting and reforming with each passing moment. Pockets of frozen time. Zones where distance meant nothing. Regions where existence itself seemed uncertain of its own configuration.","And in the middle of it all, a man seated atop a very good boy!","As much as that didn’t sound right, it was a glorious scene!","Noah patted Duke’s head calmly, his hand running through fur that felt like captured starfire.","“Alright. Let’s see what you can do.”","...!","Duke’s expression shifted into something that could only be described as pure, unbridled joy.","His eyes shone with excitement that transcended species barriers. His tail wagged with enthusiasm that generated small reality distortions. His entire body language screamed one thing:","He understood the assignment.","FWOOOOM!","In the next instant, Duke’s body became covered in neon flames!","The fire wasn’t destructive. It was kinetic. Pure velocity made manifest, wrapping around the golden retriever’s form like a second skin of crystallized speed. The flames extended outward to encompass Noah as well, coating him in protective luminescence that hummed with barely contained acceleration.","And then they moved.","WHOOOOSH!","The two of them shot out across the Wastes of THE Fallout like glimmers of neon light streaking through gray desolation!","Noah’s eyes shone brightly in the simulation as he witnessed space itself disappearing around him at rates that defied comprehension!","The Wastes blurred into indistinct smears of gray and ash. Landmarks that should have taken minutes to reach vanished behind them in heartbeats. Entire regions of corrupted reality were crossed in moments that felt like fractions of moments.","Fast.","So impossibly fast!","Duke moved with velocity that made Noah’s previous methods of travel look like crawling through mud. The golden retriever’s paws didn’t even seem to touch the ground. He simply existed in one location, then another, then another, the transitions so rapid that the concept of “movement” became almost meaningless.","This wasn’t running.","This was something else entirely.","|Simulation continues...|","|You begin to cover and map out vast distances of the Wastes with Duke as your mount.|","|Speed assessment: Unprecedented for non-Absolute classification.|","|Areas covered in minutes that would have required hours through conventional travel.|","|Your impression of Duke’s capabilities continues to grow.|","|This creature represents genuine tactical value.|","|You select Duke as another potential solution to the current problem.|","|If Lumivara and Ul’moreth can be located, Duke’s speed could enable rapid extraction.|","|If THE Weaver must be evaded rather than confronted, Duke’s velocity might provide the necessary advantage.|","|But questions remain.|","|Galileo mentioned that Duke’s full potential could be unleashed by you.|","|Current performance, while impressive, may not represent that full potential.|","|Decision Point: Attempt to unlock Duke’s latent capabilities through direct application of your authority.|","|Your eyes shine with brilliance as you make your choice.|","|You proceed to flood the body of Duke not with mere Phonemes of The First Tongue.|","|You release your Seals of Absolute Tongue into the body of this unique creature.|","|Beginning transfer...|","...!","|The 18 Primordial Seals enter Duke’s existence.|","|The Seal of Fire.|","|The Seal of Water.|","|The Seal of Earth.|","|The Seal of Air.|","|The Seal of Void.|","|The Seal of Light.|","|The Seal of Darkness.|","|The Seal of Life.|","|The Seal of Death.|","|The Seal of Time.|","|The Seal of Space.|","|The Seal of Order.|","|The Seal of Chaos.|","|The Seal of Unity.|","|The Seal of Division.|","|The Seal of Beginning.|","|The Seal of Ending.|","|The Seal of Paradox.|","|Duke stops and trembles.|","|The neon light around him buzzes with instability!|","|His form flickers between states of existence as the Primordial Seals integrate with whatever dormant potential lies within him.|","|But no grand changes occur.|","|The 18 Seals settle into his existence without triggering transformation.|","|Something is missing.|","|You continue.|","|Your 9 original Seals enter Duke’s body.|","|The Seal of Quintessence.|","|The Seal of Infinity.|","|The Seal of Tyranny.|","|The Seal of Fortune.|","|The Seal of Advantage.|","|The Seal of Narrative.|","|The Seal of Harvest.|","|The Seal of Hunger.|","|The Seal of Potential.|","|Duke stops completely.|","|He becomes utterly still.|","|And then...|","BOOM!","|The Wastes around you begin to shudder!|","|Everything in every direction becomes covered with neon brilliance!|","|The gray desolation is painted over with light that pulses in rhythms matching the heartbeat of Existence itself!|","|In the eyes of Duke, something unprecedented manifests.|","|An incandescent neon sun appears in one eye.|","|An incandescent neon moon appears in the other.|","|His Depth surges!|","|Intermediate... approaching Fundamental!|","|His existence reacts to your Seals and the breadth of The First Tongue they represent!|","|This was the key.|","|The 18 Primordial Phonemes alone were insufficient.|","|But combined with the 9 Phonemes you forged yourself?|","|The complete First Tongue, original and expanded, flowing through a creature born from that same linguistic foundation?|","|Transformation becomes inevitable.|","|AWAKENING DETECTED|","|Designation Update:|","|Former: Duke, Muspeli Lifeform|","|Current: Skoll, THE Herald of The Tongue, THE Steed of Mana|","|Core Nature:|","|Skoll moves at the speed that Mana moves to keep up the very fabric of Existence.|","|This is not conventional velocity. This is fundamental velocity.|","|Mana permeates all things. Mana connects all things. Mana IS the fabric that holds Existence together.|","|And Mana moves constantly, endlessly, to maintain that fabric’s integrity.|","|Skoll now moves at THAT speed.|","|The speed of existential maintenance. The speed of existential continuity. The speed of reality staying real.|","|Capabilities:|","|FIRST: Absolute Evasion. No entity below THE Absolute Depth can perceive or intercept Skoll’s movement.|","|SECOND: Mana Trails. Where Skoll travels, Mana concentration increases exponentially, leaving paths of enhanced existential stability.|","|THIRD: Tongue Resonance. As THE Herald of The Tongue, Skoll amplifies the authority of any First Tongue user in his presence.|","|FOURTH: Speed Transfer. Skoll can temporarily grant his velocity to riders or allies.|","|Loyalty: Absolute to THE Genesis Monarch, The One Who Awakened Him.|","...!","Noah’s eyes shone sharply at these prompts!","In the simulation, he sat atop a transformed being whose power now approached classifications that should have been impossible for a creature that had been a simple golden retriever moments ago.","But since he was viewing all of this simulation in Muspelheim...","His gaze briefly flashed over to the innocent looking Duke near him.","The golden retriever had his tongue out. His tail wagged slowly. He looked toward Noah with eyes full of simple canine devotion, completely oblivious to the potential sleeping within his fluffy form.","Duke tilted his head slightly, as if wondering why THE Genesis Monarch was staring at him so intensely.","Woof?","4/4 Onwards! Keep The Magic Castles and Golden Tickets coming!"]},{"number":4746,"title":"Chapter 4746: Chapter 4745: Simulation And Reality Collide! I","paragraphs":["Chapter 4745: Simulation And Reality Collide! I","Noah returned his gaze to the ongoing simulation.","He mentally noted that the first thing to be done after this ended was Duke’s transformation.","Because right now, the memories of the simulation showed the glorious transformed figure of Duke in the form of Skoll.","And what a figure it was!","The golden retriever’s form had undergone changes that elevated him from adorable companion to something genuinely majestic. A lion-like mane now wrapped around his neck and shoulders, composed of crystallized neon flames that flickered with colors that had no names. His vibrant golden fur carried traces of blue woven throughout, as if the authority of Mana itself had bled into every strand.","His form still remained that of a dog.","But majestic. Regal. Carrying himself with the dignity of something that knew exactly what it had become.","And those eyes!","An incandescent neon sun burned in one pupil. An incandescent neon moon glowed in the other. Day and night. Beginning and ending. The eternal cycle of Existence captured in the gaze of a very good boy who had transcended his original limitations.","His entire body emanated waves of THE Fundamental Depth!","Not approaching it. Not adjacent to it. Genuinely radiating it in pulses that made the corrupted Wastes around them stabilize wherever he stood.","Noah stroked his fur while seated atop him, feeling the warmth of captured starfire beneath his palm.","“Let’s go. As fast as you can.”","...!","Skoll’s response was immediate.","And terrifying.","The transformed Duke entirely disappeared alongside Noah!","Not moved. Not accelerated. Simply... gone.","Even the radiant glimmer of neon light that had surrounded them moments before was no longer visible. No trail. No afterimage. No indication that anything had been there at all.","Imperceptible!","This wasn’t speed that could be tracked or followed. This was speed that existed outside the framework of normal observation entirely.","|Simulation continues...|","|With the advancement of Skoll, you proceed to test his capabilities.|","|Results: Astonishing.|","|Speed Assessment:|","|Previous coverage rate with conventional travel: Hours per major region.|","|Previous coverage rate with base Duke: Minutes per major region.|","|Current coverage rate with Skoll: Seconds per major region.|","|You cover endless regions of the Wastes in a single second.|","|Distances that would have required hours before are crossed in the time it takes to blink.|","|The corrupted landscape blurs into meaningless smears of gray and ash.|","|You cover vast regions of The Wastes of THE Fallout systematically.|","|Encounters:|","|Multiple Scorched entities detected and engaged.|","|Surface Depth. Intermediate Depth. Creatures of flame and hunger and desperate survival.|","|Multiple Emerged entities detected and engaged.|","|None of them are what you’re looking for.|","|No trace of Lumivara. No echo of Ul’moreth. No signature of THE Weaver.|","|But the encounters are not wasted.|","|Skoll proves to be an eager participant in combat.|","|Being the good boy he is, he swallows Surface Depth entities in single gulps.|","|His neon flames consume their existence and convert it into fuel for his own advancement.|","|You collapse others personally.|","|Some transform into additional Fragments of Moirai Threads through your Perpetual Harvest.|","|Others have their Depths devoured to continue elevating your own immensity.|","|Your search continues.|","|One minute passes.|","|Vast territories have been covered. Over a Dozen enemies have been eliminated. Your power has grown incrementally through constant harvest.|","|But still no trace of your targets.|","|And then...|","|Your intuition begins to buzz.|","|Something is wrong.|","|The sensation is not logical. It is not based on evidence or observation. It is simply a feeling that rises from the depths of your existence with urgent insistence.|","|For Lumivara and Ul’moreth, time is running out!|","|Your efforts in the Wastes are not paying off quickly enough.|","|Decision Point: Alternative approach required.|","|You backtrack across the Wastes.|","|Destination: THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap once more.|","|You enter the Stoa of Dogmata once more.|","|THE Secretive Eon sits exactly where she was before.|","|This time, she doesn’t even glance your way.|","...!","Noah fully immersed himself into the simulation as the scene played out in front of him.","The prompts faded away, replaced by direct experience of the simulated future.","He stood in the Stoa of Dogmata with Skoll beside him, the transformed Duke’s neon flames casting strange shadows across the ancient pillars as he looked around. Eon remained seated with her legs crossed, her dark eyes fixed on the distant expanse ahead, completely ignoring his arrival.","Noah calmly brought out two objects.","The Fragment of THE Axiom of Attrition pulsed with authority that spoke of gradual erosion and patient victory.","The Fragment of THE Axiom of Differentiated Tongue burned with power that resonated with the very foundations of linguistic authority.","The light of two Axioms drew the attention of Eon.","She looked over, and for the first time since his arrival, her dark eyes held something other than dismissive disinterest.","“Both of these are yours,” Noah said calmly, “if you can track down where THE Weavers are and simply make a move to remove my people from there.”","...!","Eon looked at the two Fragments.","Her composed features shifted into something that might have been a smile.","“For these... we can make a transaction.”","Her voice remained measured, each word placed with precision that spoke of eons spent choosing exactly what to say.","“But their worth is enough for me to look for the signature of Absolutes in the Wastes. I can track down THE Weavers.” Her head tilted slightly. “That alone uses up what you’re giving. My intervention would require more. So I won’t intervene, but I can drop you off in that location as soon as I find them.”","...!","Noah’s eyes were sharp as he looked at Eon.","Man, she fucking sucked sometimes.","But this was progress!","From Eon, he should be able to learn where Lumivara and Ul’moreth were. The exact location that his own searches had failed to uncover despite covering vast territories with Skoll’s impossible speed.","And since this was a simulation, he wouldn’t lose anything!","The Fragments he offered here remained safely in his possession in actual Existence. He could test what leverage worked, discover her true price, and gain without losing anything.","As he was thinking all this, Eon’s gaze drifted away from the Fragments.","Her dark eyes settled on the burning visage of Skoll!","1/6"]},{"number":4747,"title":"Chapter 4747: Chapter 4746: Simulation And Reality Collide! II","paragraphs":["\" You seem to also have an interesting creature here.\"","Her voice carried notes of genuine curiosity that hadn’t been present before as this terrifying being turned her gaze towards Duke!","\" In exchange for it, I could put in the effort to save your people.\"","BOOM!","The weight of her words pressed against Noah’s existence!","...!","His eyes became sharp.","She wanted Duke?","He turned to look at the much more majestic dog who still held the same innocent qualities despite his transformation. Skoll’s tail wagged slightly at Noah’s attention, the neon sun and moon in his eyes shining with simple devotion that transcended his elevated classification.","A dog that even an Absolute wanted!","That was how unique Duke was. How valuable. How unprecedented.","And even though Noah could make the choice to give him away in this simulation, the choice of giving him away in real Existence was not possible.","Such a choice in the simulation would only lead to a fantasy that wasn’t achievable externally.","He wouldn’t dwell in fantasies.","And he wouldn’t sacrifice one life for another.","So...","\" My dog isn’t part of the deal.\"","His voice came calm and steady, brooking no negotiation on this point.","\" And I don’t want you to drop me off wherever they are. I want for us to go from outside this Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap to that location.\"","...!","Yes.","If Eon used her terrifying power to deny the very environment of the Fallout that stated no teleportation, Noah wouldn’t gain anything from it.","What he needed was the route!","How to get there from the areas he’d already mapped out with Skoll. The path that his own capabilities could actually traverse without relying on an Absolute’s reality-defying authority.","After he said such words, Eon smiled.","She nodded with the patience of someone who found his reasoning unique but acceptable.","Then she closed her eyes.","In the simulation, Noah focused on what happened next.","From her body...","BOOM!","He felt Existence being squeezed in a terrifying manner!","The sensation lasted for less than a nanosecond. A fraction of a fraction of a moment. But in that infinitesimal window, Noah felt pressure that made his own considerable weight feel like nothing. Authority that bent reality itself to extract information that should have been impossible to obtain.","The signature of THE Weavers, hidden somewhere in the vast corrupted expanse of the Wastes, identified and located through sheer overwhelming power.","And then it was over.","Eon opened her eyes calmly and rose from her seated position. Her small, delicate form unfolded with grace that spoke of movements refined across eons.","\" Alright. Found them. Let’s go.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply.","The power of an Absolute was displayed for barely a fraction of a nanosecond.","And it was fucking heavy!","She had done in that instant what he had been unable to do in minutes of searching with Skoll’s impossible speed. What his 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue couldn’t accomplish despite their weight and authority.","The gap between his current state and genuine Absolutes remained categorical.","But he was learning. Gathering information. Understanding exactly what he was dealing with.","With a calm gaze, Eon looked toward him.","\" Step on the platform here, and we can get going.\"","She waved her hand, and a clear white platform emerged from nowhere. It pulsed with unique THE Civilizational Authority that made Noah’s senses tingle with recognition of power far beyond his current classification.","He shook his head.","\" You go, and I will follow.\"","Eon smiled.","\" Oh?\"","Her gaze went to Skoll, the transformed Duke upon whom Noah was seated. The neon sun and moon in his eyes met her dark depths without flinching.","\" Keep up.\"","With such words...","BOOM!","She disappeared!","No trail. No warning. No gradual acceleration. Simply present one moment and gone the next, moving toward the location of THE Weavers with speed that defied conventional understanding.","Noah held on to Skoll.","And Skoll disappeared right behind her!","He wanted to know!","Just how obscene was the speed of Duke compared to a real Absolute?","Knowing this was critical. If the plan to run away from THE Weavers was going to be viable, he needed to understand exactly what Skoll could do against entities operating at THE Absolute Depth.","Could they escape if confrontation proved impossible?","Could they extract Lumivara and Ul’moreth before THE Weavers could respond?","The simulation would tell him.","And the simulation would not lie.","As Noah began to follow THE Secretive Eon atop Skoll, racing through the corrupted expanses of the Wastes...","The simulation flickered.","Just briefly. A momentary distortion in the otherwise seamless immersion that made Noah’s eyes narrow with sharp attention.","| WARNING: SIMULATION INTEGRITY COMPROMISED|","|The Full Moirai Thread utilizing the progression of a potential THE Existential Paradox Loop is discovering irregularities.|","|Core Issue:|","|Interactions with an Absolute and the continued display of simulation that portrays their Weavings of Existence is draining the capability of THE Moirai Thread at an exponential rate.|","|Previous Drain Rate: 0.3% per minute of simulation.|","|Current Drain Rate: 4.7% per minute while actively simulating Absolute-class entity.|","|Projected Consequence:|","| Early termination of simulation may occur before eventual collapse depending on continued interactions with Absolutes.|","|Definition of Early Termination:|","|The point at which the integrity of the simulation can no longer be maintained while accurately portraying Absolutes and their actions.|","|Critical Concern:|","| Ensuring that information and memories of the simulation do not feed back to the Absolutes being simulated.|","|Absolutes operate at a Scale of Existence where their perception extends into domains that should be inaccessible.|","|Even simulated versions of them carry echoes of this capability.|","|The longer an Absolute is portrayed within the simulation, the higher the risk that the real Absolute may gain awareness of being simulated.|","|Assessment:|","|Absolutes are too powerful.|","|Their very nature strains the boundaries of what THE Moirai Thread can safely model.|","|Recommendation:|","|Minimize direct interaction with simulated Absolutes.|","|Gather essential information quickly.|","|Prepare for potential early termination.|","|Current Simulation Integrity: 41%|","...!"]},{"number":4748,"title":"Chapter 4748: Chapter 4747: Simulation And Reality Collide! III","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes flashed sharply as he received this warning!","After all, what he was doing right now was considered a tremendously ridiculous thing.","Simulating a future reality.","Obtaining information he should have no access to.","Learning and interacting with an Absolute in such a simulation.","Their power of THE Absolute Depth was so overwhelming that even for things they did not know about... they could know about!","The very act of simulating them risked drawing their actual attention. Their real selves might sense echoes of being observed, being modeled, being used as pawns in someone else’s information gathering.","And he was getting another glimpse of this terrifying truth as he focused on following Eon while committing the regions of The Wastes of THE Fallout to memory.","Everything around them felt like a haze.","But Noah was seeing everything. Every distorted landmark. Every corrupted zone. Every twisted region of reality that had been reshaped by THE Fallout’s catastrophic energies.","Ahead of them, Eon seemed to be taking light steps.","Just casual, unhurried movements that looked almost lazy.","Yet she moved at speeds that Noah in Muspelheim in real Existence would never be able to follow!","As she moved, she turned her head back languidly to look at Skoll and his burning neon flames. The transformed Duke had his tongue out, flapping on the side as if he was having the time of his life chasing after her.","Such a good boy. Even when pursuing an Absolute across corrupted wastelands, he found joy in the simple act of running!","Eon’s eyes twisted into utterly deadly crescents of amusement.","\" Man, I want to abandon my principles and rob you right now of that little dog, Scale Breaker.\"","BOOM!","Her voice carried notes of genuine temptation beneath the casual delivery.","\" But ah, I’m one of the last good ones left. I’ll stick to my principles.\" She sighed with exaggerated regret. \" When you want to trade that cute doggy, let me know. For now, let’s see how quickly it can really go.\"","She waved her hand toward Skoll as if playing a game.","\" Little doggy, come on. Get!\"","...!","Skoll’s response was immediate and enthusiastic.","He surged forward with excitement, his neon flames blazing brighter as he accepted what he perceived as an invitation to play!","And shockingly, Eon accelerated to match!","Noah’s entire existence buzzed with immensity as his Seals of Absolute Tongue flowed into his eyes. He barely continued to grasp the surrounding landscape as Skoll and Eon pushed faster and faster!","The Wastes blurred into meaningless smears.","Landmarks disappeared before they could be properly observed, but he still observed them.","Reality itself seemed to protest the speeds being achieved within its corrupted boundaries.","And this continued for only a little while before Eon seemed to take it as a genuine challenge.","She went even faster.","And shockingly... she began to surge forward and disappear from their perception entirely!","One moment she was there, a small figure in white-blue robes taking casual steps through corrupted reality.","The next moment, she was simply... gone.","Skoll howled out!","The sound was glorious and majestic, carrying across the Wastes with authority that made nearby corruption stabilize in response. Neon plasma flames raged around his transformed body, blazing with intensity that exceeded anything he’d displayed before. His limbs churned with speed and power that defied comprehension, each stride seeming to glide on The First Tongue itself rather than the corrupted ground beneath them.","And yet...","Eon only got further and further away.","They almost lost her entirely!","Noah’s expression became heavy.","\" Slow down.\"","WAA!","Eon began to reappear before them soon after.","The Wastes around them constantly changed as she decelerated, regions shifting and reforming as their perception caught up to where she now waited. Her dark eyes twisted into a smile as she looked at Noah with the patience of someone who had just proven a very important point.","\" His speed is good.\"","Her voice came measured and unhurried, each word placed with precision.","\" Can be considered to touch a fraction of Absolute. But Absolute is far too grand, and far too varied.\"","She tilted her head slightly.","\" In front of THE Creature or me... the speed of that very good boy can only be considered a cute... oh, he’s a little fast.\"","The dismissal in her tone was gentle but absolute.","\"If your plan on saving your people from THE Weavers involves speeding away with them with little doggy here, I can tell you now that you will fail.\"","Her dark eyes held his without wavering.","\" Even a weak Absolute like THE Weavers will catch you in time. That initial burst of surprise of that speed will give you a lead, but they will catch you soon enough. You will be caught, Scale Breaker.\"","She glanced at Skoll with something that might have been genuine concern.","\" And this poor little doggy that you could give to me right now would also be caught by something as cruel as THE Weavers. What a shame that would be, Scale Breaker.\"","Her smile widened.","\" Do you want to change your choice now?\"","...!","WAA!","Her words were heavy.","But Noah remained calm.","\" Once we near their position, just let me know which direction to go towards without THE Weavers finding out about your existence. I will take the rest from there.\"","...!","He wanted it to be as authentic as possible.","Eon would not be with them when this simulation ended. He would be alone with Skoll in actual Existence, facing THE Weavers without an Absolute backing him up.","The aura of Eon would affect how things played out in the simulation, and he had to minimize discrepancies between what happened here and what would happen in reality.","As for her words and warning that his plan may fail...","Noah now knew this very well after observing her ridiculous speed.","But still, he had other cards up his sleeve.","There were still many things he could do. Or really, two things that he was planning out in his mind at this moment.","Contingencies upon contingencies.","Plans within plans.","Because Tyranny did not accept failure as an option.","Eon laughed.","The sound was light and almost musical, carrying across the corrupted Wastes with ease that spoke of someone genuinely entertained.","\" Don’t worry, Scale Breaker. I will take you exactly where you need to be.\"","Her smile held secrets that he couldn’t begin to fathom.","\" If you don’t want me to be perceivable to THE Weavers, I don’t have to stay away to make that happen. I can make it so that you see and perceive me, while a weak Absolute like THE Weavers...\"","She paused.","\"I can make it so that they cannot even perceive I am here.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4749,"title":"Chapter 4749: Chapter 4748: Simulation And Reality Collide! IV","paragraphs":["Terrifying words that almost stopped everything echoed out!","THE Secretive Eon.","Every time she spoke, he had to reevaluate her power again.","Such a thing was just obscene!","She could make it so that even another Absolute could not perceive her?","\"...\"","Did this not mean that if Noah wasn’t careful enough, an Absolute like her could entirely hide from his perception while following him around?","He had to be very careful about this.","He had to make sure that he didn’t have a body around an Absolute that made any trips to THE Infiniverse or other important locations.","Because even without knowing it, there could have been an Absolute watching him this entire time.","...!","As he had such thoughts, the simulation continued.","|Simulation Resuming.|","|While contemplating the implications of Absolute-class concealment capabilities, you and Skoll follow Eon across the Wastes.|","|You plan for multiple contingencies on how you will navigate this situation once the simulation ends.|","|Mental planning in progress.|","|All contingencies carry significant risk against genuine Absolute opposition.|","|Warning:|","|The integrity of this simulation continues to deteriorate with the continued revelation of the Weavings of an Absolute.|","|Current Simulation Integrity: 24%|","|In preparation for the eventual expected meeting with another Absolute soon, resources are being allocated to maintain viable simulation integrity for slightly more time after the introduction of THE Weavers.|","|Estimated additional simulation time after Absolute contact: 1 minute before critical integrity failure.|","|Use this time wisely.|","|Navigation Progress:|","|You continue mapping out the regions of the Wastes.|","|Even with the speed of Eon, an Absolute, it takes a total of 30 seconds to cross the relevant portions of the Wastes.|","|30 seconds at Absolute velocity.|","|The scale of Observable Existence post-Fallout is staggering.|","|This allows you to get a glimpse of just how far and how complex Observable Existence has become.|","|What you now understand and know is just a fraction of Everything.|","|The territories you mapped with Skoll earlier represent a tiny corner of what exists out here.|","|Humbling. Terrifying. Motivating.|","|Approaching target location...|","...!","Eon slowed down.","The corrupted landscape around them began to stabilize into something more recognizable as they approached whatever destination her Absolute perception had identified.","She smiled.","\" Oh?\"","Her voice carried notes of genuine surprise.","\" Those carrying traces of your Way actually already managed to enter Half-Step Absolute Depth?\"","She glanced back at Noah with eyes that sparkled with renewed interest.","\" What a unique thing, Scale Breaker. Your pillars are more impressive than I assumed.\"","...!","As Eon said this, Noah sensed the immense Weavings of Existence ahead. He could sense glimmers of The First Tongue as if she was talking about Half-Step Absolute Depth...this should be Ul’moreth? Up ahead, he sensed everything!","Auras of utter majesty bloomed across his perception!","He felt the maddening glimmer of Absolute pressing down over everything. A weight that made his own considerable heaviness feel insignificant. Authority that crushed the very air and bent reality into shapes that served purposes he couldn’t comprehend.","And yet...","Skoll’s speed was only barely affected.","The transformed Duke could still cross through such a region of oppression. His neon flames flickered against the Absolute pressure but did not dim. His stride remained sure even as reality itself groaned beneath the weight bearing down upon it.","Good boy. Such a good boy!","Eon smiled calmly.","\" Well... we are here, Scale Breaker.\"","She turned to face him fully, her small form somehow seeming larger than the forces pressing down around them.","\" I’ve kept up my end of the bargain.\"","Her dark eyes held something that might have been respect. Or pity. Or simply the patient observation of someone watching events unfold according to patterns she had seen countless times before.","\" Good luck.\"","With such words, Eon disappeared from his perception entirely.","No warning. No transition. Simply present one moment and gone the next, her Absolute concealment rendering her invisible even to the senses of THE Weavers who dominated this region.","And Noah arrived at the point he had been seeking this entire time.","His perception finally observed the glorious hairy entity that was Ul’moreth!","The ancient Ginnu Lifeform stood valiantly, his obsidian-gold hair flowing with defiance that refused to bow even before Absolute pressure. His massive form was positioned protectively, placing himself between the threats ahead and...","Lumivara!","She was heavily injured!","Her brilliant form flickered with instability, her Weavings damaged in ways that made Noah’s heart clench with fury. She had fought. She had resisted. And she had paid the price for standing against forces that exceeded her classification.","But she was alive.","They were both alive.","For now.","Far ahead of them, a Legion of THE entities watched on with the patient hunger of predators who knew their prey had nowhere left to run.","At the forefront stood the glorious First Leader.","Gilgamesh.","His presence radiated authority that exceeded anything Noah had encountered among THE Fundamental Depth entities. A being of genuine power and absolute loyalty to THE Living Paradox!","And above all of them...","Three shrouded figures floated grandly with a glorious air of Absolute!","Robes and hoods covered their forms entirely, concealing whatever lay beneath in shadows that seemed deeper than mere fabric should allow. Their might pressed down like sharp blades hovering over Ul’moreth and Lumivara, ready to fall at any moment.","THE Weavers.","Three of them. Not one Absolute, but three!","Noah had found them.","But what would be the cost?","How would this perilous situation be navigated?","|Simulation Integrity: 18%|","|The Clock is ticking, Master.|","|What will you do?|","What would he do in this situation?","The answer was both difficult and easy.","A great man once said that in the face of hardship, the best way out is always through.","So Noah... would simply charge through!","He knew the simulation would progressively have its integrity eroded, especially with the simulation of another Absolute and what their capabilities were. The clock was ticking. Every second spent observing was a second wasted.","So when he went forward...","He went in with a bang!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4750,"title":"Chapter 4750: Chapter 4749: Simulation And Reality Collide! V","paragraphs":["With glorious speed, Skoll surged toward the confrontation ahead!","As if things were playing out in slow motion, Noah saw the eyes of THE Weavers land on him and his mount. Everything around them solidified and became unfathomably heavy. The air itself compressed. Reality groaned beneath the attention of three Absolutes focusing their perception on a single point.","And an instant later, he appeared in front of Ul’moreth and Lumivara!","He gazed up toward THE Weavers gloriously, his expression imperious and utterly without fear.","\" You have been looking for me?\"","...!","HUUM!","His entrance was fast and unfathomably rapid!","It carried with it the glimmer of power, of velocity that only an Absolute would have! The very fact that he had crossed such distance under their suppressive authority suggested capabilities that exceeded what his classification should allow.","Behind him, Ul’moreth and Lumivara were astonished.","But before they could even say anything or react, Noah sent them both a mental message.","| Move quickly. No time to explain. Send me the memories of the entire path you have taken since THE Belly of Existence was torn open until you arrived here. Now.|","He did this for a critical reason.","If one of his two plans was forced to come to fruition, if he was forced to utilize THE Existential Paradox Loop and reverse time to an Anchor Point, he could find Lumivara and Ul’moreth across the Wastes even before they came across Gilgamesh and THE Weavers!","Prevention rather than rescue.","Both Lumivara and Ul’moreth did not delay.","Vast swathes of memories flooded into Noah’s perception. The Wastes they had crossed. The landmarks they had passed. The route they had taken through corrupted reality after THE Belly of Existence was torn open.","Everything.","While they did this, Noah also gave the command to Skoll.","| Speed Transfer to Ul’moreth and Lumivara. Now.|","The transformed Duke’s capabilities flowed outward, granting his impossible velocity to the two beings Noah had come to rescue.","He did all of this in the span of an instant.","And then he gazed up at THE Weavers.","Oh!","They were a horrid wonder to observe!","Three figures floated above everything, their robes and hoods finally parting enough for their faces to become visible beneath the shadowed fabric.","Ancient.","Decrepit .","Withered beyond what any mortal existence should endure and still function.","Their skin was papyrus-thin and gray, stretched over bones that seemed too prominent, too sharp, too angular to belong to anything that had ever been young. Deep wrinkles carved canyons across their features, each line representing eons of existence that had worn away everything soft and left only hardened purpose behind.","Their mouths were thin slashes that curved into expressions that might have been smiles or might have been the natural configuration of lips that had forgotten how to do anything else.","And their eyes!","Shockingly, those ancient orbs swirled with golden light!","Not the warm gold of dawn or the rich gold of treasure. This was the cold, calculating gold of fate itself, of threads being measured and cut, of destinies being woven and unraveled according to designs that predated the beings whose lives they manipulated.","THE Weavers!","Entities who had existed since before who kne when, who had woven the very fabric of THE Loom, who now served THE Living Paradox with the patient certainty of entities who believed they already knew how every story ended.","The more Noah locked his gaze with them, the more he felt their attention pressing against his existence like blades seeking weak points.","So he spoke.","Grandly.","Tyrannically.","\" You were looking for me, but you had not expected me to reach Absolute so quickly?\"","His voice carried weight that made the surrounding reality compress further.","\" How does it feel that my mere presence here is already locking away access to The First Tongue for all of you?\"","...!","He spoke such words grandly!","The Thesis he had utilized against THE Living Spirit and his forces was not contested in Muspelheim. He could apply it anywhere! So he began applying it freely and grandly, his authority as The One Who Laid The Claim extending outward to restrict access to The First Tongue for all who opposed him.","Around him, he began to move on to his next phase of planning.","After claiming to be an Absolute, he would bluff as if a terrifying showdown was about to unfold.","And then...he would run with Ul’moreth and Lumivara!","A moment of surprise that would decide everything!","They would run with the speed of an Absolute, and a chase would ensue. But even then, he had a plan for this. Reversing time was currently the last resort as it affected too many things.","But just as he was about to continue...","BZZT!","The immersive simulation flickered!","Not gently. Not gradually. The entire constructed reality around him shuddered with instability that spoke of imminent collapse.","|CRITICAL WARNING|","| A horrid discovery has been made.|","|Additional designations of THE Weavers identified:|","|THE Moirai.|","|THE Daughters of THE Night.|","|THE Spinners of Fate.|","|Core Capability:|","|They hold unfathomable control over fates and potentialities.|","|They perceive the threads of possibility that connect some futures to some pasts.|","|They sense when those threads are being manipulated by outside forces.|","|Current Status:|","|They are about to discover that this is a simulation.|","|They are about to perceive that another entity is encroaching upon their Absolute domain of fate and potential futures.|","|If this discovery is completed, your identity and location will be exposed to genuine Absolutes.|","|Emergency Protocol Initiated:|","|To prevent discovery...|","|To protect your anonymity...|","|To preserve the element of surprise that represents your only advantage...|","| THE Moirai Thread you utilized has snapped itself prematurely.|","|Simulation terminated.|","|All gathered information has been preserved.|","|Your existence remains hidden from THE Weavers’ perception.|","| For now.|","HUUM!","Golden brilliance erupted all around!","The immersive illusion shattered like glass being struck by a hammer, fragments of simulated reality dissolving into streams of golden light that flowed back into Noah’s existence.","He found himself fully back in Muspelheim.","THE Infiniverse floated nearby, its blue-gold radiance pulsing with patient attention.","Galileo watched with ears fully erect, his fluffy form practically vibrating with questions he knew better than to ask at this moment.","Duke sat with his tongue out, looking toward Noah with innocent eyes that had no idea what potential slept within his fluffy form.","Surtra and the other Muspeli Lifeforms gazed at him with expressions ranging from awe to concern.","And in the distance, he could sense Sigrid, Ra’Zan, Riya, The First Farmer, Titano, Protos, and multiple others who had witnessed his motionless form surrounded by golden light for however long the simulation had lasted.","Noah’s expression became heavier.","His eyes flickered brilliantly as he processed everything he had learned!"]},{"number":4751,"title":"Chapter 4751: Chapter 4750: Simulation And Reality Collide! VI","paragraphs":["Chapter 4750: Simulation And Reality Collide! VI","THE Weavers were THE Moirai. Fate manipulators who could sense when their domain was being encroached upon. The simulation had nearly exposed him to genuine Absolutes who would have then known exactly where to look for the one who dared to peer into futures they controlled.","But he had what he needed.","The route through the Wastes.","The knowledge of Duke’s transformation.","The understanding of what he faced and what his limitations were.","He turned toward THE Infiniverse.","“I will go and get Lumivara and Ul’moreth back. Ruination will bring my body that she controls here to Muspelheim. Focus on doing a partial simulation with it focused on THE Living Concept first.”","...!","He gave such orders rapidly.","THE Infiniverse pulsed with acknowledgment, and Noah could sense Ruination’s presence already shifting to comply with his commands.","Right after, he looked toward Galileo and Surtra.","“We will get to catch up after. For now, there is much to be done.”","His gaze turned to the golden retriever who perked up excitedly at the attention.","“Duke...”","The dog’s tail wagged with enthusiasm that transcended species barriers. His eyes shone with simple devotion that had no idea it was about to be transformed into something glorious.","“Let’s go.”","HUUM!","Duke blazed with brilliant neon light!","Noah seamlessly proceeded to sit on Duke’s back, his body settling into position with the familiarity of someone who had already done this many times in a simulation that no longer existed.","And they disappeared!","The burst of speed was explosive. Immediate. Neon light streaked across the burning skies of Muspelheim for a fraction of a second before vanishing entirely, leaving behind astonished Muspeli Lifeforms and even Sigrid, Ra’Zan, Riya, The First Farmer, Titano, Protos, and multiple others.","They would be filled in in time.","But time was exactly what Noah didn’t have currently.","—","In the Wastes of THE Fallout.","Noah appeared in the chaotic and grandiose Wastes as all the events that had played out in the simulation buzzed in his mind.","Gray desolation stretched endlessly in all directions.","Ashen clouds swirled overhead with energies that would destroy lesser beings.","Corrupted reality shifted and reformed with each passing moment.","In the simulation, he had lost all the Fragments of the Axioms to Eon. But he currently held all three.","The Fragment of THE Axiom of Mayhem.","The Fragment of THE Axiom of Attrition.","The Fragment of THE Axiom of Differentiated Tongue.","In turn, he had waves of information and a terrifying, dangerous future.","But his eyes still blazed with possibility!","It would be difficult, yes.","But not impossible.","For him, impossibility would always ever be... a suggestion.","So.","The first thing to be done at this moment was the transformation Duke had undergone in the simulation.","But for real.","He turned his gaze on Duke who had not yet transformed into Skoll. The golden retriever sat on the corrupted ground with his tongue out, tail wagging slowly, completely oblivious to what was about to happen.","Noah’s existence buzzed.","His glorious Seals began to be released.","The 18 Primordial Seals of Absolute Tongue flowed from his existence and into Duke’s body!","Fire. Water. Earth. Air. Void. Light. Darkness. Life. Death. Time. Space. Order. Chaos. Unity. Division. Beginning. Ending. Paradox.","Duke trembled as the Seals integrated with his existence!","The neon light around him buzzed with instability, his form flickering between states as primordial authority settled into whatever dormant potential lay within him.","But no grand changes occurred.","Not yet.","Noah continued.","His 9 original Seals entered Duke’s body!","Quintessence. Infinity. Tyranny. Fortune. Advantage. Narrative. Harvest. Hunger. Potential.","Duke stopped completely.","He became utterly still.","And then...","BOOM!","The Wastes around them began to shudder!","Everything in every direction became covered with neon brilliance! The gray desolation was painted over with light that pulsed in rhythms matching the heartbeat of Existence itself!","|AWAKENING CONFIRMED|","|As foreseen through the usage of THE Moirai Thread, the transformation has manifested in actual Existence.|","|The dormant potential within Duke has been unlocked through exposure to the complete First Tongue.|","|18 Primordial Phonemes alone were insufficient.|","|Combined with the 9 Forged Phonemes created by THE Genesis Monarch?|","|Transformation became inevitable.|","|Former Designation: Duke, Muspeli Lifeform, Anomalous Speed Entity|","|Current Designation: Skoll, THE Herald of The Tongue, THE Steed of Mana|","|Classification: Awakened Absolute-Adjacent Entity|","|Core Nature: Moves at the speed that Mana moves to keep up the very fabric of Existence.|","|The prophecy of simulation has become the reality of now.|","|Skoll has been born.|","...!","Before Noah, the transformed Duke stood in all his glory.","A lion-like mane now wrapped around his neck and shoulders, composed of crystallized neon flames that flickered with colors that had no names. His vibrant golden fur carried traces of blue woven throughout, as if the authority of Mana itself had bled into every strand.","His form still remained that of a dog.","But majestic and regal!","An incandescent neon sun burned in one pupil.","An incandescent neon moon glowed in the other.","His entire body emanated waves of THE Fundamental Depth!","Noah breathed calmly.","He reached out and stroked the fur of Skoll, feeling warmth that pulsed with captured foldfire beneath his palm. The transformed Duke’s eyes shone with glorious vibrancy, but beneath all that existential power, the same innocent devotion remained.","Such a good boy.","Even as THE Herald of The Tongue, he was still a very good boy!","“Alright. Let’s do things for real now.”","Noah’s voice came steady and sure.","“It will be dangerous, but danger and struggles go hand in hand. In the end, there should be glory as long as the difficulty is passed.”","He met Skoll’s glowing eyes directly.","“Ready?”","...!","He said such words knowing exactly what was coming.","THE Weavers. THE Moirai. Three genuine Absolutes who controlled fates and potentialities, who would sense any disturbance in the threads of destiny they wove.","But Skoll only blinked happily.","His expression remained innocent despite his transformation.","“Woof!”","Noah patted Skoll again. And just like the Simulation...","“Let’s go. As fast as you can.”","...!","Both of their bodies began to be covered by neon light that blazed brighter with each passing moment. The corrupted Wastes around them bent away from their combined radiance, reality itself recognizing that something unprecedented was about to move through its damaged fabric.","The first plan of a chase would be carried out.","And Noah had an idea of exactly where this chase would go.","Eventually, he could not outrun an Absolute.","The simulation had proven that definitively. Even Skoll’s impossible speed could only touch a fraction of what genuine Absolutes could achieve. THE Weavers would catch them in time.","But where he planned to run toward...","The tools to bypass this difficulty would appear.","And this one wouldn’t even necessarily be reliant on THE Secretive Eon!","They disappeared.","Neon light streaked across the Wastes of THE Fallout, carrying THE Genesis Monarch and THE Herald of The Tongue toward a confrontation that would determine whether his pillars survived or fell!","6/6 Onwards!"]},{"number":4752,"title":"Chapter 4752: Chapter 4751: Si Vis Pacem, Para Bellum I","paragraphs":["Si vis pacem, para bellum.","If you want peace, prepare for war.","The ancient words had echoed through countless civilizations across countless eras, spoken by generals and philosophers and common folk alike who understood a fundamental truth about Existence.","Peace was not a gift freely given.","Peace was not something that simply happened because one wished for it strongly enough.","Peace was a fortress that had to be built with blood and iron and the willingness to use both. It was a garden that could only flourish when surrounded by walls high enough to keep out those who would trample its flowers. It was a dream that required nightmares to be faced and conquered before it could become reality!","The pacifist who refused to raise a blade would watch everything they loved burn while congratulating themselves on their moral purity.","The warrior who never knew when to sheathe their blade would drown in blood of their own making until nothing remained worth protecting.","But the one who understood the paradox? The one who loved peace so deeply that they would wage war against anything that threatened it?","That one could build something that lasted!","Noah...could be considered very similar to THE Peacemaker in this regard.","He also loved peace.","He loved farming and tending to crops and watching things grow under his careful attention. He loved the quiet satisfaction of creation rather than destruction. He loved seeing his people flourish, seeing his Civilization expand, seeing the seeds he planted bloom into something beautiful.","But for his own peace?","For the safety of his people?","He would go to war with Existence itself.","This time, he was only going to war with a part of Existence.","The forces of THE Living Paradox!","His mind was filled with immensity as he crossed The Wastes of THE Fallout atop Skoll. Everything was absolutely mapped out. He knew exactly where he needed to go. Every corrupted landmark, every distorted region, every twisted zone of reality that the simulation had burned into his memory.","The route was clear.","The destination was certain.","And how could he explain the sensation that came as he got closer and closer to THE Weavers?","It was actually... serenity.","Strange, wasn’t it?","Heading toward three genuine Absolutes who could crush him with a thought, who controlled fates and potentialities, who had pinned his pillars down and prepared to collapse them.","And he felt serene.","Whatever was coming, let it come.","HUUM!","His Formless Depth and immensity roiled within his existence!","His Seals vibrated with terrifying weight! Twenty-seven concentrated expressions of everything he had become, everything he represented, everything he would continue to build.","There was no fear.","Even while going against an Absolute, there was no fear!","It wasn’t because he knew how things would turn out. The simulation had been terminated before he could see the full outcome of this confrontation. He was flying partially blind into a situation that could result in his collapse.","But simply because this was his Way.","Simply because he felt his immensity that denied anything that wished to go against him!","Tyranny did not bow.","Tyranny did not hesitate.","Tyranny stood in the open and dared Existence to challenge it.","So he patted Skoll’s fur calmly.","The transformed Duke’s neon plasma flames raged around them both, blazing with colors that had no names. The incandescent sun and moon in Skoll’s eyes burned with excitement. His mane of crystallized fire billowed backward as they moved at speeds that made reality itself struggle to keep up.","Everything seemed to play out in slow motion.","The corrupted landscape stretching endlessly.","The ashen clouds parting before their passage.","The weight of Absolute authority growing heavier with each instant.","And then...","He felt it.","That oppressive aura of THE Absolute Depth!","It pressed down upon everything like the weight of mountains made from concepts rather than stone. It crushed lesser beings simply through proximity. It demanded acknowledgment from reality itself.","And Noah passed through it!","BOOM!","The scene that unfolded was glorious!","Noah crossed into the standoff between THE Weavers and his pillars with speed that carried the signature of something only Absolutes should possess!","Ul’moreth stood valiantly, his obsidian-gold hair flowing with defiance despite the injuries that marked his massive form.","Lumivara flickered behind him, heavily damaged but alive, her brilliant existence still burning with the stubbornness of one who refused to fall.","The Legion of THE entities watched from a distance, Gilgamesh at their forefront with an expression of cold calculation.","And above everything, three shrouded figures floated with the overwhelming presence of Absolutes who had never once considered the possibility of being challenged.","Noah appeared directly before them.","He looked straight at THE Weavers!","Their decrepit faces became visible beneath their hoods. Ancient. Withered. Papyrus-thin skin stretched over bones that seemed too prominent. Deep wrinkles carving canyons across features that had existed since before differentiation.","And their eyes!","Those golden orbs swirled with light that spoke of fates being measured and cut.","But now, those ancient eyes pulsed with something new.","Surprise.","\" THE Daughters of THE Night.\"","Noah’s voice emerged with weight that compressed the surrounding reality.","\" You have been seeking an Absolute of The First Tongue. One of those who laid the claim to the Oldest Paradox of Existence.\"","His gaze held theirs without flinching.","\"If Paradox came himself, I would understand. But he actually sent you to me to die...\"","His lips curved into a smile that held no warmth whatsoever.","\"Are you ready?\"","HUUM!","His words came off filled with the vibrancy of The First Tongue!","Immensity backed his Seals as they manifested externally around himself and Skoll!","The Absolute Seal of Quintessence blazed into existence, spinning with patterns that spoke of fundamental perfection!","The Absolute Seal of Infinity stretched outward, its endless designs conveying boundlessness made visible!","The Absolute Seal of Tyranny pressed down upon everything, demanding submission from reality itself!","The Absolute Seal of Fortune! The Absolute Seal of Advantage! The Absolute Seal of Narrative! The Absolute Seal of Harvest! The Absolute Seal of Hunger! The Absolute Seal of Potential!","Nine Seals that belonged only to him!","Nine letters of The First Tongue that he had forged himself!","They displayed externally around his form like a constellation spelling out his name in the oldest language!","Oh!","There were...many things that made what happened next possible!"]},{"number":4753,"title":"Chapter 4753: Chapter 4752: Si Vis Pacem, Para Bellum II","paragraphs":["The glimmer of Phonemes shining around him with majesty that none here recognized. His words reminding all those present that his claim made him among the select company of THE Creature and THE Living Paradox and THE Primordial Chaos.","His dominant gaze.","His blazing eyes.","His words that made him look utterly glorious!","His body billowed with liquid flames that seemed to pour from his very existence! Blue-gold fire of concentrated Mana spilled from his nose and mouth with every breath, as if he was releasing immensity at every second!","He looked like a fiend descending to deliver judgment.","He looked like something that should not be challenged.","He looked like an Absolute.","All of this gave him an extremely enticing and magnetic allure!","Momentarily, even the distant Gilgamesh felt something stir within him. The First Leader who never felt fear found his blood beginning to flow with possibility. His eyes shone with calculations that had not existed moments before.","Could this entity actually be what he claimed?","Could THE First Tongue have truly produced something on this level?","And THE Weavers...","A flash of surprise flickered across those decrepit faces!","A moment of hesitation as they looked at him closely!","Immensity gathered around them as if they were questioning themselves, questioning what they perceived, questioning whether this confrontation would proceed as they had originally planned!","And in that hesitation.","The moment Noah looked into those decrepit faces and golden pupils and saw that brief flash of uncertainty...","He raised his hand.","THE Absolute Seal of Infinity began to spin above his palm, burning with patterns of boundlessness that made space itself groan!","\" When you fuck around...\"","His voice carried across the Wastes with the inevitability of judgment being delivered.","\" Eventually, you find out.\"","HUUM!","The distant Gilgamesh and the weaker THE entities from THE Loom stepped back slightly!","The weight of his words and Seals pressed against their existence with force that demanded respect!","And...!","And...!","WAP!","As everyone waited to see what this entity on the caliber of THE Creature and THE Living Paradox and THE Primordial Chaos would do...","Neon light flickered!","He, Skoll, and the shocked Lumivara and stern Ul’moreth disappeared!","Gone in an instant!","Extracted from the confrontation with speed that left afterimages of neon flame burning in the corrupted air!","...!","\"...!\"","Gilgamesh was astonished.","He froze completely, his ancient mind struggling to process what had just occurred. An entity had appeared, claimed Absolute status, displayed power that seemed to support that claim...","And then ran away?","And momentarily, THE Weavers also paused!","Their golden eyes flickered with confusion that beings of their classification rarely experienced. Their decrepit faces twisted with expressions that cycled through surprise, uncertainty, and then...","Understanding.","They had been played.","This entity had never intended to fight.","This entity had used presence and words and displayed power to create a moment of hesitation, a window of opportunity, and then exploited it with speed that should not have been possible for someone of his apparent classification.","An instant later...","BOOM!","An utterly overpowering and immense aura spilled from THE Weavers like an endless sea!","The Wastes around them cracked and fractured under the pressure of their fury! Reality itself screamed as three Absolutes released their suppressed authority in response to being deceived!","Their faces showed anger that had not touched them in eons!","Their voices spoke in unison, three ancient beings expressing the same sentiment as one!","\" VILE!\"","BOOM!","The word carried weight that would have collapsed anything below THE Fundamental Depth instantly!","An instant after, the Wastes around them fractured like broken mirrors!","THE Weavers disappeared, giving chase toward a direction only they could perceive! Their authority over fate and potentiality allowed them to track the threads of possibility that connected their quarry to their destination!","The chase had begun!","A moment after they shot out, Gilgamesh shook his head with incredulity.","Then he followed!","An Absolute had been bullshitted!","Three of them, actually!","THE Daughters of THE Night, THE Moirai, THE Weavers who controlled fates and potentialities...","Had been deceived by presence alone!","The Wastes of THE Fallout trembled as the chase thundered through corrupted reality!","---","Atop Skoll.","Noah felt the warm embrace of Lumivara who hugged him from behind.","\" Master! You were gone for such a long time! For eons I waited! For so many years... and... and...!\"","The little fox was badly injured. Her brilliant form flickered with instability, her Weavings damaged in ways that made Noah’s heart pulse. But she had him now. Her crimson-gold blood came to cover his back as she pressed against him, seemingly letting out all her grievances in that single desperate embrace.","Noah couldn’t help but soften his gaze.","He turned around to pat her head gently, his fingers running through fur that still burned with stubborn radiance despite everything she had endured.","Skoll continued to run at the fastest speed possible.","At this moment, Noah, Lumivara, and Ul’moreth were all atop the transformed Duke. Raging neon flames of The First Tongue surrounded them, blazing with colors that had no names. Noah’s Seals burned around the group in protective constellation, each one pulsing with weight that pressed against reality itself.","A Thesis was already activated.","| Skoll is fastest in Existence!|","The declaration rang through the fabric of the Wastes, asserting dominance over the concept of velocity itself. It wouldn’t hold forever against genuine Absolutes, but every fraction of advantage mattered.","While Lumivara hugged him, Noah’s gaze also came onto Ul’moreth.","The ancient Ginnu Lifeform’s radiant hairy figure seemed a bit dim after standing against THE Weavers for so long. The countless hairs around his body that usually blazed with obsidian-gold authority had lost some of their luster.","But Noah could feel his smile at this moment.","\" You have grown, Little Anomaly.\"","Ul’moreth’s voice emerged warm despite their desperate circumstances.","\" Even that doesn’t seem right at this moment... The First Anomaly? The Tongue Anomaly? Mmm... The Mana Anomaly?\"","He seemed to be genuinely contemplating what to call Noah now.","\" Either way, a lot has changed from Ginnungagap, but here we are again.\"","...!","Here they were again.","Noah patted Lumivara as he looked toward Ul’moreth with a smile. He glanced back behind them where the allure of an Absolute felt infinitely close, but it had not arrived before their perception just yet.","He replied calmly.","\" Here we are again. Last time, Absolutes were converging around us in Ginnungagap, and this time, it seems about the same. We just have to get past it ourselves.\"","His eyes blazed with certainty.","\" There’s a lot of time to catch up on, but first... is survival. You’ll see a few things here and there, so don’t be too surprised.\"","Yes!","One had to be ready for surprises!","At this moment, Noah was making a straight beeline toward THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap!","Not because of THE Secretive Eon, no.","He knew she wouldn’t move a hand to help. The simulation had proven that definitively. She would watch him struggle and fall without lifting a finger unless the price was right.","No.","He was going to the same location another body of his had arrived at. The entrance in the Stoa of Dogmata where he was supposed to save the Disciple of THE Secretive Eon.","An entity of THE Fundamental Depth.","And yet even Eon could not go to save her Disciple.","She had said THE Fallout had corrupted many things in an obscene manner. That there were Corrupted Domains with strange Weavings of Existence that didn’t follow conventional logic.","That there was a region ahead that likely nullified power through some ancient methodology.","Perhaps it stripped away accumulated Weight.","Perhaps it enforced a baseline state on all who entered.","Perhaps it did something else entirely.","These were all words Eon had said to him when she showed him the fairy-like image of her Disciple who had gotten stuck in that place!","And Eon herself did not enter to retrieve her.","She said it was for one reason or another, but what was real and what was fake?","In Noah’s mind, a place an Absolute did not wish to enter because of whatever undeniable effect such a Corrupted region had... would be a place THE Weavers would think twice before entering!","And if they did enter?","His body there had already done a partial simulation for what he could expect in that location!","If THE Weavers did enter it... it may very well be their coffin!"]},{"number":4754,"title":"Chapter 4754: Chapter 4753: Si Vis Pacem, Para Bellum III","paragraphs":["This was his ideal plan.","Not to reverse time.","But to utilize THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap. The region within it in The Stoa of Dogmata that had been gloriously distorted by THE Fallout. A core domain of THE Vault of Ginnungapbefore it was corrupted!","They simply had to reach it.","But...","HUUM!","At this moment, like a burning sun, the scorching aura of THE Weavers raged behind them!","It pressed against reality with force that made the corrupted Wastes crack and splinter! The weight of three Absolutes in pursuit created pressure that would have collapsed anything below THE Fundamental Depth instantly!","Their voices echoed out.","Glorious.","Terrifying.","Three heavy, scratching voices speaking one after another in sequence that made the air itself recoil!","\" Can the Claimer...\"","\"...of THE First Tongue...\"","\"...be such a coward?!\"","The words overlapped and intertwined, each voice completing the thought of the one before!","\" One of THE Four...\"","\"...running like a little bitch?...\"","\"...can your Way even survive such cowardice actions?!\"","...!","Such terrifying words echoed out!","Behind them, the sound as if Existence was breaking boomed through the Wastes! Obsidian-gold glimmers of light began to bloom as it felt like THE Weavers were getting ever closer! The threads of fate they controlled were pulling them inexorably toward their quarry!","Lumivara remained embracing Noah as if nothing else mattered.","Her injured form pressed against his back with desperate determination. Whatever happened, she would not let go. Whatever came, she would face it with him.","And Ul’moreth seemingly did not even pay attention to that screeching set of voices.","The ancient Ginnu Lifeform looked toward Noah with veiled eyes that seemingly held immense belief in him!","He had seen Noah grow from a curious anomaly in Ginnungagap to something that made Absolutes pause.","He believed.","Noah couldn’t betray this belief!","\" In three nanoseconds...\"","One of THE Weavers’ voices cut through the chaos with terrible precision!","\"... You will be captured in my inescapable net, Little Coward of The First Tongue!\"","WAA!","THE Weavers had their voices echo out again!","And at this time... far ahead, the outside boundary of THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap appeared!","That massive crimson-gold cloudy barrier that extended for countless miles, shrouded by the ashen clouds and flames of THE Fallout! The entrance to a domain that predated The First Tongue’s differentiation!","Noah’s eyes shone sharply!","He went even faster!","Skoll’s neon flames blazed with intensity that exceeded anything he had displayed before! The transformed Duke pushed past limits that should have been absolute, driven by loyalty and the desperate need to protect his master and those his master cared about!","They surged toward the boundary!","And the moment they approached...","CRACK !","The terrifying figures of THE Weavers shattered space behind them to finally become visible!","Three decrepit forms wrapped in robes and hoods, their ancient faces twisted with fury, their golden eyes blazing with the light of fate itself being manipulated!","The two sides managed to observe each other briefly once more!","Noah stared into those multiple golden eyes!","He saw rage. He saw determination. He saw the absolute certainty of beings who had never once failed to catch their prey!","And then he disappeared into THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap!","BOOM !","Without fail, THE Weavers silently charged forward to follow!","Their obsidian-gold authority blazed around them as they crossed the boundary without hesitation! Whatever dangers this Corrupted Domain held, they would face them! Whatever price had to be paid, they would pay it!","The Claimer of THE First Tongue would not escape!","---","Across the boundary.","An instant later, things played out as if in slow motion.","Noah, Lumivara, and Ul’moreth seated on Skoll appeared in the Stoa of Dogmata!","The endless colonnade of pillars stretched in all directions, each one carved from crystallized authority that predated differentiation itself. Inscriptions of ancient Dogmata glowed upon their surfaces.","And there, exactly where she always was...","THE Secretive Eon raised her head up in surprise from her seated position!","Her dark eyes widened slightly as she observed the neon-blazing form of Skoll carrying three passengers thundering through her domain at speeds that should not have been possible!","Noah locked his gaze onto hers calmly.","And he nodded.","Just a simple, nonchalant gesture. As if he was casually saying hi while passing through on his way to somewhere else entirely.","Then he disappeared with the speed of an Absolute toward the depths of the Stoa of Dogmata where another body of his waited!","Moments after Noah passed through...","BOOM !","The aura of genuine Absolutes spilled out as space tore apart!","THE Weavers appeared!","Their wild authority erupted in all directions, pressing against the ancient pillars of the Stoa with force that made even this primordial domain groan! They were about to continue their chase when...","BOOM!","Their decrepit gazes suddenly became shocked and stern!","They stopped immediately!","They formed a protective circle where they stood, obsidian-gold auras blazing around them as they turned to look at... THE Secretive Eon!","Their gazes were extremely heavy!","As if they had come across something utterly perilous!","As if they wondered whether they had been led into a trap!","Three Absolutes who had been pursuing with absolute confidence now stood frozen, their attention fixed entirely on the small, delicate figure seated calmly upon the obsidian ground!","But...","In the heavy silence that followed, they shockingly observed THE Secretive Eon look toward them with interest.","Then she thoughtfully looked at the distance where Noah and his forces had disappeared to.","She never made a move.","She simply sat there with her legs crossed, her chin resting on her hand, watching events unfold with the patient curiosity of someone observing something mildly entertaining.","THE Weavers seemed to look at each other in sequence.","As if they were affirming something.","As if they were communicating through threads of fate that connected them.","They observed the nonchalant gaze of THE Secretive Eon who was looking at them as if they were absolutely nothing.","Such a gaze of contempt made them extremely stifled!","But they didn’t complain.","They couldn’t complain.","Not to her.","At this moment, one of THE Weavers pulled a golden string from the air and broke it. The snap echoed through the Stoa with finality that spoke of fate being read and accepted.","\" We... are not her targets.\"","...!","After such words, THE Weavers glanced at THE Secretive Eon with care.","Then slowly... they began to surge toward the same direction Noah had disappeared!","Their prey awaited!","And whatever that Corrupted Region held, it could not be worse than remaining in the presence of THE Secretive Eon while she stared at them like insects beneath her notice!","All that was left behind was Eon herself.","She remained where she was as if she was merely an observer and not a participant in all this!","\" Interesting... very interesting.\"","Her voice emerged measured and unhurried, each word placed with precision.","\" Where did THE Scale Breaker get such a speedy dog? And to have them chasing him...\"","She smiled.","At this moment, Eon was seeing Skoll for the first time in actual Existence rather than simulation.","And this glorious moment here...","Noah’s entry.","THE Weavers’ entry.","The brief few seconds wasted by THE Weavers as they sensed the terrifying aura of Eon who at this time wasn’t hiding it.","They had stopped.","They had almost thought they were led into a trap.","All of this brought precious seconds for Noah!","He crossed the Stoa of Dogmata at impossible speed, racing toward the point where his other body stood before a massive swirling obsidian cluster of event horizons!","That body turned into a streak of light and fused into him!","He patted Skoll’s fur one final time.","The neon flaming brilliance blazed around them all!","And they delved into a Corrupted Region of THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungapap.","A region that even THE Secretive Eon did not wish to enter!"]},{"number":4755,"title":"Chapter 4755: Chapter 4754: The Shores of Kleos!","paragraphs":["THE Fallout did countless things that others could not even begin to fathom.","Only Absolutes truly understood what THE Fallout did and the long lasting effects that would carry out across Observable Existence.","But the idea of corruption and distortion was widespread throughout. One of the major things to understand was that THE Fallout came, yes, but there were always places that others had never been to. Places that even Fundamental Depth entities and Absolutes explored with caution even in Ginnungagap.","THE Vaults of Ginnungagap was one of them.","At this moment, they held the moniker of THE Corrupted Vaults of Ginnungagap!","So just what had the unique internal compartments that others may have never even been to changed into? The answer to this could only be experienced.","Because Existence was vast and filled with wonders.","THE Secretive Eon had told Noah there was much he didn’t know and understand. There was so much that many did not understand!","And he was about to experience one of those things firsthand.","---","BOOM!","Noah opened his eyes to a booming sound of Existence distorting and the sound of waves splashing on his body.","Even a partial simulation of this place had only yielded bits of information before it dissolved. It was an extremely unique place that resisted being modeled by THE Moirai Thread. But he had grasped what this place was upon initial entry.","At this time, he was looking at an endlessly blue sky filled with rivers of golden light and clouds moving above.","Not the corrupted gray of the Wastes.","Not the burning obsidian of Muspelheim.","An actual blue sky. Pristine. Ancient. Beautiful in a way that felt like it had been preserved from an era before corruption was even a concept.","He rose up from the waters hitting his body.","Nearby, Skoll shook his entire form to splash water everywhere!","The transformed Duke’s body still shone with neon flames, though they seemed dimmer than before. His mane of crystallized fire flickered with reduced intensity. The incandescent sun and moon in his eyes still burned, but with the subdued glow of power being suppressed.","Even Skoll was affected by this place.","And yet his tail still wagged. His tongue still lolled out. He was still having fun despite everything.","Such a good boy!","Nearby, Lumivara allowed the water to freely splash on her as she looked around with wonder. Her injuries from the confrontation with THE Weavers seemed less severe now, as if the waters themselves carried healing properties. Her brilliant form still flickered with instability, but there was hope in her eyes.","\" Master... where are we?\"","Her voice came soft with amazement.","The hairy figure of Ul’moreth had already stood up straight. He looked around with his veiled face showing amazement and a light of fervor. As if he had arrived at a place he had always dreamed of!","\" This is... can it be?\"","The ancient Ginnu Lifeform’s countless hairs rippled with excitement despite being suppressed.","\" Little Anomaly, do you know what this place is? Do you understand where we have arrived?\"","Before Noah could answer, a glorious set of prompts bloomed before all of them!","|WELCOME TO THE CORRUPTED PRIMORDIAL NEXUS DOMAIN|","| You have entered THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.|","|Location: Deep within THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap, accessible only through the Stoa of Dogmata.|","|Historical Context:|","|This domain was previously inaccessible. It had been locked from within to prevent entry to later generations. THE Fallout has unlocked entry and corrupted it in an unknown manner.|","|What lies within has not been witnessed by outside eyes for eons beyond counting.|","|ENTRY EFFECTS ACTIVATED|","|Upon crossing the threshold into THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, all entrants experience immediate suppression of their accumulated Weight and Depth.|","|Effect: All newcomers are reduced to THE Surface Depth regardless of their external classification.|","|Mechanism:|","|This domain operates on ancient principles that predate the modern Depth system entirely.|","| This land stands as One of THE Nexus Domain Points of all the Primordial Realms.|","|Ginnungagap. Muspelheim. Alfheimr. Jotunheim. Niflheim. Vanaheim. And others that have been lost to history and time.|","|All Primordial Realms once connected through Nexus Points like this one.|","|This place does not recognize accumulated Weight as legitimate authority.|","|It does not care what you achieved outside its boundaries.|","|Instead, it enforces a baseline state where only merit earned within the domain itself determines one’s standing.|","|Duration: Permanent while within the domain. Power returns immediately upon departure, but departure requires specific conditions to be met.|","|Exception: None.|","|Even Absolutes are reduced to THE Surface Depth upon entry.|","|Their knowledge, skills, and techniques remain, but the raw power behind them is suppressed to Surface levels.|","|You are no exception, Genesis Monarch.|","|Your 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue exist but can only express Surface-level authority.|","|Your Formless Depth has been compressed to baseline parameters.|","|Your Weight, while still present, cannot manifest beyond Surface limitations.|","| Welcome to equality.|","...!","The prompts continued without pause!","|LOCATION IDENTIFIED|","| You have arrived at The Shores of Kleos of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.|","|Kleos: Glory. Fame. Renown earned through great deeds.|","|This is the starting place of this domain.|","|THE Agora of Primordial Judgment contains:|","|- Established order maintained for eons|","|- A Complex Civilization built on philosophical foundations|","|- Society established by Primordial Lifeforms who are scholars of The Oldest Paradox of Existence|","|Those who hold true power in this particular Nexus Point are Primordial Perfected Ginnu Lifeforms.|","|Not Malformed. Not Standard. Perfected.|","|The ideal expressions of what Ginnu Lifeforms were always meant to become.|","|RANK DESIGNATION ASSIGNED|","| You have been granted the designation of HOPLITE.|","|Classification: Citizen-Soldier Rank of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.|","|Depth Limitation: THE Surface Depth|","|Status: All newcomers begin as Hoplites . This is the baseline rank, representing those who have not yet proven their worth to the society.|","|Rights:|","|- May reside within the domain|","|- May participate in public debates (but not formal Agora proceedings)|","|- May engage in commerce and trade(This is THE Vault of Ginnungagap)|","|- May petition for tasks that could earn merit|","|Restrictions:|","|- Cannot leave the domain|","|- Cannot challenge those of higher rank directly|","|- Cannot access restricted areas (libraries, armories, sacred spaces)|","|- Cannot vote on matters of governance|","| Symbol: A simple bronze pin depicting a shield|","|This symbol will manifest upon your person shortly.|","|Wear it with neither shame nor pride. It simply represents where you currently stand.|","|Rise through merit, and better symbols await.|","...!","The prompts were grand ones that outlined exactly where they had entered!","Noah rose fully while raising his hand and clenching to feel the vibrant power flowing through him!","His Way and Civilization was restricted to THE Surface Depth, yes.","But many beings at THE Surface Depth held varying Weights and Immensity.","His?","Hoho!","Even suppressed to Surface levels, he could feel the density of what he had accumulated. Twenty-seven Seals compressed into a space that should only hold a fraction of that authority. Knowledge of The First Tongue that most Surface Depth entities couldn’t even dream of. Techniques and understanding that transcended the limitations being placed upon his raw power.","And this place was one of boundless possibilities!","Beings like Ul’moreth had been looking for it whenever they delved into THE Vaults of Ginnungagap before. A place of complex and stable civilization put in place by Perfected Ginnu Lifeforms.","There were Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms like Ul’moreth who were the first tries of Existence, experimental creations that came before the template was refined.","And then there were Perfected Ginnu Lifeforms!","The ideal. The complete. The final expression of what that ancient race was always meant to become.","And...","HUUM!","Further ahead, on the sandy beaches, auras bloomed!","Noah, Ul’moreth, and Lumivara turned toward the source of the pressure.","The brilliance of one Fundamental Depth entity and three Intermediate Depth entities floated over as they looked... grand.","Even at Fundamental Depth within this domain’s limitations, the lead entity radiated presence that felt utterly suffocating. As if one was staring at a Half-Step Absolute! His Weight was that heavy!","This was what it meant to accumulate merit within THE Agora of Primordial Judgment. To build authority through contribution and wisdom rather than external power.","A voice filled with power boomed out from the forefront.","\" Newly arriving Hoplites, welcome to The Shores of Kleos.\"","The speaker was a muscular humanoid man whose body glinted with white and gold. His physique was carved from millennia of existence, every muscle defined with the precision of something that had been perfected rather than merely developed.","His face held ancient beauty that transcended conventional aesthetics. High cheekbones beneath eyes that shimmered with golden light. A strong jaw softened by lips that seemed accustomed to both stern judgment and warm welcome. His hair was dark as the void between stars but threaded with strands of silver that caught the golden rivers of light flowing across the sky.","He wore a toga of pristine white trimmed with gold, draped across his form with the casual elegance of someone who had worn such garments for longer than most civilizations had existed. A laurel wreath of living leaves crowned his head, and upon his chest, a golden pin depicted a shield, spear, and laurel wreath intertwined.","Fundamental Depth within this domain. One of the elite!","\" Welcome to THE Ideal Civilization, THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.\"","His voice resonated with authority that made the very air compress.","\" Come now, and let us see what you can contribute to the vastness of Existence. \"","...!","BOOM!","The three Intermediate Depth entities flanking him stepped forward in unison.","They were not all humanoid.","One resembled a great lion whose mane was composed of flowing golden light rather than fur. His eyes held the same ancient beauty as the leader, that sense of having been refined across eons until only perfection remained. A toga was draped across his massive shoulders in a manner that should have looked ridiculous but somehow appeared utterly natural.","Another was serpentine, her coils shimmering with scales that shifted between white and gold with each movement. Her face was humanoid but elongated, beautiful in a way that made observers question what beauty even meant. Laurels wrapped around her crown, and her toga flowed down her upper body before transitioning seamlessly into her serpentine lower half.","The third was abstract, a being of geometric shapes that constantly rearranged themselves into configurations that suggested humanoid form without ever quite achieving it. And yet even this entity carried that same grace, that same sense of ancient perfection that defined the Primordial Perfected.","These were not the Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms that Noah had encountered before.","These were not experimental creations still finding their form.","These were the Primordial Perfected Ginnu Lifeforms!","Beings who had achieved what Ul’moreth and his kind had always aspired toward. Beings who represented the final, ideal expression of the Ginnu template.","And they looked upon Noah and his companions with gazes that held neither hostility nor particular warmth.","Only assessment.","Only evaluation.","Only the patient curiosity of a civilization that had seen multiple newcomers wash upon these shores and would soon see more.","\"I am Alexandros ,\" the muscular Lifeform continued. \"I oversee the integration of new arrivals into our society. You have questions. That is natural. You have concerns. That is expected. You may even have plans to leave as quickly as possible.\"","His lips curved into a smile that held eons of experience with exactly such plans.","\" All of that can be addressed in time. For now, understand this single truth.\"","His golden eyes swept across Noah, Ul’moreth, Lumivara, and the neon-blazing form of Skoll.","\" Within THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, you are what you prove yourself to be. Nothing more. Nothing less. Your past achievements mean nothing here. Your external power means nothing here. Only what you contribute, only what you demonstrate, only what you earn through merit will determine your standing.\"","He gestured toward the beaches and the civilization that lay beyond.","\" Welcome to equality, Hoplites. Now... let us see what you are truly made of.\"","...!"]},{"number":4756,"title":"Chapter 4756: Chapter 4755: Paths And Merit!","paragraphs":["The Primordial Perfected Ginnu Lifeforms were unique in that even when Noah activated his Lens of a Civilization...","| ENTITY ANALYSIS: ALEXANDROS|","|Classification: Primordial Perfected Ginnu Lifeform|","|Rank: Polemarch (War Leader of Wisdom)|","|Depth Within Domain: THE Fundamental Depth|","|Weight Assessment: Approaches Half-Step Absolute parameters despite Depth limitations|","|Additional Information: Restricted. Higher clearance required.|","| ENTITY ANALYSIS: LEONIKOS|","|Classification: Primordial Perfected Ginnu Lifeform|","|Form: Leonine|","|Rank: Lochagos (Captain of Merit)|","|Depth Within Domain: THE Intermediate Depth|","|Additional Information: Restricted. Higher clearance required.|","| ENTITY ANALYSIS: OPHELIA|","|Classification: Primordial Perfected Ginnu Lifeform|","|Form: Serpentine|","|Rank: Lochagos (Captain of Merit)|","|Depth Within Domain: THE Intermediate Depth|","|Additional Information: Restricted. Higher clearance required.|","| ENTITY ANALYSIS: GEOMETROS|","|Classification: Primordial Perfected Ginnu Lifeform|","|Form: Abstract/Geometric|","|Rank: Lochagos (Captain of Merit)|","|Depth Within Domain: THE Intermediate Depth|","|Additional Information: Restricted. Higher clearance required.|","...!","He obtained the bare minimum information on these beings as they led them away from the shore.","The Lens of a Civilization could only pierce so far into the mysteries of Primordial Perfected entities. They were ancient beyond measure, and many things here were restricted!","Noah patted an excited Skoll who seemed ready to run off and explore everything at once.","The transformed Duke’s neon flames still burned despite being suppressed to Surface Depth. His tail wagged with enthusiasm. This place was new. This place was interesting. This place had so many things to smell and see!","Alexandros continued to speak as he led them up the beach.","\" We have had different entrants across the Weavings of Existence since THE Great Change occurred.\"","His voice carried the weight of someone who had witnessed countless arrivals over eons.","\" Some act up and need to be beaten down a little before they come to accept the terms of this place. Pride makes fools of even the powerful. They believe their external authority should translate into internal standing.\"","He glanced back at Noah with golden eyes that held knowing amusement.","\" It does not.\"","His toga rippled as he walked, the fabric catching light from the golden rivers flowing across the sky.","\" But even the dumbest ones eventually realize that this place is a paradise for power and immensity. Only those who have forged a Civilization may enter here, and those who do arrive for the first time get brought down to THE Surface Depth as this place gives you a chance to rebuild an unrivaled foundation for your Depth.\"","He paused to let those words settle.","\" To learn about expressions of power perfected over eons. Power relating to the Oldest Paradox of Existence itself. And of course...\"","His smile widened.","\" Unfathomable treasures from THE Vault of Ginnungagap. Items that have not seen the light of Observable Existence since before THE Fallout. Knowledge that predates the modern understanding of Depth entirely.\"","The beach gradually transitioned into firmer ground as they ascended a gentle slope.","\" But first, as any Hoplites get the chance to... you get to choose which path you follow.\"","And then the view opened up before them.","Massive archway gateways shimmered ahead!","Four of them, arranged in a grand semicircle at the crest of the hill. Each one was constructed from stone that seemed to have been carved by concepts rather than tools.","Pillars supported triangular pediments adorned with intricate reliefs depicting scenes of philosophical triumph. The architecture spoke of an era when beauty and function were inseparable, when every structure was built to last for eternities.","Each archway had a radiant road leading from it toward a barely discernible outline of glorious structures in the distance!","Similar to the limitation outside in The Wastes of THE Fallout, one could barely perceive anything less than a mile ahead in this domain. Many things in the distance were a haze of golden light that obscured details while hinting at grandeur beyond imagination.","But their focus was on the golden archways themselves!","They shone with brilliance that Noah, Ul’moreth, and Lumivara very much recognized!","The light of The First Tongue’s influence. The resonance of fundamental principles given architectural form.","Alexandros stopped before the four gateways and turned to face them fully.","\" The choice for any Hoplites is the path they follow.\"","He gestured toward the first archway.","\" There are the Chaosites. Followers of Chaos.\"","The archway shone with deep stellar obsidian!","Not mere black, but the darkness between stars given physical form. Within that darkness, points of light flickered and died and were born again in patterns that followed no discernible logic. The pillars seemed stable one moment and fluid the next. The pediment above depicted scenes of order crumbling into beautiful entropy.","\" Their philosophy holds that order is an illusion. Structure is temporary. Only by embracing disorder can one understand the true nature of reality. They seek truth through the dissolution of false certainties.\"","Alexandros moved to the second archway.","\" Then there are the Existentialists. Followers of Existence.\"","This archway shone with multicolored brilliance!","Every color that could be perceived and many that could not swirled across its surface in patterns that somehow remained coherent despite their complexity. The pillars pulsed with the rhythm of heartbeats, of breath, of the simple act of being. The pediment depicted scenes of entities simply existing in various forms, celebrating the fundamental fact of their presence.","\" Their philosophy holds that being precedes essence. Existence itself is the highest value. All other considerations are secondary to the fundamental fact of existing. They seek truth through the pure experience of being.\"","He moved to the third archway.","\" Then there are the Paradoxians. Followers of Paradox.\"","This archway shone with light that was simultaneously white, gold, and black!","The pillars appeared solid and ethereal at the same time. The pediment depicted scenes that showed both victory and defeat, creation and destruction, truth and lies, all occupying the same space without contradiction. Looking at it for too long made one’s perception twist in ways that were uncomfortable but strangely enlightening.","\" Their philosophy holds that truth is found in contradiction. The highest understanding comes from holding two opposing ideas simultaneously and finding meaning in their tension. They seek truth through the embrace of impossibility.\"","Finally, he moved to the fourth archway.","\" And lastly, there are the Glossarians. Followers of The First Tongue.\"","This archway shone with blue-gold radiance that Noah recognized intimately!","The pillars were inscribed with Phonemes that shifted and reformed with each passing moment. The pediment depicted scenes of words creating worlds, of language shaping reality, of speakers whose declarations became law. The very air around it hummed with linguistic authority.","\" Their philosophy holds that language is the foundation of all reality. The First Tongue is not merely a tool but the very fabric from which Existence is woven. Mastery of language is mastery of everything. They seek truth through perfect expression.\"","Alexandros turned back to face them fully.","\" So, which path will you follow?\"","His golden eyes swept across Noah, Ul’moreth, Lumivara, and Skoll.","\" Different paths, but here, everybody falls under the same rankings. All beings within THE Agora of Primordial Judgment are assigned a rank that determines the maximum Depth they can express. Ranks are earned through merit, not accumulated through external power. The Taxis of Merit!\"","He began counting on his fingers.","\" Merit is gained through contributing to society. Inventions, ideas, unique items, services that benefit the collective. Through winning formal debates in Dogma and Thesis contests. Through completing tasks assigned by higher-ranked officials. Through demonstrating philosophical insight that advances understanding. And through acts of valor in defense of the domain, though those are rare but highly valued.\"","His smile returned with warmth that seemed almost paternal.","\" You all are currently Hoplites at THE Surface Depth. But you can increase in rank as you refine your foundations. Rise to become LOCHAGOS, the Captains of Merit, with a Depth Limitation of THE Intermediate Depth. Or even become a POLEMARCH like myself, a War Leader of Wisdom who is unrivaled at Fundamental Depth!\"","...!"]},{"number":4757,"title":"Chapter 4757: Chapter 4756: Glossarians! I","paragraphs":["Alexandros said all of this with a smile while his followers remained calm.","Leonikos the lion observed with eyes that held the patience of eternity.","Ophelia the serpent watched with curiosity that seemed particularly focused on Noah.","Geometros the abstract shifted through configurations that suggested deep contemplation.","They were simply observing and learning from this entity who was higher ranked than them!","\"Master! We know where to go so we can outshine everyone, right?!\"","Lumivara spoke with excitement at this moment while looking toward a certain archway!","The blue-gold radiance of the Glossarian gate seemed to call to her, to resonate with everything they had learned and become under Noah’s guidance.","Noah and Ul’moreth couldn’t help but smile!","The path was obvious, wasn’t it? They who had claimed The First Tongue, who had forged new Phonemes, who had built their entire advancement upon linguistic mastery...","The Glossarians awaited.","And yet, at this time...","HUUM!","Far behind them, obsidian-gold light shone!","The sandy beach trembled! The shores in the distance vibrated with the arrival of something that carried authority even when suppressed!","When they turned around...","The visages of THE Weavers appeared!","Three decrepit figures wrapped in robes and hoods, their ancient faces twisted with fury that had only grown during their pursuit. Their golden eyes blazed with the light of fate itself being manipulated. Even reduced to Surface Depth, they radiated menace that made the very air recoil.","The moment they appeared, Noah only stared at them calmly.","He did not move. He did not flinch. He did not show any sign of concern whatsoever.","His gaze was purposefully raised high and imperious.","As if he were looking at ants.","THE Weavers were infuriated and calm at the same time when seeing this gaze!","How dare he?!","How DARE this creature look upon THE Moirai with such contempt?!","Their eyes seemingly broke down where they stood, analyzing the surrounding Weavings of Existence. Calculating. Planning. Preparing to strike despite whatever rules this domain might hold.","And then...","BOOM!","THE Weavers shot toward Noah and the others!","Three streams of obsidian-gold light converging on a single point! Their suppressed power still carried enough force to devastate anything at Surface Depth! Their fury drove them beyond caution!","Lumivara and Ul’moreth frowned while trying to get in front of Noah!","But he held them back while shaking his head.","Not yet.","Not necessary.","Because a moment later...","HUUM!","Alexandros moved!","The Polemarch’s form blurred with speed that should have been impossible at Fundamental Depth! The spear he carried in his hands shone a glorious golden obsidian as infinite seas of Chaos seemed to be contained within its seemingly simple form!","His blow carried unfathomable depth and weight!","A swing of his spear shockingly smashed onto THE Weavers even faster than they came!","BOOM !","The collision was catastrophic!","A paradoxical golden light of immensity buzzed around THE Weavers, their own authority trying to deflect the blow! But their faces showed calm fury as they were shockingly pushed back by Alexandros!","Pushed back!","Three Absolutes, even suppressed, forced to retreat by a single Fundamental Depth entity!","All of the surroundings darkened!","Alexandros revealed himself fully as a Chaosite!","His entire figure now burned with boundless Primordial Chaos! The toga he wore seemed to dissolve into streams of entropy that swirled around his muscular form! His golden eyes became voids filled with dying stars! His spear burned with the authority of endings that came before new beginnings!","Immense waves of Phonemes formed around him!","Chaos! Darkness! Endings!","They coalesced into dense Philologies that pressed against reality itself, constructs of linguistic authority refined over eons until they achieved perfection that modern practitioners could only dream of!","\" NO FIGHTING ALLOWED BY ANY HOPLITES!\"","His voice boomed across the shores with authority that made even THE Weavers pause!","\" REGARDLESS OF WHAT POWER YOU HELD BEFORE!\"","His spear pointed directly at the three decrepit figures.","\"IF YOU WISH TO FIGHT, DO SO IN THE GLORY OF THE ARENA OR DURING DEBATES! UNTIL THEN... BEHAVE!\"","The Chaos around him intensified until it felt like standing at the edge of a collapsing Existence!","\" YOU DO NOT WISH TO BE MARKED AS DEPLORABLES !\"","BOOM!","A glorious scene unfolded!","Absolutes knocked back by someone seemingly lesser than them!","THE Weavers floated in the air where they had been pushed, their golden eyes burning with calm fury that had no outlet. They could not attack. They could not pursue. They could not do anything without facing consequences within this domain’s rules.","They were bound by the same limitations as everyone else.","And someone of higher rank had just demonstrated exactly what those limitations meant.","Noah looked at this scene with shining eyes!","This place held boundless possibilities!","A domain where Absolutes could be challenged by those who had earned their standing through merit. Where external power meant nothing and internal refinement meant everything. Where THE Weavers, despite being genuine Absolutes outside these boundaries, were now merely Hoplites.","Just like him.","Just like Ul’moreth and Lumivara.","Equal in rank.","Equal in suppressed Depth.","But not equal in knowledge. Not equal in understanding. Not equal in the foundations they had built.","And in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, those foundations were exactly what mattered.","Noah’s smile widened as he turned back toward the four archways.","And he whispered just for THE Weavers to hear...","\" Wait for me, you old hags. Just wait for me to butcher you and eat you whole.\"","BOOM!","THE Weavers could wait for him to butcher them.","Their eyes flashed with a chilly light as they heard his words!","At this time, Noah went toward the gateway of The Glossarians as if THE Weavers had absolutely nothing to do with him.","After all, he couldn’t do anything against them right now.","An Absolute restricted to Surface Depth versus the current him right now? He wouldn’t be able to leave a scratch on them. Their accumulated knowledge, their refined techniques, their eons of Depth... all of that remained even when their raw power was suppressed.","What he needed to do was gain enough merit to become a Polemarch.","And be faster than THE Weavers at doing it.","Because with these entities at the level of Absolute, he knew they would quickly adapt in this place. They would use their terrifying power of understanding to gain merit and rapidly ascend through the ranks. They had existed for eons beyond counting. They had accumulated wisdom that most beings couldn’t even comprehend.","At that time, if he was slow...","They could challenge him in the arena or debates and butcher him instead!"]},{"number":4758,"title":"Chapter 4758: Chapter 4757: Glossarians! II","paragraphs":["So he had to work efficiently and learn more of the rulings of this unique place. Refine his foundation to even more glorious heights. And only then forge ahead!","He looked at this place as a domain of profound opportunity for his elevation.","His aim of exceeding the foundations of beings like THE Creature and THE Living Paradox and THE Primordial Chaos... could be achieved here!","A Nexus Point connecting all the Primordial Realms. A civilization built by Perfected Ginnu Lifeforms who had studied the Oldest Paradox of Existence for longer than most realities had existed. Knowledge and treasures from THE Vault of Ginnungagap that hadn’t been seen since before THE Fallout.","This wasn’t just a trap he had led THE Weavers into.","This was an opportunity he had stumbled upon, and he would seize it with both hands.","Oh, and there was also the matter of finding THE Secretive Eon’s Disciple and exiting this place with them in the end, if they even needed his help.","So, without fanfare, he walked toward the archway representing The Glossarians.","The blue-gold radiance intensified as he approached!","The Phonemes inscribed upon the pillars seemed to recognize something in him.","He stepped through.","HUUM!","Waves of blue-gold light shone around his form!","The transformation was immediate and profound. His outer garments shifted and reformed, reality itself clothing him in the manner of this ancient civilization. The style was similar to what Alexandros wore, those flowing robes that spoke of eras when beauty and function were inseparable.","But while Alexandros and the others monitoring the Shores of Kleos seemed to wear neutral colors to not reveal which path they stood on...","What Noah wore as he stepped on the other side of the archway shone radiant blue-gold!","The color of The First Tongue made manifest in fabric!","| You have begun to walk the Philosophy of The Glossarians.|","|The Glossarians: Followers of The Philosophy The First Tongue|","|An ancient and complex school of thought revolving around the Oldest Paradox of Existence.|","|Core Belief: Language is the foundation of all reality. The First Tongue is not merely a tool but the very fabric from which Existence is woven. Mastery of language is mastery of everything.|","|Historical Significance:|","|The Glossarians have existed long, long since before THE Fallout unsealed this domain.|","|They have refined their understanding of The First Tongue across eons.|","|Their debates have produced insights that shaped the very nature of linguistic authority.|","|Their archives contain knowledge of Phonemes, Declarations, Thesis constructs, and Apophasis that the outside existence has forgotten.|","|Current Status:|","|The One Who Laid The Claim on The First Tongue has silently joined a group dedicated to discussing Philosophy revolving around it.|","| This is bound to be an extremely glorious affair.|","|The Glossarians have not received a new member with such profound connection to their core subject in recorded memory.|","|GLOSSARIAN HOPLITE DESIGNATION ACTIVE|","|Rank: Hoplite (Citizen-Soldier)|","|Depth Limitation: THE Surface Depth|","|Philosophical School: The Glossarians|","|Gathering Place: The Lexicon|","|The Taxis of Merit has been initialized.|","|Current Merit: 0|","|Merit is displayed upon your toga in the numerical system of this civilization.|","|Current Display: (Zero)|","|Merit Thresholds:|","|0-99 Merit: Hoplite (Surface Depth)|","|100-499 Merit: Lochagos (Intermediate Depth)|","|500+ Merit: Polemarch (Fundamental Depth)|","|Note: These thresholds represent minimum requirements. Actual promotion requires demonstration of philosophical understanding alongside accumulated Merit.|","|Ways to Gain Merit:|","|Contributing to society: 1-10 Merit per contribution depending on value|","|Winning formal debates: 1-10 Merit depending on opponent rank and debate significance|","|Completing assigned tasks: Variable Merit based on difficulty|","|Demonstrating philosophical insight: 1-90 Merit for breakthroughs|","|Acts of valor: 1-500 Merit for exceptional defense of the domain|","|Warning:|","|Merit can also be lost through violations of domain law.|","|Fighting outside sanctioned venues: -10 Merit minimum|","|Disrespecting higher ranks without cause: -5 Merit|","|Attempting unauthorized departure: -100 Merit and potential Deplorable status|","|Deplorable Status:|","| Those marked as Deplorables lose all accumulated Merit.|","|They are barred from formal debates and Arena challenges.|","| They must perform remedial service to remove the designation.|","| Even Absolutes are not exempt from this punishment.|","...!","Noah stood on the other side of the archway in all his glory!","His muscular and toned figure became more visible through the flowing robes that draped across his form. The toga was inscribed with Phonemes of The First Tongue that shifted and reformed with each breath he took. They weren’t merely decorative. They were functional, resonating with his own authority and amplifying his connection to linguistic principles.","Upon his head, a laurel wreath materialized- a crown of leaves!","But this was no ordinary crown of leaves.","It was made of crystallized language!","Each leaf was a frozen Phoneme, a fragment of The First Tongue given physical form. They glittered with blue-gold radiance that caught the golden rivers of light flowing across the sky. They whispered with meaning that only those attuned to linguistic authority could perceive.","His dark hair framed features that had been refined through countless trials. His eyes blazed with the conviction of one who had claimed what others merely studied. His stance carried the weight of twenty-seven Seals even when suppressed to Surface Depth.","He looked like he had transformed into a glorious scholar of ancient times.","He looked fucking grand!","Upon his toga, in the space above his heart, a symbol glowed meaning Zero in an ancient language.","Zero Merit.","The starting point for all Hoplites.","But that number would change soon.","A moment after he completed his transformation, Lumivara looked toward him with shining eyes!","\" Master! You look amazing!\"","Her voice carried excitement that transcended their dangerous circumstances as she and Skoll rushed toward the gate as well!","The little fox passed through the blue-gold radiance and emerged wearing a toga of her own, smaller but no less elegant. Phonemes inscribed themselves across the fabric in patterns that complemented her brilliant nature. A laurel of crystallized language settled upon her head, the leaves seeming almost playful in their configuration.","A zero appeared upon her toga as well.","Skoll bounded through next!","The transformed Duke’s neon flames dimmed momentarily as the gate’s authority washed over him, then blazed back to life in harmony with the blue-gold radiance of the Glossarians. His massive form now wore what could only be described as a toga adapted for a very good boy. The fabric draped across his back and shoulders, inscribed with Phonemes that seemed to dance with his wagging tail.","The laurel that appeared upon his head sat between his ears at a jaunty angle.","Zero glowed upon his toga.","Even Skoll was now a Glossarian Hoplite.","And Ul’moreth...","The ancient Ginnu Lifeform turned toward the distant Weavers who had become eerily cold and calm as they looked at this scene. His veiled gaze was heavy with understanding of what was to come.","Then he also took heavy steps toward the Glossarian gate.","He passed through and emerged transformed. His countless hairs now carried traces of blue-gold that wove through their obsidian luminescence. A toga draped across his massive hairy form in a manner that somehow appeared dignified rather than absurd. The laurel of crystallized language that crowned him was large and ancient-looking.","All four of them now stood as Glossarian Hoplites ready to begin their ascent!","Behind them, at the Shores of Kleos, Alexandros still billowed with Chaos as he faced THE Weavers.","\" Are you ready to comply?\"","His voice carried the weight of authority earned through eons of merit.","The shocking scene that followed made even Noah’s eyes narrow.","THE Weavers calmly floated down from where they had been pushed back.","They landed upon the sandy beach with grace that belied their decrepit appearances. And then... they smiled.","Those ancient faces twisted into expressions of eerie amusement that held no warmth whatsoever.","\" Of course.\"","Their voices spoke in sequence, each word delivered by a different throat but forming a single continuous sentence.","\" We...\"","\"...are happy...\"","\"...to comply.\"","One of them gestured toward the archways with a withered hand.","\" Is that pathway there to Paradox? We feel a very strong inclination toward it.\"","...!"]},{"number":4759,"title":"Chapter 4759: Chapter 4758: Glossarians! III","paragraphs":["Alexandros put his spear down.","His golden eyes, still void-like with dying stars, regarded THE Weavers with cold assessment. The Chaos surrounding him did not dissipate, but it calmed into something more controlled.","\" The Paradoxians. Followers of Paradox.\"","His voice was measured now, professional rather than wrathful.","\" Their philosophy holds that truth is found in contradiction. The highest understanding comes from holding two opposing ideas simultaneously and finding meaning in their tension. They seek truth through the embrace of impossibility.\"","He gestured toward the archway that shone with light both white and black simultaneously.","\" Their gathering place is the Antinomia. Their debates are famous for producing insights that seem to make no sense yet reveal profound truths. Their members are known for being unpredictable, for seeing connections that others miss, for finding victory in apparent defeat.\"","His eyes narrowed.","\" It is a fitting choice for ones such as yourselves.\"","THE Weavers smiled wider at those words.","Then they moved.","Their steps were eerie, synchronized perfectly as if three bodies shared a single will. They walked toward the Paradoxian gate in unison, their decrepit forms casting long shadows across the beach.","They passed through.","HUUM!","The transformation was immediate and disturbing!","Their togas materialized in patterns of obsidian-gold and white. Half of each garment was dark, half was light, and somehow both halves occupied the same space without contradiction.","But their faces...","Their decrepit features morphed!","The papyrus-thin skin filled out. The deep wrinkles smoothed. The gaunt angles softened into curves that spoke of vitality rather than decay.","They became vibrant!","Bronze caramel skin filled with ecstatic beauty replaced what had been ancient horror. High cheekbones. Full lips. Features that were simultaneously young and ancient, beautiful and terrible, inviting and repulsive.","Three stunning figures now stood where three decrepit crones had been.","But their eyes remained the same.","Golden light swirling with the authority of fate itself.","And their smiles remained the same.","Eerie. Cold. Hungry.","Zero appeared upon each of their togas.","Zero Merit.","But that would change quickly!","Alexandros looked at this transformation calmly before turning to his followers.","\" Ophelia .\"","The serpentine Lochagos straightened at her name.","\" Lead the Glossarians to The Lexicon.\"","She inclined her head in acknowledgment.","\" And Geometros.\"","The abstract, geometric Lochagos shifted into a configuration that suggested attention.","\" Lead the Paradoxians to the Antinomia.\"","He nodded in his strange, angular way.","The two Lochagoi moved to fulfill their duties as Alexandros remained at the Shores of Kleos with Leonikos, prepared to greet whatever other entrants THE Fallout might deliver.","But before the groups separated...","THE Weavers turned to look at Noah with their vibrant, beautiful, terrifying faces.","Their smiles widened.","\" Yes, we must not waste any time.\"","Their voices came in sequence, each word from a different throat.","\" There are challenges...\"","\"...to be made in the Arena...\"","\"...and debates to be had, after all.\"","Their golden eyes blazed with promise.","\" We will see you again soon enough, Osmont.\"","HUUM!","With such words, THE Weavers didn’t even wait for Geometros!","They began to walk ahead on the vibrant path leading toward the Antinomia, their synchronized steps carrying them forward with purpose that spoke of plans already forming.","They knew exactly what they needed to do.","They would gain merit. They would ascend through the ranks. And then...","Noah’s eyes shone with veiled brilliance and grandeur as he watched them go.","Let them come.","By the time they were ready to challenge him, he would be ready to fuck them up.","Ophelia arrived beside Noah’s group, her serpentine form coiling gracefully as she moved. Her toga transformed to become similar to theirs, the blue-gold radiance of the Glossarians now marking her as one of their guides rather than a neutral observer.","She sighed.","\" Just how did you all enrage an Absolute outside of this place?\"","Her voice carried genuine curiosity mixed with concern.","\" It will be extremely hard. Any Absolute has an undeniable weight that will allow them to gain Merit rapidly. Even suppressed to Surface Depth, their understanding of Existence, their refined depth, their eons of accumulated wisdom... all of that translates into advantages in debates and contributions.\"","She began to lead them forward, away from the Shores of Kleos.","\" You will have to work hard. And I will root for you as fellow Glossarians.\"","Her serpentine lower half propelled her smoothly across the golden road.","\" But do not worry. You have a grace period as new Hoplites.\"","She glanced back at them with eyes that held ancient beauty.","\" Your lives are not in peril just yet. Unless you seek it yourself, no challenge for the Arena or debates can be forced on you guys just yet. The domain protects newcomers until they have had time to orient themselves and begin their journey.\"","She paused.","\" Use that time wisely. Learn the rules. Understand the paths to gaining Merit. And build your foundations before that grace period expires.\"","Her gaze grew serious.","\" Because when it does... those Absolutes will come for you. And they will not show mercy.\"","She said such illuminating words as she led them away from The Shores of Kleos and deeper into THE Agora of Primordial Judgment!","The golden road stretched before them, winding toward structures that slowly became visible through the haze of light. Towers and temples and amphitheaters built from concepts rather than stone. A civilization of scholars who had dedicated their existence to understanding the very foundations of reality.","And at its heart, awaiting Noah and his companions...","The Lexicon.","The gathering place of those who believed that language was everything!","They rapidly went across while observing everything as soon after...","\" This... is The Lower City, Kato Polis.\"","Ophelia’s serpentine form coiled gracefully as she gestured toward the sprawling expanse before them.","\" Most Hoplites of all paths have their dwellings here. But Kato Polis is divided into different sections for Glossarians, Paradoxians, Existentialists, and Chaosites.\"","Her scales shimmered with blue-gold light as she led them forward.","\" We are currently in the Glossarian sector. You will not get to interact with the other paths unless you go much further in, where all paths converge for debates and battles in the central districts.\"","She smiled with ancient beauty.","\" For now, this is your home. Learn its streets. Know its people. Understand its rhythms.\"","...!"]},{"number":4760,"title":"Chapter 4760: Chapter 4759: Glossarians! IV","paragraphs":["As she said this, Noah looked at the Lower City.","It was grand beyond measure!","The architecture seemed to have been carved from the very essence of language itself. Pillars rose in elegant columns, their surfaces inscribed with Phonemes that pulsed with quiet authority. Walls of buildings shimmered with linguistic patterns that shifted and reformed with each passing moment, as if the structures themselves were engaged in eternal conversation.","The buildings followed designs that spoke of an era when form and function achieved perfect unity. Triangular pediments crowned with intricate reliefs depicting scholars in debate. Archways that seemed to frame reality itself. Courtyards where fountains of liquid light flowed in patterns that wrote and rewrote themselves continuously.","It was ancient.","It was fantastical.","It was beautiful in ways that modern civilizations had forgotten how to achieve.","Glossarian Hoplites dotted the landscape in various states of activity. Some sat cross-legged on the roofs of their abodes, their eyes closed in deep meditation as Phonemes swirled around their forms in slow orbits. They were refining their foundations, building understanding of The First Tongue one revelation at a time.","Others moved through the streets with shining eyes of excitement, their togas rippling as they walked with purpose along a blue-gold road that led toward... the outline of a massive ancient library in the distance!","That structure dominated the horizon even through the haze of golden light that obscured distant details. Its silhouette promised knowledge beyond measure. Its presence drew scholars like moths to flame.","Noah looked at the few dozen THE Surface Depth Glossarians of different forms moving toward that place.","\" Where would everyone be going right now?\"","Ophelia smiled at his question.","\"It seems that a debate is taking place right now in The Lexicon.\"","Her eyes sparkled with the enthusiasm of someone who genuinely loved her craft.","\" The Lexicon is a massive library stretching for miles. It contains knowledge accumulated since before THE Fallout sealed this domain. Every insight, every breakthrough, every refined understanding of The First Tongue that the Glossarians have achieved across eons is recorded within its halls.\"","She gestured toward the distant structure.","\" But it also acts as the junction between The Lower City and The Middle City, Meso Polis, where Lochagoi and their households reside. The debates take place in chambers designed specifically for philosophical combat. It is where reputations are made and broken.\"","Her serpentine lower half propelled her forward as she continued leading them.","\" Do you wish to go see the debates? This is one of the ways to earn Merit here if you can show off your glory in The First Tongue compared to others!\"","...!","Ophelia said such words with genuine encouragement.","Lumivara and Ul’moreth looked toward Noah with silent smiles.","As if they knew something nobody else did!","They knew that as The One Who Laid The Claim on The First Tongue, who could argue they understood it better than he?! Who could challenge the foundations of one whose very existence was intertwined with the oldest language?!","So their eyes shone with luminosity as they were expectant for what would happen ahead!","Skoll blinked as he looked around with vibrant eyes at everything.","He noticed the smiles on Lumivara and his Master. He was simple-minded and did not understand what was making them so happy. But he wanted to be part of the excitement! He wanted to share in whatever joy they were feeling!","He barked and jumped around!","\" Woof!\"","Such a good boy!","With such enthusiasm, they went toward The Lexicon.","The Lexicon itself was another work of wonder.","As they approached, its true scale became apparent. The structure rose in terraced levels that seemed to climb toward the golden rivers of light flowing across the sky. Massive columns supported porticos that extended outward like welcoming arms. The central dome was crowned with a crystallized Phoneme that rotated slowly, casting shifting patterns of blue-gold radiance across the surrounding plazas.","The architecture blended the gravity of ancient temples with the wonder of impossible fantasy. Floating platforms connected different levels of the library. Staircases that seemed to defy conventional geometry wound between sections. Windows of solidified language filtered light into spectrums that enhanced reading and comprehension.","Statues of legendary Glossarians lined the approach, their forms captured in moments of profound insight or passionate debate. Some held scrolls. Others gestured as if delivering Declarations and Thesis that had shaped the understanding of generations.","The massive library seemed to have many compartments and regions, each one dedicated to different aspects of linguistic study. Archives of ancient Phonemic research. Chambers for practicing Dogma and Thesis. Halls where Thesis constructs could be tested without endangering surroundings.","Ophelia took them toward the right section of the massive building.","They joined the throngs of dozens of Hoplites flowing across the wide blue-gold halls of this place. The corridors were vast enough to accommodate beings of all sizes, from humanoid scholars to massive entities whose forms barely fit through the archways. All of them moved with the eager anticipation of those about to witness philosophical combat.","\" This region of The Lexicon is called the Logoseion.\"","Ophelia explained as they walked.","\" It is where Glossarians can formally debate matters of linguistic understanding. The results are recorded, Merit is awarded, and reputations are established.\"","Her eyes gleamed with interest.","\" Currently, it seems two Lochagoi are having a debate. This is rare enough to draw significant attention. Most debates occur between Hoplites seeking to prove themselves, or between Hoplites and Lochagoi where the outcome is... predictable.\"","She glanced back at Noah.","\" A debate between two Lochagoi is a spectacle worth witnessing. Their mastery of The First Tongue far exceeds what Hoplites can typically achieve.\"","As she said this, they fully entered the atmosphere of the Logoseion.","The space was filled with silent whispers that somehow carried reverence rather than distraction. What seemed to be a few hundred THE Entities filled this place, arranged in circular formation around a central clearing.","Many of them were Hoplites of different forms. Bears and serpents and humanoids and abstract beings, all wearing the blue-gold togas of Glossarians, all watching with eyes that burned with desire to learn and grow.","But a minor portion were Lochagoi!"]},{"number":4761,"title":"Chapter 4761: Chapter 4760: What!? I","paragraphs":["The Lochagoi radiated profound power at THE Intermediate Depth!","Even though their power seemed to be merely Intermediate, their foundations were astonishing enough that they could likely stomp on a Fundamental Depth entity like Gal’Thûrak if they ever met one outside in the Wastes. Their Weight within the domain’s limitations was suffocating, the result of Merit accumulated through eons of contribution and victory.","They all stood or sat in circular formation on flat seats of polished stone. Their eyes were set on two entities floating at the very center of the clearing.","And that clearing...","It looked like an infinite sea of blue-gold swirling plasma!","Dense Logos swam through it like fish through water. Philologies formed and dissolved in patterns that spoke of potential waiting to be shaped. The very air thrummed with The First Tongue’s authority, creating an environment where debates could manifest visually for all to observe.","The two Lochagoi debating floated above this sea at this moment.","Their current challenge seemed to be forging the longest combination of Logos to form a Philology that would remain stable while being the longest. A test of linguistic construction, of understanding how meaning built upon meaning without collapsing under its own weight.","One competitor was an entity that looked like a massive humanoid bear.","His fur was silver-white, his form powerful despite the scholarly toga draped across his broad shoulders. His eyes burned with concentration as Logos after Logos connected beneath him, his Philology growing longer with each addition. Sweat beaded on his brow. His paws trembled with the effort of maintaining stability.","The other was a woman.","She wore a Glossarian toga with casual elegance, as if such garments were merely extensions of her natural authority. Vibrant spectacles sat upon her nose, their lenses inscribed with Phonemes that likely enhanced her perception of structures. Her hair was dark and flowing, her features sharp with intelligence.","And her eyes held a light of profound arrogance .","She knew she was winning.","At this moment, she added another Logos onto her extremely long Philology!","HUUM!","The construct buzzed with energy that made nearby observers wince! It stretched across the plasma sea like a bridge of pure meaning, each component word connecting to the next in chains of logic that defied what most considered possible!","And yet it remained stable!","Her Philology held firm despite its impossible length!","The bear competitor tried to match it. His massive paws shaped another Logos, attempting to add it to his own construct...","BZZT!","His Philology fizzled!","The connections between Logos broke down catastrophically! Meaning collapsed into meaninglessness! His entire construct exploded into fragments of failed language that dissolved into the plasma sea below!","All those in the surroundings rose up and cheered!","The sound was thunderous, hundreds of voices celebrating the victory they had just witnessed! Hoplites stamped their feet! Lochagoi nodded with respect! The entire Logoseion vibrated with the energy of philosophical triumph!","A booming voice echoed out from everywhere and nowhere, the voice of the Logoseion itself announcing results!","\" Victory to Theoris the Articulate!\"","The woman with the spectacles smiled with satisfaction that bordered on smugness.","\" Lochagos Theoris has demonstrated superior Philological construction! Her chain of 47 stable Logos exceeds the previous record by 3!\"","The crowd cheered again!","\" She has earned 1 MERIT POINT for this victory!\"","Upon her toga, the number shifted.","Where it had displayed CDXLVII(447), it now displayed CDXLVIII(448).","448 Merit.","She was close to becoming a Polemarch.","\" Lochagos Theoris indicates she wishes to continue for another debate!\"","The booming voice carried challenge across the Logoseion.","\" Will anyone else step up and stop her chain of victories?\"","...!","At such words, Ophelia turned her head toward Noah.","She wanted to explain something.","But...she blinked.","Noah was no longer standing beside her.","Her eyes opened wide as she followed his signature through the crowded Logoseion. She found him already floating up toward the center of the domain!","He was rising to accept the challenge!","...!","Ophelia’s eyes opened wide with shock!","The surroundings quieted down again as everyone noticed what was happening. A Hoplite. A brand new arrival with Zero Merit displayed upon his toga. Rising to face a Lochagos with nearly 450 Merit who had just broken a record in Philological construction.","And then, in many areas, smiles and laughter broke out!","\" Big guy, you look grand and all, but you might be in over your head! Sit back down!\"","A humanoid Hoplite shouted from below while he smiled and laughed with other Hoplites around him. They weren’t being cruel. They were trying to save this foolish newcomer from embarrassment!","Noah paid no heed to this.","Amidst the buzzing discussions, he came to float at the opposing side where the defeated bear Lochagos had just stepped down from. The plasma sea swirled beneath him with eager anticipation. The Logos swimming within it seemed to gather closer, as if recognizing something in this new challenger.","He looked toward the entity opposite him.","Theoris the Articulate gazed back with an imperious expression.","Her eyes behind those vibrant spectacles held contempt that barely acknowledged his existence. He was beneath her time. He was beneath her notice. He was a Hoplite with zero Merit daring to stand where Lochagoi competed!","From the surroundings, the deep voice boomed out again.","\" Interesting.\"","The word carried weight that silenced the remaining whispers.","\" Sometimes, knowing one’s place is critical for survival. The wise understand their limitations. The foolish overreach and are humbled. This is the natural order of growth.\"","The plasma sea pulsed with blue-gold radiance.","\" Yet the debate between a Hoplite and a Lochagos is always allowed. It serves to show the immensity of some compared to others. It serves to show some just how distant they are from true glory.\"","The voice seemed almost sympathetic.","\" Perhaps this Hoplite seeks to learn through failure. Perhaps he wishes to understand the gap that separates him from greatness. Such humility, even when disguised as arrogance, can be the first step toward genuine advancement.\"","A pause.","\" Very well.\"","HUUM!","\" This debate shall proceed.\"","The plasma sea between Noah and Theoris began to churn with increased intensity!"]},{"number":4762,"title":"Chapter 4762: Chapter 4761: What?! II","paragraphs":["While a debate was about to unfold in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","There was a particular question worthy of an answer that Noah had also wondered a few times.","THE Living Paradox had his Loom for his War against THE Creature.","Those who sided with THE Living Paradox made the gains they made through him and through THE Fallout. They received positions within THE Loom. They gained access to resources and authority that elevated their power. They became instruments of Paradox’s designs.","But what of THE Creature?","What of those who fought alongside THE Creature? Those whose Civilizations were collapsed by THE Living Paradox? Those who had stood on the opposite side of the conflict and paid the price for it?","One could make the argument that THE Creature was much more powerful than THE Living Paradox. So what did those who stood alongside him gain? What rewards awaited the faithful who had been crushed by the enemy?","Noah had pondered such a question.","And as he was talking with Anaximander in the Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature...","HUUM!","The skies of this endless shore began to vibrate!","From above, Existence shuddered with awe and glory as something began to form. Something that radiated authority beyond what most beings could comprehend. Something that made the very fabric of reality bow in acknowledgment.","An Embodiment!","A power of an Absolute!","Noah raised his gaze up sharply as...he didn’t see any force of life as this Embodiment seemed to be just that alone, an Embodiment sent out across Existence.","And he saw things differently compared to others.","He saw clusters of 18 Phonemes make up a single Logos. Then 81 of those Logos intertwined and multiplied endlessly to form 729 Philologies. And these Philologies twisted and distorted against each other to simply declare the Embodiment that burned with THE Way of... Existence!","The construction was beyond anything he had witnessed before. Layer upon layer of linguistic authority building toward a singular expression of absolute power. The First Tongue being wielded at a scale that made his own achievements look meager!","The Embodiment blazed with multicolored radiance that contained every hue that could be perceived and many that could not. It was formless yet defined. Abstract yet undeniably present. A manifestation of the simple, overwhelming truth that things WERE rather than WERE NOT.","And then it spoke with an utterly glorious, booming voice.","The Voice of...THE Creature.","\" Those who have stood alongside Existence shall be rewarded.\"","The voice was not loud, yet it resonated through every particle of reality within the Early Veiled Shore.","\" Those who have suffered for their loyalty shall be elevated.\"","The words carried weight that pressed down upon everything.","\" Those who have been collapsed shall rise again, stronger than before.\"","BOOM!","Right after, beams of incandescent multicolored light shot out from the Embodiment!","They descended with the inevitability of gravity itself!","One smashed onto THE Living Origin!","One smashed onto THE First Hunger!","One smashed onto Anaximander!","Noah’s eyes remained locked on the Embodiment as the beam produced from it which struck Anaximander was a glorious one. He could feel it from meters away. Its immensity was suffocating enough to make one fall to their knees!","And across the Early Veiled Shore, beings did drop to their knees!","But Noah remained standing defiantly.","His own foundation, compressed though it was by the distance from his primary body, refused to bow. His Seals of Absolute Tongue pulsed with recognition of the linguistic mastery being displayed, and his eyes burned with the tyranny that defined his Way.","He saw the sheer existence of Anaximander pulse with immensity!","He saw THE Living Origin and Tor, THE First Hunger, undergo transformations that defied normal progression!","The immensity of their Depths rapidly began to rise!","They crossed into THE Intermediate Depth threshold!","They surged toward THE Fundamental Depth!","But then something unique happened.","BOOM !","From the descending pillars of light, multicolored hammers bloomed!","They smashed onto THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger as if compressing their Depth! Packing more and more immensity into them! Condensing power that should have elevated them further into denser, more refined foundations!","While they remained at Intermediate Depth, the Weight they gave off increased more and more!","It was like watching someone forge a blade. Taking raw material and hammering it repeatedly until what remained was harder, sharper, more dangerous than the original substance could ever have been.","Their foundations were being perfected!","Anaximander was unique.","He didn’t seem to emanate any waves of immensity. His form remained as calm and unassuming as ever, that ancient scientist who had seen more of Existence than most could imagine. Yet he seemed to be benefiting in his own way.","At this moment, he had a wry smile bloom as he looked toward Noah.","\" Ah, my friend, it seems I must go right some wrongs.\"","His voice was light despite the overwhelming pressure surrounding them.","\" Just like you called for me not too long ago, right now, THE Creature is calling out to me.\"","His eyes grew distant as if hearing something beyond normal perception.","\" He has said... Come, Anaximander!\"","HUUM!","The words were heavy!","Anaximander began to float upward, drawn by authority that transcended distance and dimension. His hand let go of the vibrant stick he had been carrying.","THE Goad of THE Creature!","It fell toward the grouns as Anaximander’s Weavings began to disappear, his form becoming translucent as he was pulled toward whatever summons THE Creature had issued.","He looked toward Noah one final time.","\"I will also come if you need me, just let me know.\"","His smile remained warm despite the forces acting upon him.","\" For now, if you can take care of things here just until after I return, that will b-\"","WAP!","Before his words even finished, Anaximander disappeared!","Gone in an instant, summoned by THE Creature to destinations unknown for purposes that only those at THE Absolute level could comprehend.","Noah remained imperious.","His gaze landed on THE Goad of THE Creature as it fell, the ancient artifact pulsing as it remained upright.","He gazed over to Tor and THE Living Origin.","The former gazed up with a look of annoyance and defiance. As if he didn’t want this. As if being elevated by THE Creature’s power was somehow an insult to his pride. His body trembled with the effort of containing the compressed foundation being forced upon him.","\" This ...!\" Tor growled through gritted teeth . \"I didn’t ask for this !\"","But the hammer continued to fall regardless.","While THE Living Origin... had a saddened gaze.","As if she didn’t care much for this elevation. As if she wanted something else entirely. Her ancient eyes held depths of loss that no amount of power could fill. Whatever she truly desired, it was not strength.","Noah looked at all of this with calculating eyes.","It seemed those THE Creature considered to have sided with him were getting boons and elevations right now.","THE Living Origin he could understand. She had been one of THE Creature’s most devoted followers before THE Living Paradox collapsed her Civilization and cast her adrift.","But Tor?","Tor was killed by THE Creature!","Was this his way of paying back? His way of acknowledging that the death had been... what? A mistake? Or simply a debt that needed settling?","And if THE Living Origin was receiving this boon because she had been collapsed by THE Living Paradox before...","Noah’s gaze rapidly changed!","His eyes flickered with realization!","His consciousness surged toward Muspelheim!"]},{"number":4763,"title":"Chapter 4763: Chapter 4762: What?! III","paragraphs":["There, a body of his under the control of Ruination woke up.","He had been dormant while the partial simulation of THE Living Concept was being run, but now his awareness flooded back into this vessel as he looked toward... Khor!","And as if on fucking cue...","BOOM!","The skies of Muspelheim tore open!","The same Embodiment appeared, blazing with multicolored radiance that contained the authority of Existence itself! The Muspeli Lifeforms throughout the realm almost dropped to their knees as pressure beyond their comprehension descended upon their burning domain!","A similar multicolored beam of existential light smashed into Khor!","Her Depth and Weight rapidly became elevated! Her form, already powerful at THE Surface Depth, began to condense further! A flaming hammer appeared above her and smashed down, compressing her power at an alarming degree!","It was forging her foundation here and now!","Taking what she had built through eons of Hunger and refining it into something denser, harder, more lethal!","In the surroundings, THE Infiniverse watched on with stern eyes.","And shockingly, it wasn’t only a single beam of light!","Another one descended on... THE First Farmer!","The ancient cultivator who had tended to farms since before most civilizations existed found himself bathed in multicolored radiance! His connection to Effort and harvest pulsed with new authority as his foundation was similarly compressed and refined!","And then another beam descended on...","Sigrid!","THE Living Order!","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes buzzed as he watched one of his closest pillar become engulfed in light! The multicolored radiance wrapped around her form, and a hammer of pure Existence descended to forge her foundation alongside the others!","Even Sigrid? Who had siphoned off and effectively crippled THE Dead Order?","Why would THE Creature do this?","|An Embodiment has manifested across multiple locations simultaneously.|","|This Embodiment carries the authority of THE Creature.|","|The One Who Laid The Claim to Existence Itself.|","|Analysis of Current Event:|","|Certain entities and their Ways have been ordained as targets for this terrifying Embodiment.|","|Selection Criteria Identified:|","|1. Entities who sided with THE Creature during the conflict against THE Living Paradox|","|2. Entities whose Civilizations were collapsed by THE Living Paradox or his instruments|","|3. Entities who have demonstrated loyalty to THE Creature’s designs|","|Targets Confirmed:|","|THE Living Origin - Collapsed by THE Living Paradox. Former backer of THE Creature.|","|THE First Hunger (Tor) - Killed by THE Creature. Debt being repaid.|","|Anaximander - Ally of THE Creature|","|Khor- Collapsed by instruments of THE Living Paradox. Ally of your Civilization.|","|THE First Farmer - Ally of your Civilization. Has history with THE Creature.|","|Sigrid, THE Living Order - This one even I’m shocked by.|","|Boon: Your allies grow stronger. Their foundations become more refined. Their potential increases.|","|Burden: This marks your Civilization as openly opposed to THE Living Paradox in the eyes of all who observe.|","|There is no neutrality after this moment in the ongoing War.|","...!","Noah saw these vibrant prompts as he kept his eyes on that Embodiment!","That Embodiment!","It blazed above Muspelheim with authority that made everything. It was a declaration, a statement that could not be misunderstood by anyone who witnessed it.","THE Creature was making moves.","The Embodiment continued to blaze overhead.","The hammers continued to fall.","And across Observable Existence, the balance of power shifted ever so slightly!","THE Creature made a move to elevate multiple entities with a terrifying Embodiment as Noah observed it all happening and analyzed everything.","He cared not that a beam of light didn’t descend on him.","He never expected any handouts.","His path had always been forged through his own efforts, his own struggles, his own relentless pursuit of advancement. He did not need THE Creature’s direct intervention. He did not want it.","But...","That was HIS First Tongue that Embodiment utilized!","Every Phoneme. Every Logos. Every Philology that constructed that terrifying manifestation of Absolute power drew upon the linguistic foundation that Noah had laid claim to. THE Creature was using The First Tongue at a scale that dwarfed anything Noah could currently achieve, wielding authority that technically belonged to Noah’s domain.","He wanted to gain the full harvest and benefit of those using his Claim in their own complex ways!","His eyes flashed brilliantly as he kept an eye on Sigrid and Khor. The hammers continued to fall upon them, compressing their foundations into something denser and more refined. They would emerge from this stronger than before.","Good.","Let them grow.","Let all his pillars grow.","He gave control of this body back to Ruination, trusting her to manage affairs in Muspelheim while he focused on another body of his.","---","In THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.","In The Stoa of Dogmata.","Another body of Noah appeared in this region where THE Secretive Eon sat calmly.","Her brows raised at his appearance. Again. This Scale Breaker kept showing up in her domain like he owned the place.","Her hand went toward her chin as she smiled with interest.","\" You continue to surprise me again and again, Scale Breaker.\"","Her voice emerged measured and unhurried, each word placed with precision.","\" All these bodies running around everywhere, and you have an Absolute on your trail. Whatever could you be doing right now?\"","She said such words as Noah remained calm and looked at her while positioning himself to float in a region that was a few miles away from her.","\"I have entered THE Agora of Primordial Judgment where your Disciple entered.\"","His voice came steady and informative.","\"A place where every single entrant that arrives in it for the first time gets locked onto THE Surface Depth. I can understand why someone like you, who has plans on top of plans, would not take the risk to enter such a place and expose yourself to so many possibilities.\"","He paused.","\"Is it likely that there are one or two Absolutes already in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment?\"","...!","He said such words calmly.","THE Secretive Eon looked at him and smiled even more. Those dark eyes that could swallow civilizations sparkled with amusement at his probing questions.","\" You have a curious imagination, Scale Breaker.\"","Her voice carried notes of gentle correction.","\" The biggest thing I can tell you about Existence is that there are countless rules and impossibilities out there. And Absolutes exist in order to deny such rules and impossibilities.\"","Her head tilted slightly.","\" What may be applicable to one Absolute that they cannot deny may not be applicable to another Absolute. We are not all the same. We do not all share the same limitations or capabilities.\""]},{"number":4764,"title":"Chapter 4764: Chapter 4763: What?! IV","paragraphs":["She waved her hand dismissively.","\" But really, what are you doing here again when you have to focus on not getting collapsed by an Absolute? Splitting your attention too much, especially while facing an Absolute, could also have detrimental consequences for you.\"","She said such words as if she was actually concerned about him.","Noah knew otherwise.","But he knew of the information hidden within her deflection. Different Absolutes had different capabilities. Different limitations. What affected one might not affect another.","He looked toward the entrance of the Stoa of Dogmata as he continued speaking.","\" When I was moving around in The Earliest Folds, I caught the gaze of a particular tyrant who was curious enough about me to send his curiosity to nearly collapse me and my people some time ago.\"","His eyes burned with remembered fury.","\"I made a promise back then that I would get him back. And he should be...\"","HUUM!","Just as his words were finishing, space in the distance fluctuated!","Reality tore and reformed as something powerful forced its way into the Stoa of Dogmata! The ancient pillars trembled slightly. The inscriptions of Dogmata flickered with recognition of a new presence.","And a moment later...","Gilgamesh appeared!","The First Leader!","His figure was glorious and imposing, radiating authority that made the surrounding atmosphere compress. His form was humanoid but idealized, as if someone had taken the concept of \"leader\" and given it flesh. Golden armor adorned his body in patterns that spoke of conquest and dominion. His eyes were sharp, calculating, filled with the intelligence of one who had commanded legions since before most civilizations existed.","He looked around with those sharp eyes, assessing his surroundings with the caution of a veteran who had survived countless conflicts.","...!","Either he had followed the trail of the chase between Noah and THE Weavers, or THE Weavers had purposefully left a trail that brought him here!","He would have likely gone in and entered THE Agora of Primordial Judgment to continue his pursuit.","But Noah had other plans.","At this moment, he looked toward Gilgamesh calmly!","Because at this moment, he was doing a little thing the kids liked to call... divide and conquer.","The moment Gilgamesh appeared, he locked his eyes on Noah!","And Noah looked back calmly.","\" You were looking for me this whole time, big guy.\"","His voice carried across the Stoa with steady confidence.","\" You were curious about me since The Earliest Folds. At this moment, I wish to close off this curiosity.\"","BOOM!","THE Fundamental Depth of Gilgamesh burned with imperious brilliance!","His aura exploded outward, pressing against reality with the weight of countless victories and endless ambition! The pillars of the Stoa groaned under the pressure! The inscriptions of Dogmata blazed brighter as if responding to the challenge being issued!","And shockingly...","His eyes or gaze did not even turn toward THE Secretive Eon even once.","As if he did not know that she even existed here.","Noah only noted this with veiled interest.","Had this ridiculous being actually made herself imperceptible to anyone else right now? It seemed that Gilgamesh genuinely unaware that an Absolute sat mere miles away, watching this confrontation unfold with amused curiosity.","Well.","That was more than okay.","This was between him and Gilgamesh.","Noah looked toward the First Leader as behind Gilgamesh, golden pools of brilliance began to form like black holes in reverse! Vibrant tips of weapons began to edge out one after another from those pools! Spears and swords and axes and hammers, each one burning with immense Depth and power!","The glory of the First Leader!","Gilgamesh nodded slowly as he observed Noah’s calm demeanor.","\"I have been curious.\"","His voice was deep and resonant, carrying the weight of one who had commanded armies since before time learned to count.","\"I detest that my Weavings and my existence have been led by THE Living Paradox and THE Weavers. I detest that a being like me, a leader among glorious leaders, has been moving under the commands of another.\"","Something flickered in his sharp eyes.","\"I actually envy you a little, Osmont.\"","The words came with surprising honesty.","\" Nobody commands you to do this or that. You decide for yourself how you go about things. Like how you decided to be here right now, however foolish that may be.\"","His lips curved into something that was almost a smile.","\" For that, I am truly envious.\"","HUUM!","His Depth spilled out gloriously!","The air of Unity and Paradox radiated all around him, the dual nature of his allegiance manifesting in visible auras that pressed against reality! Weavings of The First Tongue began to bloom over all of his emerging weapons, linguistic authority coating each blade and spear with enhanced lethality!","At this sight...","Noah’s eyes flashed dangerously.","\" You fucking bum.\"","His voice came out domineeringly and commandingly.","\" Did I say you could use The First Tongue?\"","BOOM!","His words carried the weight of absolute authority!","The Thesis that had not been denied since Muspelheim was applied to Gilgamesh!","None who oppose THE Genesis Monarch may utilize The First Tongue!","The effect was immediate and devastating!","The weapons emerging from Gilgamesh’s golden gates dimmed greatly! The linguistic authority coating them flickered and died! The Weavings of The First Tongue that had been blooming across his arsenal simply... stopped!","He was cut off!","And the Way he expressed became noticeably dimmer!","His aura, which had burned with the combined authority of Unity and Paradox enhanced by The First Tongue, now burned with only its base components. Still powerful. Still dangerous. But noticeably reduced from what it had been moments before.","And yet...","Even when such a thing happened, the figure of Gilgamesh actually began to smile more and more!","An air of brutality and wonder permeated around his skin!","He laughed!","The sound was deep and genuine, filled with the excitement of one who had finally found a worthy challenge after eons of predictable victories!","The paradoxical light around him became more and more intense, his remaining authority surging to compensate for what had been stripped away!","\" Good!\"","His voice boomed across the Stoa.","\" You are the real thing!\"","His eyes blazed with something that looked almost like joy.","\"I have always wanted to break away from Paradox and THE Weavers. Today, at this time, I pit every ounce of my Depth and being here!\"","He raised his arms, and the weapons in his golden gates surged forward despite their diminished state!","\"I lay all that Gilgamesh is... I lay all those I have led and all my accomplishments on this fight!\"","His aura exploded to its maximum intensity!","\"I either come out the other side glorious and with your Claim beneath my feet, or the name and the legend of Gilgamesh shall stop here now!\"","His smile became something feral and beautiful.","\"It can only be one or the other!\"","HUUM!","The words were gloriously heavy and imposing!","After they were said, Noah looked at this being and nodded lightly.","Behind him, a magnificent blue-gold Seal began to rise.","THE Absolute Seal of Infinity!","It burned with patterns of boundlessness that made space itself groan! Endless designs conveyed the concept it represented, and the weight it carried pressed against Gilgamesh’s aura with force that demanded acknowledgment!","\" Then fight.\"","Noah’s voice came calm and certain.","\" Because this... will be the last fight of your existence.\"","...!","The Stoa of Dogmata trembled as two powers prepared to collide!","In the distance, unseen by Gilgamesh but fully visible to Noah, THE Secretive Eon watched with eyes that sparkled with genuine interest.","She had her chin resting on her hand.","She was smiling!"]},{"number":4765,"title":"Chapter 4765: Chapter 4764: What?! V","paragraphs":["In his existence, battles were a dime a dozen.","They came and went like waves upon a shore. Some were memorable. Most were not. Violence was simply a tool to be wielded when necessary, discarded when it no longer served a purpose.","But he wanted to give special attention to Gilgamesh.","Purely because of what this being had done when he sent an attack of curiosity across time.","That golden light that had descended upon Noah and his people in the Early Veiled Shore. That casual display of power that had nearly collapsed everything he was building. That arrogant inquiry from a being who viewed others as interesting specimens rather than equals.","Noah remembered.","And he always collected his debts!","Due to how rapidly he progressed, there were times when enemies he detested... he bypassed their power so completely that it wasn’t even fun when they collapsed beneath his Weight. By the time he was ready to face them, they had become insects beneath his heel. The satisfaction of vengeance was hollow when the target couldn’t even comprehend what was happening to them.","Gilgamesh was at a sweet spot that was just right!","His own Weight and Immensity was breaking toward Fundamental as Gilgamesh would be a worthy existence to carve out his glory! A genuine challenge. A meaningful victory. Something he could savor rather than simply execute.","And as he did this here, he was particularly focused on the actions of his body in the deeper areas of this Vault of Ginnungagap.","He felt like it was time to spread the Phonemes he created.","After seeing THE Creature lay out an Embodiment utilizing The First Tongue and gaining nothing from it... Noah wanted to collect taxes on all the harvest and usage of The First Tongue. He would be able to do so more closely with his personally forged Phonemes!","The 18 Core Phonemes had existed before his Claim. Others had been using them for eons. Harvesting from that usage was indirect, filtered through layers of established practice as the harvest was a mere percentage and ongoing.","But his 9 original Phonemes?","Quintessence. Infinity. Tyranny. Fortune. Advantage. Narrative. Harvest. Hunger. Potential.","These were his creations. His contributions to The First Tongue. Every being who learned and used them would be using something that Noah had personally brought into existence.","The harvest from that would be direct.","The harvest from that would be his alone as he would tax absolutely everyone!","So as a glorious battle began to show a supposed leader what a true tyrannical leader was like, his gaze flickered to another place deeper from here.","Back in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment!","In the library of The Glossarians that represented an opportunity to collapse an Absolute while reinforcing his Way again and again, and obtaining the treasures lying within this Vault of Ginnungagap!","---","In the Logoseion.","The atmosphere was thick with anticipation.","Noah floated above the swirling blue-gold plasma sea, his toga inscribed with shifting Phonemes, his laurel of crystallized language catching light that seemed to come from nowhere. The zero upon his chest marked him as a newcomer. A Hoplite with zero Merit daring to challenge a Lochagos with nearly 450.","Opposite him, Theoris the Articulate maintained her position with casual elegance. Her vibrant spectacles reflected the plasma sea below. Her dark hair flowed in currents of linguistic energy that swirled around her form. Her toga displayed CDXLVIII in glowing numerals.","The surrounding Glossarians watched in silence.","This was the scholarly air of the Logoseion. Even though many carried looks of mocking amusement, even though laughter had rippled through the crowd moments before, they did not scream or roar out their entertainment. They stayed silent while watching the debate ahead.","This was a place of learning.","Even foolishness could teach valuable lessons.","Hoplites of various forms sat in circular arrangement, their eyes fixed on the confrontation. Bears and serpents and humanoids and abstract beings, all wearing blue-gold togas, all curious to see how badly this newcomer would be humiliated.","The Lochagoi present observed with more nuanced expressions. Some showed pity. Some showed boredom. A few showed the faintest glimmers of interest, wondering if perhaps this Hoplite knew something they didn’t.","Ophelia watched from the crowd with wide eyes, her serpentine form coiled tightly with concern for the newcomer she had been assigned to guide.","Lumivara’s tail swished with barely contained excitement.","Ul’moreth’s veiled eyes burned with anticipation.","Skoll sat on his haunches with his tongue out, not understanding what was happening but happy to be here with his new Master.","Theoris gazed at Noah with imperious confidence.","\"I will not even push for a complex debate of Logos or Philologies for you.\"","Her voice carried the patient condescension of a teacher addressing a particularly slow student.","\" We can simply conjure a single Phoneme and see who writes it out the best. To its truest expression.\"","She adjusted her spectacles with one finger.","\" This is the most basic test of linguistic understanding. If you cannot even express a single Phoneme with clarity, there is no point discussing higher constructs.\"","Her lips curved into a smile that held no warmth.","\" Consider this a lesson, Hoplite. Learn from your failure today, and perhaps in a few centuries, you might be worthy of standing where you currently stand.\"","...!","Her words were calm with a hint of majesty.","As if she was taking the time to educate a junior!","As if this debate was already decided and she was simply going through the motions out of obligation!","The surrounding Glossarians nodded with approval at her generosity. She was giving this foolish newcomer the simplest possible test. She was being merciful.","Theoris raised her finger.","Light began to gather at its tip.","She inscribed the Phoneme of Fire into the air before her!","The construct blazed into existence with fiery brilliance! Crimson and blue light intertwined in patterns that spoke of combustion and heat and transformation! The Phoneme burned above the plasma sea with intensity that made nearby observers shield their eyes!","It was beautiful.","It was precise.","It was the work of someone who had spent eons refining their understanding of this single concept. Every curve of the inscription was perfect. Every line carried meaning that supported and enhanced the whole. The Phoneme of Fire as Theoris expressed it was a masterwork of linguistic artistry.","The crowd murmured with appreciation.","This was why she was close to becoming a Polemarch. This was the standard against which this foolish Hoplite would be measured.","Noah looked at it.","His eyes traced every line. Every curve. Every subtle inflection of meaning that Theoris had woven into her expression of Fire.","Then he nodded.","\" Adequate .\"","...!","The word hung in the air.","What?","Adequate?","ADEQUATE?!","Whispers erupted through the Logoseion! Hoplites exchanged glances of disbelief! Lochagoi raised eyebrows at the sheer audacity of this newcomer!","Theoris’s expression flickered with the first hint of irritation.","\" Adequate ?\" she repeated, her voice carrying dangerous edges. \" You dare call my expression of Fire merely adequate? Do you have any idea how many years I have spent refining-\"","But before she could finish.","Before anyone could react.","Noah waved his hand.","And he revealed not merely the Phoneme of Fire.","He revealed THE Absolute Seal of Fire!","BOOM!","The moment it fully came to fruition, the entire Logoseion shuddered!","The Seal blazed into existence above Noah’s palm with radiance that made Theoris’s Phoneme look like a candle beside a sun! It was massive, perhaps ten meters in diameter, and it burned with patterns of such impossible complexity that observers felt their minds straining just to perceive its edges!","This was Fire.","Not the Fire that mortals understood. Not the Fire that even ancient scholars had spent eons studying.","This was Fire as it existed in the deepest foundations of reality. Fire as a concept so fundamental that it predated the formation of stars. Fire as one of the 18 pillars upon which The First Tongue itself was constructed.","And more than that...","Within the Seal, compressed and refined and made infinitely more dense, were the Stanchions that Noah had absorbed into this singular expression. Every aspect of combustion. Every facet of heat. Every nuance of transformation through burning.","All of it contained in one perfect, impossible construct.","Theoris was stunned!","Her vibrant spectacles seemed to fog over as she looked the Seal up and down, her enhanced perception struggling to process what she was witnessing!","It was the Phoneme of Fire.","But so much more glorious!","So much more... complete!","She had spent years on years perfecting her expression of Fire. She had believed herself among the greatest practitioners of this particular Phoneme in all of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","And this newcomer had just casually displayed something that made her life’s work look like a child’s first attempt at writing!","She was not the only one affected.","When Glossarians looked up and saw the Seal, they were initially confused.","What was this? It looked like the Phoneme of Fire, but the structure was wrong. No, not wrong. Different. More. It was as if someone had taken the Phoneme they all knew and revealed that it was merely a shadow of something far greater.","Then shock rippled through the crowd!","This was real. This was actually happening. A Hoplite with zero Merit had just displayed mastery of Fire that exceeded anything the Logoseion had witnessed in recorded memory!","Then contemplation descended.","An immense silence fell across the entire chamber. All eyes focused on that Seal. All minds struggled to understand what they were seeing. All preconceptions about this debate were being violently restructured.","That Seal!","That impossible, glorious, reality-defining Seal!","Even Ul’moreth and Lumivara looked at it with vibrant eyes!","They had not fully seen Noah’s Seals before. They had witnessed his mastery of The First Tongue. But seeing it displayed here, in this ancient place of linguistic study, surrounded by beings who had dedicated their entire existences to understanding these concepts...","It hit differently.","At this time, Noah allowed the Seal to continue burning above his palm.","He looked out at the gathered Glossarians with eyes that held the calm certainty of one who knew exactly what he was doing.","\" Today, I wish to do many things.\"","His voice carried across the silent Logoseion with weight that pressed against every listener.","\" This is just a glimpse.\"","He gestured toward the Seal of Fire, toward the impossible perfection it represented.","\" Barring this debate, I wish to make a contribution and elevate what the Glossarians know about The First Tongue.\"","The Seal pulsed with radiance that made the plasma sea below churn with excited energy.","\" Today...\"","His eyes swept across Hoplites and Lochagoi alike.","\"I wish to teach.\"","...!","BOOM!","The words landed like hammers upon the foundations of everything the Glossarians believed!","A Hoplite.","A newcomer with zero Merit.","Claiming that he wished to TEACH those who had studied The First Tongue for eons?!","But that Seal continued to burn above his palm.","That impossible, undeniable proof of mastery that exceeded anything they had achieved.","And slowly, one by one, the mocking expressions faded from faces throughout the Logoseion.","Something was happening here!"]},{"number":4766,"title":"Chapter 4766: Chapter 4765: I Wish To Expand! I","paragraphs":["A Hoplite wished to teach after they showed a Lochagos a much grander version of the Phoneme of The First Tongue!","And first and foremost, because of this...","The booming voice of the Logoseion echoed out with weight that made the plasma sea churn!","\"A unique construct of the Phoneme of Fire of The First Tongue has been presented!\"","The words resonated through every corner of the chamber.","\" The Hoplite has triumphed over Lochagos Theoris the Articulate! His expression of Fire exceeds all recorded variations within the Logoseion archives! This is unprecedented for a newcomer!\"","Theoris floated in stunned silence, her vibrant spectacles still reflecting the impossible Seal that burned above Noah’s palm.","\" 5 MERIT POINTS awarded for winning a debate against someone of higher ranking and showing what has been deemed to be new!\"","The voice paused with what might have been curiosity.","\" And now, you wish to... teach? What should you be referred to as, Hoplite?\"","...!","The voice asked such a question as at this time, on Noah’s toga, the Merit points changed.","Zero became V.","Zero became five.","The first step on a long climb.","Noah looked out at the gathered Glossarians with eyes that held the calm certainty of absolute conviction.","\" Osmont. THE Genesis Monarch.\"","WAA!","He said his distinction out clearly!","The words landed with weight that made several nearby Hoplites take unconscious steps backward. THE Genesis Monarch. Not merely a title, but a declaration of what he was and what he represented.","The booming voice of the Logoseion echoed out again.","\" THE Genesis Monarch wishes to make a contribution to the Glossarians. He has proven himself worthy of attention through unprecedented expression of a Core Phoneme.\"","A pause.","\" Permission has been granted to display any novelty and wonder. The Logoseion awaits.\"","Many eyes went toward him.","Hundreds of Glossarians. Hoplites who had mocked him moments ago now watching with uncertain expressions. Lochagoi who had expected entertainment now leaning forward with genuine interest. Even a few Polemarchs in the distant shadows stirred.","Noah looked back at the masses.","Then he spoke.","\" Language is the foundation of reality.\"","His voice carried across the Logoseion with the weight of absolute truth.","\" This is what the Glossarians believe. This is what I know to be true. The First Tongue was not merely discovered. It was the medium through which Existence itself was first expressed. Every Phoneme represents a fundamental concept. Every Logos builds meaning from those concepts. Every Philology weaves those meanings into complex truths.\"","He let those words settle.","\" But at times, the letters of a language are not enough to portray the full immensity of what the language could express.\"","His eyes swept across the gathered scholars.","\" Languages evolve. Languages grow. Languages expand to encompass new ideas that their original creators never imagined. This is the nature of all communication, from the simplest grunts of primitive beings to the most sophisticated expressions of Absolute authority.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\" Sometimes, someone has to rise. Someone has to look at a language and say... this is something I can add on to. This is something I can make more complete. This is something I can elevate beyond what it currently is.\"","He raised his hand.","\" And that is what I wish to do.\"","The Seal of Fire above his palm pulsed with anticipation.","\"I wish to expand The First Tongue.\"","BOOM!","What!","WHAT?!","The reactions were immediate and overwhelming!","Since they were scholars, nobody erupted in screaming or shouting. The Logoseion maintained its atmosphere of academic dignity even in the face of such outrageous claims.","But the Depths and Immensities of all those present flared!","Every Hoplite locked onto Noah with gazes that burned with incredulity!","Every Lochagos released waves of suppressed authority that pressed against his existence!","Even the distant Polemarchs stirred with displeasure that made the very air compress!","It was as if they were already admonishing him for his words!","To expand The First Tongue?!","Who did he think he was?!","The First Tongue was THE First Tongue! It had existed since before differentiation! It was complete! It was perfect! It was the foundation upon which all of reality was built!","18 Phonemes with countless variations that could make countless Logos and Philologies! Who among them had ever thought of expanding it? Adding another letter?! This was preposterous! This was blasphemy! This was the ravings of a madman who had somehow stumbled upon a single impressive technique!","But this was the Logoseion.","This was a place of learning and debate.","Even with their heavy reactions, they listened.","They had to listen.","Because that was what scholars did.","Noah turned his gaze toward Ul’moreth.","The ancient Ginnu Lifeform who had acted like his teacher in Ginnungagap what seemed like eons ago. Who had taught him how to write the Phoneme of Fire. Who had shared knowledge that had fundamentally transformed his understanding of linguistic authority.","Today, the roles would reverse.","\" Existence is vast and full of wonders.\"","Noah’s voice came measured and certain.","\" Something always needed in a language is the sense of endless immensity that Existence can have. The concept of boundlessness. The idea that there are no limits to what can be achieved, no barriers that cannot be overcome, no horizons that cannot be exceeded.\"","He raised his finger.","\" And for that...\"","He began to write.","The first stroke cut through the air with precision that made several Lochagoi gasp!","Blue-gold light trailed from his fingertip, leaving behind lines of concentrated linguistic authority that burned with power none of them had ever witnessed in a mere inscription!","The second stroke curved outward, connecting to the first in ways that spoke of expansion without end!","The third stroke folded back upon itself, creating patterns that suggested infinity through elegant recursion!","Stroke after stroke, Noah wrote the Phoneme of Infinity in slow motion!","Each movement was deliberate. Each line was perfect. Each curve carried meaning that built upon the previous curves to create something that had never existed before in the understanding of these ancient scholars.","The Phoneme took shape.","It was not like the 18 Core Phonemes they all knew. It was not a variation or a refinement of existing concepts. It was something genuinely new. Something that filled a gap they had never realized existed in The First Tongue.","And when Noah completed the final stroke...","HUUM!","The Phoneme of Infinity blazed into existence!","All Glossarians looked up with widening eyes of horror and astonishment!","It was real.","It was genuine.","It was a Phoneme of The First Tongue that none of them had ever seen, ever studied, ever imagined could exist!","Ul’moreth trembled!","The ancient Ginnu Lifeform who had taught Noah the basics of linguistic inscription now stared at something his student had created! His countless hairs rippled with emotion that transcended normal expression! His veiled eyes burned with tears that were not tears but concentrated wonder!","This was what his Little Anomaly had become!","This was what Noah had achieved!","The brilliance of the Phoneme of Infinity cast blue-gold radiance across every face in the Logoseion. It burned with patterns of boundlessness that made observers feel as if they could perceive eternity itself. It was beautiful. It was profound. It was undeniably, impossibly real.","Noah looked at his creation with calm satisfaction.","\" For my contribution at this time, I give you the Phoneme of Infinity.\"","His voice carried across the stunned silence.","\" An addition to the letters of Existence. The 19th Phoneme of The First Tongue.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4767,"title":"Chapter 4767: Chapter 4766: I Wish To Expand! II","paragraphs":["His words were like pouring oil into fire!","Boundless Depths rose and surged all around!","All Hoplites and Lochagoi here clamored with utter incredulity as they analyzed this brand new Phoneme! Their minds raced to understand what they were seeing! Their foundations trembled as core beliefs were being restructured in real time!","In the distance and hidden in the back, a few Polemarchs floated forward with faces of shock!","These were beings who had achieved THE Fundamental Depth within this domain! Beings whose mastery of The First Tongue had been considered supreme among the Glossarians! And they looked at this new Phoneme with expressions that ranged from disbelief to dawning wonder!","Most wanted to say this was impossible.","Most wanted to declare that such a thing could not be viable.","But as Glossarians, they could tell it was genuine and true!","The Phoneme of Infinity was not a trick. It was not an illusion. It was not some elaborate deception designed to fool those who should know better.","It was real.","It was functional.","It was a genuine addition to The First Tongue itself.","So much so that in the next moment, with trembling fingers, one of the Polemarchs floated fully into view.","He looked like an old man despite being a Primordial Perfected Ginnu Lifeform. White hair flowed around a face carved with lines of ancient wisdom. His toga displayed Merit points in the hundreds. His eyes burned with the need to verify what he was witnessing.","In this heavy silence, he raised his finger.","He began to mimic what Noah had just written.","Stroke by stroke, trembling with each movement, the ancient Polemarch inscribed the Phoneme of Infinity into the air before him.","And it worked.","HUUM !","A smaller, less refined version of the Phoneme blazed into existence before the Polemarch!","\" Infinity...!\"","He said such words as if they were sacred!","His voice cracked with emotion that beings of his caliber rarely displayed! He looked at the Phoneme he had just created, then looked toward Noah with astonishment that bordered on reverence!","All Glossarians looked toward Noah with astonishment!","Their minds were buzzing!","There was a singular question permeating throughout the Logoseion, whispered and shouted and contemplated in equal measure!","Who had the capability to design a new letter of The First Tongue?!","Who was this being?!","What was THE Genesis Monarch?!","But even before they could fully contemplate this...","Noah spoke again.","But these words were not for them.","These words were for himself alone, declarations made in the depths of his existence where only his own consciousness could hear.","\" This Phoneme, and others I shall unveil, shall have an Existential Tariff imposed on them!\"","His internal voice carried the weight of absolute decree.","\" In addition to any cost to enact this Phoneme, users must pay an additional 100% Existential Tariff for any usage of my Core Phonemes!\"","His eyes blazed with Tyranny.","\" And a 1,000% Existential Tariff for any usage by those aligned with Paradox!\"","His Seals pulsed with enforcement authority.","\" Every time anyone utilizes these Phonemes, a cost must be paid to me as if it were an inherent weight needed to be paid! This is the price of using what I have created! This is the tax upon my intellectual property! This is my harvest!\"","...!","| EXISTENTIAL TARIFF SYSTEM INITIALIZED|","|You have chosen to fully and extensively spread your designed Core Phonemes across Existence.|","|Beginning with the Phoneme of Infinity.|","|Tariff Structure Established:|","|Base Tariff: 100% of Existential Cost for any usage of your 9 Core Phonemes|","|This means: For every Unit of Everythings spent to utilize Infinity, Quintessence, Tyranny, Fortune, Advantage, Narrative, Harvest, Hunger, or Potential, an equal amount is automatically harvested and transferred to THE Genesis Monarch.|","|Paradox Alignment Tariff: 1,000% of Existential Cost|","|This means: For any entity aligned with THE Living Paradox who utilizes your Core Phonemes, ten times the power spent is automatically harvested.|","|This includes all members of THE Loom, all servants of Paradox, and all who have sworn allegiance to his designs.|","|Collection Mechanism:|","|Harvest occurs automatically upon Phoneme activation.|","|No action required from THE Genesis Monarch.|","|Collected essence is filtered directly into your Weight and Immensity.|","|This compounds with existing harvest from The Arche of Perpetual Harvest.|","|Spread Protocol:|","| As your Core Phonemes are taught, learned, and utilized across Existence, the Tariff system expands accordingly.|","|Every new user becomes a source of passive harvest.|","|Every utilization feeds your advancement.|","|The more your Phonemes spread, the greater your harvest becomes.|","|Current Projection:|","|The Glossarians of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment represent approximately 5,000 entities.|","|If even 10% adopt and regularly utilize your Core Phonemes, projected harvest exceeds current intake by 340%.|","|As knowledge spreads beyond this domain, projections become incalculable.|","|Warning:|","|This system will make you a target for those who resent paying tribute for linguistic authority.|","|Entities aligned with Paradox will particularly despise the enhanced Tariff imposed upon them.|","|Tariff System: ACTIVE|","|Harvest Collection: ENGAGED|","| Let the taxes flow.|","...!","Amidst the shock of the Glossarians, Noah began talking again as if nothing was happening.","As if he hadn’t just restructured his entire harvest system.","As if he wasn’t about to become exponentially more powerful with every usage of what he was teaching.","\" Existence contains not just infinity, but also the essence of what things fundamentally are.\"","His voice drew their attention back from their spiraling thoughts.","\" The purest expression of any concept. The ideal form that all variations aspire toward.\"","He raised his finger again.","\" Quintessence.\"","And he began to write.","The Phoneme of Quintessence took shape in the air, burning with authority that spoke of fundamental perfection! Its strokes were different from Infinity, carrying meaning that complemented rather than duplicated!","The Glossarians watched with eyes that couldn’t look away!","\" And Existence contains the will to dominate. The drive to stand above all others. The refusal to bow before any authority but one’s own.\"","His finger moved again.","\" Tyranny.\"","The Phoneme of Tyranny blazed into being, pressing down upon observers with weight that made even Polemarchs shift uncomfortably!"]},{"number":4768,"title":"Chapter 4768: Chapter 4767: Change! I","paragraphs":["\" Existence contains the flow of fortune. The currents of luck that determine outcomes beyond mere skill. This is Fortune.\"","Another Phoneme joined the growing constellation!","\" Existence contains the constant seeking of advantage. The drive to be better positioned than any opponent. That is Advantage.\"","BOOM!","The Phoneme burned with competitive radiance!","\" Existence contains stories. The power of narrative to shape reality through the tales we tell.\"","\"Narrative.\"","This Phoneme seemed to whisper of possibilities yet to be written!","\" Existence contains the gathering of rewards. The collection of what has been earned through effort and victory. That can only be Harvest.\"","The Phoneme pulsed with acquisitive energy that made Noah’s own foundations resonate!","\" Existence contains the endless desire for more. The drive that pushes beings to consume and grow without limit.\"","\"Hunger.\"","This Phoneme burned with appetite that made several observers unconsciously step back!","\" And Existence contains the seeds of what could be. The unrealized possibilities waiting to bloom into actuality. That is Potential.\"","The final Phoneme joined its siblings, burning with promise that spoke of futures yet to unfold!","In the end, 9 radiant Phonemes nobody here had seen before floated vibrantly above the plasma sea!","Infinity! Quintessence! Tyranny! Fortune! Advantage! Narrative! Harvest! Hunger! Potential!","Nine new letters of The First Tongue!","Nine additions to a language that had been considered complete since before differentiation!","Noah looked at his creations with the satisfaction of a craftsman displaying his finest work.","\" This... is my contribution to The First Tongue.\"","His voice carried across the utterly silent Logoseion.","\" 9 Phonemes that will give rise to countless more Logos and Philologies. 9 letters to complete the language.\"","BOOM!","As the Glossarians observed the 9 Phonemes, absolutely nobody could say a single word!","Their eyes only reflected these letters!","It was as if their entire lives, they had only known of numbers one through nine.","And now, they were learning that ten and eleven and twelve and thirteen and fourteen and fifteen and sixteen and seventeen and eighteen existed!","Their understanding of The First Tongue had just been fundamentally, irrevocably expanded!","And the one who had done this...","THE Genesis Monarch...","Stood before them with zero expression of pride or arrogance.","Only the calm certainty of one who knew exactly what he was worth.","Oh!","Everything was eerily quiet.","As if nobody even knew how to proceed.","The Logoseion itself seemed to question the reality of what had just occurred. That booming voice that had presided over countless debates across eons of existence was also stumped. The plasma sea below churned with uncertain energy. The Phonemes floating above cast their radiance upon faces frozen in expressions of incomprehension.","And then...","Noah’s toga pulsed.","The number of Merit Points displayed upon his chest began to jump by the dozens every moment!","V became X(5 became 10).","X became XX.","XX became L.","L became C(50 became 100).","The numerals shifted and changed with increasing rapidity as the Logoseion’s assessment systems struggled to quantify what had just been contributed! Each new Phoneme represented value beyond normal parameters! Each addition to The First Tongue exceeded anything the Merit system had been designed to reward!","The Glossarians had their eyes locked onto the Phonemes floating in the air gloriously. Nine new letters of the oldest language. Nine additions to what had been considered complete and unchangeable since before Observable Existence took its current form.","Only now did the voice of the Logoseion echo out.","But it was filled with an immense sense of heaviness and grandeur that had not been present before.","\" In Existence, there are none who can add on to something unchanged since Observable Existence came to be.\"","The words resonated through every corner of the chamber.","\" The First Tongue has remained constant across eons beyond counting. Civilizations have risen and fallen. Absolutes have emerged and collapsed. Reality itself has been reshaped countless times.\"","A pause that seemed to stretch into eternity.","\" And through all of that, The First Tongue remained the same. 18 Phonemes. No more. No less.\"","The plasma sea churned with agitation.","\" On this day, a contribution has been made to THE Agora of Primordial Judgment that exceeds all parameters. The maximum number of Merits Glossarians can give are being granted to THE Genesis Monarch.\"","Noah’s toga pulsed again.","C became CC.","CC became CCC.","The numbers continued climbing toward heights that would soon breach the threshold of Lochagos entirely.","\" As a show of recognition of this unfathomable accomplishment, and speaking on behalf of all those here...\"","The voice grew heavier.","More serious.","More profound.","\" THE Genesis Monarch is asked... are you HIM?\"","HUUM!","The voice was booming and serious!","As if it had to ascertain something that was unfathomably grand!","Only a single entity would be able to do something as ridiculous as expand the language of Existence. Only one being in all of reality held the authority to add new letters to The First Tongue itself.","So at this moment, these entities that had studied The First Tongue for all their lives had to ask...","Was he HIM?!","Was this newcomer, this Hoplite who had arrived mere moments ago with zero Merit...","Was he The One Who Laid The Claim?!","Noah looked at these ancient entities of variable power.","He could sense more and more Polemarchs and their auras arriving from the distance, drawn by disturbances in the linguistic fabric that they could feel even from miles away. They were converging on the Logoseion with speed that spoke of desperate need to understand what was happening.","He raised his head imperiously.","\"I am HIM.\"","The words landed like hammers upon the foundations of everything.","\" And as of today, the newborn Phonemes of The First Tongue shall be released for usage and integration across Observable Existence.\"","His eyes swept across every face present.","\" Learn of them. Utilize them. And witness glory.\"","His voice rose with the weight of absolute decree.","\" Witness immensity!\"","BOOM!","His declaration was heavy and grand at the same time!","It began like so.","A simple set of words that were only a Declaration.","But what they stood for and consisted of was far too grand!"]},{"number":4769,"title":"Chapter 4769: Chapter 4768: Change! II","paragraphs":["Many significant entities across Existence had sensed that something had changed regarding The First Tongue when Noah had initially designed the nine brand new Phonemes. They had felt disturbances in the linguistic fabric. They had perceived alterations to something that should have been immutable.","But they did not know exactly what.","At this moment, the one who designed what was new allowed for it to be fully spread out!","And it was only after he was ready to tax everyone on it!","So this Declaration, even though it was simple in nature, began to grow in immensity and grandeur!","It permeated across THE Agora of Primordial Judgment!","It spread even further, reaching toward the boundaries of this Corrupted Domain!","It grew from a Declaration... and went toward an Embodiment!","Well, partial.","A power that only a special subset of beings held across Existence!","It burned brightly to become... another Partial Embodiment that Noah had uttered!","The First Tongue had been altered!","And at this time, THE Genesis Monarch made it available to all!","---","Across Observable Existence.","Countless things were tainted and corrupted, but the musings of Paradox and Existence continued clashing like always.","At this moment, if one could envision an endless sea of obsidian-gold Paradox and an endless sea of multicolored Existence clashing... they would see the meeting of an unstoppable force going against an immovable object!","Two fundamental approaches to reality engaged in eternal conflict!","Two of THE Four locked in struggle that had defined the shape of everything since before differentiation!","Everything seemed to be at a balance in these endlessly roiling seas of conflict.","Paradox pushed against Existence.","Existence pushed back against Paradox.","Neither gained ground.","Neither lost it.","An equilibrium maintained across fronts that spanned Observable Existence itself.","And yet at this time...","A subtle change bloomed!","Something that affected both!","At the center of the endlessly twisting sea of Paradox, the visage of THE Living Paradox could be observed.","All around him, unfathomable waves of immensity seethed! Obsidian-gold light that contradicted itself with every fluctuation! Authority so profound that reality simply stopped trying to make sense in his presence!","And at this moment, his barely discernible face frowned.","He sensed something.","The Phonemes of The First Tongue that existed in the periphery of this place buzzed with new energy. They vibrated with alterations that should have been impossible. They carried meanings that had not existed moments before.","He turned his attention toward them.","And yes, they were in the periphery.","Because gloriously, for gigaparsecs around THE Living Paradox, there was only Paradox.","Around him, Existence was not made up of substrates and particles that everyone knew. There were no conventional building blocks of reality. There was only Paradox! Absolute Paradox! A domain where contradiction was the fundamental law and impossibility was the default state! No First Tongue. No Chaos. No Existence. Only...PARADOX!","But Existence was still Existence.","And The First Tongue permeated across Existence.","Even here, in the periphery of Paradox’s domain, language existed. Even here, Phonemes carried meaning. Even here, the oldest authority maintained its presence.","At this time, he sensed the alteration in The First Tongue.","A new makeup freely unveiled itself!","The perceptive eyes of THE Living Paradox were grand as he very quickly saw through everything. He saw new musings of The First Tongue freely express themselves as they were...","\" Infinity...\"","He listed the first one, tasting the concept as it manifested before his perception.","\" Quintessence...\"","His frown deepened.","\" Tyranny... Fortune... Advantage...\"","Each Phoneme he named seemed to pulse with recognition of being observed by something at his level.","\" Narrative... Harvest... Hunger... Potential...\"","The Paradoxical seas around him seethed with agitation!","Nine new Phonemes!","Nine additions to The First Tongue!","Nine changes to something that had remained unchanged since he himself had laid his own Claim!","This was a change.","And change could be good.","Change could be bad.","Or in this case... change simply complicated things!","THE Living Paradox gazed out from his domain of absolute contradiction. He didn’t even look toward the distant multicolored sea of Existence that he had been fighting against in multiple different fronts across Observable Existence.","He gazed out toward the far distance.","Toward where THE Weavers had reported discovering Osmont before information from them became cut off. Toward the last known location of his instruments before silence had descended. Toward where something was clearly happening that demanded his attention.","He thought about many things.","The Scale Breaker who had claimed The First Tongue.","The anomaly who had forged new Phonemes.","The variable who kept introducing unpredictability into carefully laid plans.","And then... he smiled.","It was not a pleasant expression.","It was the smile of someone who saw opportunity in apparent setback.","\" Change is change.\"","His voice echoed across the Paradoxical seas with authority that made contradictions multiply!","\" Change to The First Tongue is a change with wide-ranging consequences.\"","His obsidian-gold eyes burned with the light of something that had existed since before differentiation itself.","\"I was waiting for this unpredictability. I was waiting for the Paradox of change to the language that cannot be changed.\"","His smile widened.","\" Every utilization will now aid you. Every time someone uses your precious new Phonemes, you will gain from it. This is your trap.\"","He laughed.","The sound made reality itself flinch.","\" But I can pay the cost, Osmont.\"","His voice carried across distances that defied conventional measurement.","\"I can pay it.\"","BOOM!","With such words, change was ushered across Observable Existence!","This time enacted by another one of THE Four!","THE Living Paradox acknowledged the alteration to The First Tongue. He accepted that his own usage of Infinity, Quintessence, Tyranny, and the others would now feed the one who had created them.","And he was willing to pay that price.","Because whatever advantage Osmont gained from harvesting usage of his Phonemes...","THE Living Paradox was confident it would not be enough.","Not nearly enough.","The Paradox of paying taxes to your enemy while still crushing them... that was a contradiction he could embrace!","And across Observable Existence, the change began fully spreading all around!","A man had imposed a tax.","And he wanted to be paid!"]},{"number":4770,"title":"Chapter 4770: Chapter 4769: Existence Is Too Vast! I","paragraphs":["Across Observable Existence.","In a region filled with multicolored flames, the visage of Anaximander was sitting in an incandescent sea of a massive Embodiment.","The sheer magnitude and concentration of Existence itself was unfathomable!","Waves of multicolored radiance lapped against his ancient form like tides of pure being. The authority of Existence pressed down from all directions, not oppressively, but with the overwhelming presence of something that simply WAS in ways that defied comprehension.","And then came a terrifying contrast.","Anaximander was not sitting alone.","His back was actually facing the back of another entity also seated down.","But the size difference alone was nearly a million times!","Anaximander appeared as nothing more than a speck against the vastness of the figure behind him. A single grain of sand resting against a mountain that stretched beyond the horizon in all directions.","It was not because the other side wanted to show off how much grander they were.","No.","The Weavings of Existence simply at this moment in time did not make it easy for this entity to take their size down to a level that many beings could comprehend. The very Depth and Immensity of their existence would seemingly not allow it.","When one’s being was so fundamentally tied to the concept of Existence itself, reducing oneself became an act of self-contradiction that even THE Creature found difficult to maintain for extended periods.","This massive entity was swirling with incandescent flames all around!","Multicolored fire that contained every hue that could be perceived and many that could not! Flames that did not burn but simply EXISTED with such intensity that observation itself became a challenge!","A unique process was currently taking place between him and Anaximander.","Something that required proximity.","Something that required the ancient wanderer to sit back-to-back with one of THE Four.","At this time, Anaximander raised his head and looked around.","He sensed imperceptible changes in the fabric of reality surrounding them. Subtle shifts in how The First Tongue resonated within this domain. Alterations that most beings would never notice but that his scientific mind immediately began cataloging and analyzing.","And he also felt something from the entity behind him.","Even though THE Creature was so massive that his entire body was shrouded by multicolored flames that would make his entire figure hazy and barely observable... Anaximander could barely perceive a smile on this being.","On THE Creature!","One of THE Four was smiling!","This was notable enough to make Anaximander’s heart beat slightly faster.","So Anaximander looked around as his own scientific mind began to break down exactly what had changed in the Weavings of Existence.","\" Your mood seems to be a little happier.\"","His voice came casual and measured, as if he was talking to any being rather than one of the most powerful entities in all of reality.","\" What just happened?\"","He asked such a question as if inquiring about the weather.","And behind him, the entity shrouded in such terrifying flames of dense Weavings of Existence was quiet for a moment.","The silence stretched.","The multicolored flames crackled with energy that predated most of the Observable Existence.","Then his deep voice echoed out.","It was like listening to the surrounding existence itself speak. Not loud, but resonant in ways that made every particle of Anaximander’s being vibrate.","\"It seems that your friend has gotten a bit more serious.\"","The words were calm and heavy.","\" And is tweaking that which he has laid a claim on.\"","...!","The words were simple in construction but vast in implication!","When Anaximander heard them, his eyes flashed brilliantly!","He seemed to think about all of it heavily. There were many things to be broken down from the simple words of THE Creature. Layers of meaning that unfolded the more one contemplated them.","Your friend.","THE Creature referred to him as Anaximander’s friend.","Has gotten a bit more serious.","This implied that previous actions had been considered less than fully committed. That what came before was merely preliminary.","Tweaking that which he has laid a claim on.","The First Tongue.","Anaximander knew exactly who the entity in question was.","The swirling maelstrom of Existence in the form of this humanoid made a simple motion a moment later.","Just a casual gesture.","But the force alone could crush THE Fundamental Depth entities into paste! The mere movement of THE Creature’s fingers displaced enough authority to collapse lesser beings simply through proximity!","He pinched his fingers.","Moments later, multiple Phonemes of The First Tongue began to gather around him.","The 18 Phonemes everyone was so used to blazed into existence first! Fire and Water and Earth and Air and all the others, arranged in configurations that spoke of absolute mastery!","And additionally...","9 more!","Infinity! Quintessence! Tyranny! Fortune! Advantage! Narrative! Harvest! Hunger! Potential!","They gloriously arranged themselves before THE Creature, new letters joining old in a display that no other being in Existence could casually summon!","Moments later, this entity began to wave his fingers.","Old Phonemes and new Phonemes began to mix!","Hundreds of Logos being formed and broken down rapidly! The process was mesmerizing to observe, combinations that would take most scholars years to construct appearing and dissolving in fractions of seconds!","Then dozens of Philologies began to be formed and broken down at speeds that would even make Absolutes be astonished!","But THE Creature simply seemed to be familiarizing himself with old and new!","Testing how they integrated!","Seeing how the additions changed the possibilities of what could be expressed!","It was like watching a master linguist encountering new letters for the first time, except this linguist had existed since before language itself was differentiated from raw Existence.","Anaximander observed this scene with perceptive eyes.","There were many things he wanted to ask.","About Noah. About the changes. About what this meant for the ongoing conflict with THE Living Paradox. About countless mysteries that accumulated whenever one spent time in the presence of THE Creature.","But ultimately, he asked something simpler.","Something that had been weighing on his mind.","\" Can he also not be considered your friend?\"","...!","Anaximander asked such a simple question.","And truly, it should be simple.","Noah had helped THE Creature’s cause in numerous ways. His Civilization opposed THE Living Paradox. His actions aligned with what Existence represented.","By any reasonable measure, they should be allies.","Friends, even.","And yet...","The moving fingers of THE Creature paused momentarily.","The Phonemes and Logos and Philologies he had been constructing froze in mid-formation.","As if he was deeply pondering this question.","The seconds passed.","The multicolored flames continued their eternal dance.","The Embodiment surrounding them thrummed with energy that exceeded comprehension.","And still, Anaximander did not receive an answer!","The silence grew heavier.","More suffocating!","Eventually, in that heavy, suffocating silence, THE Creature replied.","\" Maybe.\"","His voice came slower than before.","\" Maybe not .\"","A pause that seemed to contain eternities.","\" Existence is vast, Anaximander. Far, far too vast.\"","The multicolored flames around him flickered.","\" And there are many things that even I do not know.\"","...!","BOOM!","The words landed with weight that made reality itself groan!","THE Creature, one of THE Four, the one who had laid the claim on Existence itself...","Admitting that there were things he did not know!","Admitting that even his perception had blind spots!","Anaximander sat in contemplative silence!"]},{"number":4771,"title":"Chapter 4771: Chapter 4770: Existence Is Too Vast! II","paragraphs":["In an entirely different portion of Observable Existence.","THE Living Elemental had a wry expression as he followed THE Living Emotive across the Wastes of THE Fallout toward... a floating obsidian hut.","The scene was a unique one.","THE Living Elemental looked like an entity shrouded by the Phonemes of Fire, Air, Earth, and Water. Four fundamental concepts swirled around his form in constant rotation, each one manifesting as brilliant displays of their respective elements. Flames licked across his shoulders. Winds howled around his arms. Stone formations crystallized and dissolved across his torso. Water flowed in impossible streams around his legs.","He was power made manifest. Authority over the building blocks of physical reality given form.","And yet he followed behind THE Living Emotive like a subordinate trailing after their superior.","THE Living Emotive didn’t seem to have any particular air of power around her.","No swirling elements. No visible manifestations of authority. No overwhelming displays of Depth or Weight that would mark her as something significant.","She appeared almost... ordinary.","A woman of indeterminate age with features that shifted subtly with each expression. Her hair changed color depending on the angle of observation. Her eyes held depths that seemed to contain every feeling that had ever been felt.","And yet the silent aura of an Absolute permeated across those eyes.","Something that transcended mere power. Something that spoke of authority over concepts so fundamental that even other Absolutes treated her with caution.","She was humming and skipping as she moved.","Her entire existence buzzed with manic energy that made the corrupted landscape around them seem calm by comparison. She hopped over twisted formations. She twirled past corrupted zones. She moved with the carefree abandon of a child playing in a garden rather than an Absolute traversing one of the most dangerous regions in Observable Existence.","As they neared the hut...","\" Oh, Big Bad Chaos! We are here!\"","Her voice rang out with cheerful irreverence that made THE Living Elemental wince.","\" And we seem to be arriving at an opportune time...\"","HUUM!","As she finished her words, the door of the hut flung open!","Within it, the figure of an entity circled by endless chaos sat in contemplation.","THE Primordial Chaos.","One of THE Four.","The one who had laid claim to the fundamental principle of disorder itself.","His form was humanoid but shrouded in constantly shifting patterns. Order could not exist in his presence. Predictability fled from his vicinity. Even the simple act of sitting still became an exercise in contradiction when chaos itself was your domain.","His expression had been that of boredom.","But it was slowly changing to interest at this moment.","He was already looking up, sensing the changes that were permeating across Existence. The alterations to The First Tongue. The new Phonemes that had been released.","Things were becoming more chaotic.","And chaos was his domain.","Emotive looked up as she continued to walk into the hut floating in the Wastes of THE Fallout. Her eyes twinkled with amusement that bordered on madness.","She looked toward THE Primordial Chaos with the casual familiarity of someone who had long since stopped being impressed by such entities.","\"I would ask you how you have been, big guy, but this entire moment seems to be stolen by this Osmont fucker.\"","Her voice carried notes of genuine annoyance mixed with fascination.","\"Is it true that you had him in your grasps in The Infinite Unfurling, and you simply let him go because you were playing your games of choices?\"","She said such words calmly.","As if questioning the decisions of one of THE Four was something she did casually.","As if criticizing THE Primordial Chaos to his face was merely nothing!","A moment later...","HUUM!","THE Primordial Chaos did not even turn his gaze toward her.","But his terrifying immensity slightly exerted itself!","Everything nearby began to tremble and shake with utter chaos! The obsidian walls of the hut rippled with instability! The air itself seemed to forget which direction it was supposed to flow! Reality groaned under the weight of disorder being applied to its foundations!","He waved his hands casually.","The Phonemes of The First Tongue began to circle around him. All 18 of the originals appeared first, spinning in orbits that defied conventional physics. And then he began to perceive the letters that had not been there before.","Infinity.","Quintessence.","Tyranny.","Fortune.","Advantage.","Narrative.","Harvest.","Hunger.","Potential.","Nine new additions, now made free and accessible to everyone.","He studied them with eyes that had witnessed the birth of chaos itself.","\" Pay him the respect he deserves when you talk about him.\"","His voice emerged like the collision of folds. Deep. Resonant. Filled with authority that made lesser beings instinctively want to prostrate themselves.","\" There are countless upon countless creatures across Observable Existence. And he became one of THE Four.\"","The new Phonemes continued to orbit around his form, being analyzed and cataloged.","\" It is not by pure luck. It is not by happenstance.\"","His eyes finally turned toward Emotive.","\" Treat him with the same respect as you would treat THE Creature or THE Living Paradox or me.\"","...!","His words were dangerous!","Filled with threat that made THE Living Elemental take an unconscious step backward!","And yet...","Shockingly, the figure of Emotive simply twisted her head and smiled eerily!","\" But I don’t give a fuck about THE Creature or THE Living Paradox or you?\"","Her voice came light and musical, as if she was discussing her favorite foods rather than dismissing the most powerful beings in Existence.","\" Just four old dudes claiming everything.\"","She shrugged with exaggerated nonchalance.","\" My emotion of fear toward all of you has long since disappeared. I have been around all you three, and none of you have proceeded to kill me just yet.\"","Her smile widened into something that was almost unhinged.","\" Now Osmont... Osmont I am dying to meet.\"","...!","Her words were utterly heavy!","This woman spoke to THE Primordial Chaos as if he were merely an acquaintance she found mildly annoying. She dismissed THE Four as if they were irrelevant obstacles.","THE Primordial Chaos regarded her with eyes that swirled with infinite disorder.","\" There is still time for you to be collapsed if you keep playing around, Broken Doll.\"","As he said this, he brought his hand toward the cheek of THE Living Emotive.","His fingers, wreathed in chaotic energy that would destroy most beings on contact, grasped her chin. He moved her face left and right as if examining goods at a market. Turning her this way and that. Analyzing her features. Studying her existence.","And she smiled brilliantly at this treatment!","As if being manhandled by one of THE Four was exactly what she wanted!","As if being called a Broken Doll was a compliment she cherished!"]},{"number":4772,"title":"Chapter 4772: Chapter 4771: Existence Is Too Vast! III","paragraphs":["While this occurred, her voice echoed out with casual command.","\" Elemental, how long are you going to stay out there like a scared fucking bum?\"","Her eyes didn’t even turn toward him.","\" It’s just Chaos here. If you want to hitch a ride on us, you have to get used to this.\"","Her smile grew sharper.","\" Move the fuck in. We have lots to discuss.\"","...!","Emotive said such words commandingly!","THE Living Elemental floated into the hut with a cloudy expression. His gaze was wary as he looked at Chaos, watching for any sign of hostility.","But THE Primordial Chaos didn’t even spare him a glance.","His attention remained fixed entirely on Emotive, his hand still holding her chin as if he found her far more interesting than any elemental authority could ever be.","THE Living Elemental’s pride stung at being so thoroughly ignored.","He spoke out for the first time since entering.","\" The First Tongue that we know is effectively incomplete. New letters have now been added. I can sense-\"","\"Hush.\"","HUUM!","The booming voice of THE Primordial Chaos echoed out in the small obsidian hut!","He didn’t even gaze at Elemental.","Didn’t acknowledge his existence.","Simply commanded silence with a single word that carried the weight of absolute authority.","Elemental’s expression became even more cloudy. Humiliation and frustration warred across his features. He was an Absolute in his own right. He had claimed authority over fundamental elements of reality.","And he had just been silenced like an unruly child.","But not a single word escaped from his mouth thereafter.","He knew better than to test THE Primordial Chaos.","With her chin still held by Chaos, Emotive turned over to stare at Elemental with a mocking gaze. Her eyes sparkled with cruel amusement, as if she were laughing at his predicament.","As if his humiliation was the entertainment she had been hoping for.","At this time, Chaos let go of her.","He had ascertained something from his examination. Whatever he had been looking for in her features, in her existence, in the depths of her emotional authority... he had found it.","Or confirmed it.","\" Alright.\"","His voice came measured now, the threat from moments ago replaced by calculating interest.","\" What do you want?\"","What did Emotive want?","Why would Chaos even entertain her?","These were questions that THE Living Elemental desperately wanted answered. He had followed Emotive here because she had promised something. She had claimed to have plans that would benefit them both.","But watching her interact with THE Primordial Chaos as an equal...","He began to wonder what he had gotten himself into.","Emotive smiled brilliantly at this moment.","Her beauty went on full display, features shifting into configurations that seemed designed to captivate and disarm. Every emotion that could make someone attractive manifested across her face simultaneously.","\" Oh, I want many things.\"","Her voice became almost dreamy.","\"I want Osmont.\"","The name hung in the air with weight.","\"I want THE Creature.\"","Even heavier.","\"I want things that even THE Four cannot give.\"","Her smile became something sharp and hungry.","\" But hey, a gal’s gotta start somewhere.\"","She shrugged with theatrical helplessness.","\" There’s Osmont, and then there are...\"","Her eyes met those of THE Primordial Chaos directly.","\"The matters of my own complete Axiom.\"","...!","The Broken Doll seemed to have grand ambitions!","\" And for that...we have to go to THE Creature’s Alfheimr.\"","WAA!","—","Change was initiated as many people reacted differently to what occurred.","When Noah managed to enact this Partial Embodiment, he felt the changes most closely. There were many things that he could now do and look forward to when it came to The First Tongue.","He was able to lay down high percentages of taxes right now for the Phonemes that he had developed himself. He would be able to increase these percentages as his Depth rose.","Everyone had to pay him one hundred percent taxes.","And those related to Paradox had to pay 1,000%.","These numbers were not simply arbitrary, but what he felt like he could manage to declare at this point in time. His current authority, his current Weight, his current standing among THE Four... all of it factored into what he could impose and enforce.","The grander he became, the more he could do.","He could increase the percentage for anything related to Paradox.","He could even begin taxing those related to Chaos.","And if he felt like it... those related to Existence. Those related to THE Creature!","There were many things that he could do, and he had to do them absolutely!","Because at this moment, the influx of harvest he was already receiving within the first few seconds was already astonishing!","|HARVEST ANALYSIS: PHONEME TAXATION SYSTEM|","|Usage and interpretation of your Phonemes of The First Tongue is already collecting enough harvest to be the equivalent of devouring the Depth of a THE Surface Depth entity every second.|","| Every. Single. Second.|","|This rate of collection exceeds all previous harvest mechanisms by orders of magnitude.|","|Anomaly Detection:|","|This current rate is determined to be an outlier.|","|Contributing Factors:|","|1. Countless lifeforms across Observable Existence who have access to The First Tongue and can utilize it are doing so for the first time.|","|2. The novelty of new Phonemes is driving experimentation across all factions and civilizations.|","|3. Scholars, warriors, and leaders alike are testing the capabilities of Infinity, Quintessence, Tyranny, and the others.|","|Critical Assessment:|","|Such harvest can only be reaching these levels as a result of the usage of your letters by multiple Absolutes.|","|Confirmed or Suspected Users:|","|- THE Living Paradox (1,000% Tariff Applied)|","|- THE Creature (100% Tariff Applied)|","|- THE Primordial Chaos (100% Tariff Applied)|","|- THE Secretive Eon (100% Tariff Applied)|","|- Multiple Others and Half-Step Absolutes|","|- Countless Fundamental, Intermediate, and Surface Depth entities|","|Projection:|","|Such harvest is grand but may only be this inflated for this short period of time.|","|As the novelty fades, usage will normalize.|","|However, even normalized harvest will exceed previous intake by estimated 340-500%.|","...!"]},{"number":4773,"title":"Chapter 4773: Chapter 4772: Existence Is Too Vast! IV","paragraphs":["The prompts were unique ones.","Noah read them calmly while feeling the continued immensity of his existence grow with each passing moment.","The immensity of his Physique of THE Indestructible Lexicon of Absolute Weight that was made up of THE 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue... he felt it all get so much heavier!","Even though his actual power was supposed to be spilling into THE Fundamental Depth!","Even though he should have been advancing toward higher classifications!","But at this moment, as if he could envision muscles for THE Surface Depth and THE Intermediate Depth...","Especially because of his body here in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment...","He felt like the muscles of these prior Depths were still thin.","As if they had not been worked out enough.","As if they were not as big as they could potentially be.","So the terrifying harvest that was stemming from the usage of his Phonemes across Observable Existence for the first time...","|FOUNDATION REINFORCEMENT IN PROGRESS|","|Incoming harvest is flooding into your Foundational Physique to reinforce your determined immensity at THE Surface Depth and THE Intermediate Depth simultaneously.|","|This is an unprecedented event.|","|Most entities advance through Depths and never look back.|","|Their foundations at lower Depths remain static, unchanged from the moment they progressed.|","|You are different.|","|Your foundations continue to grow even as you advance.|","|Current Assessment:|","|A rough approximation has been made based on comparative analysis with known Absolute-class entities.|","|THE Surface Depth:|","|Your Weight at this classification currently exceeds 175/100th of what current powerful Absolutes like THE Creature held at the same stage.|","|You are nearly twice as heavy at Surface Depth as THE Creature was when he occupied that classification.|","|THE Intermediate Depth:|","|Your Weight at this classification holds 200/100th of what current Absolutes held at the same stage.|","|You are exactly twice as fat at Intermediate Depth as THE Creature was.|","|THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons Assessment:|","|Likely, much grander immensity is possible.|","|Its pages are still blank and ready to be filled with endless compressed foundations.|","|The ceiling has not been found.|","|The limit has not been reached.|","|Continue building.|","...!","Yes!","He felt gloriously fat and heavy all around!","Every single one of the twenty-seven Seals that represented his compressed power... it felt like each one was becoming so dense, so weighty, so impossibly heavy that if he took just one and threw it at an enemy...","He would smash a Fundamental Depth entity with it and reject a Declaration!","This was the power that he was building!","This was the foundation that would eventually support his ascent to heights that even THE Four had not reached!","At this time, his eyes opened wide to the immense silence in the Logoseion.","The Glossarians were looking at him with awe after his proclamation.","Hoplites stared with expressions that had transcended mere shock into something approaching fervor. Lochagoi analyzed the nine floating Phonemes with desperate intensity, trying to memorize every stroke, every curve, every nuance of meaning. Even the Polemarchs who had emerged from the shadows watched with eyes that burned with questions they barely dared to ask.","After this brief period of silence...","Moments later, multiple Polemarchs began to come out one after another!","Primordial Perfected Ginnu Lifeforms who held the heavy power of Fundamental Depth entities! Beings whose Weight within this domain made them feel like they were nearing the level of Half-Step Absolute Depth! Ancient scholars who had dedicated their existences to understanding The First Tongue!","They encircled the figure of Noah!","Not threateningly. Not with hostility. But with the careful reverence of those who had just witnessed something that exceeded their understanding of what was possible.","One was an entity that had a humanoid body seemingly made out of countless blue-gold pages.","Her form rustled with every movement, inscriptions shifting across her surface as if she was a living library given consciousness. Her eyes shone brilliantly at this moment, filled with questions that multiplied faster than she could process them.","\" Is it possible if we take sir out of here momentarily to another place?\"","Her voice came respectful but urgent.","Whatever she wanted to discuss, whatever questions she needed answered... they were too important for the public setting of the Logoseion.","Noah looked at this and nodded.","Then he turned around and pointed toward Lumivara, Ul’moreth, and Skoll.","The little fox watched with shining eyes, her injuries from Gilgamesh and THE Weavers’ assault seemingly forgotten in the excitement of what her Master had just accomplished.","Ul’moreth stood with ancient dignity, his countless hairs rippling with pride.","And Skoll sat like a very good dog while looking up toward Noah, his tail wagging slowly, his neon flames flickering with patient loyalty. He didn’t understand what had happened. He didn’t need to understand. He was simply happy to be here with his Master!","\" Them as well.\"","...!","Noah’s words were simple but absolute.","The Polemarch in front of him nodded without hesitation.","She waved her hands, and a light of white-gold Mana flashed from her form! It wrapped around Noah, Lumivara, Ul’moreth, and Skoll with gentle authority as...","They disappeared from the Logoseion!","The Polemarch turned to the Glossarians who remained, her page-like body rustling with the weight of command.","\" Continue comprehending and utilizing the newly introduced Phonemes of The First Tongue.\"","Her voice carried across every corner of the chamber.","\" Keep your loyalty to The First Tongue tight.\"","Her eyes swept across Hoplites and Lochagoi alike.","\" And your mouths even tighter.\"","...!","The warning was clear.","What had happened here was not to be discussed casually. The arrival of THE Genesis Monarch, the revelation of nine new Phonemes, the implications for everything the Glossarians believed... all of it was sensitive information that required careful handling.","After she said this, she, Ophelia, and other Polemarchs disappeared as well!","Only a few remained behind to maintain order in the Logoseion.","And not even seconds later...","HUUM!","From different directions, lights of Chaos, Paradox, and pure Existence shone!","The boundaries between philosophical schools meant nothing when something this significant occurred!","Polemarchs of the Paradoxians appeared first!","Their togas of obsidian-gold and white rippled with contradictory energy! Their faces held expressions that were simultaneously shocked and unsurprised, as if they had expected something unexpected!","Polemarchs of the Existentialists arrived next!","Their simple white togas blazed with multicolored radiance that spoke of pure being! Their eyes burned with the need to understand what had just altered the fundamental fabric of linguistic reality!","Polemarchs of the Chaosites materialized last!","Their forms swirled with entropy and disorder! Their expressions held the manic excitement of those who thrived when established orders were disrupted!","They looked toward the nearby Glossarian Polemarchs they knew very well!","A Chaosite Polemarch who looked like a massive obsidian titan stepped forward. His body was carved from solidified disorder, constantly shifting and reforming in ways that hurt to observe directly.","\" What happened?\"","His voice rumbled like collapsing mountains.","The Glossarian Polemarch who remained looked up with a shining gaze.","He looked around at the other Glossarians still present in the Logoseion. At the Hoplites and Lochagoi who were already attempting to inscribe Infinity and Quintessence and Tyranny into the air before them. At the nine brilliant Phonemes that still floated above the plasma sea, slowly beginning to fade now that their creator had departed.","\" We have uncovered new Phonemes of The First Tongue.\"","His voice came measured and careful.","\" As you all sensed.\"","He spread his hands in a gesture of shared confusion.","\" We are just as shocked as you all are!\"","They said such words with clear eyes!","The lie was masterfully delivered. Not a complete falsehood, but a careful omission. They HAD uncovered new Phonemes. They WERE shocked. They simply failed to mention the entity who had revealed them.","The surroundings buzzed with activity!","Polemarchs of all four philosophical schools began attempting to write the new Phonemes for themselves! Infinity took shape beneath trembling fingers! Quintessence blazed into existence with expressions of wonder! Tyranny pressed down upon those who inscribed it, making them feel its weight!","The other Primordial Perfected Ginnu Lifeforms were breathless!","They knew there was something larger here.","Nine new Phonemes didn’t simply appear from nowhere. Someone had revealed them. Someone had fundamentally altered The First Tongue in ways that shouldn’t have been possible.","But they did not wish to make their suspicions too obvious!","Not yet.","Not until they understood more.","But at this time, Noah could be considered to have fully arrived in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment!","He had made a contribution nobody else could.","His Merit Points continued to increase even now as he was escorted away by Polemarchs!","The numbers on his toga climbed higher and higher, approaching and then exceeding the threshold of Lochagos, pushing toward territories that even ancient scholars took centuries to reach!","One had to wonder...","Just what would be obtained from this region of the Vault of Ginnungagap by contributing what he contributed?","What rewards awaited someone who had given the Glossarians nine new letters of their most sacred language?","What treasures from before THE Fallout would be unveiled for THE Genesis Monarch?","The answers awaited in whatever destination the Polemarchs were taking him!"]},{"number":4774,"title":"Chapter 4774: Chapter 4773: THE Villa Dei Boscoreale I","paragraphs":["Existence moved in cycles.","Birth and death. Rise and fall. Beginning and ending, only to begin again.","Noah had come to understand this truth deeply across his journey. Every event led to another. Every action created reactions that rippled outward to touch things that seemed entirely unrelated. Every choice opened doors while closing others, and those closed doors would eventually open again in different forms.","One had to be an active participant in Existence in order to enjoy the boons of Existence.","Those who sat idle, waiting for opportunities to come to them, would wait forever. Existence rewarded movement. It rewarded engagement. It rewarded those who stepped forward and seized what they wanted rather than hoping it would be given.","Before THE Fallout and even now, Noah continued to actively move with Existence as events unfolded.","And those events had now brought him to THE Vault of Ginnungagap, albeit in a different form than he had originally expected.","He had expected to see THE Vaults of Ginnungagap in The Infinite Unfurling. That had been the plan. Before THE Primordial Chaos offered him a choice.","His traversal was ended short before he could go.","And now, eons later, here he was!","Not through Temporal Traversal. Not through the methods he had originally intended.","The cycles of Existence were strange like that!","When he thought about Temporal Traversal and its possibility right now...","|The capability of Temporal Traversal still persists within your arsenal.|","|It carries heavy influence in THE Existential Paradox Loop.|","|Current Status:|","|Utilizing Temporal Traversal for movement to the Earliest Folds or Infinite Unfurling before the emergence of THE Fallout is nearly impossible.|","|THE Fallout has created temporal barriers that resist penetration.|","|The corruption extends across time as well as space.|","|Attempting traversal to pre-Fallout eras risks catastrophic paradox formation.|","|Analysis:|","|Feasibility studies are still being conducted.|","|Potential methods of circumvention are being explored.|","|Current recommendation: Focus on present opportunities rather than past destinations.|","|What you sought in the past has manifested in the present.|","|Perhaps...this was always the intended path.|","...!","Noah regarded the prompts calmly.","Then he looked out at the surroundings the Polemarch had brought them to.","They seemed to have arrived inside a bronze hall stretching out into the distance.","The architecture was ancient beyond measure. Inscriptions covered every surface, Phonemes of The First Tongue arranged in patterns that spoke of knowledge accumulated across eternities of study.","The hall led to a massive villa visible in the distance.","Grand columns supported a structure that seemed to have been designed for beings far larger than those currently walking these corridors. Terraces and balconies extended outward at various levels. Windows of crystallized language filtered light that came from no discernible source.","Around the hall, seas of blue-gold Phonemes flowed all around!","Rivers of authority that carried meanings Noah could read if he focused. They swirled past in endless streams, each one representing concepts and ideas that had been refined across eons of Glossarian scholarship.","Noah could already feel his Seal of Harvest buzzing.","There was so much to collect here. So much knowledge. So much authority. So much potential harvest waiting to be gathered by one who knew how to take it.","Skoll rubbed against his leg with enthusiasm.","The transformed Duke’s neon flames flickered happily as he pressed his massive form against Noah’s side. He didn’t understand where they were or why they had been brought here. He simply wanted to be close to his Master.","Before them, the Polemarchs turned to face the group.","The Polemarch whose entire body was made up of countless blue-gold pages stepped forward. Her form rustled with every movement, inscriptions shifting across her surface. She gave a slight bow that spoke of respect rather than subservience.","\" Polemarch Lunaris greets The One Who Laid The Claim.\"","Her voice emerged like pages turning in an ancient library.","\"I brought you here first because out of THE Four, you are the last one to have crossed this Nexus of the Primordial Realms.\"","Her page-like eyes met his directly.","\" THE Creature, THE Primordial Chaos, and THE Living Paradox have all crossed here various times in the Infinite Unfurling. They walked these halls when the Vaults were not yet corrupted. They contributed to what we have built. They took what they needed and left marks upon our society that persist to this day.\"","She paused.","\" And while THE Agora of Primordial Judgment has set rules to be followed, THE Change corrupted many things. There could be a great deal of differences between what they experienced and what you will experience. Much has altered since those ancient times.\"","Her form straightened.","\" So until everything is ascertained, it is the job of any Glossarian to ensure the safety of THE Glossarian.\"","BOOM!","THE Glossarian!","Noah gained another distinction so easily!","The words of Lunaris were heavy ones! She was not merely calling him a member of their philosophical school. She was designating him as THE Glossarian. The supreme representative of their Way.","All of THE Four had passed here before him.","Was this the place where they also forged their foundations? Was this ancient Nexus Point one of the crucibles that had shaped the most powerful beings in Observable Existence?","As he thought of this, he nodded.","Then he turned his gaze toward the distant villa.","\"I have a few things that I wish to accomplish here.\"","His voice came measured and direct.","\"I have an Absolute that came in with me. One Absolute with three separate bodies who has gone ahead to the Paradoxians.\"","His eyes blazed with calculation.","\" What do I need to watch out for if I wish to speedily collapse them before they earn enough Merit to reclaim all their power? I should have enough Merit to exceed the distinction of a Lochagos, but there seems to be certain conditions I have yet to meet.\"","...!","He asked an equally heavy question!","Ophelia, Lunaris, and the other Polemarchs in this region frowned with concern at his words. Collapsing an Absolute, even one suppressed, was no simple task. The implications of such an endeavor were vast.","At this time, Ul’moreth spoke up with his deep and heavy voice.","Vibrant obsidian-gold light flowed around the ancient Ginnu Lifeform as he stepped forward. His countless hairs rippled with the weight of what he was about to share.","\" My senses are unique ones, Scale Breaker.\"","His veiled eyes turned toward the distant reaches of the domain.","\"I cannot say definitely, but apart from THE Weavers... there should be 4 other Absolutes here.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\"I can feel their heat as if they were blinding suns. It was how I was able to locate Little Lumivara who was being stalked by Gilgamesh and THE Weavers.\"","...!"]},{"number":4775,"title":"Chapter 4775: Chapter 4774: THE Villa Dei Boscoreale II","paragraphs":["Ul’moreth said such words as Noah turned to him with sharp eyes!","4 Absolutes in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment!","Apart from THE Weavers who had just entered!","That meant this domain already contained beings of the highest classification. Beings who had been here long enough to establish themselves.","As Noah thought of this, Lunaris nodded.","\" Yes, THE Glossarian. This is where one of the difficulties for you will lie, and also why we brought you here.\"","She began walking toward the distant villa, gesturing for them to follow.","\" In our Agora of Primordial Judgment, there are 4 Absolutes sitting atop each faction.\"","Her pages rustled as she moved, each step measured and deliberate.","\" Khaotikos the Unbound leads the Way of Chaos. He has existed within this domain since The Infinite Unfurling. His mastery of disorder is legendary even among other Absolutes. He is unpredictable in all things, which makes him both dangerous and occasionally beneficial.\"","...!","They passed through sections of the bronze hall where the Phonemes flowing around them changed in character.","\" Ontikos the Unwavering leads the Way of Existence. His dedication to the fundamental principle of being is absolute. He rarely takes action, preferring to simply exist and observe. But when he does act, his authority is overwhelming. He represents the most stable of the four leaders.\"","The villa grew larger as they approached.","\" Paradoxos the Dual leads the Way of Paradox. He... or they... are perhaps the most difficult to understand. Two minds in one form, constantly disagreeing yet always speaking in unison. His relationship with THE Living Paradox is complex. They share a philosophical foundation but not necessarily goals.\"","Her voice grew more cautious.","\" And Glossikos the Articulate leads the Way of The First Tongue. She had been...seeking to also lay The Claim since The Infinite Unfurling. Of all four leaders, she is most likely to support you. But do not mistake likely support for guaranteed alliance.\"","She stopped before the entrance to the villa.","\" All four of these Absolutes carry the status of Strategoi. Supreme Commanders of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.\"","Her page-like eyes met Noah’s with gravity.","\" The rank of Strategos is the highest achievable within this domain. It exceeds Polemarch in all ways. The Depth Limitation for a Strategos is THE Absolute Depth if the entrant was originally an Absolute, or THE Fundamental Depth as the maximum for non-Absolutes.\"","She continued explaining.","\" Strategoi are the supreme authorities of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment. They govern all aspects of society. They judge the most important debates. They hold the power to grant or deny departure to any being within the domain.\"","Her pages shifted to display relevant inscriptions.","\" To become a Strategos, one must achieve this rank through one of two methods. The first is the Trial of Primordial Judgment. This is a series of debates against all four leaders of the Ways simultaneously. The candidate must demonstrate understanding of Chaos, Existence, Paradox, AND The First Tongue. All four philosophies. All four approaches to reality.\"","She paused.","\" The second method is Unanimous Acclaim. All current Strategoi must unanimously agree that the candidate has contributed something of unprecedented value to the domain. No dissent. No abstention. Complete agreement from all four.\"","Her expression grew more serious.","\" As a Strategos, one gains full restoration of their original Depth. Absolutes who achieved this rank would regain their Absolute power within the domain. They would have complete authority. They could grant departure to any being. They could alter the laws of the domain with the consensus of other Strategoi. And they would gain access to The Primordial Archive.\"","Her voice dropped.","\" The Primordial Archive contains knowledge from before THE Change. It is perhaps the greatest repository of ancient wisdom in all of Observable Existence.\"","She raised a cautionary hand.","\" But Strategoi carry restrictions as well. They cannot leave the domain themselves. They are bound to it. They must defend the domain against existential threats. It is a position of ultimate authority but also ultimate responsibility.\"","...!","Lunaris looked toward Noah with grave eyes.","\"I am...confident Glossikos the Articulate will stand with you, THE Glossarian. Your contribution of nine new Phonemes is unprecedented..\"","Her pages shifted uneasily.","\" But I am not so sure of the other Strategoi. Khaotikos may support you simply because it would be chaotic to do so. Ontikos may oppose you because change disrupts the stability of existence. And Paradoxos... Paradoxos is impossible to predict.\"","She gestured toward the villa before them.","\" That is why I have brought you here first. To THE Villa Dei Boscoreale.\"","The massive structure loomed above them, ancient and magnificent.","\" This villa requires 9 Polemarchs to open for one they deem to have contributed tremendously to the Glossarians. It is the highest tier vault within THE Agora of Primordial Judgment apart from the one that Strategoi have access to.\"","Her pages rustled with significance.","\" Here, THE Glossarian can use the tools within to elevate your ranking and move toward the standing of a Polemarch. Before that, the goal of collapsing a Paradoxical Absolute, especially under the watch of Paradoxos the Dual...\"","Lunaris smiled at this moment.","A teasing look appeared on her pages, unexpected from someone who had been so grave moments before.","\" Respectfully, as grand as THE Glossarian is right now, your Depth is very different from those like you.\"","Her smile widened.","\" If sir debated with me on The First Tongue, you would win. Your understanding exceeds mine. Your authority exceeds mine. Your contribution to our Way exceeds anything I could offer in a lifetime.\"","She tilted her head.","\" But if you debated me on raw Depth... sir would lose.\"","The words were not meant as insult but as honest assessment.","\" And I am not confident of being able to collapse an Absolute, even if they haven’t recovered their standing in here.\"","She met his eyes directly.","\" Sir has... lots of work to do.\"","She gestured toward the villa’s entrance.","\" But what is inside there should help. THE Villa Dei Boscoreale contains treasures of utter wonder, and they scale depending on your contribution.\"","Her pages settled into something like anticipation.","\" Will you enter, THE Glossarian?\"","...!","Noah looked at the ancient villa with eyes that blazed with possibility."]},{"number":4776,"title":"Chapter 4776: Chapter 4775: THE Villa Dei Boscoreale III","paragraphs":["Noah stood before the golden doors of THE Villa Dei Boscoreale.","Around him, Lunaris, Ophelia, and seven other Polemarchs touched the Merit points on their togas simultaneously. Their authority flowed into the ancient seals protecting this vault, recognizing them as worthy guardians granting access to one they deemed worthy.","The golden doors flung outward and opened!","Ancient light spilled from within, carrying warmth that spoke of treasures accumulated across eons.","The door and the villa itself almost seemed to be purely decorative. The external structure outside was just that, a structure. Inside was a place spanning countless distances. A pocket of reality that existed independent of normal spatial limitations.","Noah went down and played with Skoll’s head.","\" I’ll be right back.\"","The transformed Duke’s tail wagged with enthusiasm despite not understanding what was happening. His neon flames flickered happily at the attention. He was content to wait as long as his Master would return!","Noah then nodded to Lumivara and Ul’moreth.","\" Hang on tight for me.\"","The little fox’s eyes shone with confidence in her Master. Ul’moreth’s veiled gaze held ancient wisdom and sterness at this moment.","His gaze then went to Lunaris and Ophelia.","\" Help them become Lochagoi in the meantime if possible. I don’t know how long this will take.\"","The Glossarians nodded with enthusiasm at this task.","Lunaris’s pages rustled with genuine warmth.","\" Good luck, sir.\"","With such words, Noah took a step toward the golden gate.","And disappeared!","This time, the movement he felt was a smooth one. As if he was simply stepping through a door and entering another room. No violent transportation. No disorienting transition. Just a single step that carried him somewhere else entirely.","Yet vibrant Philologies unfurled all around him!","Dense constructs of linguistic authority swirled past his perception, welcoming him to this ancient place! They carried meanings that spoke of refinement and purification, of foundations being strengthened and impurities being burned away.","He entered a region filled with mist of ancientness and wonder.","|You have arrived in THE Thermae of Cyclic Refinement.|","|The Baths of Foundation.|","...!","Baths?","Noah almost shook his head with incredulity.","The vibrant treasures from THE Vaults of Ginnungagap began with a bath?","Even as he had this thought, he smiled.","He felt all his 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue vibrating with expectation! They resonated with this place as if recognizing something fundamental about its nature! As if they had arrived somewhere that would feed them in ways nothing else could.","And glorious it was!","It was quiet.","Not a single other soul was in sight.","Only a faint golden gateway stood behind him, marking the path he had taken to arrive here.","Noah looked around at what lay before him.","The region resembled ancient bathing complexes of impossible grandeur.","Pools of various sizes filled chambers that stretched beyond normal perception! Some were intimate, designed for solitary reflection. Others were vast enough to qualify as small seas. Steam rose from waters that glowed with blue-gold luminescence, carrying warmth that penetrated not just the body but the very foundations of one’s existence.","Mosaics covering the floors and walls depicted the journey of refinement. Beings entering as rough stones, jagged and unpolished. The same beings emerging as gems of perfect clarity, their edges smooth, their surfaces brilliant.","When he looked up, he saw a ceiling open to an artificial sky.","And that sky displayed the 27 Phonemes of The First Tongue in slow rotation!","The original 18 blazed with authority accumulated across eons.","And his 9... they were already there!","Infinity! Quintessence! Tyranny! Fortune! Advantage! Narrative! Harvest! Hunger! Potential!","They had found their place in the artificial sky, rotating alongside the originals as if they had always belonged there.","Their light filtered down to bless those who bathed below, and Noah could feel the resonance between this place and his own existence.","This seemed to be part of the reason why he was receiving such a grand harvest every second to his foundation!","Apart from his Phonemes being used by Absolutes across Observable Existence, they were also being used HERE! In this ancient vault!","As he stared at the radiant pools in the distance that seemed to call out to his existence, The First Tongue within him received waves of information.","|THE THERMAE OF CYCLIC REFINEMENT|","|The Baths of Foundation|","|This region allows one’s current Depth to undergo Passive Refinement when specific treasures are consumed.|","|The more one consumes, the more rounds of refinement they cross until they attain the highest cycle of Depth Refinement possible within this vault.|","| The treasures will descend based on determined contribution to the Glossarians and THE Agora of Primordial Judgment overall.|","|The Nine Cycles of Katharsis (Purification):|","|1. Prima Katharsis (First Purification): Initial cleansing of foundational impurities. Weight increases by 10%.|","|2. Deutera Katharsis (Second Purification): Compression of scattered authority into denser forms. Weight increases by 20%.|","|3. Trita Katharsis (Third Purification): Harmonization of conflicting aspects within one’s Depth. Weight increases by 30%.|","|4. Tetarta Katharsis (Fourth Purification): Strengthening of the boundaries between Depth levels. Weight increases by 40%.|","|5. Pempte Katharsis (Fifth Purification): Integration of external knowledge into core foundations. Weight increases by 50%.|","|6. Ekti Katharsis (Sixth Purification): Refinement of the connection between Way and Depth. Weight increases by 60%.|","|7. Evdomi Katharsis (Seventh Purification): Approaching the theoretical limits of current classification. Weight increases by 75%.|","|8. Ogdoi Katharsis (Eighth Purification): Transcending normal parameters for current Depth. Weight increases by 90%.|","|9. Enati Katharsis (Ninth Purification / THE Wheel of Foundation): The absolute pinnacle of refinement possible without advancing to a higher Depth. Weight increases by 100%, effectively doubling one’s foundation at current classification.|","|Historical Note:|","|Most Polemarchs who enter THE Villa Dei Boscoreale achieve only 1-3 cycles of Katharsis.|","|Reaching the 5th cycle is considered exceptional.|","|The 7th cycle is legendary.|","|The 9th cycle has been achieved by only... a select few.|","...!","The Nine Cycles of Katharsis flowed before his mind!","Noah jubilantly took more steps within, already liking this place very much.","Unlike others, with his Formless Depth, he could elevate the foundation of his Surface and Intermediate Depth even now. There was still a ways to go before those foundations reached their theoretical maximum.","Exceeding the foundation that THE Creature or THE Living Paradox built was nice and all.","But why not exceed it tremendously?","Why not outstrip it completely?!"]},{"number":4777,"title":"Chapter 4777: Chapter 4776: THE Villa Dei Boscoreale IV","paragraphs":["So he stepped deeper toward the vibrant pools.","Above him, the artificial sky seemed to shimmer with anticipation. The contribution he had made would allow the descent of loot for him to consume in these pools to refine his foundation even further.","As he neared the pools, his existence was literally fed more information through The First Tongue!","|TREASURES OF THE THERMAE|","|The treasures in this region take the form of consumable items that must be ingested while bathing in the pools.|","|Each treasure contributes to progression through the cycles of Katharsis.|","|Examples of Known Treasures:|","|Ambrosia Pellets: Small golden spheres that taste of honey and starlight. Contributes 1% toward next Katharsis cycle. Classification: Common.|","|Nectar of the Muses: Liquid silver that flows upward when poured. Contributes 5% toward next Katharsis cycle. Enhances comprehension during refinement. Classification: Uncommon.|","|Ichor Crystals: Crystallized essence that pulses with inner light. Contributes 10% toward next Katharsis cycle. Temporarily elevates perception during consumption. Classification: Rare.|","|The Apples of the Hesperides: Golden fruits that never rot, warm to the touch. Contributes 25% toward next Katharsis cycle. One of the most sought-after treasures. Classification: Very Rare.|","|Prometheus’s Ember: A fragment of an infinite flame contained in a small bronze vessel. Contributes 50% toward next Katharsis cycle. Burns away impurities with divine fire. Classification: Extremely Rare.|","| The Cornucopia Draught: Liquid that contains the essence of endless abundance. Instantly completes current Katharsis cycle regardless of progress. Classification: Legendary.|","| Kronos’s Crystallized Moment: A frozen instant of time given physical form. Completes current cycle AND provides 50% progress toward the next. Only 3 have ever been found. Classification: Mythical.|","...!","The treasures ranged from common to mythical!","One may ask... just what would the one who contributed 9 new letters of The First Tongue obtain in a treasure vault of Glossarians that protected and studied The First Tongue itself?","Noah had a brilliant smile as he thought of this.","He arrived before an incandescent obsidian-blue pool.","The moment his eyes landed on it, its details unveiled before him!","|You have arrived before The Pool of Lethe (Forgetting).|","|Function: Helps one forget inefficient patterns in their foundation, allowing for reconstruction.|","|Stepping into any pool will also allow for the generation and acceptance of treasures based on the quality and immensity of your contributions.|","|This pool is particularly effective for those seeking to rebuild foundations that have accumulated flaws over time.|","...!","A glorious pool lay before him!","Noah’s steps didn’t stop.","He went down the glistening blue-gold stairs that led into the vast pool. It looked more like a mini sea than a bathing area, stretching outward until steam and distance obscured its far edges.","And it felt...","\" Well damn...\"","It felt fucking hot!","The steam emanating from the Pool of Lethe did not do justice to the level of heat the waters held! Just halfway in, Noah felt the scorching temperatures penetrate into his skin and toward his existence.","The heat sought any and all inefficiencies to eradicate!","It burned through patterns that had calcified without his notice.","It seared away assumptions that had become limitations.","And while it did so...","Noah fully submerged his body!","The obsidian-gold waters surged around his upper chest, lapping against his muscular form with heat that would have vaporized normal THE Surface Depth entities!","He reclined back gloriously, finding a position that allowed him to relax while the waters worked their magic.","He raised his head to see the shimmering artificial sky.","The 27 Phonemes continued their slow rotation, and the sky itself began shining gold! No doubt allowing many vibrant treasures to manifest soon.","But...","At such a time.","The obsidian waters a few meters away from him churned.","His eyes became sharp.","He looked over with the alertness of one who had survived countless ambushes.","And shockingly... a vibrant head of hair began to rise from beneath the surface!","An...entity.","The only way Noah could describe the emerging head and figure was that of a Dryad.","Her hair was composed of flowing vines and leaves that seemed perpetually in bloom, colors shifting between emerald and gold with each movement.","Her features were delicate but ancient. Her skin had a faint bark-like texture that spoke of connection to primordial nature itself!","Her upper body emerged from the waters with casual grace, revealing form that was simultaneously organic and grand. Shoulders that seemed to grow from living wood. Arms that flowed like branches reaching toward sunlight. A presence that spoke of forests that had existed before differentiation gave them names.","And her eyes!","They had a brilliant obsidian-blue swirl of immensity and glory.","Depths that contained ages of accumulated wisdom! Light that spoke of authority earned through eons of dedication! Patterns that seemed to write and rewrite themselves with each passing moment.","While looking at her, Noah could have sworn he felt the aura of a Muspeli Lifeform.","That particular resonance of fire and transformation that marked those born in Muspelheim.","But this being whom he did not sense or observe before they showed themselves... she gazed at him calmly.","Her eyes were filled with analysis that missed nothing. Every detail of his existence was being cataloged. Or she was trying to anyways.","Then she waved her hand.","A wall of pure Mana formed behind her!","She leaned back on it casually, just like Noah, her arms outstretched behind her in a pose of complete relaxation.","Steam swirled around her form, obscuring and revealing in equal measure!","And Noah... could not sense any aura from her at all.","Nothing.","As if she simply didn’t exist from a perceptual standpoint.","And yet Noah felt the same perception from her that he had now felt from a few others.","That stifling sensation of oppression.","That heaviness that felt undeniable!","That brilliance as if one was standing too close to the sun.","It was without a doubt the brilliance of an Absolute!","An Absolute that at this moment looked at Noah with eyes that held ancient amusement.","\" You come into someone’s spring unannounced, and you don’t even introduce yourself?\"","Her words were oppressive.","Her voice carried authority that made the waters around them ripple in response! The artificial sky above seemed to dim slightly in deference to her presence! Even the heat of the Pool of Lethe seemed to intensify, as if recognizing its master.","Her gaze was even more so!","Those obsidian-blue eyes bore into Noah with weight that would have crushed most beings into submission. They demanded acknowledgment! They required respect!","Yet Noah stared back calmly.","His voice came out soon after, steady and unshaken.","\" You must be Glossikos the Articulate.\"","...!","BOOM!","Glossikos!","An entity that was one of the four Absolutes in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment!","The supreme leader of the Glossarians!"]},{"number":4778,"title":"Chapter 4778: Chapter 4777: Leaders and Kings I","paragraphs":["Glossikos.","Noah looked at this being with a calm gaze.","She seemed to be trying to utilize her immensity to see if he would crack. To see if he would show weakness. To see if the weight of an Absolute pressing against his existence would make him flinch or bow or reveal some vulnerability she could exploit.","But Noah had stood before THE Creature.","He had faced THE Primordial Chaos in the Infinite Unfurling.","He had been pursued by THE Weavers across the Wastes of THE Fallout.","One more Absolute, even one bathing in the same pool as him, was not enough to make him falter.","Moments later, Glossikos spoke.","\" How did you do it?\"","Her voice came grand and oppressive, carrying power that made the waters around them ripple in response.","\" How did you take your position among THE Four?\"","Her obsidian-blue eyes bore into him with intensity that would have crushed lesser beings into submission.","\"I learned everything about The First Tongue. I spent eons perfecting my understanding of every Phoneme, every Logos, every Philology that could be constructed from its foundations. I pushed further than any other scholar in the history of the Glossarians.\"","Her voice grew heavier.","\" And I could still never lay a claim on it. Not completely.\"","Something flickered in those ancient eyes.","\" Every time that I tried, I felt like I had to take a step. And the moment that I did, the immensity of The First Tongue itself would come crashing down on me completely. As if the language knew I was reaching for something I wasn’t meant to grasp.\"","Her smile became dangerous.","\" So how did someone so much weaker than me manage to do what I could not do?\"","She tilted her head, studying him like a predator considering prey.","\" And... if I were to take a gulp and eat you up right now... would I have whatever you had that allowed you to lay this claim?\"","BOOM!","She smiled dangerously as she finished saying these words!","The threat hung in the air between them, heavy with the promise of violence that an Absolute could deliver without effort.","Noah looked at her for a few seconds.","Then he stretched his arms out behind him even more, getting even more comfortable in the pool. He actually looked up to the artificial sky where vibrant treasures had begun to form, golden light coalescing into shapes that promised power beyond measure.","\" Now that I have integrated my own designed Phonemes across The First Tongue permeating through Existence, the level of control that I have over it is rising.\"","His voice came casual and glorious, as if discussing the weather rather than responding to a death threat from an Absolute.","\" Not too long ago, I applied a Thesis that allowed me to negate the usage of The First Tongue for a Fundamental Depth entity and a Half-Step Absolute entity. And then somewhat on an Absolute, but there wasn’t much time there...\"","He continued gazing at the sky.","\" Right now, I feel like I can apply this Thesis, if I so wish, and deny the usage of The First Tongue absolutely to even an Absolute entity.\"","His eyes finally returned to meet hers.","\" Now, I am sure that you would have other means to move against me apart from The First Tongue. Your sheer Weight and Depth would allow you options that don’t rely on linguistic authority.\"","His smile matched hers in danger.","\" But I don’t think you ever wish to experience the Rejection from the letters of Existence that you have been so closely studying and perfecting the usage of for eons now. Something that you have been trying to lay a claim on.\"","He let those words settle.","\"If I tried to think of it myself, it would feel unbearable if a day ever came when Mana itself rejected me. Do you want that?\"","...!","She had begun the conversation with a threat.","So he simply threw out a threat himself, even though he was facing an Absolute entity.","His words were heavy, carrying the weight of someone who could actually deliver on the promise they implied.","Glossikos regarded him for a long moment.","The dangerous smile on her face shifted. Changed. Became something that looked almost like... acceptance.","\" The one who took the position that I sought all my life...\"","Her voice came softer now, though no less weighted.","\"I am glad to see that it is someone with a pair of balls.\"","She laughed, and the sound was surprisingly warm despite the tension that had filled the air moments before.","\"It would have been even more unbearable for me to say The First Tongue was claimed by someone feeble of mind and stature.\"","Her obsidian-blue eyes sparkled with something that might have been approval.","\" You seem big. You feel big.\"","At these words, Noah looked back at the Dryad with eyes that held no false modesty.","\"I am big. Bigger than many across Observable Existence dismiss me to be. I won’t posture and brag at this moment as the best time to do so will be when I stand atop the cliff that shows all others below me. Until then...\"","BOOM!","A heavy silence settled between them.","As if they were staring each other down across the steaming waters of the Pool of Lethe. Two entities who had both dedicated their existences to The First Tongue, now measuring each other’s worth through gaze alone.","A moment later, Glossikos sighed.","The tension didn’t disappear, but it transformed into something more bearable. More... productive.","\" Your eyes are most similar to... THE Primordial Chaos.\"","Her words came contemplative.","\" Unpredictable. Grand.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed.","This was the first time that he had been compared to THE Primordial Chaos.","Most of the time, others drew parallels between him and THE Creature.","But THE Primordial Chaos?","That was a different comparison entirely.","Glossikos continued, not waiting for him to respond.","\" Go through the Cycles of Katharsis. We can talk meanwhile.\"","She settled back against her wall of pure Mana, getting comfortable as if preparing for an extended conversation.","\" Even though I lost, I still want to see if I am better than you in The First Tongue.\"","\"Oh?\"","Noah blinked toward this entity.","\" Are you able to make new letters of The First Tongue?\"","Glossikos blinked calmly and replied.","\" No?\"","And Noah replied once more.","\" Then you are not better than me in The First Tongue. You can’t make any new letters, while I already made 9.\"","He shrugged with casual dismissal.","\" So let’s not waste time there.\"","BOOM!","His words were calm and almost commanding!","Glossikos smiled dangerously in response!","\" Ho? You seem to have gone from bold to commanding.\"","Her voice carried edges that promised consequences.","\" Don’t forget where you are and where I am. Even if you represent what I want the most, I can still make life miserable for you.\"","Noah looked at her.","Then he shook his head with surety.","\" But you won’t.\"","His voice came absolute and unwavering.","\" And I’m sure of that as I’m sure that the first treasure I will grasp will be... the highest tiered one.\"","His eyes met hers directly.","\"I am sure of that because I am The First Tongue. And a follower of it, regardless of their power, must follow me.\"","...!","The words landed like declarations of absolute truth!","And then Noah raised his hand toward the artificial sky.","The golden light that had been coalescing above responded to his gesture!","From the shimmering expanse where the 27 Phonemes rotated in eternal dance, the first treasure began to float down based on his contribution!","It descended with the inevitability of prophecy being fulfilled!","And it was...","Kronos’s Crystallized Moment!","A frozen instant of time given physical form!","It appeared as a small sphere of impossible clarity, no larger than a fist, yet containing depths that seemed to stretch into infinity. Within its crystalline structure, light moved in ways that defied normal observation...simultaneously frozen and flowing, static and dynamic, past and future occupying the same space.","The sphere pulsed with temporal authority that made the Pool of Lethe’s waters still momentarily around it.","This was a Mythical-tier treasure.","Only 3 had ever been found in the entire history of THE Villa Dei Boscoreale.","And now a fourth descended to Noah’s waiting hand.","He grasped it.","The moment his fingers closed around Kronos’s Crystallized Moment, he felt time itself acknowledge his touch. Eons compressed into instants. Instants stretched into eternities. The boundaries between moments blurred and sharpened simultaneously.","Then he swallowed it.","Without hesitation. Without ceremony. Without the reverence that most beings would show to something so impossibly rare.","He simply put it in his mouth and let it slide down his throat.","HUUM!","The effect was immediate and overwhelming!","His muscles undulated and vibrated with energy that transcended normal physical response! Every fiber of his being began to compress and refine! The Pool of Lethe churned around him, waters that had been calm now surging with the force of the transformation occurring within!","The inefficient patterns in his foundation were erased from the timeline of his existence entirely! As if they had never been there to begin with! As if his foundation had always been pristine!","His immensity began to rise!","The Cycle of Katharsis that would have required 100% progress to complete?","Kronos’s Crystallized Moment completed it instantly!","And provided 50% progress toward the next!","Prima Katharsis would be achieved!","And Deutera Katharsis would be at 50% progress!","And he wasn’t even worried about utilizing it now or later. Because he was also sure that...more would come.","Opposite him, Glossikos was looking at him with very sharp eyes.","Those obsidian-blue orbs had widened slightly, the first genuine surprise she had shown since revealing herself here!"]},{"number":4779,"title":"Chapter 4779: Chapter 4778: Leaders and Kings II","paragraphs":["How could he describe the feeling of going through the Cycles of Katharsis?","The Pool of Lethe worked all around him, its scorching waters penetrating into every layer of his existence. It sought out the inefficiencies that had calcified over time. The assumptions that had become limitations. The patterns that served no purpose but had settled into his foundation simply because they had been there long enough to feel permanent.","And Kronos’s Crystallized Moment acted like a hammer and fire to cleanse his existence.","It was not gentle or particularly pleasant.","It felt like his very being was being melted down and reforged. Like every Seal of Absolute Tongue within him was being pulled apart, examined for flaws, and reconstructed with precision that transcended mortal craftsmanship. His muscles trembled not from exertion but from fundamental reconstruction. His bones hummed with frequencies that spoke of foundations being compressed into denser, more perfect forms.","Prima Katharsis burned away the surface impurities.","It was like shedding a skin he hadn’t realized was dead. Like exhaling breath he had been holding for eons without knowing. His Weight at the Surface Depth solidified into something harder, sharper, more absolute than it had been moments before.","Deutera Katharsis went deeper.","It compressed scattered authority into denser forms. The twenty-seven Seals within him, already impossibly heavy, grew heavier still . They pressed against the boundaries of his existence with weight that would have crushed lesser beings into paste. But Noah was not a lesser being. He was THE Genesis Monarch. And his foundations welcomed the compression like starving wolves welcoming meat.","|KATHARSIS PROGRESSION CONFIRMED|","|Prima Katharsis: COMPLETE|","|Initial cleansing of foundational impurities achieved.|","|Weight increase at current Depth: 10%|","|Deutera Katharsis: 50% PROGRESS|","|Compression of scattered authority into denser forms: ONGOING|","|Estimated completion upon consumption of additional treasures.|","|The Weight of your Surface Depth and Intermediate Depth continue to elevate alongside your elevating foundation.|","|Current Surface Depth Weight: 192/100th of baseline Absolute parameters (previously 175/100th)|","|Current Intermediate Depth Weight: 220/100th of baseline Absolute parameters (previously 200/100th)|","|Your foundations are approaching theoretical limits.|","|THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons confirms: Pages remain blank. Ceiling not found. Continue building.|","...!","As all of this occurred, Noah kept his eyes on Glossikos.","This terrifying entity maintained her calm smile throughout his transformation. Those obsidian-blue eyes watched him with the patient attention of someone who had witnessed countless beings attempt what he was doing now.","As big as he talked, he also knew Absolutes were unpredictable.","She could have done something crazy regardless of his warnings. She could have decided that eating him was worth the risk of rejection from The First Tongue. She could have simply overwhelmed him with Depth and Weight that no Thesis could fully counter.","But against Absolutes, he had gotten the act of bullshitting down to an art.","If one simply talked big, especially in his position with the standing he had, things were a lot better this way. Confidence bred hesitation in opponents. Certainty made enemies second-guess themselves.","What did they say?","Fake it until you made it?","Even though he wasn’t an Absolute, he simply needed to continue throwing his weight around until he was one.","Even though his power did not match the title, the distinction of The One Who Laid The Claim to The First Tongue gave him his own unique power. It contributed to his Formless Depth, making him unable to be placed into any single classification. Neither Surface nor Intermediate nor Fundamental could fully contain what he was becoming.","He existed between categories.","And in that liminal space, he found advantages that conventional power could never provide.","As he was thinking all this...","Glossikos spoke.","\" You contributed 9 brand new letters to The First Tongue.\"","Her voice came measured and contemplative, eyes still fixed on him with that unreadable smile.","\" In THE Villa Dei Boscoreale, not even THE Creature would be blessed as much as you.\"","She tilted her head slightly.","\"I wouldn’t be surprised if you do get more Kronos’s Crystallized Moments. And if you don’t complete all the Cycles of Katharsis after receiving such treasures...\"","Her smile sharpened.","\" You would truly be a useless bum.\"","As she said this, she leaned back on the Pool of Lethe and began to float fully once more. Her body submerged slowly, the obsidian-gold waters swallowing her form inch by inch until only her face remained free, staring up at the artificial sky with the lazy contentment of someone who had all the time in existence.","Noah looked at her.","Then he asked what he had been wondering since learning of the Absolutes bound to this place.","\" You and the other Absolutes here... just what is going on?\"","His voice came direct and probing.","\" THE Creature, THE Primordial Chaos, and THE Living Paradox came here and left. You are Absolutes just like them. Why are you bound to this realm?\"","His eyes narrowed with calculation.","\" Are you feeling particularly talkative to share anything about this?\"","...!","What secret did THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap truly hold?","What kept four Absolutes imprisoned in a domain they could not leave?","What price had been paid, and by whom?","Glossikos smiled while staring at the artificial sky.","And ridiculously, as if to punctuate the absurdity of this conversation, another Kronos’s Crystallized Moment began to float down toward Noah.","A second Mythical-tier treasure.","Descending to him because his contribution warranted it.","Glossikos watched it fall with eyes that held ancient exhaustion.","\" As long as one is not an Absolute, they do not understand the vastness of Existence.\"","Her voice came different now. Heavier. Laden with weight that spoke of secrets carried for far too long.","\" Or the results of choices that many beings make across it.\"","She paused.","\" The results of the actions of THE Creature when he made his Belly of Existence. The results of the actions of THE Living Paradox when he ushered THE Fallout.\"","Her laugh was bitter.","\" You would think they would learn. You would think they would stop.\"","The second Kronos’s Crystallized Moment continued its descent.","\" They never do.\"","...!"]},{"number":4780,"title":"Chapter 4780: Chapter 4779: Leaders and Kings III","paragraphs":["Her obsidian-blue eyes found his.","\" You Four... THE Four... always want more. Fucking insatiable monsters you are.\"","The words landed like accusations.","\"It almost makes me wonder why you all were the ones to lay the claims, when all you do is change things again and again. When all you do is make things harder for everyone who has to live with the consequences of your decisions.\"","She exhaled slowly.","\" We... those of us here in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment... and in other places like this... we exist to act as glue. To hold a few critical things together.\"","Her voice grew colder.","\" The Primordial Realms are a unique part of Observable Existence. They share the secrets of its emergence. The foundations upon which everything else was built. Ginnungagap. Muspelheim. Alfheimr. Jotunheim. All of them connected through Nexus Points that predate the modern understanding of reality.\"","She stared at the artificial sky with something that might have been hatred.","\" We are bound to places like this forever precisely because you Four exist and do the things that you do.\"","The second Kronos’s Crystallized Moment reached Noah’s waiting hand.","\" We all... hate you all so, so much.\"","The words were spoken with the casualness of stating objective fact.","\" But it is a unique hate. I do not hate what you stand for, for example. The First Tongue is beautiful. Mana is necessary. Chaos has its place. Paradox... well, Paradox is Paradox.\"","Her smile became something sharp and wounded.","\" But the things you all do are so detestable. And they bring us all ever closer to extinction. All for the sake of...\"","She paused.","\" Higher Scales.\"","The word hung in the air.","\" Scales.\"","Repeated with growing venom.","\" Scales.\"","And again.","\" Scales.\"","Her voice dropped to something barely above a whisper.","\" Man, fuck you all and your Scales.\"","...!","BOOM!","The words landed with weight that exceeded their apparent simplicity!","Noah held the second Kronos’s Crystallized Moment in his hand, feeling its temporal authority pulse against his palm.","Higher Scales.","THE Four pursuing something beyond their current positions.","And beings like Glossikos paying the price for that pursuit.","He looked at this Absolute who had just cursed him and everything he represented, and he found that he didn’t have an immediate response.","Because what could he say?","He was pursuing Higher Scales himself.","He was changing things again and again.","He was, by her definition, exactly the kind of insatiable monster she described.","And yet...","He swallowed the second Kronos’s Crystallized Moment.","Because regardless of what she thought, regardless of what any of them thought...","He would not stop.","He could not stop.","The powerless were ground to dust in the endless weavings of time.","And he refused to be powerless.","Even if it meant the entire Observable Existence learned to hate him for it.","But...","Hatred!","There was actually genuine hatred in the eyes of Glossikos the Articulate.","Did the other three Absolutes in here feel the same way?","If they did feel like this... why didn’t they actively move against beings like him and THE Creature?","Noah looked at her as he asked directly.","\" Are you going to tell me any concrete details, or keep the air of mystery? I’ve gotten the information that you all are bound here and protect this place.\"","His eyes narrowed with calculation.","\" Who are you protecting it from? Besides THE Four, what else is there that only Absolutes know about?\"","He asked such a simple question.","And yet Glossikos smiled toward him with something between amusement and contempt.","\" Maybe we are protecting it from the likes of you. The disruptors and chaotic things all of you are.\"","She laughed, but there was no warmth in the sound.","\"I actually ponder every day how all signs point to THE Primordial Chaos being the strongest. Because all of you bring so much chaos that he can only benefit. And yet THE Creature and THE Living Paradox did their own designs to somehow keep their edge.\"","She waved her hand dismissively.","\" Ah, it doesn’t matter to you now. You won’t be able to do anything now. You need to be an Absolute, otherwise it is meaningless.\"","Noah looked at her with a defiant glare.","The second Kronos’s Crystallized Moment permeated across his existence, its temporal authority weaving through every fiber of his being.","The transformation was even more intense this time.","His existence reconstructed itself from foundational principles upward. The twenty-seven Seals of Absolute Tongue within him blazed with incandescent brilliance that made the waters of the Pool of Lethe boil around his form. His skin seemed to glow from within as compressed authority sought release through every pore. His muscles trembled with the force of power being packed into denser and denser configurations.","Deutera Katharsis completed with the force of a dam breaking.","Scattered authority that had been spread across his existence compressed into forms so dense that they approached singularities of concentrated power. His Weight at every Depth solidified into something that felt less like flesh and more like existential constants given physical form.","Trita Katharsis followed immediately after.","The harmonization of conflicting aspects within his Depth created resonances that made the entire Thermae tremble. Elements of his foundation that had existed in tension now aligned with perfect precision. The result was a whole that exceeded the sum of its parts by orders of magnitude.","|Deutera Katharsis: COMPLETE|","|Compression of scattered authority into denser forms: ACHIEVED|","|Weight increase at current Depth: 20% (cumulative with Prima Katharsis)|","|Trita Katharsis: COMPLETE|","|Harmonization of conflicting aspects within your Depth: ACHIEVED|","|Weight increase at current Depth: 30% (cumulative with previous cycles)|","|FOUNDATION ASSESSMENT UPDATE|","|Current Surface Depth Weight: 248/100th of baseline Absolute parameters|","|Current Intermediate Depth Weight: 286/100th of baseline Absolute parameters|","|You now exceed what THE Creature held at equivalent classifications by a factor of 2.48 at Surface Depth and 2.86 at Intermediate Depth.|","|These numbers continue to climb.|","|POOL EFFICIENCY NOTIFICATION|","|The effectiveness of The Pool of Lethe has been fully extracted.|","|All foundational impurities that could be forgotten have been forgotten.|","|All inefficient patterns that could be erased have been erased.|","|Recommendation: Enter another pool to continue Katharsis progression.|","|Remaining cycles: Tetarta, Pempte, Ekti, Evdomi, Ogdoi, Enati|","...!"]},{"number":4781,"title":"Chapter 4781: Chapter 4780: Leaders and Kings IV","paragraphs":["Noah looked at all of these prompts as he turned his gaze back to Glossikos.","\" Nothing is ever meaningless.\"","His voice came heavy with conviction.","\"I may not have the Depth of an Absolute, but I can do things that only Absolutes can. And I can even do things that no Absolutes can.\"","His eyes blazed with the fire of someone who refused to accept limitations imposed by others.","\" You, nor THE Creature, nor any others can design new letters of The First Tongue, and yet I did.\"","...!","His words were heavy!","Glossikos looked at him and smiled.","Then she laughed with genuine amusement.","\" You wouldn’t be able to understand or do anything about anything before Absolute. Simple as that.\"","Her voice carried the certainty of someone stating fundamental truth.","\" You can hate me for this just as I hate what THE Four stand for. When you get to that point, you actually won’t even need for me or anyone else to tell you anything.\"","Her obsidian-blue eyes held his without flinching.","\" You will know yourself.\"","...!","Noah frowned at these words.","Cryptic nonsense or genuine wisdom?","He couldn’t tell.","But he didn’t have time to dwell on it.","He rose up out of the Pool of Lethe.","The obsidian-gold waters cascaded off his form as he emerged, steam rising from skin that had been fundamentally transformed by the Cycles of Katharsis. His muscular figure gleamed with vitality that exceeded what it had held mere moments before. His toga wrapped around him with renewed elegance, the fabric seeming to recognize that its wearer had become something grander.","Glossikos looked at him from where she remained floating in the pool.","\" Oh, what I can do is bypass all the other requirements for you to grasp the Lochagos ranking and attain the Polemarch ranking.\"","Her smile became something sharper.","\" You have been saying you wanted to kill THE Weavers that arrived in here, right?\"","She laughed.","\" Haha, a tall fucking order, but good luck. The most I can do is make Paradoxos not interfere.\"","She waved her hand casually.","\" But I can at least allow you to be a Polemarch to try it.\"","...!","She finally said something good!","And she acted on it immediately!","HUUM!","The glorious change that unfolded was visible to the naked eye!","Noah’s toga shifted and transformed!","The simple garments of a Hoplite dissolved into light, replaced by the more elaborate attire of a Lochagos, multiple layers of inscribed fabric, Phonemes burning brighter across the surface. But even that didn’t last.","The toga transformed again!","The adornments of a Polemarch materialized around his form!","Rich blue-gold fabric that seemed woven from crystallized authority itself. Inscriptions that didn’t just display Phonemes but actively channeled their power. A laurel wreath that burned with the light of compressed linguistic mastery. Upon his chest, a golden pin depicted a shield, spear, and laurel wreath intertwined...the symbol of a War Leader of Wisdom.","|RANK ADVANCEMENT CONFIRMED|","|Previous Rank: Hoplite (Citizen-Soldier)|","| New Rank: POLEMARCH (War Leader of Wisdom)|","|Advancement Method: Direct elevation by Strategos Glossikos the Articulate|","|Requirements bypassed: Lochagos promotion, Trial demonstrations|","|POLEMARCH RIGHTS ACTIVATED|","|Depth Limitation: THE Fundamental Depth|","|Your suppressed power has been restored.|","|You may now express authority up to Fundamental Depth within THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.|","|Additional Rights:|","|- Full access to all libraries and sacred spaces|","|- May participate in governance with voting rights|","|- May judge formal debates and assign Merit|","|- May assign tasks to lower ranks|","|- May access the Path of Departure (requires Strategos approval for actual departure)|","|Note: As a Polemarch, you may now formally challenge other Polemarchs and even Strategoi to debates or Arena combat.|","|THE Weavers, despite being Absolutes externally, are currently classified as Hoplites within this domain(Well, maybe? We haven’t really checked).|","|You outrank them(Maybe? Likely.).|","|Use this advantage wisely.|","...!","Noah looked over the prompts calmly.","And then he felt it.","The immensity of his Way fully returned to its fullest state!","The suppression that had compressed his power to Surface Depth levels shattered like glass struck by a hammer! His Formless Depth surged through his existence, filling every corner that had been emptied by the domain’s restrictions!","Blue-gold flames billowed around him as if unleashed from a prison!","His figure became bathed in plasmic fire that spoke of Mana and The First Tongue intertwined! The flames didn’t burn the Thermae around him...they simply existed, declaring his authority through their very presence!","And when he breathed, his nose and mouth released flaming Logos and Philologies!","Or really, what stood for his definition of Philology.","His Genesis Principles had been transformed into Archai, fundamental statements of reality that went beyond mere linguistic constructs. And now those Archai spilled from him with every exhalation, declarations of existence that made the artificial sky above pulse in response.","When Glossikos looked at him now, she laughed with something that sounded almost like delight.","\" Haha, well, now you look a lot more like THE Creature. That guy always had multicolored flames raging around him.\"","As she said such words, Noah looked at her with eyes that now burned with restored authority.","\" Thanks for the advancements in status.\"","The words were simple but sincere.","As he spoke, he floated over to the next pool in this place.","He was about to enter it when Glossikos spoke again.","\" Hold on a second.\"","Her voice carried casual command.","\" Let me make it even easier for you as another favor.\"","She rose slightly from the Pool of Lethe, her Dryad form glowing with the authority of an Absolute preparing to exert her power.","\" Oh, and these are favors that I will call upon sooner or later.\"","Her smile held promise of future debt.","\" The pools in this place are nice, but you don’t have to go through them one by one. If the power of an Absolute exerts itself truly here...\"","She raised her hand.","BOOM!","The entire Thermae of Cyclic Refinement transformed!","All the pools covered by mist in this vast domain began to move! The floor changed and altered seamlessly, ancient stone rearranging itself as if it were liquid rather than solid! Channels opened. Barriers dissolved. Currents formed where none had existed.","The pools converged!"]},{"number":4782,"title":"Chapter 4782: Chapter 4781: Leaders and Kings V","paragraphs":["The Pool of Mnemosyne flowed toward the center, its waters that helped one remember and integrate all knowledge they had ever encountered merging with the streams from other sources!","And multiple other pools followed!","One massive swirling sea formed where six separate pools had been!","The waters churned with colors that shifted and merged, obsidian and gold and silver and crimson and white-hot flame and the deep blue of existential depths! Steam rose in patterns that wrote Phonemes in the air! The artificial sky above blazed brighter as if recognizing the magnitude of what had been created!","|The following pools of THE Thermae of Cyclic Refinement have been temporarily combined by Strategos authority:|","|The Pool of Mnemosyne (Memory): Helps one remember and integrate all knowledge they have ever encountered.|","|The Pool of Styx (Invulnerability): Hardens foundations against external corruption during refinement.|","|The Pool of Acheron (Sorrow): Allows one to process and incorporate painful experiences into strength.|","|The Pool of Cocytus (Lamentation): Releases trapped potential that grief has locked away.|","|The Pool of Phlegethon (Fire): Burns away weaknesses with purifying flame.|","|The Pool of Oceanus (The Existence-River): Connects one’s foundation to the fundamental flow of Existence itself.|","|COMBINED EFFECT:|","|Stepping into the sea combining all pools will grant exponentially greater effect to Katharsis.|","|Multiple cycles may be completed simultaneously.|","|Warning: The intensity of this combined refinement may exceed normal parameters.|","|Recommendation: Proceed. Your fat foundations can handle it.|","...!","With shining eyes, Noah looked at the nonchalant Glossikos who remained in The Pool of Lethe.","\"Thanks.\"","The word was simple.","But it carried genuine gratitude.","Then his body delved into the vibrant sea.","The multicolored waters surged around him the moment he entered! They penetrated into every layer of his existence! Memory and invulnerability and processed sorrow and released potential and purifying flame and Existential connection all merged into a single overwhelming experience.","The waters bubbled and churned!","Then they surged into his existence with force that would have destroyed anything less than what he had become.","As such a process began, Noah found himself in a very nostalgic mood.","He felt the immensity of his 27 Seals heading toward an unfathomable level as everything happening here was all connected.","Because as he continued to get stronger here every second...","A battle outside THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, in The Stoa of Dogmata, was being greatly affected by the rising immensity of his brilliance.","In a heavy and disastrous battle, many would only see the flashy impacts and terrifying expressions of power.","They didn’t truly have an idea how those involved in the battle were feeling.","At this moment, in the Stoa of Dogmata, with an Absolute watching calmly in the distance, Noah had his eyes on Gilgamesh.","Every move he made was for the purpose of bringing Ruin against this being.","He really felt like fights were a unique thing. To fight against something, one did not necessarily have to hate it.","When he first fought against apes and wolves in the first few dungeons after he became a Hunter, he didn’t particularly hate them. For him, they were only beasts that served as obstacles. He found them, killed them, and moved on with the loot.","But then, there were a few enemies across his existence where he genuinely hated them.","When he fought against these enemies, he found himself unfathomably focused. Truly and fully weaponizing his hatred in the most efficient manner until the enemy before him had that brilliance in their eyes collapse into nothingness.","So...","BOOM!","Even though Gilgamesh was surrounded by swirling weapons rushing from golden pools endlessly, each one carrying his Depth...","And it was a heavy Depth at that...","Noah threw his Absolute Seal of Infinity forward!","It acted like an unstoppable hammer, crashing and pulverizing the swirling weapons around Gilgamesh before it was eventually knocked back toward him!","But this was seconds ago.","Before he began Katharsis.","As his Weight became grander and grander, the Weavings of Gilgamesh that were already on the defensive... he began to pierce through them while nothing passed through to him.","Because he had the fragment of THE Axiom of Differentiated Tongue floating around him!","Anything that neared was broken down and dissolved into components of The First Tongue! Spears became Phonemes. Swords became scattered Logos. Axes became fragments of meaning that dispersed harmlessly into the air.","He proceeded ahead toward Gilgamesh more and more.","And all this time, his expression still remained bright.","At this moment, Noah took the 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue swirling around him and branded them over his skin!","One by one, they pressed into his flesh like tattoos being seared into existence itself!","Infinity blazed across his right arm!","Quintessence burned over his left!","Tyranny marked his chest!","The remaining Seals spread across his body in patterns that spoke of absolute authority, each one adding its Weight to the whole!","His entire body became shrouded with plasmic blue-gold flames!","\"A leader shows the path forward.\"","His voice came heavy with conviction.","\"I will lead you now and take you on your path to a grave of endless darkness.\"","His eyes locked onto Gilgamesh with the focus of someone about to end an existence.","\"I’m getting a bit more serious. Get ready.\"","BOOM!","The moment he said this, his body erupted outward like an Existential nuclear warhead!","His Weight and Immensity became so terrifying that the very air compressed before him! The Stoa of Dogmata groaned under the pressure! Ancient inscriptions on the surrounding pillars flickered and dimmed.","He smashed across all weapons surrounding Gilgamesh.","Golden spears shattered!","Existential swords broke!","Legendary axes that had conquered civilizations crumbled into fragments!","He appeared right before Gilgamesh in an instant!","Gilgamesh’s eyes opened wildly!","A Declaration instantly erupted from him, golden light blazing with authority that had commanded armies since before most civilizations existed!","But Noah didn’t even care for what such a Declaration was or what it was trying to accomplish!","His fist blazed with the Absolute Seal of Quintessence.","His left hand grabbed the shoulder of Gilgamesh with grip that could crush mountains!","He looked deeply into the stern eyes of this being.","Then his right fist thundered and hammered itself into his chest!","DOONG!","It was like metal meeting metal!"]},{"number":4783,"title":"Chapter 4783: Chapter 4782: Leaders and Kings VI","paragraphs":["The impact sent shockwaves rippling through the Stoa of Dogmata! Ancient pillars cracked! The floor beneath them cratered!","Noah held him down with one hand while using another hand filled with the Weight of his Way to heavily impose and hammer everything that Gilgamesh stood for!","How exactly was the Weight of someone that exceeded even the foundation of THE Creature at THE Surface Depth and THE Intermediate Depth by more than 200% each?","At this moment, Noah knew.","It was enough to rock Gilgamesh, who was grander than other THE Fundamental Depth entities, to the extent that his golden pupils developed cracks in them.","BOOM!","His left hand remained on Gilgamesh’s shoulder as he clamped down.","He looked into the eyes of this being calmly.","\" With that strike just now, I saw cracks permeating across your Unity.\"","His voice came measured and analytical.","\" An impossible thing for you to fathom, I imagine.\"","His grip tightened.","\" I’m sure that like me, you dreamed of your path and all that you would accomplish after THE Fallout. Was the future you saw brilliant? Filled with your glory?\"","As he said such words...","BZZT!","His stomach buzzed with impact!","The tips of two spears grabbed by Gilgamesh smashed onto him! They carried a Declaration of being capable of piercing anything.","The authority behind them would have punched through Fundamental Depth entities without resistance!","And yet 15 Seals were swirling over his front!","They ground down and denied that Declaration completely.","The spears stopped as if they had struck an immovable wall!","Thereafter, Noah looked at this being as he spoke out.","\" My fist carried a severing light that is meant to sever Unity above all else.\"","BOOM!","A heavy Thesis backed by the Weight of a foundation that even THE Creature could not match!","Noah threw his hand out again!","It smashed into Gilgamesh’s chest like a hammer forged from the authority of Existence itself.","The blast and impact caused blue-gold flames to flash and burst around their two figures like a volcanic eruption! Fire and light and concentrated power exploded outward in waves that made the entire Stoa tremble.","The ancient inscriptions on the walls blazed brighter as if trying to contain the devastation!","And after he did it once...","Noah proceeded to do it again.","BOOM!","The second impact cracked something fundamental in Gilgamesh’s chest!","Gilgamesh laid out his own Declaration! Weapons swirled from all around to pierce into Noah! Golden spears and swords and legendary axes descended like rain!","But they were dissolved into Phonemes before they could touch him!","BOOM !","The third impact! The fourth!","Even when weapons neared his body, the Seals covering his skin dissipated them into harmless light!","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","The fifth! The sixth! The seventh! The eighth!","Each strike carried the severing light meant to destroy Unity! Each impact added to the cracks spreading across Gilgamesh’s existence! Each hammer blow pushed The First Leader closer to collapse.","BOOM!","On the ninth impact, Gilgamesh’s body was filled with cracks!","Crimson-gold blood leaked from fissures that had formed across his golden armor. His flesh, saturated with Paradox and Unity intertwined, showed damage that should have been impossible for something at his level to sustain.","And yet his face remained regal.","That of a leader.","That of a king.","Even broken and bleeding, he did not show weakness. He did not show fear. He showed only the dignity of one who had commanded since before time learned to count.","But...","\" Your Unity is tattered, pounded, and broken down.\"","Noah said such words calmly while his left hand continued to literally hold the Depth and Immensity of Gilgamesh right before him.","And at this time, Gilgamesh held a light of defiance!","He didn’t even acknowledge this assessment!","And because he didn’t acknowledge it, it almost acted like a Declaration!","His Way began to heal itself!","Unity putting itself back together piece by piece!","But...","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","In a femtosecond, Noah smashed out 18 times!","The combined Weight of his 27 Seals battered against Gilgamesh with force that transcended normal parameters of violence! Each strike was a statement! Each impact was a Thesis! Each hammer blow declared that Unity would break before Noah’s authority.","On the 18th time, his hand cleanly pierced into the chest of Gilgamesh!","It went through golden armor that had withstood the attacks of countless others!","It went through flesh saturated with the authority of one who had led since the earliest ages!","It went through everything that protected what lay within!","And his hand grasped a beating Heart of Unity.","THE Heart of Unity!","The core of Gilgamesh’s Civilization!","The representation of everything he had built, everyone he had led, every accomplishment he had achieved across eons of existence!","With a single pull...","Noah ripped it out!","The sound was horrific!","Flesh tearing! Bone breaking! The wet separation of something that was never meant to be removed from its housing.","Crimson-gold blood sprayed across Noah’s face as the Heart came free!","It continued beating in his grasp, each pulse sending ripples of fading authority through the air.","Multiple Seals flared all around Noah like chains.","They wrapped around the hands of Gilgamesh!","They bound his feet!","They dragged him down to his knees with weight that even The First Leader could not resist.","Then the Seal of Tyranny formed into a purple throne behind Noah!","It materialized from concentrated authority, a seat of power that declared dominion over all who knelt before it!","Noah proceeded to regally sit upon it as he breathed out.","His hand grasped the beating Heart of Unity as he examined it with clinical interest.","It had bright hues of purple and gold, the colors of leadership and glory intertwined. And mixed in here and there, threads of obsidian that spoke of Paradox woven into its very structure.","\" Hatred brings with it a sense of brutality.\"","His voice came heavy with something that might have been regret.","\"I don’t need to do this. I truly don’t.\"","His eyes met Gilgamesh’s defiant gaze.","\" But I am only human. I wish to express my hatred. I wish to give back. I wish to answer your curiosity.\"","...!","The image was one that would burn itself into the memory of any who witnessed it!","The First Leader, Gilgamesh, bound by Seals of terrifying Immensity!","Kneeling before a throne of Tyranny!","The Heart of his Civilization, something that one had to protect against all cost, grasped by another!","And while he grasped it and sat grandly upon his throne, Noah looked at the defiant visage of Gilgamesh.","Then he took the Heart of his Civilization...","And began to take bites out of it.","The first bite tore away a section of beating muscle!","Immense Depth was devoured!","Crimson-gold blood savaged leaked around Noah’s mouth, running down his chin in streams that painted his chest! The taste was iron and authority and the accumulated glory of eons!","His eyes remained locked with Gilgamesh this whole time!","He chewed.","He swallowed.","He took another bite.","It was brutal!","It was savage!","It was the act of a predator consuming the very essence of its prey while that prey watched!","And while he did this, Declarations were shockingly forming around Gilgamesh even now.","Even with his heart torn out!","Even with his body bound!","Even with his Unity shattered!","The First Leader still fought back!","Golden light blazed as he tried to reclaim what was being taken! Authority surged as he attempted to stop the consumption of everything he had built.","But every single Declaration was dissolved or dispersed.","Noah’s presence, his Weight, his authority over The First Tongue itself... it negated everything Gilgamesh tried.","Noah continued eating.","Blood ran down his chin.","His eyes never left Gilgamesh’s.","\"I am doing everything I can so that one day, I never sit where you sit. Watching another man devour my Civilization.\"","He took another bite.","\" This is my leadership to you as I show the Way.\"","Another bite.","\" However brilliant you were, this was not something you saw being possible.\"","Another bite.","\" However brilliant I am, I will take this as a lesson.\"","He swallowed the last piece of the Heart of Unity.","\" Keep the defiant light. Remain true to who you are to the very end.\"","His voice grew softer.","\" At the very least, you will not lose your title of a Leader.\"","...!","Noah said such heavy words as he brutally finished devouring the Civilization of Gilgamesh.","The First Leader knelt before him, bound and broken, his Unity consumed, his Civilization destroyed.","And yet those golden eyes still blazed with defiance that refused to die.","In the distance, THE Secretive Eon looked at this scene with shining eyes.","Moments later, she shockingly licked her lips.","As if she was parched.","As if she felt...a bit hungry herself."]},{"number":4784,"title":"Chapter 4784: Chapter 4783: The Ultimate Failure I","paragraphs":["Brutality .","There were different forms of it across Civilizations.","Some said it was not necessary. That violence begat violence. That cruelty only bred more cruelty in an endless cycle that consumed all who participated in it.","But truly, sometimes, brutality was warranted.","And sometimes, it was a must.","When an enemy sought to destroy everything you built, was gentleness the answer? When a predator came for your people, was kindness the response? When someone sent an attack of curiosity across time that nearly collapsed your existence and everyone you cared about...","Was restraint truly the moral high ground?","Noah had long since made peace with this truth. Observable Existence was cruel.","Those who held back when brutality was required found themselves and everyone they loved ground to dust in the endless Weavings of time.","He would not be ground to dust.","And so, he would not hold back.","---","With every bite of The Heart of Unity he took, his gaze never left Gilgamesh.","The crimson-gold blood ran down his chin. The taste of accumulated authority and ancient glory filled his mouth. The Depth of a Civilization built across eons dissolved into his existence with each swallow.","And through it all, those golden eyes of The First Leader remained defiant.","Even broken. Even bound. Even watching his very heart being consumed.","Defiant.","Noah respected that, barely.","After the final bite, he spoke.","\" After a certain point, the necessary brutality has to be brought to an end.\"","His voice came measured and calm, as if discussing philosophy rather than the destruction he had just wrought.","\"I won’t be so cruel as to torture you.\"","He wiped the blood from his chin with the back of his hand.","\"I have collapsed your Way of Unity. I am eating the very Heart of your Civilization. Your Depth and Immensity continues to reduce as you will very soon fall to the level of Pre-THE.\"","His eyes studied the kneeling figure before him.","\"I was planning to devour you completely. But out of curiosity, I will give you a choice.\"","He leaned forward on his throne of Tyranny.","\" You see, THE Four, especially THE Primordial Chaos, like to act all mysteriously and play around with choices. I’ve experienced a few aspects of who they are.\"","His smile held no warmth.","\" Right now, I’ll give you a choice.\"","He paused.","\"I’ve collapsed many beings across my life. Every life I take, however rapid or futile it may seem, I know that it is complete cessation and darkness for the other side. The end of everything they were, everything they could have been, everything they hoped to become.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\" Do you want complete darkness? Or will you submit?\"","The words hung in the air.","\" If you do, I will send you to an inescapable prison where even THE Living Paradox would never be able to take you away from.\"","...!","Noah said this calmly as he looked at Gilgamesh!","He was a glorious and distinguished being. After having collapsed the entirety of his Civilization, Noah had already gained immensely from the vibrant Depth of a Fundamental Depth entity like Gilgamesh.","But if he could continue to gain and use such a being...","If he could have them reforge their Way in THE Infinite Desmoterion...","That was an even grander punishment.","He held the prompts at bay as he waited.","And on the face of The First Leader, there was still defiance.","But something else flickered in those golden eyes now.","Something that looked almost like... clarity.","As if the consumption of his Heart had stripped away illusions he had been carrying for eons.","Gilgamesh was silent for a long moment.","Then he laughed.","It was not the laugh of madness or desperation. It was the laugh of someone who had finally understood a joke that had been played on them across the entirety of their existence.","\"I seem...to have been under the banner of others for too long.\"","His voice came heavy with the weight of accumulated regret.","\"I thought Existence was mine. I thought I was Gilgamesh, The First Leader, commander of armies, conqueror of civilizations, the one whose name would echo across Existence.\"","His golden eyes met Noah’s directly.","\" But I was never truly leading, was I? I was being led. Guided by threads I couldn’t see. Moved by hands I refused to acknowledge.\"","He shook his head slowly.","\"It seems I failed the moment I agreed to go under the banner of Paradox.\"","The words landed with weight.","\"The moment that choice was made, my fate was sealed. Every battle I fought afterward, every victory I claimed, every civilization I conquered... all of it was in service to another’s design. All of it was building toward this moment.\"","His laugh came again, bitter and clear.","\" What a waste.\"","...!","BOOM!","The words were heavy!","Noah looked at this being who had just rejected survival in favor of ending. Who had chosen complete darkness over servitude! Who had, in his final moments, found the clarity to see what he had truly been all along.","Not a leader, but as a follower who had convinced himself he was leading.","\" So you choose collapse.\"","Noah’s voice came without judgment.","\"I choose to finally make a decision that is truly mine. Not Paradox’s. Not THE Living Paradox’s. Not THE Weavers’. Mine.\"","His golden eyes blazed with something that transcended defiance.","\"If I cannot live as Gilgamesh, I will die as Gilgamesh. The First Leader. The one who knelt to no one at the end.\"","He straightened his spine despite the Seals binding him. Well, he said all that, but he was technically being forced to kneel right now!","Noah looked at this being for a long moment.","He had expected the practical choice. He had expected Gilgamesh to choose survival, to choose the possibility of future escape, to choose anything over the absolute finality of complete collapse.","But The First Leader had surprised him.","In the end, he had chosen to be what he always tried to be.","A Leader.","Someone who made their own choices, even if that choice was death.","Noah rose from his throne of Tyranny.","\"In the end, you made a choice that was yours. And for that, I will grant you a clean collapse. No torture. No drawn-out suffering. Just... ending.\"","Gilgamesh closed his eyes.","Noah’s hand blazed with the combined authority of his 27 Seals.","Gilgamesh said no more as even at this moment, he looked ridiculously grand.","...!","BOOM!","Noah’s hand descended!","Brilliant blue-gold flames erupted from his palm with force that transcended normal violence! They consumed the bound form of Gilgamesh completely! Not slowly, not painfully, but instantly and absolutely!","The First Leader did not scream as he simply... ended.","His existence, accumulated across eons of conquest and command, collapsed into nothingness in the span of a heartbeat. His Depth, already diminished by the consumption of his Heart, dissolved into Noah’s flames. His Way of Unity, already shattered and devoured, ceased to be entirely.","Gilgamesh, The First Leader, was no more.","The Stoa of Dogmata fell silent.","Where he had knelt, only scorched stone remained.","Not even ash.","Just... absence.","Oh!"]},{"number":4785,"title":"Chapter 4785: Chapter 4784: The Ultimate Failure II","paragraphs":["The area became unfathomably quiet as Noah stared at the place where a Leader used to be.","The attack of curiosity all the way from The Earliest Folds ended like this after all this time.","What a wonder existence was.","Noah closed his eyes as before him, prompts began to descend.","|VICTORY|","|Opponent: Gilgamesh, The First Leader|","|Classification: THE Fundamental Depth|","|Affiliation: THE Living Paradox, THE Loom|","|Status: COMPLETELY COLLAPSED|","|You have devoured the Heart of a Civilization that held immense comparative Weight at THE Fundamental Depth.|","|Gilgamesh’s Unity exceeded normal/average Fundamental Depth parameters by estimated 340%.|","|Additional harvest obtained from complete collapse of remaining existence.|","|This harvest has provided sufficient Depth to trigger advancement.|","|Your Civilizations of Mana and Hunger, though they dont necessarily fit into this classification as they are in totality, Formless, can officially be considered to have advanced to THE Fundamental Depth.|","|You may now begin refining and reinforcing your foundation at THE Fundamental Depth.|","|You may elevate its Weight and Immensity through continued harvest and Katharsis.|","|At this current moment, not enough information has been gathered to make a truly accurate statement regarding the comparative Weight you currently hold at THE Fundamental Depth compared to THE Creature and others like him.|","|Preliminary estimates suggest your foundation exceeds normal parameters, but precise measurements require additional data.|","|Recommendation: Continue building. Continue harvesting. The ceiling has still not been found.|","|Gilgamesh, The First Leader, has been completely collapsed.|","|Former Status: Warden of THE Loom|","|Current Status: Non-existent|","|His accumulated knowledge and authority have been absorbed into your foundations.|","|His existence will never return. Complete collapse is absolute.|","|This action will be known to THE Living Paradox soon enough.|","|Similar to how you found the potential collapse of Lumivara and Ul’moreth through your connection to your followers...|","|THE Living Paradox will sense the permanent loss of Gilgamesh through his connection to THE Loom.|","|Prepare for potential retaliation.|","|Prepare for potential escalation.|","|THE Weavers remain at large within THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.|","|Your original objective has not been completed.|","|Gilgamesh was a distraction. A worthy one, but a distraction nonetheless.|","|THE Weavers must still be collapsed.|","...!","Noah smiled at such words as Ruination was having her fun.","|Your advancement to THE Fundamental Depth does not change your Formless classification.|","|You remain unplaceable within conventional Depth categories.|","|Your Fundamental Depth foundation: Assessment pending. Data insufficient.|","Noah opened his eyes to the gaze of THE Secretive Eon looking at him up and down with a slight smile.","She had been watching the entire time and now, she seemed ready to share her thoughts.","\" No death or collapse is good.\"","Her voice came imposing and mysterious, holding the weight of someone who had contemplated these truths across eons.","\"I actually consider death to be a failure of Existence. A failure of someone to completely master what Existence has presented them.\"","Her eyes held depths that seemed to swallow light itself.","\" Even the peasant born without any authority always has another chance to continue living. Another path to find. Another way to survive what Existence throws at them.\"","She tilted her head slightly.","\"If they meet death, they simply were not successful. They did not solve the puzzle that their circumstances presented. They did not overcome the obstacles that could have been overcome.\"","Her smile grew sharper.","\" The most fearsome peasant that I know is THE Living Paradox. Look at where he arrived after all of that adversity. Born into nothing. Given nothing. And yet he clawed his way to become one of THE Four. He solved every puzzle. He overcame every obstacle. He refused to accept failure.\"","She paused.","\" Whatever life that Gilgamesh led before his death, whatever glory and accomplishments he had... to me, all of it is worth absolutely nothing.\"","Her voice grew colder.","\" Because in the end, he could not stop his collapse. In the end, he faced the ultimate failure.\"","THE Secretive Eon shook her head as she said this.","Noah turned to observe her calmly.","He did not reply right away.","He thought more about her words. The cold logic of them. The brutal assessment that reduced an entire existence to a simple binary of success and failure. Live or die. Overcome or be overcome.","There was truth in what she said.","And yet...","In the end, he chose not to reply.","He simply held a moment of silence.","Whether it was for himself or for another, he did not know. Perhaps for Gilgamesh, who had at least chosen his own ending. Perhaps for the countless beings across his journey who had faced the ultimate failure under his hands. Perhaps simply to acknowledge that existence was vast, and not everything could be reduced to equations of success.","After a few seconds of this silence, he turned toward THE Secretive Eon.","\" If your Disciple could choose between any of the philosophies of the oldest powers in Existence, which one would she choose?\"","He asked such a question simply.","THE Secretive Eon yawned before she replied.","\" Existence.\"","The word came casual and dismissive.","\" She was always a fool when it came to Existence. She idolized THE Creature even though I told her... in the end, I would stand above him and collapse him as well.\"","BOOM!","A fool when it came to Existence and THE Creature!","When Noah thought about this, he couldn’t help but turn his head in a particular direction.","Toward The Early Veiled Shore of THE Creature.","Toward where another body of his currently stood.","---","The Embodiment that THE Creature had laid out had ended moments ago.","And the results were astonishing to observe.","Noah stood near the figures of THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin as both of them at this moment held radiant Fundamental Depths!","They were power-leveled ridiculously by a single Embodiment of THE Creature!","The Depth of THE Living Origin seemed even more potent, as if she was not that far away from Half-Step Absolute. Her entire existence thrummed with authority that had been compressed and refined by forces beyond normal comprehension.","It made some sense.","THE Living Spirit and THE Living Concept who sided with THE Living Paradox within THE Loom each had power at Half-Step Absolute. They had followed different paths, aligned with different philosophies, served different masters.","But in the end, they achieved the same destination."]},{"number":4786,"title":"Chapter 4786: Chapter 4785: The Ultimate Failure III","paragraphs":["And yet, even with the level of power that Tor and THE Living Origin currently held, both had complex expressions.","As if they did not truly want this.","Noah looked at the two of them and shook his head.","He was already receiving an influx of Harvest from the fact that entities who backed his Way of Existence had attained this level of Depth. Their advancement fed into his foundations through the connections they shared.","But with them acting like this...","\" Power is power, regardless of where it came from.\"","His voice came direct and practical.","\"A poor man will never question if a mountain of gold fell into his house one day and wallow about it. Why should you two?\"","Tor’s gaze was bright as he shook his head.","\" Imagine being collapsed by someone, only for that someone later on to say, oh, here you go. A higher level Depth for you.\"","His voice held notes of bitter irony.","\" But alas, you are right. I won’t complain.\"","...!","The vibrant waves of Hunger from him became even more potent!","His foundation, newly elevated to THE Fundamental Depth, pulsed with appetite that seemed to devour the very air around him. Whatever conflicted feelings he held, they did not diminish the power he had been granted.","Noah looked at the figure of THE Living Origin next.","She stood with serene glory that transcended her previous state. Her form seemed to glow from within, multicolored light playing across features that had been refined by THE Creature’s Embodiment. Her eyes held depths that spoke of authority approaching the threshold of Half-Step Absolute.","\"I...have always been chasing after THE Creature.\"","Her voice came measured and heavy with accumulated history.","\" My Everything burned for THE Creature. I first met him in Alfheimr, before he even became an Absolute.\"","Her eyes grew distant with memory.","\" He was brilliant. Every word he said, every action he took... I was enticed completely. I followed him across realms and eons. I gave My Everything I had to support his rise.\"","Something flickered in her expression.","\" But of course, Emotive came along.\"","Her voice grew harder.","\"I truly don’t know what that malevolent creature has to make her jump from one Absolute to another, but...\"","She paused.","\"I am not satisfied with how I was treated. I do not take this as an answer.\"","Her eyes blazed with determination.","\" So I will seek my own answer. For now, I will return to Alfheimr. There, whether he wants to or not, THE Creature will have to give me an answer.\"","BOOM!","THE Living Origin said many heavy words!","Her eyes were thinking of none other than THE Creature.","And near her, Noah turned to see the crimson-obsidian gaze of THE First Hunger.","His gaze seemed to only be directed toward... THE Living Origin.","One was looking at someone at an extremely distant place, seeking answers that may have already been given.","While another was looking at someone right in front of them who would not even gaze their way.","The words of THE First Hunger echoed out as he said calmly.","\" Alfheimr? I’ll tag along for fun.\"","His voice came measured and seemingly casual.","\" You can navigate there even in THE Fallout?\"","He asked this question as if the answer didn’t matter.","Origin looked at him and blinked.","\"I will always know my way back home.\"","BOOM!","With such words, she turned toward Noah.","\"I will make this little trip, if that is okay with you.\"","It almost seemed like she was asking for permission.","Because at this moment, she no longer backed THE Creature.","She backed him instead.","Noah smiled lightly as he waved his hand.","He allowed the emergence of a small Seal of Quintessence to flow toward THE Living Origin. It drifted through the air with lazy grace before settling into her palm, its radiance pulsing with compressed authority.","\" Just keep this with you in case of emergencies. If anything happens, let me know.\"","THE Living Origin nodded at such words.","She and THE First Hunger prepared to make an exit into the Wastes of THE Fallout.","Their destination was Alfheimr.","Where THE Creature had first risen.","—","In THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","In The Thermae of Cyclic Refinement.","Noah had his struggles across Existence, but he liked when things were comparatively easier as well.","Among THE Four, he was the weakest.","But at this moment, he was getting his dues.","The contribution of 9 new letters to The First Tongue inside THE Agora of Primordial Judgment... how could it be beat? Especially when the rewards stemmed from the very philosophy of Glossarians?","THE Villa Dei Boscoreale which held the treasures of THE Corrupted Vaults of Ginnungagap flowed into him steadily. The entire time, only one Kronos’s Crystallized Moment after another descended. As soon as he finished one, another would float down from the artificial sky. Mythical-tier treasures that should have been impossibly rare fell into his grasp like common fruits from an abundant tree.","In less than an hour in the combined pools of The Thermae of Cyclic Refinement...","His existence felt a sense of exuberance and immensity that gave him a sense of invincibility.","A false sense of invincibility, but it was there nonetheless.","Because after all, the 9 Cycles of Katharsis were all passed gloriously!","His skin shone with a crystalline blue-gold allure as if he was a Primordial treasure given flesh. Light seemed to emanate from within him, filtering through flesh that had been refined beyond normal biological parameters. Every pore radiated authority. Every inch of his form spoke of foundations compressed to impossible densities.","His Depth and Weight felt utterly suffocating.","Even Glossikos, an Absolute nodded as if saying hey, not bad!","|All Nine Cycles of Katharsis have been successfully completed.|","|The Pool of Mnemosyne (Memory): All knowledge you have ever encountered has been perfectly integrated into your foundations. Nothing is forgotten. Everything is accessible.|","|The Pool of Styx (Invulnerability): Your foundations have been hardened against external corruption. Attempts to destabilize your Depth through foreign influence will face exponentially increased resistance.|","|The Pool of Acheron (Sorrow): All painful experiences across your existence have been processed and incorporated into strength. Trauma that once weakened now fortifies.|","|The Pool of Cocytus (Lamentation): Trapped potential that grief had locked away has been released. Capabilities you did not know you possessed are now accessible.|","|The Pool of Phlegethon (Fire): All weaknesses have been burned away with purifying flame. What remains is only that which serves your advancement.|","|The Pool of Oceanus (The Existence-River): Your foundation has been connected to the fundamental flow of Existence itself. You resonate with reality at frequencies that most beings cannot perceive.|","...!"]},{"number":4787,"title":"Chapter 4787: Chapter 4786: The Ultimate Failure IV","paragraphs":["The prompts continued to flow before his eyes.","|CYCLE COMPLETION BREAKDOWN|","|Tetarta Katharsis (Fourth Purification): Strengthening of boundaries between Depth levels. Weight increase: 40%|","|Pempte Katharsis (Fifth Purification): Integration of external knowledge into core foundations. Weight increase: 50%|","|Ekti Katharsis (Sixth Purification): Refinement of connection between Way and Depth. Weight increase: 60%|","|Evdomi Katharsis (Seventh Purification): Approaching theoretical limits of current classification. Weight increase: 75%|","|Ogdoi Katharsis (Eighth Purification): Transcending normal parameters for current Depth. Weight increase: 90%|","|Enati Katharsis (Ninth Purification / THE Wheel of Foundation): The absolute pinnacle of refinement possible without advancing to higher Depth. Weight increase: 100%|","|Total cumulative Weight increase from all nine cycles: 445%|","|COMPARATIVE WEIGHT ASSESSMENT|","| THE Surface Depth:|","|Current Weight: 950/100th of baseline Absolute parameters|","|You exceed what THE Creature held at Surface Depth by a factor of 9.5|","|THE Intermediate Depth:|","|Current Weight: 910/100th of baseline Absolute parameters|","|You exceed what THE Creature held at Intermediate Depth by a factor of 9.1|","|You are now approaching a theoretical maximum, and it is becoming even harder to reach it.|","...!","The numbers felt surreal for the most part.","But even when he checked again, they remained the same!","The jumping off point of his foundation was grander, and it continued to be so.","More prompts came as his existence buzzed.","|DISTINCTION ACHIEVED|","|Due to attaining the 9th Cycle of Katharsis, you have gained the distinction of:|","| ABSOLUTE IMMOVABLE OBJECT|","|This is a quality mainly gained by those with THE Absolute Depth.|","|You have achieved it at THE Fundamental Depth.|","|This is unprecedented.|","|Boons of the Distinction of Absolute Immovable Object|","|1. Absolute Existential Anchoring: Your existence is now anchored to reality at a fundamental level. Attempts to displace, banish, or forcibly relocate you require authority that exceeds your total Weight. For most beings below Absolute classification, this is unfathomably hard.|","|2. Declaration Resistance: Declarations that target your existence directly must overcome the cumulative Weight of all your Depths simultaneously. This creates layered defense that compounds with each foundation.|","|3. Immutable Core: The core of your existence cannot be altered by external forces without your consent. Existential control and manipulation, and existence rewriting face resistance proportional to your total refined Weight.|","|4. Absolute Gravitational Authority: Your Weight passively influences reality around you. Lesser beings will feel instinctive pressure in your presence.|","|5. Collapse Resistance: Complete collapse of your existence now requires force sufficient to overcome all refined Depths simultaneously. Partial damage will not cascade into total failure.|","|WARNING: This distinction does not make you invincible. Absolutes possess authority that can still challenge these protections. But for all beings below Absolute classification, you have become functionally immovable.|","|Even though sufficient information has not been fully collected regarding the comparative Depth of THE Creature and others at Fundamental classification...|","|A rough and potentially inaccurate estimation has been made.|","|Current Fundamental Depth Weight: Approximately 2/100th of THE Creature’s Fundamental Depth|","|This disparity appears significant, but context is required.|","|ANALYSIS|","|It is hypothesized that THE Creature and others felt the insufficiencies of their prior foundations at THE Surface and Intermediate Depths.|","|In order to build a strong foundation for the sake of becoming Absolutes, their Fundamental Depths were built to unfathomable levels.|","|They may have spent eons at Fundamental classification, accumulating Weight that you have only begun to gather.|","|As of now, all of this stands to only be conjecture.|","|There could be another reason for the disparity.|","|Further data collection is required for accurate assessment.|","|Your Surface and Intermediate foundations now exceed all known parameters.|","|Focus on building Fundamental Depth to match.|","|The ceiling has not been found.|","...!","The prompts were heavy to observe.","But Noah’s eyes remained brilliant as he felt the changes of his foundation and Seals.","Each of the 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue had become so dense that they felt like collapsed Folds embedded in his existence. When he focused on any single one, he could feel its Weight pressing against the fabric of reality itself. They no longer merely represented compressed power. They had become anchors that tethered him to Existence at fundamental levels.","His Physique of THE Indestructible Lexicon of Absolute Weight had transformed into something that transcended its previous state. What had once been impossibly heavy now felt like the foundation upon which Primordial Mountains could be built. Upon which civilizations could stand. Upon which even the machinations of Absolutes could be resisted.","The distinction of Absolute Immovable Object thrummed through every fiber of his being. He could feel reality bending slightly around him, space itself acknowledging that he had become something that could not be easily displaced!","A Fundamental Depth entity could hit him, and he wouldn’t even be forced to move back a step!","As he analyzed all of this...","In the corner of his eye, he saw the visage of Glossikos rising up fully from the Pool of Lethe.","With a frown.","Her glorious figure of a Dryad emerged from the obsidian-gold waters with grace that belied the displeasure on her features. Vines and leaves that composed her hair dripped with liquid that seemed reluctant to leave her form. Her bark-like skin glistened with moisture that caught the light of the artificial sky.","The immensity she gave off was unmistakable. Even rising from a casual bath, she radiated authority that pressed against everything around her. The air grew heavier. The steam swirled in patterns that spoke of power being exerted without conscious effort.","Her frown quickly became anger.","Something had happened.","Noah frowned as well.","\" What happened?\"","His voice came sharp with concern.","Glossikos’s obsidian-blue eyes blazed.","\" THE Weavers, now at the Lochagos ranking, have been granted a special Right of Challenge that cannot be denied.\"","Her voice dripped with distaste.","\" By Paradoxos.\"","\"A Polemarch can deny such a challenge with the support of a Strategos. But a Lochagos or Hoplite cannot refuse when the Right is properly invoked.\"","\" She must have discovered that you cannot be challenged directly. Your Polemarch status, combined with my backing, makes you untouchable through normal means.\"","Oh?","Noah frowned deeper.","And Glossikos continued, her anger barely contained.","\" THE Weavers have uniquely issued the Right to Challenge... to a dog instead.\"","BOOM!","The words landed like hammer blows.","\" To the Hoplite Muspeli Lifeform you left out there. I assume it is to force your hand. Or perhaps them making a move before you can advance too much.\"","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes opened wide.","But there was no panic in them.","Only burning calmness and immensity.","His dog?","THE Weavers went after his dog?!","Skoll.","The transformed Duke who had followed him loyally since Muspelheim not too long ago!","The good boy who sat waiting patiently while his Master refined his foundations.","The innocent creature who had no understanding of the machinations occurring around him.","THE Weavers had targeted Skoll!"]},{"number":4788,"title":"Chapter 4788: Chapter 4787: Egregious! I","paragraphs":["One could make many mistakes in life.","But some mistakes were so unfathomably egregious compared to others that someone had to ask... why would that person do that?","Hunt Noah? Okay, not a problem.","Scheme and plan and make things difficult for him? No problem! Struggles were part of Existence, after all!","But why would they go after his dog that he had just gotten a chance to be with in such a short time span?","For him, the matter of time was actually inconsequential when it came to the relationship itself.","The moment that Duke passed from the hands of Galileo and came to him. The moment that he awakened him from Duke to Skoll. The moment that this simple dog helped him rescue others of his Civilization and even escape the hands of an Absolute.","At the moment all of these things came to pass, Duke was already part of his camp.","Part of his family.","The time of it did not matter too much.","Bonds were not measured in duration. They were measured in weight. In meaning. In the willingness to stand beside someone at times of great difficulty.","Skoll had stood beside him.","And now THE Weavers had targeted him?","As if THE Weavers had seen all of this, she had decided to skip Lumivara and Ul’moreth. She went straight for his dog. The innocent one.","It was an utterly egregious mistake.","One that Noah would be sure to let THE Weavers know to their last breath.","Glossikos spoke with measured calm.","\" The challenge has already been issued. Your dog has been directly transported to the Arena.\"","Her obsidian-blue eyes studied him.","\"A few other things seem to be happening behind the scenes. But what will you do?\"","What he would do was already set in stone.","Now, it just meant that it would happen with even more brutality and blood.","Noah’s eyes pulsed with the weight of the Seal of Infinity. Blue-gold radiance spilled from his gaze as if his very perception had become weaponized.","\" I’m sure they did this to pull me out. So I will put myself forward.\"","His voice came cold and absolute.","\" Pass the word for me. I will stand to replace the one that THE Weavers have challenged.\"","The figure of Glossikos sighed and lightly nodded.","\" Absolute is Absolute, regardless of where you currently stand.\"","Her voice carried warning.","\" If you are not an Absolute yourself, regardless of how astonishing you are...\"","She did not finish her words.","As if their ending would truly not be a great one.","But she did continue.","\" Originally, there is another location within this Villa Dei Boscoreale apart from The Thermae of Cyclic Refinement that would have served you well.\"","Her eyes grew distant with contemplation.","\"It is filled with items and weapons that have a level of power similar to, or even sometimes exceeding, Fragments of Axioms.\"","Her gaze returned to him.","\" This region is THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts. The Museum of Destiny.\"","She began to explain.","\" THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts contains item-based treasures. Unlike the Thermae where consumption is guaranteed to provide benefits, the Mouseion operates on principles of fate and worthiness.\"","Her voice grew more serious.","\" If one is fated to receive a particular artifact, they will be drawn to it and the barriers will part. If one is not fated, the barriers remain impenetrable regardless of power level.\"","She paused for emphasis.","\" Even Absolutes cannot force their way to artifacts not meant for them.\"","Her hand waved, and images seemed to shimmer in the steam around them.","\" Some items include The Stylus of Cadmus. A bronze writing implement that never dulls. Anything written with this stylus becomes a binding Declaration for 24 hours.\"","The image shifted.","\" The Lyre of Orpheus. A golden stringed instrument that plays itself when held. Music from this lyre can influence emotions of beings up to one Depth above the player.\"","Another shift.","\" The Thread of Ariadne. An unbreakable golden thread on a spindle. It always leads the holder to what they truly seek.\"","The images continued to flicker.","\" The Caduceus Shard. A fragment of the original herald’s staff. It allows communication across any distance. It can broker truces that cannot be broken.\"","She dismissed the images with a wave.","\" There are countless others. Weapons that can pierce through Declarations. Shields that can absorb the weight of Absolutes. Items that defy conventional understanding of what is possible.\"","Glossikos looked at him directly.","\" I’ll make sure you don’t miss that opportunity.\"","Her voice grew practical.","\" Give me a unique signature of your Depth and I will take it to THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts. Whatever is fated for you... will come to you anywhere in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.\"","Her smile held a dangerous edge.","\" Even while you are facing THE Weavers in the Arena.\"","She said such words as Noah nodded.","He waved his hand.","A brilliant blue-gold Seal of Infinity emerged from his palm, spinning with authority that told of foundations refined beyond normal parameters. It carried the unique signature of his Depth. The weight of his existence compressed into a single spinning construct.","His dominating body turned around.","And disappeared a moment later.","The Seal of Infinity continued spinning toward Glossikos like a coin flipping through air.","She grasped it in her hands.","She looked it over up and down with careful attention. The weight of it. The density of it. The sheer authority compressed into something so small.","A contemplative look entered her eyes.","\" Would he truly be able to make a significant enough difference?\"","An Absolute wondered.","And it was a wonder in itself as to what exactly she was contemplating.","Was she thinking about the battle ahead?","Was she thinking about the future of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment?","Or was she thinking about something else entirely?","Something that only Absolutes knew?","The questions hung in the steam-filled air of The Thermae as Glossikos began moving toward THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts.","Carrying the signature of THE Genesis Monarch with her."]},{"number":4789,"title":"Chapter 4789: Chapter 4788: Egregious! II","paragraphs":["Outside of THE Villa Dei Boscoreale.","WAP!","Noah reappeared.","He observed the solemn and angered figures of Ul’moreth and Lumivara who now had on the togas of Lochagoi. Their advancement had occurred while he was undergoing the Cycles of Katharsis. Their expressions spoke of fury barely contained.","The Glossarian Polemarchs were also in the surroundings with equally nasty gazes. They had welcomed Noah. They had protected his companions. And now THE Weavers had circumvented their protection through bureaucratic manipulation.","Skoll was nowhere to be seen.","Lunaris turned toward Noah as she was going to speak when...","Her figure pulsed with astonishment!","She sensed the immensity his figure emanated!","Especially now, when he looked a little bit... mad?","His crystalline skin glowed with blue-gold radiance. His eyes burned with weight that pressed against everyone in proximity. His presence alone made the air heavier, made breathing slightly more difficult, made reality itself acknowledge that something dangerous had arrived.","He looked devilishly dashing with such a serious gaze, didn’t he?","The moment she had such a thought, she shook her pages as she refocused on the situation at hand.","\" Sir, they have already taken your companion due to a Challenge that even we could not deny.\"","Her voice came serious and professional.","\" The Esteemed Glossikos has informed us. We are ready to bring you to the Arena for you to accept this challenge instead.\"","She paused.","\" We do have to warn you that now, you will be under the scrutiny of all those in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.\"","...!","She said such words as Noah turned to her, reigning in his unfolding waves of Tyranny.","The pressure that had been pressing against everyone eased slightly.","But only slightly.","His voice came out calm.","Too calm.","The kind of calm that preceded storms.","\" Let’s just go.\"","His eyes burned with blue-gold fire.","\" Some Absolutes need to understand what happens when they make someone lock in.\"","BOOM!","The words landed with weight that made several Polemarchs take unconscious steps backward.","Not from fear of him.","But from recognition that whoever stood on the other side of that statement was about to experience something terrible.","Lunaris nodded and began leading the way.","Toward the Arena.","Toward THE Weavers.","Toward a confrontation that would be witnessed by every faction in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","And Noah followed with steps that made the ground tremble, Ul’moreth and Lumivara joining him as brilliant blue-gold light began to wrap around all of them!","—","THE Palaestra of Primordial Reckoning!","This was the name and distinction of the grand Arena within THE Agora of Primordial Judgment. It was a place of existential and combat training where battles determined fundamental truths about the combatants’ worth and existence.","Different factions called it by different names.","Glossarians called it \"The Lexicon of Blood,\" where Declarations were written in violence. Paradoxians called it \"The Contradiction Ring,\" where impossibilities became possible. Existentialists called it \"The Crucible of Being,\" where existence was tested. Chaosites called it \"The Entropy Pit,\" where order broke down into beautiful disorder.","Four names for one place.","All of them true.","THE Palaestra of Primordial Reckoning sat at the exact center of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, equidistant from all four philosophical territories.","It was accessible from any faction’s domain through dedicated pathways called \"The Roads of Reckoning.\" These roads were neutral ground where no faction held authority. Stone inscribed with Phonemes of The First Tongue paved the way, each step a reminder that this place belonged to everyone and no one.","The Arena existed partially underground and partially above, creating a structure that resembled a massive amphitheater built into a depression in reality itself.","Some said the depression was created by a battle between THE Creature and THE Primordial Chaos during the Infinite Unfurling. Others said it was always here, waiting for conflict to fill it.","The truth was likely somewhere in between.","The Arena itself looked like a colossal structure of bronze, marble, and crystallized Existence. Its outer walls rose approximately 500 meters high, covered in bas-reliefs depicting legendary battles.","THE Entities clashed across the stonework. Absolutes warred in frozen tableaus. The history of violence made beautiful through artistic preservation.","Noah floated across the vast roads leading to this place.","Polemarchs surrounded him, their presence a statement of Glossarian support. Ul’moreth and Lumivara flanked him, their newly achieved Lochagos togas marking their advancement within this domain.","Beside him, Ul’moreth had a worried look as he spoke.","\" Absolute is difficult. Truly difficult, even if weakened to a lesser level.\"","His countless hairs rippled with concern.","\" A redundant sentence has been said that Absolutes can only ever Absolutely be taken down by other Absolutes. Do you have a plan?\"","...!","A plan.","Noah kept his eyes ahead as he replied.","\"An idea of a plan. Audacious and ridiculous by all accounts, but an idea of a plan.\"","\"...\"","Ul’moreth fell silent as he nodded.","What else could he say? His Little Anomaly had grown into something that exceeded comprehension. If anyone could find a way to challenge an Absolute without being one, it would be THE Genesis Monarch.","Ahead, Lunaris, Ophelia, and others led them through The Gate of Tongues.","The Glossarian entrance stood before them, constructed from pages of crystallized knowledge fused into solid form. Every known Logos and Philology covered its surface in inscriptions so dense they seemed to shimmer with accumulated meaning. The gate itself seemed alive, aware of those who approached it.","There were many Glossarians by the hundreds crossing into the Arena at this moment. Hoplites and Lochagoi streamed through the entrance, drawn by word that something significant was about to occur.","Lunaris and Ophelia passed through first.","The moment they crossed the threshold, the gate spoke.","\" Polemarch Lunaris has entered The Palaestra of Primordial Reckoning.\"","The voice was ancient and resonant, carrying across the surrounding area.","\" Lochagos Ophelia has entered The Palaestra of Primordial Reckoning.\"","Each name was recited with the same weight, the same significance.","And when Noah finally passed through...","\" THE Genesis Monarch has entered The Palaestra of Primordial Reckoning.\"","BOOM!","His name burned with glory!"]},{"number":4790,"title":"Chapter 4790: Chapter 4789: Egregious! III","paragraphs":["The voice seemed to carry extra weight when speaking his distinction. Extra resonance. As if even the ancient gate recognized that something unprecedented was walking through its threshold.","Many Glossarians made way for him.","Their looks were those of awe and wonder. This was the being who had contributed 9 new letters to The First Tongue, as some very well knew. This was THE Glossarian. This was someone who had achieved what even Absolutes could not.","Ahead, heavy noise bustled!","Noah looked at it all.","The interior of the Arena opened before him in magnificent scope. It followed a modified amphitheater design with distinct sections arranged in concentric circles descending toward the central combat floor. Thousands upon thousands of seats filled with beings of every description.","He saw entities of the other three philosophies here.","Chaosites and Paradoxians were roaring with fervor! They cheered and shouted, their sections a cacophony of noise and movement! Some celebrated the challenge itself! Others celebrated the chaos it would bring! Their energy was infectious, spreading excitement through the crowd like wildfire!","Existentialists watched on calmly and silently.","Their section was still. Observant. They did not cheer or jeer. They simply existed, witnessing what would unfold with the patience of those who understood that all things eventually revealed their truth.","And on the very bottom of the Arena floor...","There was a dog looking around while frowning cutely!","Skoll sat in what appeared to be a Substitution Circle, his neon flames flickering with uncertainty. His massive head turned this way and that, trying to understand why he had been brought here.","Why so many beings were watching him.","Why the nice people who had been helping his Master suddenly couldn’t help him anymore.","He looked confused.","He looked worried.","But he was still a good boy, sitting patiently and waiting for his Master to come.","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply as he saw this.","He went further in.","Lunaris spoke as they descended deeper into the Arena, her pages rustling with the formal delivery of necessary information.","\" Within The Palaestra of Primordial Reckoning, certain rules are absolute.\"","Her voice carried professional weight.","\" No faction may attack another’s members outside the combat floor. This neutral ground is sacred. Violations are punished by all four Strategoi acting in unison .\"","They continued descending.","\" Strategoi cannot directly interfere with challenges they did not issue. Glossikos the Articulate cannot intervene on your behalf, no matter how much she may wish to.\"","Her pages shifted uneasily.","\" The Right of Challenge, once properly invoked, cannot be withdrawn. THE Weavers began this. It must be seen through to conclusion.\"","They passed through rings of seating.","Hoplites watched with wide eyes as Noah passed. Lochagoi nodded with respect. Polemarchs observed with calculating gazes.","Lunaris continued her explanation.","\" The combat floor is called The Circle of Reckoning. It is the heart of The Palaestra.\"","Her pages displayed diagrams as she spoke.","\" Circular, approximately 1 kilometer in diameter. The floor can expand or contract based on the nature of the battle. For Absolute-level conflicts, it extends to accommodate existential-warping combat.\"","They were getting closer now.","\" The surface is composed of Reckoning Stone, a material that absorbs and neutralizes residual Civilizational Authority as it bears dozens of Philologies. It is inscribed with a massive seal combining elements from all four philosophies. The central point is called The Nexus of Truth. It glows faintly at all times.\"","She gestured toward the compass points of the Arena floor.","\" The Four Pillars stand at cardinal directions around arena itself...\"","Noah could see them now.","\" The Pillar of Words to the North. Glossarian. It records everything said during combat. The Pillar of Contradiction to the South. Paradoxian. It displays paradoxes emerging from battle. The Pillar of Being to the East. Existentialist. It tracks the existential state of combatants. The Pillar of Entropy to the West. Chaosite. It measures chaos generated by conflict.\"","Her voice grew more serious.","\" The Arena can generate environmental challenges based on the nature of the conflict. Barriers can be erected to contain specific types of energy as even Strategoi may not be able to leave until the battle is over, and none...can interfere.\"","She paused.","\"In short, sir, once you step onto that floor, you cannot leave until the challenge is resolved.\"","Noah barely gave a glance to all the things she mentioned.","His gaze remained on Skoll.","But he was also looking around at the higher areas of the Arena. The concentric rings of countless seats had Hoplites just above the Arena floor. Then Lochagoi in the next ring up. Then Polemarchs higher still.","And far above them all...","The Strategoi Thrones floated at the highest level.","Four massive throne platforms positioned above their respective faction’s gates.","Glossikos the Articulate’s Throne hung above the North Gate. It was constructed from living pages that constantly wrote and rewrote themselves. Floating Phonemes orbited around it like satellites.","The seat itself was carved from crystallized First Tongue, each armrest inscribed with her personal Theses. Currently empty, as she was in The Mouseion on his behalf.","Paradoxos the Dual’s Throne floated above the South Gate. Two thrones fused into one, facing opposite directions yet somehow both facing the Arena. Half obsidian, half gold, the division line constantly shifting. Observers reported seeing one occupant or two depending on the angle of observation. Currently occupied by... something. Someone. It was difficult to tell. It could also be empty.","Ontikos the Unwavering’s Throne sat above the East Gate. A single block of uncarved white marble, utterly simple yet radiating profound presence. No decorations. No inscriptions. Just pure existence given form. The most stable structure in the entire Arena, unmoved by any battle below.","Khaotikos the Unbound’s Throne existed above the West Gate. Or it didn’t. The throne refused to maintain consistent form. Sometimes it appeared as a pile of debris, sometimes as an elaborate seat, sometimes as nothing at all.","As Noah watched all of this, there was no sign of THE Weavers anywhere.","The of the four thrones of Absolutes far above may or may not be occupied, but THE Weavers themselves were absent from the Arena floor.","So he simply took a step.","He appeared on the Arena floor in an instant.","Skoll turned toward him immediately!","The massive dog’s tail began wagging with enthusiasm! His neon flames brightened! His worried frown transformed into canine joy as he bounded over to his Master!","Noah rubbed his head with a smile.","\" You okay, boy?\"","He asked such a simple question.","And Skoll...","Woof!","Nodded affirmatively!","His tail wagged even harder. Everything was fine now. His Master was here. Whatever had been confusing and scary before no longer mattered.","Such a good boy!","And a moment later, a voice boomed out across the bustling Arena.","The noise of the crowd diminished as The Voice of Reckoning spoke.","\" The challenge today has been intercepted. The Polemarch, THE Genesis Monarch, is stepping in for the challenged Hoplite.\"","A murmur rippled through the crowd.","\" The Challenger has no qualms about this.\"","The Voice paused.","\" They are now called to the stage.\"","...!","All eyes turned toward the South Gate.","The Paradoxian entrance.","Where THE Weavers would emerge."]},{"number":4791,"title":"Chapter 4791: Chapter 4790: Absolute Denial!","paragraphs":["In an area not too far from the Arena.","In a region filled with waves of Paradox and Immensity, the bodies of THE Weavers were floating above an obsidian-gold sea. The liquid below churned with contradictions made manifest, patterns that should have been impossible coexisting in constant flux.","In front of them was a throne of an Absolute.","Paradoxos the Dual sat upon it.","Or they sat upon it.","The entity defied singular description. Two figures occupied a single space, their forms overlapping and separating in constant rhythm. One face was masculine, carved with sharp features that spoke of cold logic. The other was feminine, softer lines that held warmth that contradicted the coldness of its counterpart. Both faces existed simultaneously, neither dominant, neither subservient.","Their body was half obsidian, half gold, the division line shifting with each breath. Sometimes the left side was dark and the right was bright. Sometimes it reversed. Sometimes both sides were both colors at once.","They wore robes that flowed in two directions simultaneously, fabric that defied the laws of physics by moving with and against gravity in equal measure.","Their eyes were the most unsettling aspect.","Four eyes total, two per face, each one holding depths that seemed to look at everything and nothing. They perceived truth and falsehood as the same thing. They saw possibility and impossibility as interchangeable concepts.","This was Paradoxos the Dual.","Strategos of the Paradoxian Way.","An Absolute bound to THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","And they were looking toward THE Weavers with distaste .","Yet THE Weavers remained calm.","All three bodies spoke in unison, their voices layering into something that was one and many simultaneously.","\"I can understand the hatred of you four toward us all.\"","Their golden eyes held no concern for the displeasure being directed at them.","\" But you still follow the philosophy of Paradox. The one who claimed it all can forever put you in his service.\"","Their smiles were identical across three faces.","\" Because how can you deny that which you follow?\"","...!","The three bodies of THE Weavers spoke as one.","Golden threads moved all around them, countless strings of fate and destiny swirling in patterns that only they could fully perceive. Two of the three bodies held golden scissors, and they were cutting multiple threads all at once. Snip. Snip. Snip. Each cut severed something important somewhere in Existence. Each cut altered the weavings of reality according to their design.","They worked even while conversing.","Even while facing an Absolute who clearly despised them.","Paradoxos looked at THE Weavers with a cold gaze.","Then both mouths opened, and their voice boomed out with weight that made the obsidian-gold sea churn violently.","\" We can respect and hate with great intensity.\"","The words came from two throats as one sound.","\" All of us are Absolutes, yet who decided for some of us to be locked while others run free? Who decided that the rest of us had to constantly fight?\"","Their four eyes burned with ancient grievance.","\" It does not matter either way.\"","The tone shifted to something more businesslike.","\"I have sent a message to THE Living Paradox that his three ugly little weapons have somehow landed in my place.\"","THE Weavers’ scissors paused momentarily.","\" He wanted me to tell you that your other little project, Gilgamesh, is gone.\"","The words landed with weight.","\" You did not manage to protect a good seed, he said. That in itself is a failure.\"","Paradoxos leaned forward on their contradictory throne.","\" And after this, there can be no more. There can be no surprises.\"","Their voice grew heavier.","\" So he asks you... Osmont is not an Absolute, but he is one of THE Four. If you are not confident, step out of the way, and I can take care of it.\"","The air grew thick with tension.","\" Because the glory of THE Four is written in their impossibilities that they perform. Gilgamesh now lies on that wall of impossibility, and THE Living Paradox would much prefer if THE Weavers did not join it.\"","Both faces smiled without warmth.","\" So he asks again. Are you confident?\"","...!","BOOM!","The question was a heavy one!","The three Weavers had their golden pupils spin with a sense of insult and glory! How dare anyone question their confidence? How dare THE Living Paradox himself suggest they might not be capable of handling one being who wasn’t even an Absolute?","They were about to reply when Paradoxos continued.","\" This was not a question for you to answer.\"","Their voice cut through the beginning of THE Weavers’ response.","\" He has already answered it on your behalf.\"","Paradoxos waved their hands.","\" He has paid a heavy cost to lend you this from me.\"","HUUM!","The space before THE Weavers began to distort!","Something emerged from the contradiction between existence and non-existence!","It held a blinding obsidian light of Paradox that could barely be observed! The radiance hurt to look at, not because it was bright, but because it shouldn’t have been possible to perceive! It was a thing that existed and didn’t exist, a concept given form that defied the very nature of conceptualization!","It was a collection of multiple Fragments of an Axiom!","And it looked nearly complete!","Paradoxos gestured toward the impossible object.","\" An almost complete Axiom.\"","Their voice held weight that made reality itself pay attention.","\" THE Axiom of Absolute Denial.\"","The name alone made the air grow heavier.","\" Its capability is simple, yet it is perhaps the most terrifying of all Axioms that exist, if only it were complete...\"","Paradoxos’s four eyes fixed on THE Weavers.","\" Whatever the wielder wishes to deny... is denied. Absolutely.\"","The words were simple.","The implications were not.","\" An attack coming toward you? Denied. A Declaration being enacted against you? Denied. The very concept of your defeat? Denied.\"","Their voice grew colder.","\" In its complete form, wielded by an Absolute, it would make the user nigh invincible. Nothing could touch them. Nothing could harm them. Nothing could affect them in any way they did not permit.\"","The almost complete Axiom pulsed with obsidian light.","\" This version is not complete. It has limitations. But against someone who is not an Absolute...\"","Paradoxos smiled with both faces.","\"It should be more than sufficient.\"","...!","THE Weavers looked at the almost complete Axiom of Absolute Denial.","All three bodies studied it with golden eyes that spun with calculation and growing excitement.","Then all three smiled eerily.","\" Man, now this is just overkill.\"","Their voices layered into amused acknowledgment.","\" Okay .\"","They reached out, and the almost complete Axiom flowed into their collective existence. It merged with their being, its obsidian light intertwining with the golden threads that perpetually surrounded them.","With such words, THE Weavers looked at Paradoxos.","They stopped cutting the golden strings around them.","\"I believe I have been called.\"","Their smiles held promise of violence to come.","\" See you on the other side.\"","Then, with a flash of brilliance, she disappeared!","The obsidian-gold sea continued to churn in their absence.","Paradoxos remained on their throne, four eyes staring at where THE Weavers had been with contemplation!"]},{"number":4792,"title":"Chapter 4792: Chapter 4791: Making History!","paragraphs":["Sometimes, one had to tune out the noise completely.","Regardless of whether there were thousands of entities who had all forged their Civilizations situated across The Palaestra.","Regardless of whether the four Absolutes sat on their thrones or not!","Noah looked at Skoll and finished rubbing his head.","\" Alright, go to that hairy old man there and the little fox. Stay with them no matter what, okay?\"","He pointed toward the distance where Ul’moreth and Lumivara stood alongside Lunaris and Ophelia and other Glossarians.","Skoll nodded with shining eyes!","He was no longer bound by the power that had kept him in the Substitution Circle. With a flash of neon light, he disappeared and reappeared right between Ul’moreth and Lumivara!","His tail wagged happily as he sat down like a good boy, ready to watch his Master do whatever his Master needed to do.","Noah stood up imperiously.","He looked at the other end of the Arena where at this moment, there was nobody on the other side.","And yet he remained standing.","His body began to billow with flames.","Blue-gold plasmic fire wrapped around his form like a second skin, his toga shining resplendently beneath the radiance. The Phonemes inscribed across his garments blazed brighter. The adornments of his Polemarch status caught light that seemed to come from within him rather than from any external source.","His immense foundations exceeding even THE Creature at this stage began to leak out and spread!","A sense of suffocation radiated from him!","Absolute Immovable Object!","He was an absolute immovable as at this moment, where his feet stood, he would not be moved! The Reckoning Stone beneath him seemed to groan under the weight of his presence. The air compressed around his form. Reality itself acknowledged that something heavy had planted itself in this spot.","And his aura stretched out maddeningly!","Even from afar, a sense of suffocation no Fundamental Depth entity should have radiated from him. Hoplites in the lowest seats felt their breathing grow labored. Lochagoi shifted uncomfortably under the pressure. Even some Polemarchs raised eyebrows at the intensity bleeding off this single being.","The loud noises turned into hushed whispers soon enough.","And Noah continued tuning everything out.","An instant later...","WUU!","The figures of THE Weavers appeared on the other end of the Arena!","Three bodies materialized simultaneously, each one identical to the others. Ancient crones with skin like weathered parchment, eyes of spinning gold that seemed to perceive threads invisible to all others. Their white hair flowed in patterns that defied natural movement. Their fingers were long and spindly, built for the task of cutting and weaving fate itself.","They gazed toward Noah with smiles and malice.","All three bodies even waved at him, casual gestures of greeting as if they were saying hello to a friend they were about to destroy. Their golden scissors gleamed at their sides. Their threads swirled around them in lazy spirals.","The disconnect between their friendly waves and the murderous intent in their eyes was jarring.","Moments after she appeared, three of the four thrones above seemed to have gained immense weight!","But Glossikos’s throne remained empty.","OOOH!","The Voice of Reckoning boomed out across The Palaestra.","\" Welcome to The Circle of Reckoning! The Challenger, THE Weavers, Lochagoi of the Paradoxian Way, have arrived!\"","The voice carried across every corner of the Arena.","\" And though this may seem unfair as it appears to be three against one, the three are actually a single body separated! One existence divided across three forms! This is permitted under the rules of Challenge!\"","A dramatic pause.","\" And what a Challenge this is! This debate and battle is a grand one that depicts Paradox against The First Tongue in ways that many here do not even comprehend! This is a battle of philosophies that will-\"","\"Shut the fuck up.\"","BOOM!","Noah spoke such words calmly!","The Voice of Reckoning cut off instantly!","Immense quietness descended all around as he looked at THE Weavers!","The entire Arena fell silent. Thousands of beings who had been murmuring and shifting went still. The Voice itself, ancient and supposedly unstoppable, simply... stopped.","Because THE Genesis Monarch had told it to.","And in this place, in matters concerning The First Tongue, his authority was not something that could be easily dismissed.","His imperious glare swept across the distance toward his opponents.","Radiant Seals flickered over his skin, the 27 Absolute constructs pulsing with weight that pressed against reality itself. His eyes burned with blue-gold fire. His stance was that of someone who had already decided how this would end.","He didn’t even gaze above to spare a glance at the three Absolutes he hadn’t seen before.","They were irrelevant to this moment.","He kept his gaze on THE Weavers.","\" When was the last time that an Absolute fell?\"","His voice carried across the silent Arena.","\" Do you happen to know?\"","BOOM!","The words were heavy!","THE Weavers cackled in response!","All three bodies laughed simultaneously, the sound layering into something that was one voice and many at once. Their smiles widened as terrifying pressure leaked from their bodies. The cheerful wave was replaced by something far more ancient.","Their forms shifted.","The pretense of friendly old women fell away, revealing what truly lay beneath. Decrepit ancient beings whose age transcended normal comprehension. Entities who had existed since The Infinite Unfurling, since before the modern shape of Existence was formed. Their skin grew more weathered. Their eyes burned brighter with golden malevolence. Their fingers elongated into things that looked less like appendages and more like instruments of fate itself.","\" Absolutes do not die.\"","All three voices spoke as one, carrying weight that pressed against Noah’s aura.","\" For those who do fall at the hands of other Absolutes...\"","Their smiles became something knowing and cruel.","\" We respect them enough not to spread stories of their demise. Their endings are private affairs. Their collapses are not entertainment for lesser beings.\"","...!","\" Oh?\"","Noah nodded his head at this.","Then he smiled.","\" Then it looks like I will be making history today.\"","His flames blazed brighter.","\" Come on now, you decrepit hags. Let’s see what you have up your sleeves.\"","BOOM!","The words landed like a challenge that could not be taken back!","THE Weavers’ golden eyes spun faster!","The Arena held its breath!"]},{"number":4793,"title":"Chapter 4793: Chapter 4792: You Could Never Be Me! I","paragraphs":["How exactly did one go about collapsing an Absolute that could not be collapsed?","Not even one at that, but three bodies of a single Absolute. Each body still emanated the ridiculous Depth of an Absolute Depth entity.","If you proposed this problem to any other being that did not have the level of an Absolute, they would begin digging their grave and simply wait to walk into it.","Because it was an impossible fucking situation.","And yet...","Noah held this impossible situation and was not digging his grave just yet.","He was not even thinking about utilizing an Anchor Point to activate THE Existential Paradox Loop!","This was a safeguard for his Civilization and Way, but it was not the final solution to everything. If he went across Existence with a mindset that if things were impossible to overcome, there was always the fact that he could reverse time itself... he knew that he would not achieve anything glorious in his journey.","He still treated everything that he did as if there was no safety net.","So even though he was facing an Absolute at this very moment, he did not plan to die and instead would be trying out a daring action.","THE Weavers were at the Lochagoi ranking. Even with whatever help they had received from Paradoxos, they could not raise their Merit as fast as he did with his contributions to The First Tongue.","So they were effectively supposed to be only expressing the aura of an Intermediate Depth entity.","But the sheer Immensity they radiated was enough to crush any Fundamental Depth entities.","An Absolute had to be given their respect.","Normally.","But Noah would not be giving any respect to these three shrewd fuckers.","Now, back to the main point.","The collapse of an Absolute.","His plan was actually a relatively simple one. It may only be capable of working once, maybe multiple times if he did not have an audience. But since he did not have this luxury, he merely acted.","And he...","While everyone watched breathlessly to see what move would be made by the combatants in the Arena...","Noah shockingly took his right hand and plunged it into his chest!","His muscles opened freely as if allowing everything to happen!","Crimson-gold blood leaked out to form swirling rivers around him that shaped themselves into infinity symbols! The blood moved with purpose, painting patterns of boundlessness in the air itself!","And from the hand that he plunged into his chest, he shockingly grasped an incandescent object.","And pulled out... a Heart.","DUM! DUM! DUM!","The beat of the Heart permeated across this entire place!","Every single entity in The Palaestra felt a sense of exhilaration and trepidation wash over them! The sound was not merely auditory. It resonated through their very foundations. It made their own Hearts beat in sympathy. It made their very Ways tremble with recognition of what they were perceiving!","His Heart!","THE Heart of THE Genesis Monarch of Infinite Lexicons!","It was unfathomably glorious!","The size of two fists pressed together, it blazed with blue-gold radiance that made the artificial lighting of The Palaestra seem dim by comparison. Veins of crystallized Mana ran across its surface in patterns that wrote and rewrote themselves constantly. It pulsed with life that transcended mere biological function.","Twirling Archai orbited around it like satellites around a star!","Seals of Absolute Tongue wrapped around it in protective embrace!","This was not merely an organ. This was the concentrated essence of everything Noah had become. His Claim. His Way. His authority over The First Tongue itself.","A moment later, from Noah’s head, a radiant blue-gold book also emerged!","It was none other than THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons!","Its pages opened to the halfway point, blank sheets waiting to be filled with compressed foundations. He shockingly took his Heart and placed it upon the pages of the Grimoire.","Its terrifyingly sacred aura erupted immensely in the next moment!","Every single follower of The First Tongue in The Palaestra rose to their feet in shock!","Glossarians gasped!","Hoplites fell to their knees!","Lochagoi stumbled backward!","Polemarchs reached out as if they could grasp what they were seeing from across the Arena!","The empty throne of Glossikos far above was instantly filled!","She appeared with a look of shock that transcended her normally composed demeanor! Her pages rustled violently! Her obsidian-blue eyes widened to impossible degrees!","Moments later, all others rose with utter solemnity!","Paradoxos stood on their contradictory throne, four eyes fixed on what was happening below.","Khaotikos looked over, his expression shifting to something unreadable!","Ontikos... even Ontikos seemed to lean forward slightly, a movement that for him was equivalent to screaming!","Thereafter, Noah took the Grimoire and Heart before him...","And pushed it out calmly.","It floated toward THE Weavers.","All three bodies of THE Weavers had an incredulous look on every single one of their faces.","Noah’s imposing figure stood with an open chest, crimson-gold blood still flowing in infinity patterns around him. His eyes burned with certainty that defied the madness of what he was doing.","\" That right there is the entirety of my Way and Claim of The First Tongue.\"","His voice carried across the silent Arena.","\" Many want my Claim. Many want to be one of THE Four.\"","He gestured toward the floating Grimoire and Heart.","\" As an Absolute, you should be able to tell whether it’s genuine. That right there... is everything that many dream of.\"","His smile held no warmth.","\" Take it, and you can effectively claim The First Tongue.\"","He spread his arms.","\" My... Everything.\"","...!","BOOM!","His singular action was so ridiculous and devastating and unbelievable all at once that even THE Weavers didn’t know how to react!","The Grimoire and the Heart floated toward them rapidly!","Outside the Arena, the figure of Paradoxos stood up and floated above as if they wanted to enter the Arena themselves. Their four eyes fumed with greed that contradicted itself! Two faces twisted with desire that was the same and different simultaneously!"]},{"number":4794,"title":"Chapter 4794: Chapter 4793: You Could Never Be Me! II","paragraphs":["The figure of Khaotikos the Unbound floated up and laughed madly!","His voice boomed out like bells of chaos!","\" BAHAHA! WHAT IS THIS?! WHAT IS HAPPENING?!\"","Ontikos remained still, but his body flared with multicolored flames that had not been there before. The most stable structure in the Arena was experiencing agitation.","And Glossikos...","She looked toward Noah with a gaze as if she had been betrayed!","As if she asked... dude, what the fuck?!","If he was going to give away the Claim of The First Tongue, he was just with her bathing inside pools moments ago! He had contributed 9 new Phonemes! He had gone through all 9 Cycles of Katharsis! He had achieved the distinction of Absolute Immovable Object!","And now he was just... giving it away?!","What was most anger-inducing was the fact that none of them could even interfere in this battle or enter the Arena.","Unless...","Glossikos looked toward Paradoxos.","Paradoxos also turned to look at her.","And the two of them turned to look at the other two Absolutes on their thrones.","If all four of them came to the same decision, they could override the rules of anything in this domain!","Beings at this level communicated extremely fast. Glossikos and Paradoxos communicated with Khaotikos and Ontikos as they got closer and closer to the Arena boundary, asking for all four of them to be in agreement to open it up.","Whoever could get to the Heart first, it was fair game!","And yet...","\" Bahaha... where’s the fun in that? NO!\"","Khaotikos shockingly denied them!","Glossikos and Paradoxos looked toward him with anger that could have collapsed lesser beings.","They could only whip their heads back to observe.","A radiant book and Heart which represented the very Claim for The First Tongue was floating toward THE Weavers!","Now, with how every single Absolute who could not get their hands on it was reacting, one could understand how THE Weavers felt when they had the very thing that everybody wanted coming straight for them.","Their eyes seemed to pulse with disbelief and incredulity.","They didn’t even need to ascertain whether this was a trick or anything, because as Absolutes, they could feel it!","They could feel that Noah had truly and completely laid out his Claim in that Heart and in that Grimoire!","If they took it...","If they accepted the weight of that Way and Civilization...","They would effectively be holding the Claim to the very First Tongue.","One of THE Four!","THE Four!","OH!","\" Mine! Mine!! MINE!\"","BOOM!","All three bodies of THE Weavers surged with Immensity!","Their hands outstretched toward the book and the Heart! Even the three of them, which were the same person, were fighting over who could get their hands on it first.","\" MINE!\"","The joy and euphoria on the faces of THE Weavers was absolute.","Every single one of them grabbed hold of the Grimoire and Heart.","And they sensed it!","Unbelievably, they sensed the Claim to THE First Tongue in their hands!","Even now, as they held it right in their hands, they turned toward Noah at his open chest. He was looking at them calmly.","As if they were looking at him and shaking their heads while asking... what the fuck, man? This is like, really real?!","Thereafter, they only shook their heads as if to say, what a fucking buffoon that guy was!","The euphoria of The First Tongue was just that intense.","Because this effectively meant they would be in the rare company of entities like THE Creature and THE Living Paradox and THE Primordial Chaos!","As they held the Heart and Grimoire, Glossikos outside howled out with agony and valor as if she was seeing her lover taken by another right in front of her eyes.","Paradoxos had an extremely vile expression, both faces twisted with identical fury!","Khaotikos continued to laugh, but even his laughter had taken on an edge.","Ontikos remained still, but the multicolored flames around him blazed brighter.","And in the Arena, THE Weavers roared out...","\" THE First Tongue is mine! Mine! I shall take it from the hands of the unworthy! I shall claim... THE First Tongue!\"","THE Weavers cackled while saying such words.","Incandescent blue-gold light shone everywhere.","On the other side, Noah watched on with an imperious glare.","THE Weavers began to flicker with an endless light of Mana!","An Infinite light of Mana!","An Infinite light of The First Tongue!","And...","Shockingly, their cackling laughter came to a stop.","Their expressions changed soon after.","And in the next moment...","...!","\" KAAAAA!\"","An unfathomably piercing screech that could have shattered the Depth of any Fundamental entity boomed out!","The bodies of THE Weavers trembled.","At this moment, all of their golden pupils cracked and became hollow sockets.","\" What is this?! WHAT IS THIS?! IT IS TOO MUCH!\"","BOOM!","The cracks spread across their bodies in an unfathomable progression!","Shockingly, their very Depth seemed to be collapsing inward in an unfathomable manner!","Noah watched this scene with imperious eyes.","He took a single step and appeared right before THE Weavers.","Right before the storm of billowing brilliance!","He stood inches away from them.","They were holding both his Heart and Grimoire. Their Existence was collapsing in on itself. Every single one of them was trying to pry their hands away from his Heart and Grimoire as if they no longer wanted The First Tongue.","But their fingers would not obey.","The Claim had been accepted.","And now it was consuming them!","Because... what was the only reason Noah was able to lay a Claim on The First Tongue?","What did he have that nobody else held?","Noah’s figure shone with interminable glory as he spoke at this moment.","\" You seek to hold and claim The First Tongue.\"","His voice came cold and absolute.","\" But... do you hold any Infinities within you to bear the Infinity of The First Tongue?\"","BOOM!","The words were akin to a death sentence!","THE Weavers turned their eyeless sockets to him!","He could see the incredulity, trepidation, and disbelief in their hollow gazes!","At this moment, he did not attack.","He did not even conjure up a single Seal.","Because THE Weavers... were bearing the full weight of THE First Tongue they sought to claim!","And yet they didn’t have any Infinity to back their Claim!","Their very Depth should be getting collapsed by the Immensity of THE First Tongue that permeated across all of Observable Existence.","The First Tongue was not merely a language.","It was the foundational authority of reality itself.","It permeated through every corner of Observable Existence.","It was spoken by countless beings across countless realms.","And the weight of all of that... was now pressing down on THE Weavers.","Without Infinity to bear it.","Without the capability to hold what they had so greedily grasped.","\" This... is... impossible...\"","Three voices croaked out at once.","Noah looked at them with lividity.","He raised his head imperiously.","\" You try to claim what I have when you can’t even express a glimmer of who I am?\"","His voice grew heavier.","\" You threaten my dog?\"","Heavier still.","\" You try and kill my people?\"","His eyes blazed with blue-gold fury.","\" You have THE First Tongue before you, and you can’t even claim it!\"","He took a step closer.","\" You try to do what I did, when you could never do it!\"","His voice became absolute.","\" You... COULD NEVER BE ME!\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4795,"title":"Chapter 4795: Chapter 4794: History! I","paragraphs":["As he said such terrifying words, an unfathomable Immensity that nobody could sense or see passed down.","It was the weight of all of THE First Tongue across Observable Existence pressing down on an Absolute...","And snuffing out absolutely everything!","Someone had failed their Claim on one of the four aspects of the Oldest Paradox of Existence.","And the penalty for failure... was annihilation.","Before Noah, the bodies of THE Weavers stood still.","\"...\"","No words.","No Immensity.","Nothing.","Even Noah breathed hard as if he couldn’t half believe it had occurred. As if he couldn’t believe it had worked!","He beckoned to his Heart and Grimoire.","They floated back to him.","His Heart reinserted itself into his chest, muscles closing around it as if welcoming it home. His Grimoire sank back into his existence, its pages closing with finality.","And a moment later...","His expression became heavy.","His existence buzzed with pain.","Crimson-gold blood began to leak from his nose and mouth.","| You have taken a dangerous and unprecedented action with your Claim.|","|Allowing another to attempt claiming The First Tongue has caused grievous injury to your Way.|","|Your Claim is too distinguished to be passed around freely.|","|The weight of THE First Tongue pressing down through your offered Claim has damaged the foundations you built.|","|CONSEQUENCE|","|Your comparative Way has fallen from THE Fundamental Depth to THE Intermediate Depth.|","|Your overall Formless Depth has been shaken slightly.|","|Recovery will require time and resources.|","|BUT...|","|Your Way and actions have achieved something unfathomably remarkable.|","| An Absolute has fallen.|","|I repeat, an Absolute...has fallen.|","...!","Noah felt breathless.","It had... worked?","An Absolute... had fallen?","The moment such a thing was truly ascertained...","BOOM!","From where THE Weavers floated, cracks appeared in reality itself!","These cracks glowed with obsidian-gold brilliance that shattered Existence itself.","The cracks spread outward from the point of death, spanning across The Palaestra in branching patterns that looked like lightning frozen in space!","From all around, Hoplites scrambled away from the spreading fractures.","Lochagoi fled toward the edges of the Arena.","Polemarchs erected barriers to protect themselves and those near them.","The Reckoning Stone beneath the point of collapse began to crumble!","The Four Pillars trembled!","The Nexus of Truth blazed with light it had never shown before.","Glossikos and the other Absolutes... stood where they were with a myriad of expressions and incredulity.","Glossikos looked at Noah with something that transcended shock. Her figurr had gone completely still.","Paradoxos wore expressions of fury and disbelief on both faces simultaneously.","Khaotikos had stopped laughing entirely, his features frozen in something that might have been awe.","Ontikos... for the first time in recorded history, Ontikos moved. He leaned forward on his throne of uncarved marble.","As such a terrifying thing occurred, the region where THE Weavers stood collapsed entirely!","It became a terrifying vacuum!","The bodies of THE Weavers disappeared into the void created through their failure!","Nothing remained where they had been!","Only an absence!","Only a wound in reality where something that should have existed no longer did!","| You have triggered the first death of an Absolute across Observable Existence after THE Fallout.|","|What... have you done?|","|An Unknown and Unfathomable process is beginning as a connection with something Absolute has been established.|","| THE Absolute Everythings that made up THE Absolute you collapsed are yours to claim:|","|- Their Weavings (the accumulated threads of fate they had cut and woven)|","|- Their Bodies, Their Depths (the authority they had gathered across eons)|","|- All Items on their Existence at the time of collapse|","|This includes: THE Axiom of Absolute Denial (almost complete), Fragments of Axioms|","|This includes: The Golden Scissors of Fate (three sets)|","|This includes: Accumulated threads representing countless severed destinies|","|WARNING|","|Due to the collapse of an Absolute, unknown changes are unraveling.|","|Reality is adjusting to accommodate the absence|","|Error.|","|Information procurement and analysis is temporarily being hindered. Hold on.|","BOOM!","Noah stood at the edge of the vacuum that had once been THE Weavers.","Blood continued to leak from his nose and mouth.","What truly happened when an Absolute died?","It was such a rare and impossible thing.","At this moment, at the point where the vacuum bloomed where THE Weavers used to be...","BOOM!","The vacuum collapsed in on itself again and again.","The cycle repeated with increasing intensity, reality itself unable to process what had just occurred! The absence where an Absolute had existed moments before was too profound for normal space to accommodate! It was not merely empty. It truly and unimaginably was the negation of fullness. The opposite of presence. A wound in Existence that refused to heal.","The entire scene felt tense and sacred.","As if something sacred had fallen.","As if reality itself was holding its breath, uncertain how to proceed.","And at such a moment...","An obsidian-gold pillar of Paradox instantly shot up and down.","It pierced through the ceiling of The Palaestra, through the artificial sky, through barriers that should have been impenetrable! It drove downward through the Reckoning Stone, through the foundations of the Arena, through layers of reality that descended beyond normal perception.","Other pillars of Paradox shot out in all other ordinal directions.","North and south! East and west! And diagonal trajectories that shouldn’t have existed in normal space! The pillars spread outward like the death throes of something fundamental, announcing to all of Observable Existence that one of its Absolutes had ceased to be.","Noah observed all this while his body floated gloriously and illustriously.","His chest had sealed. His Heart and Grimoire had returned to their proper places. But blood still leaked from his nose and mouth, evidence of the price he had paid for this victory.","|INFORMATION EXTRACTION CONTINUING|","|Processing with some difficulty due to unprecedented nature of event.|","|Additional information has been obtained.|","|An Absolute’s Depth is not only contained within their body like lesser beings.|","|It has permeated into Observable Existence itself through eons of existence.|","|THE Weavers existed since before THE Fallout.|","|Their authority had woven itself into the fabric of reality across countless weavings of Existence, and all of this has been collapsed.|","|DEATH CONSEQUENCE|","|When an Absolute dies, this Depth begins to hemorrhage back out of Existence.|","|All Absolutes across Observable Existence will sense the hemorrhaging Depth of another Absolute.|","|They will know what has occurred.|","|The Depth that is hemorrhaging will go toward...!|","| WATCH OUT!|","BOOM!"]},{"number":4796,"title":"Chapter 4796: Chapter 4795: History! II","paragraphs":["The words of Ruination in the form of prompts only arrived as a blinding pillar of obsidian-gold light shot forth from the vacuum!","It smashed into Noah with force that would have obliterated anything less than what he had become!","But since he was an Absolute Immovable Object, he was not moved back.","He took the impact with a changing expression.","An unbelievably dense concentration of Civilizational Authority flowed toward him.","It was... Absolute Civilizational Authority! The accumulated power of an entity that had existed since before THE Fallout, compressed and channeled directly into his existence.","But it was so unfathomably heavy and painful that he almost felt like he would unravel!","His foundations, already damaged from offering his Claim, groaned under the additional weight before they ate everything and began to recover in an unfathomable way, basked and seeking to integrate what wss coming in.","His Seals of Absolute Tongue blazed with desperate intensity as they tried to process the incoming Depth!","His very Way trembled as authority that belonged to Paradox attempted to merge with authority that belonged to The First Tongue!","But...","|Your Formless Depth withstands against the Immensity of THE Absolute Depth of Absolute Sovereignty flowing into your Existence.|","|You are the entity who caused the causal collapse of an Absolute.|","|By the weavings of Existence, you inherit...most of what they held.|","|By the nature of your Formless classification, you can bear what others could not.|","|Integration proceeding.|","|Integration painful.|","|Due to the collapse of an Absolute, something unique has began to permeate across Observable Existence.|","|THE SILENCE|","|For a brief moment, everything stops.|","|All conflict pauses.|","|All noise ceases.|","|Existence itself seems to mourn, or celebrate.|","|The passing of an Absolute is acknowledged by all aspects of reality.|","...!","Noah felt his Immensity burning and surging up!","But more than this, Existence seemed to truly be mourning.","When he looked around, he felt threads of Paradox mourning.","They wept in ways that transcended normal emotion. The obsidian-gold Weavings that permeated Observable Existence trembled with loss. One of their own had fallen. One who had served THE Living Paradox since before THE Fallout. One who had cut and woven countless destinies.","Gone.","He felt threads of Chaos mourning and buzzing with excitement simultaneously.","The contradiction was pure Chaos. Sorrow and joy coexisting. Loss and gain indistinguishable. Khaotikos’s domain recognized both the tragedy and the opportunity in equal measure.","And surrounding Weavings of Existence and The First Tongue... mourning!","Even his own Claim grieved for what had been lost!","Why?","Why would they be mourning the death of an Absolute?!","THE Weavers had been an enemy! They had hunted him! They had threatened his people! They had targeted his dog!","And yet reality itself wept for their passing!","Noah’s gaze was one of immense glory and Tyranny as if he wanted to rebuke the very aspects of the Oldest Paradox of Existence!","How dare they mourn his enemy?","How dare Existence grieve for those who sought to destroy him?","But he stood there, beginning to accept the rewards and, apparently, the consequences of killing an Absolute.","What he was receiving now seemed to only be the tip of the iceberg.","Since prior to this, he had seen the prompts that detailed the bodies of THE Weavers and everything they held. Which apparently included an Axiom that was almost complete among other things.","All his to claim.","So he stood in what used to be an Arena.","And yet, right now, it was an immense vacuum caused by the collapse of an Absolute. The void continued to collapse in on itself while pillars of incandescent waves of Paradox radiated all around.","The seats that had held thousands of observers were shattered or displaced. The Four Pillars that had stood at compass points around The Circle of Reckoning were cracked and leaning. The Reckoning Stone itself had fractured into countless pieces that floated in the altered gravity around the vacuum.","Around the destroyed Palaestra, four Absolutes gazed toward him with grave eyes.","Eyes as if they were all looking at... an enemy!","As if none of them had truly believed the collapse of an Absolute here was possible.","Glossikos floated near her empty throne, her eyes completely still. Whatever she had found in THE Mouseion of Fated Artifacts remained unknown, as she had returned the moment she sensed what was happening. Her obsidian-blue eyes held something between awe and immensity.","Paradoxos stood on the edge of the destruction, both faces twisted with identical fury. Their four eyes burned with hatred that transcended their normal contradictions. One of THEIR Absolutes had been killed. One who followed THEIR philosophy. And the one who had done it stood before them, covered in blood but very much alive.","Khaotikos’s laughter had stopped.","But one could see his eyes trembling with veiled excitement and wonder.","\" The first Absolute to fall was from Paradox.\"","His voice echoed out across the ruined Arena.","\" And the first one to kill an Absolute was not any of the oldest Four...\"","His grin returned, but it held edges that cut.","\" But the youngest and weakest of THE Four!\"","He laughed, but it was not the carefree chaos of before.","\" Haha... haha!\"","His menacing words echoed out as something far too immense had occurred here.","At this time, Paradoxos stood up grandly.","Their visage emanated waves of menace as they looked toward Noah! The contradiction of their dual nature seemed to have resolved into a singular purpose. Hatred. Pure and undiluted.","Glossikos had her chest rising up and down as if she was on the cusp of making a truly grand decision.","Her eyes flickered between Noah and the vacuum where THE Weavers had been. Between the one who had given her hope for reclaiming what she never had, and the evidence of what that one was capable of doing to Absolutes.","And Ontikos... well, he was particularly unique.","The multicolored glow and flames of Existence around him took on an even heavier intensity. The glow focused on his eyes. They became glazed over as if... as if another was looking through them.","And through that gaze alone, it seemed like a Depth that was more than ten times as grand, if not unfathomably more, was looking at Noah.","Observing THE Genesis Monarch standing amidst the ruins of an Arena, covered in his own blood, surrounded by the hemorrhaging Depth of a dead Absolute.","The death of an Absolute was already an impossibility.","The one who collapsed that Absolute was even more of an impossibility.","It was a single action.","But its effects only just began!"]},{"number":4797,"title":"Chapter 4797: Chapter 4796: THE Youngest Moves First I","paragraphs":["Observable Existence was unfathomably vast.","So vast that one could say the only entities who could truly understand the scope of its vastness had to be entities that had attained THE Absolute Depth.","But in the vastness of Existence, far from the Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap or the endless Weavings of The Wastes of THE Fallout...","In a Primordial Realm known as Alfheimr.","Primordial Realms of Existence were each different. No single one was the same as the other. Some could argue that some realms were lesser, while others were grander.","For anyone making such an argument, Alfheimr... could be considered one of the places that sat at the very top.","At this moment.","The realm stretched out in wonders of impossible beauty. Forests of crystalline trees rose toward skies that shifted between aurora and starlight. Rivers of liquid radiance flowed through valleys carved from solidified dreams. Mountains of pure condensed Mana pierced through clouds that sang when the wind passed through them.","Everything here was more!","More vibrant, ore alive, nore real than reality had any right to be.","In a region where the crystalline forests gave way to meadows of luminescent grass, three figures moved across serenely.","THE Primordial Chaos walked with the casual ease of someone who owned everything and nothing simultaneously. His form shifted constantly, never maintaining the same appearance for more than a few moments.","One instant he was tall and imposing, the next compact and dense. His features rearranged themselves according to no discernible pattern.","THE Living Emotive floated beside him, her body crackling with emotions that changed faster than expressions could form.","THE Living Elemental trailed behind them, his form shrouded by the Phonemes of Fire, Air, Earth, and Water. The four fundamental concepts swirled around him in constant rotation, each one manifesting in brilliant displays.","He moved with the caution of someone who knew he was in the presence of beings far more powerful than himself.","And yet a moment later, their gazes were those of astonishment!","They looked up and saw the illusion of an endlessly blinding pillar of obsidian-gold light shooting across Alfheimr itself!","It wasn’t physically present.","It was a sign.","A signal that permeated across Observable Existence.","Now, the vision of Absolutes was unique. They directly knew what the pillar that they saw meant. Due to their status, they were even able to understand and read what this pillar meant in ways that others could never imagine.","After all, this was a signal that permeated across Observable Existence, but for the most part, it was mainly Absolutes who would gaze upon it and understand exactly what it meant.","And they had not expected to see something like this so soon.","It meant the collapse of another Absolute!","\" This is the signature of THE Weavers!\"","THE Living Emotive’s voice came out in a shriek of disbelief and excitement.","\" THE fucking Weavers! What happened?!\"","Her eyes shone with an ecstatic and crazy light as if seeing such a thing gave her a thrilling high!","\" Did THE Creature go scorched Existence?!\"","She was genuinely shocked!","Even though THE Weavers were what could be considered entities from her camp. Since she also moved alongside THE Living Paradox and THE Loom.","Even though at this very moment, she was standing beside THE Primordial Chaos.","But this woman seemed to have absolutely no allegiances.","At this moment, both her and Elemental looked deeply into this pillar that represented the collapse of an Absolute. It communicated many things for those who could perceive them.","Right now they knew the identity of who had been collapsed.","And they were reading the sign that permeated across Observable Existence to seek out... who had done the collapsing.","But before they could fully arrive at an answer...","THE Primordial Chaos frowned.","His grand and magisterial figure billowed with waves of disorder as he spoke calmly.","\" It is not THE Creature. He would not kill.\"","His voice held certainty that transcended normal perception.","\" It is... THE Youngest.\"","BOOM!","Chaos did not even need to look at the dazzling sign above to find out information on exactly what had happened.","He simply knew.","\" THE Youngest? Who the fuck is the youngest?\"","Emotive’s expression shifted through confusion and dawning realization.","\" Wait... you don’t mean...\"","She was astonished!","She wanted to see it for herself!","Focusing on the Sign above, she poured her perception into reading its message. Moments later, a barely imperceptible image formed within the obsidian-gold light.","An image of... Osmont!","It looked grand. Immovable. Standing imperiously in a toga, surrounded by blue gold flames!","But it was there.","Emotive and Elemental were shocked to confirm it!","Osmont!","Osmont?!","That fucker wasn’t even at THE Surface Depth before THE Fallout, right?!","THE Living Elemental had sent him a savage curse of burning from THE Loom. At that time, Osmont was not at THE.","He had been nothing!","A speck!","An ant that Elemental had tried to crush.","And now...","\" Haha... no fucking way, right?\"","THE Living Emotive’s body shone with a manic light of countless emotions!","\" The weakest of THE Four is the first one who made a move to kill an Absolute?!\"","Her laughter echoed across the luminescent meadows of Alfheimr.","\" And not just any Absolute, but THE Weavers?! I mean, I know they’re a bit shit since they fully rely on Paradox, but still... damn!\"","Her emotions cycled faster and faster as she processed the implications!","And then her expression shone as if she gained a new understanding.","She looked toward THE Living Elemental.","Who had an absolutely ashen expression.","A brutal and somewhat heavy scene unfolded as THE Living Emotive pointed at him while she laughed with mania!","\" Haha, Elemental, you’re absolutely fucked!\"","Her finger jabbed toward him accusingly.","\" Did you not curse the youngest before he even became THE?! He must fucking hate you!\"","Her laughter grew more unhinged.","\" And you... you are not stronger than THE Weavers, are you? Maybe about the same?\"","She tilted her head with mock concern.","\" Woah woah woah... this means your existence is on a timer!\"","Her grin became something feral.","\" That... is fucking hilarious!\"","...!"]},{"number":4798,"title":"Chapter 4798: Chapter 4797: THE Youngest Moves First II","paragraphs":["THE Living Emotive said such terrifying words.","THE Living Elemental looked at her with icy and flaming eyes simultaneously.","But he did not respond.","Because what could he say?","This entire time, the calm figure of THE Primordial Chaos looked between the two of them as if he was watching children bickering.","\" THE Youngest killed that tiny Absolute...\"","His voice came measured and thoughtful.","\" Before they grasped Absolute themselves.\"","He paused.","\" But when it comes to whether he has the capability to collapse any Absolutes similar to the little Weavers...\"","His shifting features settled into something resembling certainty.","\" He is not there yet.\"","...!","These words were heavy!","THE Living Emotive instantly turned toward THE Primordial Chaos.","Her body slid up behind him, arms wrapping around his massive form in an embrace that should have been impossible given their size difference. She whispered in his ear with the intimacy of a conspirator sharing secrets.","\" Big guy, what did you find out? Can you share with us?\"","Her voice dripped with curiosity and hunger for information.","THE Primordial Chaos was unbothered by the actions of THE Living Emotive.","He simply waved his hands.","And in the next moment, a massive illusory screen appeared above them.","It played out events that had occurred in a distant Palaestra within THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","It showed THE Weavers and Osmont.","It showed Osmont... presenting them with a beating Heart!","The scene played out in perfect clarity. THE Weavers grasping for the Grimoire and Heart. Their euphoria. Their screams. Their collapse.","THE Primordial Chaos’s expression billowed with endless obsidian Weavings of Chaos as he spoke.","\" If you do not want to face an early collapse from the hands of THE Youngest... just leave his Heart alone for now.\"","His voice held warning.","\" He was able to grasp The First Tongue for a reason.\"","His shifting features darkened.","\" THE Weavers did not have that reason. And they tried to do the same.\"","Contempt entered his tone.","\" They read countless fates. And yet they were foolish enough not to know what would happen?\"","He shook his head.","\"It is a waste for any Absolute to fall, but...\"","A glorious and grand expression flashed across the eyes of THE Primordial Chaos!","\" Chaos is rising now and gaining an edge. While this entire time, Paradox and Existence have been seeking supremacy.\"","His smile became something vast and terrible.","\" With the collapse of the first Absolute... hmmm.\"","He hummed to himself with satisfaction that made the air around them vibrate with disorder.","Emotive and Elemental could not take their eyes away from the events playing out on the illusory screen!","---","At this same time, and even actually in the same place.","In a different region of Alfheimr.","A serene area of radiant waterfalls cascaded from floating islands that hung gloriously in the air. The islands themselves were composed of crystallized Mana so pure that they glowed with soft inner light.","Waterfalls caught the aurora light of Alfheimr’s ever-shifting sky, refracting into countless colors that painted the mist with rainbows that never faded.","On one waterfall, the figure of THE Living Origin sat.","She played with the water as if she was playing with something from home.","And it was home to her.","She and THE First Hunger had just arrived in Alfheimr!","The journey through The Wastes of THE Fallout had been harrowing, but Origin knew paths through the chaos that others did not. She had walked these routes long before THE Fallout had transformed them into nightmares.","Tor stood behind her and watched her back calmly.","His crimson-obsidian eyes observed her as she played with the water and enjoyed being back home after so long. His expression was unreadable, but there was something in the way he positioned himself that was a bit...protective!","THE Living Origin raised her gaze at this moment.","She turned to look at Tor, her hair and eyes shining with gorgeous white-gold radiance. The Origin within her seemed to resonate with Alfheimr itself, as if this realm recognized one of its oldest daughters.","She began speaking to him with a somewhat difficult expression.","\"I can’t...\"","Before she could say the rest of her words, she looked up in shock!","Tor looked up alongside her!","They saw the pillar of obsidian-gold light tearing across the skies of Alfheimr!","Origin was astonished.","Tor was confused.","He tilted his head and said with genuine uncertainty in his voice.","\" What is that?\"","Origin had a grave expression as she replied.","\" That is the sign of collapse of an Absolute.\"","Her voice carried weight that made the water around her grow still.","\"I wonder which one of those monsters has made the move...\"","...!","Monsters.","She was thinking along the lines of either THE Living Paradox or THE Primordial Chaos, or even potentially THE Creature!","She was not an Absolute, so she was not able to fully read that sign. But she had seen a sight like that before. Long ago. In ages that most had forgotten!","She could recognize it.","She wondered.","Just which monstrous thing collapsed an Absolute?","---","Far from Alfheimr.","In a completely different Primordial Realm with its own musings of Existence.","Within... Jotunheim!","The realm stretched out in wonders of brutal grandeur. Mountains of black ice rose toward skies that crackled with perpetual lightning. Glaciers the size of continents groaned as they shifted across landscapes carved by violence that predated memory.","And across these frozen wastelands, the glorious Chaos Giants of Existence moved!","Beings of impossible scale, their forms composed of elemental fury given flesh. Some stood hundreds of meters tall, their footsteps causing earthquakes that reshaped the terrain. Others were smaller, merely the size of mountains, but no less fearsome.","Their skin was the color of storms and obsidian. Their eyes burned with the light of dying folds. They were chaos incarnate, descendants of forces that had existed since before differentiation.","Most of them were Pre-THE entities, powerful but not having crossed the threshold into true Depth classification.","But there were also a few hundred entities who had formed their Depth here.","Sitting at THE Surface and Intermediate Depths and Fundamental Depths!","They were the elite of Jotunheim’s Chaos Giants!"]},{"number":4799,"title":"Chapter 4799: Chapter 4798: THE Youngest Moves First III","paragraphs":["An ancient citadel dominated one region of this brutal realm.","The Citadel of Churning Eternities.","It was carved from a glacier that had been frozen since before time learned to count. Its walls were black ice infused with threads of Chaos that made them stronger than any mundane material. Spires rose toward the lightning-filled sky like accusations against the heavens.","Chaos Giants moved across its battlements and through its halls, their massive forms somehow fitting within architecture that seemed too small to contain them.","Inside that grand citadel, elevated above everything else, sat a temple.","The Temple of Temporal Observation.","Its construction defied normal understanding. Parts of it existed in multiple timeframes simultaneously. Its walls showed scenes from past, present, and futures that might or might not occur. The floor was made from crystallized moments, each tile a frozen instant of history.","It was forged specifically for one being!","Inside the temple...","Three figures sat around a bonfire.","But the bonfire was not mere flame.","It was a Fragment of an Axiom.","Burning with authority that transcended normal fire, it cast shadows that moved independently of the light source. It crackled with power that made the air heavy with potential.","Around the three figures, beautiful Chaos Giants moved to serve them.","These were not the brutal warriors of the citadel’s exterior. These were refined, elegant beings whose chaos had been shaped into grace. They carried Sacred Drinks in vessels carved from frozen lightning. They offered Sacred Panaceas on platters made from solidified time.","Out of the three being served here, the most powerful was an entity shrouded by dancing purple flames of time.","THE Living Temporal.","His face was ancient beyond ancient. Lines of accumulated eons carved into features that had witnessed the birth and death of countless civilizations. His eyes were not eyes at all, but windows into the Rivers of Time themselves, purple depths that showed currents flowing in all directions simultaneously.","His hair was silver-white, flowing like temporal streams around a face that held wisdom and cruelty in equal measure. He was neither young nor old, but both and neither, his age existing in superposition.","The aura of an Absolute around him was so heavy that one might mistake him as one of THE Four.","He was not.","But he was close enough that the distinction barely mattered.","When a fucker could mess with time so much, the potential to become powerful was insane.","And the other two near him also radiated auras of Absolutes.","One shone with the multicolored glow of prismatic light. Her eyes burned like prisms, refracting everything she looked at into component spectrums.","THE Living Quantum!","The other had silver brilliance surrounding him completely, making his entire body hazy. He existed in multiple locations simultaneously, his form never quite settling into a single position!","THE Living Dimensional.","At this moment, their heads were raised high.","They looked at the imposing pillar of obsidian-gold light that tore across the skies of Jotunheim.","As Absolutes, they had already discerned what that sign meant.","Who was killed.","And who had done the killing.","And they were silent because...","\" Well...\"","THE Living Dimensional was the first to speak.","His voice came deep and resonant, slightly echoing as if arriving from multiple directions at once. His bald head gleamed in the light of the Fragment Axiom bonfire. His thick beard was silver like the rest of him, braided with threads of dimensional energy.","\" We set up shop in Jotunheim because you told us that in a possible future timeline, Osmont passes here, Temporal.\"","He turned toward THE Living Temporal with eyes that held calculated concern.","\" But now the question is... do we want to be here when he passes if this freak has already begun killing Absolutes?\"","BOOM!","The words landed with weight that made the Sacred Drinks ripple in their vessels!","THE Living Temporal turned to look at Dimensional with eyes that contained rivers flowing through them.","\"We do not know the nature of how things unfolded.\"","His voice came measured and calm.","\" At this time, THE Youngest of THE Four has not yet reached the stage of an Absolute. It would be part of the reasons why he is killing without understanding anything.\"","...!","THE Living Quantum put down her cup.","She tasted the Sacred liquid on her lips, her prismatic eyes dancing with colors that shouldn’t exist in normal spectrums.","\" And what an entrance this being is making.\"","Her smile held appreciation.","\" Not even an Absolute, and yet, he has taken down an Absolute.\"","She tilted her head with genuine curiosity.","\" Could any of you have done that before you became Absolutes?\"","She was calm as she asked this question.","The two beside her did not reply for a moment.","Because the answer was obvious.","No.","None of them could have.","Maybe THE Creature and THE Primordial Chaos. Definitely THE Living Paradox.","An instant later, THE Living Temporal raised his gaze.","Rivers of Time and Wheels of Time passed through his eyes with immensity and glory. Purple flames danced higher around his form as if responding to his focus.","\" In Observable Existence, countless geniuses, anomalies, and tremendous beings have always risen and fallen over time.\"","His voice came with the weight of someone who had seen it all.","\" THE Primordial Paradox was an unfathomable genius. A tremendous anomaly of an existence.\"","He paused, letting the words settle.","\" And he had everything that he built devoured alongside his Claim by THE Living Paradox. A peasant.\"","His eyes met those of his companions.","\" Existence is grand and unfathomable. And the Rivers of Time are relentless in nature.\"","He took a Sacred Drink from a serving Chaos Giant, sipping it with the unhurried grace of someone who had all the time in Existence.","\" When their churning waters cool, who knows who will still be breathing with their heads raised high?\"","He set the drink down.","\" And who knows who will be lying at the bottom of the bottomless Rivers of Time?\"","His smile was thin and knowing.","\" Even Absolutes have no guarantee.\"","He leaned back, the purple flames of time dancing around him like loyal servants.","\" Whatever you two decide, I will stay here.\"","His eyes turned toward the fading pillar of obsidian-gold light.","\" Waiting for Osmont.\"","...!"]},{"number":4800,"title":"Chapter 4800: Chapter 4799: THE Youngest Moves First IV","paragraphs":["THE Living Quantum and THE Living Dimensional exchanged glances.","THE Living Temporal remained grand and unbothered as if he truly held all the time in Existence.","The sign of an Absolute’s collapse continued to radiate across the skies of Jotunheim.","And in the Temple of Temporal Observation, three Absolutes contemplated what this development meant for the future that was already beginning to shift!","---","In THE Corrupted Vault of Ginnungagap.","Noah stared into the calm eyes of THE Secretive Eon.","She had been looking at him without a word ever since the pillar of obsidian-gold light signifying the collapse of an Absolute permeated across this space.","Ever since it became clear that he had collapsed THE Weavers!","The eyes of this terrifying entity seemed to be trying to grasp something. Or look at something within him. But they couldn’t quite get to it.","His Formless Depth made him difficult to read.","His foundations that exceeded THE Creature in some aspects made him difficult to assess.","And whatever she was searching for remained hidden behind layers of authority that even an Absolute could not easily penetrate.","Eventually... she spoke.","\"Do you remember when the last time was that an Absolute died before today?\"","Her voice came calm and measured, as if asking about the weather rather than the death of beings who shaped reality itself.","Noah shook his head grandly.","\"I actually haven’t been around all that long to know such things.\"","His voice held honesty!","\"I was a tiny wee little human with no power or say while THE Living Paradox had already had THE Loom established for eons. While all THEs and THE Creature was suppressed...\"","He paused.","\"I am actually too young to even remember such things.\"","...!","He truly was too young!","A bit over 3 years back, he awakened to become a Hunter.","At that time, things had already been unfolding across scales he couldn’t comprehend.","His mind simply had no idea.","He knew nothing of THE Creature and his Belly of Existence while he was hunting Apes in The Ape’s Paradise Dungeon. He had been focused on survival, on getting stronger.","He knew nothing about Wheels of Existence and Folds and Early Veiled Shores. He had been worried about rent payments and why his Focus, why his Mana, was blank.","Time... was such a unique thing.","On this major milestone of collapsing an Absolute, he found himself... reflective.","Where had he been three years ago?","Where was he now?","Standing in the aftermath of killing an Absolute, speaking with another Absolute as if they were equals.","The journey between those two points felt both impossibly long and impossibly short.","And yet in front of him...","THE Secretive Eon laughed!","The sound was musical and unsettling, holding depths that made the air around them vibrate with hidden meaning.","\" You were too young?\"","Her smile grew wider.","\" You were active more than billions of years ago in The Earliest Folds. And I saw you in Ginnungagap even further before that.\"","Her eyes sparkled with ancient knowledge.","\" Age is a unique thing. Some can claim to be young...\"","She leaned closer.","\"But not you. You cannot claim to be young.\"","BOOM!","...!","The words landed with weight!","\" But, if you haven’t seen it, then you haven’t seen it.\"","THE Secretive Eon waved her hand dismissively.","\" The collapse of an Absolute... everything mourns it. Existence mourns it.\"","Her voice grew more serious.","\" Because Absolutes are critical. Observable Existence loves Absolutes.\"","Noah raised his brows at such words.","He looked at Eon with eyes that held challenge.","\" Are you truly going to be lecturing me on the importance of Absolutes and not killing Absolutes when you are planning to kill Absolutes with me?\"","His voice came direct and unafraid.","\" You wish to collapse THE Four. Arguably the most critical of the Absolutes.\"","He tilted his head.","\" Where exactly would your argument be going here?\"","...!","His eyes were radiant as he said this!","And the figure of THE Secretive Eon looked at him.","She put her hand on her chin.","And smiled even brighter.","\" Your words to me seem to be getting bolder and bolder as you do more and more things.\"","Her eyes danced with something that might have been approval.","\"Is there a confidence growing, O Scale Breaker?\"","She laughed again.","\" But anyhow... what you do and what I do is different .\"","Her voice grew more instructive.","\" When you collapse an Absolute, you take away what they contribute to overall Existence. THE Weavers contributed to the fate-weaving aspects of Paradox. Now that contribution is gone. Observable Existence is slightly diminished.\"","She paused.","\" When I collapse an Absolute, I replace.\"","Her smile held pride that transcended normal ego.","\" Nothing is lost.\"","She began pacing slowly, her form drifting through the air with casual grace.","\"I have the potential capability to collapse THE Primordial Chaos under the right circumstances... and be capable of taking on what he contributes to the overall Existence. I would become what he was. His Claim would become my Claim. His role would become my role.\"","She turned back to face him.","\"I will commend you for doing something I did not believe the current you could do. I give credit where credit is due.\"","Her eyes sharpened.","\" But whether you can successfully carry out the other half of the actions required after collapsing an Absolute is yet to be seen.\"","She tilted her head.","\" Has THE Absolute Existential Palace formed yet? It should be about time soon...\"","THE Absolute Existential Palace?","Noah raised his brows at this unfamiliar term.","THE Secretive Eon smiled and explained.","\" It is the remnant of Existence that forms after an Absolute dies. Where you can claim all that the Absolute held...items, depth, memories...\"","Her voice grew heavier.","\" And whether their collapse will be a complete loss for Existence, or not.\"","She paused dramatically.","\" Of course, I know about this because...\"","Her eyes met his directly.","\" You are not the only one who has collapsed an Absolute.\"","BOOM!","The words landed like thunder!"]}]);
